### Trajectory analysis

The 2025 edition marked a clear acceleration: attendance up 50%, exhibitors up 17% and net exhibition space up 62% compared with the previous edition. This momentum, driven by the convergence of civil and military drone uses, led the organisers to move UAV Show from a biennial to an annual rhythm from 2026, in order to keep pace with the acceleration of innovation and the geopolitical context of the sector.', seo_title_en='UAV Show 2026 Bordeaux: professional drone trade show (7-9 October)', seo_description_en='UAV Show 2026, the 9th edition of the European professional drone and autonomous systems trade show, from 7 to 9 October at the Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux. Civil, defence, dual-use: 110 exhibitors, Demo Day, conferences.' WHERE slug='air-drone-bordeaux';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **The trade show for customer experience, artificial intelligence, digital marketing, e-commerce and data**: All4Customer Paris brings together CX, AI, data, retail and digital commerce under a single banner.
- **Organiser**: Weyou Group, which has been developing a unique model of highly qualified business meetings across Europe since 2009. An **annual** trade show, it became All4Customer Paris in 2024 following the merger of the Stratégie Clients and E-Marketing Paris shows.
- **Next edition**: 23, 24 and 25 March 2027 at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), Hall 6.
- **2026 results (organiser figures)**: 15,996 participants, 233 exhibitor stands, 145 sessions (17 plenaries, 27 expert conferences, 71 masterclasses, 30 workshops).
- **Positioning**: a hybrid trade show + expert conference format, focused on marketing and customer-relations operations, with generative and agentic AI running as the common thread of the recent edition.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The exhibitor offering is organised around four families: customer-relations management and user experience, digital marketing strategies and tools, e-commerce and digital commerce solutions, and data collection and analysis. You will find CRM and CCaaS software publishers, conversational AI platforms, UX/UI agencies, customer-relations outsourcing service providers, and data and personalisation solutions. Presence formats range from bare stands to turnkey stands (4 to 16 sq m), with an Innovation Village zone dedicated to start-ups (3 sq m).

### Notable exhibitors

The 2026 edition featured Odigo as Gold sponsor, and Verint, Zoho, Mitel and Foundever as Silver sponsors. The full list, classified by category, is published on the [official exhibitors page](https://www.all4customer-paris.com/exposants).

### Quality of attendance

The 2026 edition gathered 15,996 participants (organiser figure). Attendance is mainly made up of decision-makers and operational staff in marketing, customer relations, e-commerce and data, on both the advertiser and the service-provider sides.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The conference programme is a cornerstone of the event: 145 sessions in total at the 2026 edition, split into 17 plenary conferences, 27 expert conferences, 71 masterclasses and 30 workshops. The Verdi and Mozart amphitheatres host the expert conferences and masterclasses. The themes of the recent edition gave pride of place to applied AI (customer-service automation, agentic AI in contact centres, AI and sales performance), to omnichannel, to the voice of the customer, and to aligning CX with financial performance.

### Institutional partners

All4Customer Paris draws on a network of trade associations in customer relations and digital marketing. In 2026: CPA France, AFRC, ESCDA, AMARC and SP2C were among the official institutional partners. ESCDA (a customer-relations certification scheme) is a partner of the trade show, distinct from the event itself.

### Community & networks

The event relies on the Weyou Group ecosystem and on specialist media partners: E-marketing, Relation Client Mag, Blog du Modérateur, Agora News Experience Client, Sens du Client, CX Advisor, My Digital Week.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking, transport and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the trade show:
- 2027 dates: Tuesday 23, Wednesday 24 and Thursday 25 March 2027.
- Location: Hall 6, 2 place de la Porte de Versailles, 75015 Paris.
- Opening hours (recent edition): 9am-6pm on day 1, 9am-8pm on day 2 (late opening), 9am-5pm on day 3. To be reconfirmed on the website before visiting.
- Visitor registration and badge via the official Weyou Group platform.

## How much it costs to exhibit

The stand pricing grid is not published in open access on the official website: the quote is built on request from Weyou Group depending on surface area, location and package (Gold/Silver sponsoring, conference speaking slots, visibility options). The available formats range from bare stands to turnkey stands (4 to 16 sq m), with a start-up formula (3 sq m in the Innovation Village) and speaking options at an expert conference (capacity 100-150 people, with video recording) or an agora workshop (40 people, reserved for exhibitors).

<BudgetTable warning="Indicative sector ranges (B2B professional trade show, Porte de Versailles). No pricing is published by the organiser: to be confirmed by quote." rows={[{ "poste": "Equipped stand (depending on surface area)", "low": "9,000 €", "high": "30,000 €" }, { "poste": "Fit-out, furniture, signage", "low": "3,000 €", "high": "12,000 €" }, { "poste": "Sponsoring / conference speaking slot", "low": "5,000 €", "high": "25,000 €" }, { "poste": "Staff, travel, accommodation", "low": "4,000 €", "high": "12,000 €" }, { "poste": "Marketing, leads, goodies", "low": "2,000 €", "high": "8,000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (indicative)", "low": "~23,000 €", "high": "~85,000 €" }]} footer="Indicative estimate intended for budget framing. Request an official quote from Weyou Group." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- **6 months out**: choice of package (bare/equipped stand, sponsoring, conference), booking of the location in Hall 6.
- **4 months out**: stand brief, scheduling of a conference speaking slot if relevant, plan for prospecting meetings.
- **2 months out**: invitation campaign to your database, preparation of AI/CX demos, qualification of targets.
- **2 weeks out**: build logistics, training the team on the pitch and lead scanning.

### For the decision-maker visitor

Prepare a targeted route by universe (CX, digital marketing, e-commerce, data, AI), pre-select the conferences in the Verdi and Mozart amphitheatres, and plan your meetings with software publishers in advance. The conference-dense format rewards reading the programme before arriving.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Weyou Group runs a CSR/ESG programme at group level, built around the environment (reduction of its carbon footprint, waste optimisation, circular economy, an SNCF partnership for the low-carbon mobility of participants: 136.75 kg CO2e saved per person), ethics, sustainability and inclusivity. The group is based in High Environmental Quality buildings and is a signatory to the Principles for Responsible Investment (PRI). On the content side, the trade show incorporates CSR/ESG and responsible digital marketing topics into its exhibitor offering and its conferences. The detail of these commitments is set out on the organising group''s CSR/ESG page.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2027 (upcoming)", "dates": "23-25 March 2027", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles, Hall 6", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "2026", "dates": "24-26 March 2026", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles", "visiteurs": "15,996", "exposants": "233" }, { "edition": "2024", "dates": "26-28 March 2024", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles, Hall 4", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }]} sources="Official All4Customer Paris website (Weyou Group), 2026 edition results." />

### Trajectory analysis

All4Customer Paris is the product of a consolidation: the merger, carried out by Weyou Group, of the Stratégie Clients (customer relations) and E-Marketing Paris (digital marketing) shows, brought together under a single brand from the 2024 edition onwards. The logic is to cover the marketing - data - customer experience - e-commerce chain in one go, where the two original shows addressed complementary but separate segments.

The recent repositioning places artificial intelligence, first generative then agentic, at the centre of the message, which broadens the audience towards data and tech functions without losing the historic customer-relations and marketing base. With nearly 16,000 participants and a programme of 145 sessions in 2026, the trade show displays a hybrid trade show + media/content profile, a format that shapes the visitor experience as much as the exhibitor offering.', seo_title_en='All4Customer Paris 2027: dates, exhibitors, programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='All4Customer Paris 2027: 23-25 March at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles (Hall 6). Trade show for customer experience, AI, digital marketing, e-commerce and data. 15,996 participants, 233 exhibitors in 2026.' WHERE slug='all4customer-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International trade fair for packaging and intralogistics. Packaging, processing and logistics solutions for every sector.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **ALL4PACK Emballage Paris** (official name: **ALLFORPACK EMBALLAGE PARIS**) returns for its 2026 edition from **24 to 26 November 2026** at [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte), **Hall 5**. The operational brief cites 23-26 November, but the official website and Comexposium announce Tuesday 24 to Thursday 26 November 2026 (Monday 23 Nov. corresponds to exhibitor set-up).
- **Biennial** trade fair (even years), organised by **[Comexposium](/organisateurs/comexposium)**. The current identity stems from the 2014 merger of the historic **Emballage** (created in 1947) and **Manutention** trade fairs under the ALL4PACK brand. Rebranded in 2022 under the strapline "Lead the revolution", then repositioned for 2026 under the strapline **"Unbox your potential"**.
- 2024 edition results (4-7 November 2024): **27,303 professional visitors** (of whom 26% were international, from 88 countries, and 63% were decision-makers or prescribers), **1,022 exhibitors and brands** (50% international). Targets announced for 2026 by Comexposium: around 850 exhibitors and 24,000 visitors (the 2022 pre-event marketing communication advertised 66,000 expected visitors, never reached).
- 2026 structures its offering around **4 sector hubs**: Packaging & Materials, Design & Printing, Process & Packaging, Intralogistics & Transport. The **Paris Talks** conference programme is built around 3 pillars, "Reinvent, Regenerate, Radiate" (AI, data and automation, PPWR regulation, green logistics, circular economy).
- Under the high patronage of the **Ministry for the Economy, Finance and Industrial, Energy and Digital Sovereignty**. Institutional support: CNE (Conseil National de l''Emballage), Citeo, ELIPSO, GEPPIA, Secimep, Carton Ondulé de France, EPAL France, EPDA, France Bois Forêt, World Packaging Organization.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The leading European trade fair for packaging, conditioning, printing and intralogistics. The 2026 offering is segmented into four worlds:

- **Packaging & Materials**: primary and secondary materials, plastic, paper-board, glass, metal, wood, bio-based and mono-material alternatives, circularity and industrial trade-offs.
- **Design & Printing**: transforming packaging through creativity, digital printing, traceability, eco-design and regulatory compliance.
- **Process & Packaging**: conditioning machines, production lines, process equipment, demonstrations and product presentations.
- **Intralogistics & Transport**: mobile robots, AGVs, machinery regulation, warehouse decarbonisation, end-of-line and logistics.

User markets in 2024: food and beverage (25%), e-commerce distribution (14%), multi-industries (13%), transport and logistics (8%), industrial goods (8%), health and pharma (7%), beauty and hygiene (5%).

### Notable exhibitors

The list of 2026 exhibitors is on the [official exhibitors page](https://www.all-for-pack.com/en/exhibitors). Confirmed historic presence at the 2024 edition (Innovations Awards winners): **Mondi** (100% recyclable paper envelopes), **Packsize** (X5 made-to-measure box machine), **SEE / Sealed Air** (Korrvu Rapid Fix system). Exhibitors cover the entire value chain: machine manufacturers, materials, printers, intralogistics integrators and packaging service providers.

### Visitor quality

B2B industrial visitors: packaging managers, industrial buyers, R&D, supply chain and logistics, SME and mid-cap general management, decision-makers from food, pharma, cosmetics and e-commerce. 26% international in 2024 (88 countries represented), 63% decision-makers or prescribers in the purchasing process. 75% of 2024 exhibitors said they were satisfied with the quality of the visitors, and 81% judged their participation important for their company.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**Paris Talks** is the trade fair''s official conference programme, free for accredited visitors. Three thematic pillars for 2026: **Reinvent** (materials, design and process innovation), **Regenerate** (circular economy, reuse, recycling), **Radiate** (international reach, growth and industrial performance). Themes confirmed on the programme: artificial intelligence and value-chain automation, the European **PPWR** regulation (Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation), green logistics, circular economy, new consumer expectations.

### Awards & accolades

**ALLFORPACK INNOVATIONS Awards** (official verbatim wording). 4 categories for 2026 (verbatim wording from the official website): **Reinvent** (optimising packaging features and performance: AI, data, smart packaging, security), **Regenerate** (reducing environmental impact: reduction, reuse, recyclability, recycled materials), **Radiate** (boosting packaging appeal: structural and graphic design, services, convenience), **Machines & industrial efficiency** (performance of tools and processes: productivity, energy efficiency, space optimisation). In 2024, the Pack Expert jury had selected **7 winners from 20 finalists**: **Mondi** (Recycling, Protective Mailer envelope), **Packsize** (Reduction, X5 machine), **Raja** (Reuse, Re-Zip packaging), **SEE / Sealed Air** (Functionality and use, Korrvu Rapid Fix system), **Screen Europe** (Industrial efficiency, Truepress PAC 830F digital press), **Novatec Industry** and **Releaf Paper** (Innovative materials category).

### Signature spaces

- **ALL4PACK CIRCULARITY**: a space dedicated to innovative start-ups and players committed to circularity (reduction, reuse, recycling, bio-based alternatives, mono-materials, compostable and reusable packaging).
- **Re-generation**: a zone devoted to renewable packaging uses (reusable, recyclable, compostable).
- **Ruptures créatives** and **Matières à penser**: two experimental zones to question the role of packaging in a changing world (verbatim wording from the official website).

### Community & networks

Under the high patronage of the **Ministry for the Economy, Finance and Industrial, Energy and Digital Sovereignty**.

Institutional partners and sector federations officially listed on the website: **CNE** (Conseil National de l''Emballage), **Citeo** (packaging eco-organisation), **ELIPSO** (union of plastic packaging manufacturers), **GEPPIA** (process and packaging equipment suppliers), **Secimep** (packaging machinery union), **Carton Ondulé de France**, **EPAL France** (pallets), **EPDA** (European Packaging Design Association), **France Bois Forêt**, **Pôle Emballage Bois**, **La French Fab**, **World Packaging Organisation**.

### What''s new in 2026

- Repositioning under the strapline **"Unbox your potential"** (new visual identity and strapline, succeeding "Lead the revolution" used in 2022).
- Reorganisation of the offering into **4 sector hubs** (Packaging & Materials, Design & Printing, Process & Packaging, Intralogistics & Transport) to ease navigation and reflect the sector''s cross-cutting nature.
- **Paris Talks** conference programme structured around the 3 pillars Reinvent / Regenerate / Radiate.
- Format reduced to **3 days** (24-26 November) compared with 4 days in 2024 (4-7 November).
- Move to **Hall 5** at Paris Nord Villepinte.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte) page.

Specific to the trade fair:

- **Pavilion location:** Hall 5, Parc des Expositions Paris Nord Villepinte.
- **Dates and times:** Tuesday 24 to Thursday 26 November 2026. Exact times to be confirmed on the official website as the event approaches.
- **Visitor badge:** free pre-registration for professionals via the official website ([all-for-pack.com](https://www.all-for-pack.com/)).

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 18 months out: make contact with the Comexposium sales team and request a stand booking, select the target sector hub from the 4 worlds.
- 12 months out: apply for the **ALLFORPACK INNOVATIONS Awards** (4 categories in 2026: Reinvent, Regenerate, Radiate, Machines & industrial efficiency), decide between a standard stand and participation in the signature spaces (CIRCULARITY, Re-generation).
- 9 months out: activate the partner-federation channels (CNE, Citeo, ELIPSO, GEPPIA, Secimep) for upstream communication.
- 6 months out: product demonstration briefing. The live demonstrations in the Process & Packaging and Intralogistics & Transport hubs have historically concentrated decision-maker footfall.
- 3 months out: team accreditations, product pitch brief, business meeting targeting (the official ALL4PACK app offers an exhibitor-visitor matchmaking module).

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free online pre-registration of the badge on the official website.
- Identify the relevant hubs in advance according to your profile (primary packaging, machines, intralogistics).
- Allow at least 1 full day to cover Hall 5. The 2026 density (~850 exhibitors expected in a single hall) calls for a prepared route.
- Target the Paris Talks PPWR and AI sessions (capacity is often full).
- Access via RER B (Parc des Expositions Villepinte station) or by road via the A1/A104. In mid-November, allow extra time (heavy Paris-region traffic).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

ALL4PACK features a dedicated "Our CSR commitments" page on its official website. The trade fair positions ecological transformation and circularity as the central theme of the 2026 edition (the **Regenerate** pillar of the Paris Talks programme). Three signature spaces structure this CSR line:

- **ALL4PACK CIRCULARITY** highlights bio-based alternatives, mono-materials, compostable and reusable packaging, as well as start-ups committed to circularity.
- **Re-generation** brings together reusable, recyclable and compostable solutions.
- The **Regenerate** pillar of the conference programme addresses the European PPWR regulation, the circular economy and green logistics.

Comexposium, the organiser, is also a major player in the French events industry and applies, across all its trade fairs, the ISO 20121 and Net Zero Carbon Events sector approaches promoted by the UFI member organisers. A formal commitment specific to the ALL4PACK trade fair (ISO 20121 certification, Net Zero pledge) has not been explicitly published as at the date of this page.

## How the trade fair has evolved

