After 50 years under the name Arab Health, the trade show has switched to the WHX Dubai (World Health Expo) identity, backed by operator Informa Markets and its global network of health events. The 2026 edition already amassed 235,000+ professional visits and 4,200+ exhibitors on the WHX Dubai side (post-show results, worldhealthexpo.com). The 2027 edition, from 25 to 28 January, marks an organisational milestone by fully integrating WHX Labs within the main event, bringing the two events together under a single identity and across both sites (Dubai World Trade Centre and Dubai Exhibition Centre) for the first time. This scaling-up confirms the trade show''s position as the leading healthcare hub in the MENA region and one of the largest in the world.', seo_title_en='Arab Health 2027 (WHX Dubai): dates, exhibitors, info | Agoris', seo_description_en='Arab Health, now WHX Dubai, takes place from 25 to 28 January 2027 at the Dubai World Trade Centre. The largest health trade show in the MENA region: 4,200+ exhibitors, 235,000+ pro visits, 90,000 unique visitors. CME programme, Innov8, practical info.' WHERE slug='arab-health-dubai';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Architect@Work Lyon is not an open trade show: it is an invitation-only business convention, reserved for architects, interior designers and specifiers from the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region → exhibiting here targets the quality of specification, not volume.
- 176 exhibitors in 2024, presenting more than 400 new products pre-selected by a committee (source: Batiweb, Architecture Bois Magazine) → a "best of" format with filtered applications, not a catalogue format.
- No attendance figure published for the Lyon edition (source: no official data or press coverage found) → value is measured by the quality of the specifier audience, not by a headline volume.
- 2026 edition: 10-11 June, Halle Tony Garnier in Lyon, organised by Expo Conseil (the French subsidiary of the Xpo Group), on the theme "Courts-circuits" (local supply chains, regional materials) (source: architectatwork.com, Light ZOOM Lumière).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers of materials and systems for architecture and interior architecture, filtered by a steering committee. The 2026 edition is marked by a strong lighting and electrical presence (XAL, Delta Light, Bega, Signify, DCW Éditions). Regional partners: Fibois AuRA, Cluster Éco-Bâtiment AuRA (source: Light ZOOM Lumière).

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [architectatwork.fr](https://www.architectatwork.fr).

### Visitor quality

- 100% specifiers: architects, interior architects, designers and engineering consultancies from the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region
- Access by invitation and pre-registration: no general public visitors
- No published attendance figures for the Lyon edition

## Features & community

### Conference programme

2026 theme "Courts-circuits": local supply chains, regional materials, reduction of the carbon footprint. Conferences (Academy) on local timber, building transformation, bio-sourced materials and circular urban systems. More than 250 pre-selected innovations (source: Light ZOOM Lumière).

### Satellite events

"Cocorico" exhibition on French materials, showcasing short supply chains (timber, earth, stone, plant fibres) (source: Light ZOOM Lumière).

### Community & networks

A multi-city format (Paris, Lyon, and other European cities): an exhibitor can roll out its presence across several editions. Regional partnerships with Fibois AuRA and Cluster Éco-Bâtiment AuRA. Specialist architecture press in attendance (Light ZOOM Lumière, Architecture Bois).

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue:** Halle Tony Garnier, 20 place des Docteurs Charles et Christophe Mérieux, 69007 Lyon.
- **Dates and opening hours:** 10 and 11 June 2026, 10am-7pm.
- **Visitor badge:** standard entry fee of 100 € (2024 edition, to be confirmed for 2026, source: halle-tony-garnier.com). A free invitation code is available from an exhibitor. Reserved for specifiers (architects, interior designers).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: quotation on request from Expo Conseil (the French subsidiary of the Xpo Group). As with the other Architect@Work editions, the format imposes a standardised type of stand, which can reduce scenography costs but limits visual differentiation.

## Preparing your visit

Architect@Work Lyon is not an open trade show: access requires an invitation code.

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: application to Expo Conseil (the French subsidiary of the Xpo Group) with a proposed product (or products). The steering committee rules on eligibility.
- 6 months out: if approved, contracting and choice of location.
- 3 months out: preparation of materials, selection of the specifier guests to target.
- 6 weeks out: sending of invitation codes.
- 1 week out: final team briefing.

### For the specifier visitor

- Obtain an invitation code from an exhibitor or from Expo Conseil (the French subsidiary of the Xpo Group). Proof of professional activity required.
- 2-day format: 1 day is enough for a targeted tour of the pre-selected new products.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

CSR is the common thread of the 2026 edition: the "Courts-circuits" theme highlights local supply chains, regional materials and the reduction of the carbon footprint, with the "Cocorico" exhibition dedicated to French materials and the promotion of bio-sourced materials (earth, stone, plant fibres) (source: Light ZOOM Lumière). The Fibois AuRA and Cluster Éco-Bâtiment AuRA partnerships anchor this regional sustainability dimension.

## How the trade show has evolved

