 { "edition": "2025", "dates": "3-6 April", "lieu": "Grand Palais", "visiteurs": "87,275", "exposants": "170" },
 { "edition": "2024", "dates": "4-7 April", "lieu": "Grand Palais", "visiteurs": "", "exposants": "" }
 ]}
 sources="artparis.com, France Conventions"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

Founded in **1999**, Art Paris managed to hold its ground throughout the decade of FIAC''s dominance, before benefiting from the shift in the Parisian market from 2022 onwards: FIAC was replaced by **Paris+ par Art Basel** (renamed **Art Basel Paris** in 2024), now positioned in late October at the Grand Palais. During the renovation of the Grand Palais between 2021 and 2023, Art Paris kept its appointment at the **Grand Palais Éphémère** on the Champ-de-Mars (a structure designed by Wilmotte), before returning to the restored Grand Palais in **2024**.

The current positioning is clear: Art Paris occupies the **April** slot (the Parisian spring) with a **mid-market + French scene** format, where Art Basel Paris (24 to 26 October 2025 at the Grand Palais, 206 galleries, around 73,000 visitors) holds the **autumn** slot in the **international high-end** segment. The April fair reached its **all-time attendance record** in 2025 (87,275 visitors), and is launching a 28th edition in 2026 with a tighter target of 160 to 165 galleries, two demanding curatorial trails (Babel, La Réparation), a consolidation of the Prix MAIF Métamorphoses, and a CSR approach that remains without documented equivalent among international art fairs.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='art-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Construction, renovation and fit-out trade show for building and civil engineering professionals across the Grand Ouest.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 87% of visitors come from the Grand Ouest (source: artibat.com) → Artibat is a regional trade show, not a national one. Exhibit to target the Grand Ouest, not to go international.
- 46% of visitors are decision-makers, prescribers or buyers (source: artibat.com) → high decision-making density for a regional trade show, but more than half of the visitor base is still made up of operatives.
- 44% new visitors at each edition (source: artibat.com) → structurally high renewal on a biennial rhythm; first-time exhibitors reach a fresh audience at each gathering.
- 1,100 exhibitors across 62,000 m² in 2025 (sources: Le Moniteur, batipole.com), 10% of them international → it is the largest French regional construction trade show, ahead of Nordbat and Eurobois.
- Organiser: CAPEB Pays de la Loire, the federation for building-trade craftspeople → this organisational grounding orients the positioning towards craftspeople rather than large industrial groups.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A construction trade show covering the entire building sector of the Grand Ouest: craftspeople, manufacturers, distributors, builders'' merchants. The offering is structured around 5 hubs: Structural works, Finishing works, Equipment and tooling, Technical, and Civil engineering plant and machinery. 10% of exhibitors are international (source: artibat.com).

### Notable exhibitors

The list of exhibitors is on the official website: [exposants.artibat.com](https://exposants.artibat.com).

### Visitor quality

- 87% from the Grand Ouest (Brittany, Pays de la Loire, Basse-Normandie, Centre)
- 46% decision-makers, prescribers or buyers
- 63% of visitors are companies, vs. individual craftspeople
- 44% new visitors at each edition

Source: organiser (artibat.com).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

Record from the 2025 edition: programming structured around the building sector''s ecological transition, the digitalisation of the trades, and the integration of robotics and AI (sources: acpresse.fr, batiweb.com).

### Awards & accolades

The "Millésime ARTIBAT" competition: a panel of construction experts selects the most high-performing and innovative products at each edition. 45 innovations were recognised at the 2025 edition against the criteria of efficiency, environmental impact and resource optimisation (source: acpresse.fr).

### Satellite events

"Collab''Zone": a 400 m² forward-looking space introduced in 2025, dedicated to robotics and AI in the building sector, in partnership with Nantes Université and the École de Design Nantes Atlantique. 7 partner companies present their solutions there across the themes of workplace safety, reducing physical strain, and productivity (sources: acpresse.fr, batiweb.com).

### Community & networks

Organiser: CAPEB Pays de la Loire, the federation for building-trade craftspeople.

Specialist press: Le Moniteur, Batiactu, Batirama. Official app "Pocket Artibat": exhibitors, visit itineraries, floor plan, new products.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc Expo Rennes](/lieux/parc-expo-rennes).

Specific to this trade show:

- **Dates:** 20-22 October 2027 (Wednesday-Friday). Opening hours: Wednesday 9 am-7 pm, Thursday 9 am-9 pm (late opening), Friday 9 am-6 pm (source: artibat.com/infos-pratiques).
- **Visitor badge:** free for professionals with proof of activity; €40 incl. VAT without proof. Free up to age 14 (source: exposants.artibat.com).
- **Services:** official "Pocket Artibat" app, free shuttle from Rennes TGV station and the airport (source: batirama.com).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: the "stand packs" page states "Prices available from our sales team". Request a quote at commercial@artibat.com or +33 (0)2 40 89 54 81 (source: artibat.com). Six pack formulas have been identified (without public prices): Stand Base, Pack Eco, Pack Eco+, Pack Personnalisé, Pack Prestige, Pack Vision.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: request a quote from CAPEB Pays de la Loire, book a space by thematic hub.
- 6 months out: order the stand from a stand builder.
- 3 months out: final stand plan, team brief, activity programme.
- 6 weeks out: accreditations, equipment logistics, accommodation.
- 1 week out: final brief, equipment check, stand delivery.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Allow 1 day for a focused prescriber itinerary, 2 days for a multi-hub buyer itinerary (62,000 m² in 2025) (source: batipole.com).
- Anticipate the Paris-Bruz journey: TGV to Rennes then free shuttle, around 2 hrs door-to-door.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Artibat''s CSR dimension is expressed through three documented elements: the Millésime ARTIBAT competition includes environmental impact and resource optimisation among its selection criteria; the Collab''Zone structures part of its space around workplace safety and reducing physical strain; the building sector''s ecological transition is a recurring theme of the conference programme.

## How the trade show has evolved

