 sources="artibat.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

The number of exhibitors rose from 1,040 in 2023 to 1,100 in 2025 (source: artibat.com), i.e. +5.8% over a 2-year cycle in a strained French construction economy. The 21st edition (2027) is announcing a target almost identical to 2025 in exhibitors and a return to 45,000 visitors: the organiser is projecting stability rather than strong growth. Variable to watch: the impact of the 2026-2027 construction economic context on actual attendance.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='artibat-rennes';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International construction trade show. The meeting point for the entire building sector: materials, equipment, construction systems.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Batimat has been biennial for over 60 years; exhibiting in 2026 means waiting 2 years for the next edition: those who miss an edition lose 2 years of visibility within the sector.
- 1,473 exhibitors in 2024, including 559 newcomers (38%), a high proportion of first-time exhibitors, though established players retain a positioning advantage.
- 85% of attendees are French, with 45% from the Île-de-France region; Batimat is first and foremost the trade show of the national construction sector, not a show for commercial internationalisation.
- The exhibitor model has evolved considerably: Batimat no longer sells space alone, but a complete package (Pack Business Builder) including a digital profile, badge scanning, lead capture and visibility tools; the real budget goes well beyond the cost per m² alone.
- The Innovation Awards (229 entries in 2024, a record) are a free visibility lever for entrant exhibitors, and a strong signal for attendees looking for sector trends.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A multi-specialist trade show covering the entire building value chain, from materials manufacturers to construction-site management software. Project owners, project managers, architects, installers, distributors. A strong presence of French SMEs and mid-sized companies alongside multinationals.

### Notable exhibitors (2024)

Saint-Gobain, Knauf, Schneider Electric, Legrand, Velux, Isover, Mapei, Vicat, Parexgroup, Somfy, Hager, Renson, Siemens Building Technologies. Integration of Equipbaie-Métalexpo in 2024 (388 additional exhibitors, +50% vs the previous edition).

### Retention rate

Around 62% returning exhibitors (38% newcomers in 2024, 45% in 2022). The biennial rhythm structurally builds loyalty among those for whom Batimat is their only major Paris event.

### Attendee quality

85% French (45% Île-de-France). International: strong representation from the Maghreb countries (Morocco leading). A varied decision-maker profile: tradespeople, site managers, prescribers (architects, design offices), industrial purchasing departments, distributors.

## Programme & community

### Conference programme

400 conferences over 4 days, in formats including Batitalks, Renotalks, Architalks and symposia. 2024 themes: building decarbonisation, energy renovation, digitalisation & BIM, adaptation to climate change, diversity in the construction sector.

### Awards & accolades

Innovation Awards, 229 entries in 2024 (an all-time record, +36% vs the previous edition). 230 innovations awarded. Winners benefit from dedicated exhibition spaces, a major visibility lever for innovative SMEs.

### Satellite events

Climate Sense: an immersive experience simulating site conditions at +50°C. The "L''Art des Déchets" exhibition (works made from recycled materials). TV studios and live broadcasts. Startup pitch spaces. The "Hommes et Femmes du Bâtiment" initiative (diversity).

### Community & networks

Partners: FFB, CAPEB, UNSFA, UNTEC. Specialist press partners: Le Moniteur, Batiactu, Batirama, Le Journal du Bâtiment. A pre-scheduled meeting platform integrated into the digital package. The official Batimat app.

### What''s new in 2026

Batimat 2026: **28 September - 1 October, Porte de Versailles, 4 days**. In 2026, Le Mondial du Bâtiment brings together **4 trade shows**: Batimat + Interclima + Idéobain + **Renodays**. The exhibitor model is structured around a Pack Business Builder (digital tools, badge scanning, performance dashboard). A published CSR commitments page: carbon neutrality by 2040, -50% GHG by 2030, signatory of the Climate Pledge and Net Zero Carbon Events (source: batimat.com/zero-carbone-2050).

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **6 halls / 8 exhibition zones** (Le Mondial du Bâtiment occupies the entire site, source: batimat.com)
- **Transport access**: Metro L12 (Porte de Versailles) or L8 (Balard). Tram T2/T3a. October: heavy traffic, allow 30-45 min of leeway from central Paris.
- **Parking**: On-site and nearby car parks, foreseeable saturation on the first days. Shuttles from certain partner hotels may be available.
- **Accommodation**: The 15th arrondissement (Convention, Vaugirard) as a priority. Book 4-6 months in advance, as Batimat week mobilises the entire national sector.
- **Opening hours & badges**: 9am-7pm on all 4 days. Visitor badge: €30 excl. VAT before 20 September, €60 excl. VAT after. Reduced rates: teachers, students, press. Free badges via partner exhibitors.
- **Services**: On-site catering in each hall. Networking areas. TV studios. Award-winning innovation spaces. The official Batimat app.

## How much it costs to exhibit

