### Trajectory analysis

Batimat presents a significant historical discontinuity to bear in mind: a continuous decline at Villepinte (2009-2019), followed by a clear rebound on its return to Porte de Versailles in 2022. The 2024 figures are not directly comparable with previous editions due to the reconfiguration of the scope (integration of Equipbaie-Métalexpo). The +19% rise in exhibitors is the most reliable signal of positive momentum. The 2026 edition remains over 4 days and forms part of Le Mondial du Bâtiment, bringing together 4 trade shows (Batimat + Interclima + Idéobain + Renodays).', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='batimat';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **BAU** is the world''s leading trade fair for architecture, materials and building systems. It takes place every two years (odd-numbered years) in Munich, organised by **Messe München GmbH**.
- Next edition: from 11 to 15 January 2027 at the exhibition grounds of the [Messe München](/lieux/messe-munchen).
- 2025 results (final figures published on bau-muenchen.com and messe-muenchen.de): more than 180,000 visitors and 2,230 exhibitors from 58 countries, across 200,000 m² spread over 18 fully booked halls.
- Strong international reach: 52% of exhibitors came from abroad in 2025 (a record share according to the organiser), along with 44% of visitors.
- Sister fair to the construction and construction machinery trade fair [bauma](/salons/bauma-munich), also organised by Messe München on the same grounds.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers of building materials and systems, façades and the building envelope, joinery, roofing, insulation, finishing trades, and digital solutions for building planning and productivity. The visitor base brings together architects, planners, investors, developers, representatives from industry and trade, as well as the building trades.

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [bau-muenchen.com](https://bau-muenchen.com/en/). Exhibitors at the 2025 edition included GEZE, Hörmann, ERLUS, KLEUSBERG and ALHO Group (source: bau-muenchen.com).

### Visitor quality

- More than 180,000 visitors in 2025, of whom 44% came from abroad
- 97% of visitors rated the fair "good to excellent" according to the survey by the Gelszus institute; 95% of exhibitors rated it "good to excellent" (source: messe-muenchen.de)

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The 2027 programme is built around four major themes announced by the organiser: materials and resources, climate protection and adaptation, the transformation of living spaces, and digitalisation and productivity. The 2025 edition featured keynotes from renowned architects, including Carlo Ratti, Satoshi Ohashi, Verena von Beckerath and Elisabeth Endres (2025 programme archived on bau-muenchen.com). The detailed 2027 programme will be published as the fair approaches.

### Awards and accolades

Several awards are presented on site. Official titles:

- **Innovation Award Architecture + Building**, presented by the magazine AIT and AIT-Dialog in cooperation with Messe München GmbH
- **BAKA Award - Award for Product Innovation**, presented by the BAKA Bundesverband Altbauerneuerung e.V.
- **Balthasar-Neumann-Prize**, presented by Bauverlag / DBZ / BDB
- **Auf IT gebaut - Bauberufe mit Zukunft**, presented by the RG-Bau im RKW-Handelszentrum

2027 winners to be confirmed as the fair approaches (source: bau-muenchen.com).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Messe München](/lieux/messe-munchen) listing.

Specific to the fair:

- **Opening hours:** Monday to Friday, 9:30 to 18:00 (source: bau-muenchen.com).
- **Mobility:** combined BAU Rail Special ticket for the train, airport shuttle during the fair and car-sharing incentives.
- **Visitor badge:** online ticketing, mobile scan at the entrance.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: get in touch with Messe München, choose positioning by themed halls.
- 9 months out: apply for the Innovation Award Architecture + Building (AIT) to showcase a product innovation.
- 6 months out: prepare the stand with sustainable construction partners (meplan, Arno Design) and brief the demos.
- 3 months out: weave the major 2027 themes (resources, climate, living spaces, digitalisation) into the sales pitch.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Register online in advance, mobile-scan badge.
- Allow 1 to 2 days to cover the 18 halls and 200,000 m².
- Target conferences and keynotes ahead of time: programme published several weeks before the fair.
- Favour the train via the BAU Rail Special ticket to reach the grounds.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Messe München publishes BAU''s sustainability commitments on its [Sustainability](https://bau-muenchen.com/en/trade-fair/sustainability/) page. Concrete commitments on display: resource-efficient stand construction with partners meplan and Arno Design, recycling of assembly and dismantling waste and a revised materials recovery strategy, local and seasonal catering under the principle of "avoid rather than offset", and reduction of food waste.

On the visitor side: free water fountains for reusable cups and bottles, encouragement to reuse badge lanyards across multiple visits, digital ticketing (mobile scan), reduced paper printing in favour of digital formats, and mobility encouraged via the rail ticket and the airport shuttle. The organiser states verbatim that "no major event can be entirely sustainable", with the stated aim of acting in the most sustainable way possible. No ISO 20121 certification is mentioned to date (source: bau-muenchen.com/sustainability).

## How the fair has evolved

<HistoryTable
