UPDATE salons SET description_en='15th edition of the gathering for IT & Data decision-makers who are industrialising AI, the longest-running data/AI trade show in France. 2026 targets: 15,000 attendees, 200 exhibitors, 300+ speakers, 350+ conference sessions across 3 rooms.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Big Data & AI Paris is **the gathering for IT & Data decision-makers who are industrialising AI**, the longest-running data/AI trade show in France in terms of seniority (founded in 2012) and reputation, organised under the **high patronage of the President of the Republic, Emmanuel Macron**.
- 15th edition on **15 and 16 September 2026** at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), **Hall 7.2**. Announced targets: **15,000 attendees**, **200 exhibitors/sponsors**, **300+ speakers**, **350+ conference sessions, workshops, demos and pitches** across **3 rooms** (tech, governance, business).
- **Major shift in 2026: the move to paid visitor access** for the first time in the trade show''s history, as part of a drive to qualify a large-account decision-maker audience. Expected effect: a two- to threefold increase in company delegations on the decision-making visitor side.
- 3 editorial themes structure the 2026 conferences: **Modern Data Architecture**, **Governance & Regulation**, **Data & AI for Business**, paired with 3 new spaces (Village Advanced Computing, Talent Hub, SME Support Zone).
- Organiser: **RX France** (Reed Exhibitions) since the acquisition of the assets of **Corp Agency** in 2023, the agency that created the event in 2012. Year the "& AI" element was added to the trade show''s name: 2023, alongside the change of organiser.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Big Data & AI Paris addresses the entire data and AI value chain within the enterprise:

- **Hyperscalers and cloud**: AWS, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud, OVHcloud (French sovereign cloud).
- **Data & AI platforms**: Snowflake, Databricks, Qlik, Dataiku, Mistral AI (French AI champions showcased in the digital sovereignty strand).
- **IT services firms and data consulting**: Capgemini, Sopra Steria, Talan, Smile, CGI, MeltOne, alter way.
- **CRM and data-driven SaaS**: Salesforce and the connected ecosystem.
- **Governance, security, MLOps**: vendors specialising in data quality, observability and model monitoring.
- **Advanced computing**: new in 2026, with a village dedicated to HPC, quantum computing, semiconductors and photonics, co-developed with **Systematic Paris-Region**.

A deliberate refocusing in 2026: 200 exhibitors/sponsors targeted, compared with 220 brands present in 2025. A logic of curation rather than volume, consistent with the shift to paid visitor access.

### Notable exhibitors and recent award winners

The **Big Data & AI Innovation Awards** are split into 3 categories: **Startup**, **SME / Large Enterprise**, **Big Data & AI for Good** (jury prize, projects serving the public interest).

Recent winners identified:

- **2024**: **Deema**, winner of the Techno Award, an AI platform applied to medical imaging.
- **2023**: **Iktos Robotics**, in the Big Data & AI for Good category.
- **2022 (11th edition)**: **NamR** (Startup, geolocated data for real estate), **La Javaness** (SME / Large Enterprise for the C-in.City project), **Holis** (Jury Prize).

### Visitor quality

The visitor base has historically been highly decision-oriented: CIOs, CDOs, Chief Data Officers, Head of AI roles, and business functions (marketing data, finance data, supply data) from major French and European companies. 2025 review (1 to 2 October, 14th edition, Hall 3.2): **17,000 attendees expected**, 220 exhibitors, 300 conference sessions, focused on digital sovereignty, frugal and responsible AI, and emerging open-source technologies.

The **2026 Advisory Board** anchors the large-account decision-maker positioning: **Chafika Chettaoui (AXA), Caroline Chopinaud (Hub France IA), Isabel Gomez Garcia de Soria (L''Oréal), Claire Mathieu (Suez), Frédéric Pascal (Paris-Saclay), Aldrick Zappellini (Crédit Agricole)**. First organisations announced among the 2026 speakers: **Airbus, Accor, Thales, Coface, Bouygues Telecom**.

## Activities & community

### 2026 conference format

The programme is structured across **3 rooms** aligned with the 3 editorial themes:

1. **Modern Data Architecture**: data platforms, lakehouse, streaming, MLOps, GenAI in production.
2. **Governance & Regulation**: AI Act, GDPR, data governance, AI ethics, digital sovereignty.
3. **Data & AI for Business**: business use cases, ROI, the transformation of data-driven organisations.

A mix of formats: **plenary conferences, workshops, startup pitches, demo sessions and tech sessions**, with an overall target of 350+ speaking slots across 2 days.

### New spaces in 2026

- **Village Advanced Computing**: HPC, quantum computing, semiconductors, photonics. Co-developed with **Systematic Paris-Region**, a strong signal regarding the sovereignty positioning.
- **Talent Hub**: recruiters, specialist HR platforms and experts on the data / AI skills shortage. A direct response to the bottleneck in the tech jobs market.
- **SME Support Zone**: institutional partners, IT services firms, vendors and training providers, addressing SMEs at the AI industrialisation stage.

### Innovation Awards

3 categories: **Startup**, **SME / Large Enterprise**, **Big Data & AI for Good** (jury prize, projects serving the public interest). The "for Good" category has existed since 2022 and embodies the editorial strand dedicated to frugal and responsible AI, which took shape in 2025.

### Community & networks

A strong presence of **French AI champions** (Mistral AI, Dataiku, OVHcloud), consistent with the digital sovereignty strand. The partnership with **Systematic Paris-Region** on the Village Advanced Computing connects the trade show to the long-standing competitiveness cluster of the Île-de-France digital sector. The **Hub France IA** is represented through Caroline Chopinaud on the Advisory Board.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates and times**: 15 and 16 September 2026, a 2-day format.
- **Hall**: **7.2** (compared with 3.2 in 2025; the move is to be confirmed on the official floor plan).
- **Access**: **paid for the first time in 2026** on the visitor side; professional proof of identity should be anticipated. Ticket pricing not published to date.
- **Digital platform**: matchmaking and the programme can be found on bigdataparis.com (rebranded Big Data & AI Paris since 2023).
- **Catering and services**: see the Paris Expo Porte de Versailles listing.

## How much it costs to exhibit

