## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact with RX France, choose your positioning (Modern Data Architecture, Governance & Regulation, Data & AI for Business) and decide between a stand and conference sponsorship.
- 6 months out: apply for the **Innovation Awards** (Startup, SME / Large Enterprise, Big Data & AI for Good) and the **startup pitches**, a greater visibility lever than a stand alone for early-stage players.
- 4 months out: align your messaging with the 3 editorial themes and with the digital sovereignty and frugal AI strand, which the large-account decision-maker visitor base will expect.
- 3 months out: if you offer HPC, quantum, semiconductors or photonics, request placement in the **Village Advanced Computing** co-developed with Systematic Paris-Region.
- 6 weeks out: brief the team, activate the matchmaking platform, and prepare live demos (the demo session and tech session format is highly valued).

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online registration is mandatory, with a **paid badge for the first time in 2026**; anticipate budget approval.
- Prioritise targeting one of the 3 rooms (Modern Data Architecture, Governance & Regulation, Data & AI for Business) rather than flitting around over the 2 days.
- Schedule your meetings via the matchmaking platform in advance; the **17,000 attendees expected in 2025** make walk-in inefficient.
- For HR and skills issues: head to the **Talent Hub**. For SMEs industrialising AI: head to the **SME Support Zone**.
- Follow the **Innovation Awards**, particularly the **Big Data & AI for Good** category, to spot projects serving the public interest.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

**Frugal and responsible AI** has been a structuring editorial theme since the 2025 edition, and the **Big Data & AI for Good** category has existed within the Innovation Awards since 2022. In concrete terms, the trade show programmes sessions dedicated to measuring the environmental impact of models, algorithmic frugality, eco-design of code and infrastructure, and AI ethics. The 2026 **Governance & Regulation** editorial theme extends this logic on the compliance side (the European AI Act, GDPR, data governance).

## How the trade show has evolved

