### Trajectory analysis

Bijorhca Paris is the **oldest B2B jewellery trade show in Europe**. Its origins date back to the **Semaine de la Bijouterie**, created in 1930 in Paris by the **BOCI** (Bureau Officiel pour le Commerce de l''Industrie de la Bijouterie/joaillerie, a professional federation founded in the 1930s) at the Hôtel Moderne, with 41 exhibitors. The event has crossed the decades while keeping its status as an unmissable fixture for the sector, reaching its **150th edition on 21 to 24 January 2022**.

The takeover of the organisation by **WSN Développement** at the BOCI''s request marked a change of scale: an upgraded scenography, internationalisation of exhibitors (top 5 now Spain, Greece, Italy, Germany, India), creation of the Fashion Pass and integration into the **Room 0126** cluster orchestrated by Comexposium. This cluster logic, which pools Who''s Next, Bijorhca, Shoppe Object, SIL and Interfilière, turns Bijorhca into a component of a one-stop fashion-accessories-jewellery shop of **1,760 brands** and **38,000 unique visitors** (cluster figures, January 2026 edition).

The current positioning is clear: Bijorhca occupies the **biannual January + September** slot in a **dense 3-day** format, with a precious + costume + components mix that neither Vicenzaoro (pure fine jewellery) nor Inhorgenta Munich (watchmaking) covers. The co-location with Who''s Next is the number-one asset both for exhibitors (visibility to fashion buyers) and for visitors (cross-cutting sourcing in 3 days). The official site **bijorhca.com** redirects to **whosnext.com**, the canonical URL being **wsn-events.com/events/bijorhca**.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='bijorhca-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- BIM World Paris, now branded **Digital Twin | BIM World**, is **the benchmark event for digital technology in construction and urban development** in France: BIM (Building Information Modelling), digital twins and the digital transformation of buildings, cities and infrastructure. Official strapline: "the must-attend digital event for construction and urban development".
- Organiser: **Beyond Event SAS** (BIM World France), based in Saint-Mandé. The technical and data management of the trade show is handled by the service provider EVEOS (La Défense). A strictly professional trade show, with access reserved for registered visitors.
- Next edition: **31 March & 1 April 2027** at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), halls 5.2 and 5.3. Announced opening hours: 9:00 am-6:30 pm on 31 March, 9:00 am-5:30 pm on 1 April.
- Latest reported figures (2025 edition): more than 10,000 participants, 230 to 260 exhibitors depending on the source and around 120 conferences. Figures provided by the organiser, not audited by a third party to our knowledge.
- Broad thematic coverage: BIM and interoperability, the digital twin of territories, construction tech, data, AI and cybersecurity, decarbonisation, energy and flexibility, real-estate asset management, skills and training.
- Structuring themed villages: Construction Tech (in partnership with the CCCA BTP), Digital Twin of France and Territories, Autodesk ADN, Energy Flexibility & DC World, and the buildingSMART France Forum on digital continuity.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

BIM World Paris addresses the entire value chain of digital technology for construction and development:

- **BIM software vendors and collaborative platforms**: Autodesk, Dassault Systèmes (3DEXPERIENCE), Nemetschek Group, Trimble, ACCA Software, KROQI.
- **Digital twin and data players**: modelling platforms, IFC / open BIM interoperability, data governance.
- **Construction tech and start-ups**: the Construction Tech village backed by the CCCA BTP, which brings together many young companies in the sector.
- **Energy and decarbonisation players**: energy flexibility, direct current (DC World), eco-design and low carbon.
- **Institutions and federations**: FFB (Fédération Française du Bâtiment), CAPEB, buildingSMART France, BPI France.

The target audience brings together architects, design and engineering firms, project owners, construction companies, property developers, planners, software vendors and IT service companies, training organisations, local authorities and manufacturers of building products and equipment.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of exhibitors, partners and the floor plan can be found on the official website: [bim-w.com](https://bim-w.com/). Executive partners identified for the upcoming edition: Autodesk, Dassault Systèmes, Nemetschek Group, Trimble, ACCA Software, KROQI, Orisha Construction, Once For All, along with the organisations buildingSMART France, FFB, CAPEB and CCCA BTP (source: bim-w.com, partners page).

### Audience quality

- A professional, decision-making audience from the construction and real-estate sector: technical and BIM management, architects, engineers, project owners, innovation and digital transformation directors.
- Access reserved exclusively for registered professionals.
- A strong institutional presence (FFB, CAPEB, buildingSMART France, BPI France, local authorities), which anchors the trade show''s sector positioning (source: bim-w.com, partners page).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The programme combines conferences, keynotes and workshops grouped by theme (BIM and interoperability, digital twin, data, AI and cybersecurity, decarbonisation, energy, asset management, skills and training). The 2025 edition offered around 120 conferences (source: bim-w.com, organiser communication). The detailed programme and the theme of the 2027 edition will be published closer to the event on bim-w.com.

### Awards & accolades

No official trophy or award (of the "BIM d''Or" type) is highlighted on the official website for the upcoming edition at the time of writing. If an awards programme is announced for 2027, it will be published on bim-w.com (source: bim-w.com, verified June 2026).

### Community & networks

BIM World Paris draws on the sector''s institutional ecosystem: **buildingSMART France** (data governance and digital continuity, with a dedicated forum at the trade show), **CCCA BTP** (apprenticeships and the WinLab'' incubator, a partner of the Construction Tech village), **FFB** and **CAPEB** on the building-sector employers'' side. This anchoring connects the trade show to the sector''s training, standardisation and professional representation networks (source: bim-w.com, partners page).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris La Défense Arena](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Please note: the 2027 edition takes place at **Paris Expo Porte de Versailles** (halls 5.2 and 5.3, 1 place de la Porte de Versailles, 75015 Paris), and not at La Défense. Check the exact venue on the practical information page before booking.

Specific to the trade show:

- **2027 dates and hours:** 31 March (9:00 am-6:30 pm) and 1 April (9:00 am-5:30 pm).
- **Halls:** 5.2 and 5.3 at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles.
- **Access:** reserved for registered professionals. Visitor pricing terms not published to date on the official website.
- **Registration:** online at bim-w.com, visitor support via the organiser.

