## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact with the organiser Beyond Event, choose your positioning (BIM and interoperability, digital twin, construction tech, energy and decarbonation) and decide between a stand and themed-village sponsorship.
- 6 months out: if you have an early-stage construction tech offering, request placement in the Construction Tech village backed by the CCCA BTP, a stronger visibility lever than a classic stand for start-ups.
- 4 months out: align your messaging with the trade show''s key themes (digital twin, data and AI, decarbonisation, buildingSMART digital continuity).
- 3 months out: activate the relevant institutional partnerships (FFB, CAPEB, buildingSMART France) and prepare your platform demos.
- 6 weeks out: brief the team, arrange meetings via the trade show''s platform, prepare workshops and keynotes.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online registration is mandatory at bim-w.com, with access reserved for professionals.
- Check the venue: the 2027 edition is at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles (halls 5.2 and 5.3), not at La Défense.
- Identify the useful themed villages in advance (Digital Twin of Territories, Construction Tech, Energy Flexibility & DC World, buildingSMART France Forum).
- Build a two-day itinerary: the conference programme is dense (around 120 sessions at the 2025 edition), so walking in is inefficient.
- For standardisation and digital continuity matters, prioritise the buildingSMART France Forum.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Decarbonisation and sustainable development are among the trade show''s structuring themes: sessions dedicated to decarbonising cities and construction sites, eco-design, building energy performance and energy flexibility (Energy Flexibility & DC World village) (source: bim-w.com).

At the time of writing, no ISO 20121 certification or formalised event CSR policy is highlighted on the official website for the running of the trade show itself. The subject is treated as editorial and sector content rather than as a CSR commitment of the event. Information to be confirmed with the organiser Beyond Event (source: bim-w.com, verified June 2026).

## How the trade show has evolved

