### Trajectory analysis

BioFIT is an itinerant business convention that changes host city with each edition, following its lead clusters: Strasbourg in 2022, Marseille in 2023 (12th edition, more than 900 participants announced), Lille in 2024 (13th), Strasbourg in 2025 (14th), then a return to Marseille in 2026 for the 15th edition. The 2023 edition reported more than 950 participants from over 35 countries, around a hundred exhibitors, some sixty international speakers and more than 3,000 business meetings scheduled via the partnering platform. The co-positioning with [MedFIT](/salons/medfit-marseille) and MEDigIT broadens the scope from biotech technology transfer towards MedTech, diagnostics and digital health. The final figures for the 2026 edition will be published as the trade show approaches.', seo_title_en='BioFIT 2026 Marseille: dates, exhibitors, biotech partnering | Agoris', seo_description_en='BioFIT 2026, the 15th edition of the European business convention for life sciences technology transfer, on 10 and 11 December in Marseille (Parc Chanot). Organisers, partnering, exhibitors and practical information.' WHERE slug='biofit';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='B2B trade show for the water sector. Water management, sanitation, networks, treatment and technologies for local authorities.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Carrefour des Gestions Locales de l''Eau** (CGLE) is the major annual French gathering for the water sector, bringing together public and private players around the water cycle: drinking water and resources, collective and non-collective sanitation, stormwater and GEMAPI.
- Organised by **idealCO**, a professional platform dedicated to public-sector players, in partnership with **Région Bretagne** and the **Agence de l''Eau Loire-Bretagne**.
- Next edition: 28th edition, on 27 and 28 January 2027 at the [Parc Expo Rennes](/lieux/parc-expo-rennes), spread across 5 themed halls.
- Figures announced for the 2026 edition: 19,000 participants, 650 exhibitors and more than 200 conferences across around twenty expert tracks.
- A trade show long established in Rennes: the 24th edition was held in January 2023 (13,900 participants).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Equipment manufacturers and industrial players in water treatment and sanitation, engineering and design consultancies, suppliers of networks, pipework and trenchless solutions, providers of digital and remote-management software, manufacturers of measurement and pumping equipment, operators and delegated service providers. The trade show is organised into 5 themed halls covering the entire water cycle.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of exhibitors is available on the official website: [carrefour-eau.com](https://www.carrefour-eau.com/). The offering is arranged by themed sectors (drinking water and resources, collective sanitation, non-collective sanitation, stormwater, GEMAPI), with a village dedicated to trenchless technologies and an area devoted to nature-based solutions.

### Quality of attendance

For the 2025 edition, the breakdown of attendees was as follows (source: revue-ein.com):

- 53% from companies, 22% from local authorities, 25% from schools, design consultancies and public bodies
- 92% French attendees, 8% international
- Strong regional roots: more than 35% from Brittany, 18% from Pays de la Loire, the remainder spread between Île-de-France, Normandy and other regions

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2026 edition featured more than 200 conferences and over 100 hours of conferences, round tables and interviews, organised around around twenty expert tracks. The opening plenary session addressed the theme "Water and soils: an essential alliance", co-organised with the Agence de l''Eau Loire-Bretagne and the Région Bretagne. The issues covered included structural drought, ageing infrastructure, integrated stormwater management, soil preservation and the digital transformation of the sector. The 2027 theme and programme have not yet been published (source: carrefour-eau.com).

### Community and networks

idealCO operates the professional platform behind the trade show, with a community of more than 400,000 local-authority officers and directors. The show''s programme is co-developed each year with the event partners, foremost among them the Région Bretagne and the Agence de l''Eau Loire-Bretagne.

## Environmental commitments

No dedicated page on environmental or CSR commitments is published on carrefour-eau.com at the time of writing. As the water sector is by its very nature oriented towards resource preservation, the show''s commitments will be added as soon as they are officially published.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc Expo Rennes](/lieux/parc-expo-rennes).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Halls:** the show occupies halls 4, 5, 7/8, 2/3 and 1 of the Parc Expo Rennes (source: rennesparcexpo.fr).
- **2027 opening hours:** Wednesday 8.30am-9pm, Thursday 8.30am-5pm (source: rennesparcexpo.fr).
- **Recruitment area:** an enhanced employment and training zone with recruiter meetings at recent editions.

## Planning your visit

### For exhibitors

- 9 months out: making contact with idealCO and choosing positioning among the 5 themed halls.
- 6 months out: preparing the stand and demonstrations, identifying the expert tracks relevant to targeting your audience.
- 3 months out: applying for the activities and conferences co-developed with the partners.
- 6 weeks out: confirming meetings with local authorities and design consultancies.

### For decision-maker visitors

- Register online at carrefour-eau.com.
- Allow 1 to 2 days depending on your scope (drinking water, sanitation, stormwater, GEMAPI).
- Target the expert tracks and conferences in advance: more than 100 hours of programming spread across around twenty tracks.
- Make use of the employment and training zone for recruitment within the sector.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "2027 (28th, upcoming)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" },
  { "edition": "2026 (27th, announced)", "visiteurs": "19,000", "exposants": "650" },
  { "edition": "2023 (24th)", "visiteurs": "13,900", "exposants": "500+" }
 ]}
 sources="carrefour-eau.com, rennesparcexpo.fr, revue-ein.com, monreseaudeau.fr"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

The Carrefour des Gestions Locales de l''Eau has established itself as the reference venue in France for the water sector, with marked growth: from 13,900 participants for the 24th edition in 2023 to 19,000 announced for the 2026 edition. The show has broadened its scope from technical equipment alone towards integrated-management issues (stormwater, GEMAPI, nature-based solutions, trenchless technologies). The 2027 edition, on 27 and 28 January at the Parc Expo Rennes, extends this momentum, drawing on idealCO''s stewardship and the structuring partnership with the Région Bretagne and the Agence de l''Eau Loire-Bretagne. The 2027 figures and theme will be confirmed as the show approaches.', seo_title_en='Carrefour de l''Eau 2027 Rennes: dates, exhibitors, programme', seo_description_en='The Carrefour des Gestions Locales de l''Eau (CGLE), 28th edition on 27-28 January 2027 at the Parc Expo Rennes. Organised by idealCO: 650 exhibitors, 5 halls, expert tracks for the water sector.' WHERE slug='carrefour-de-leau-rennes';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- CES (Consumer Electronics Show) is the world''s largest trade show for consumer and professional technology, organised every year in Las Vegas by the **Consumer Technology Association (CTA)**. Official strapline: "The Global Stage for Innovation".
- Next edition: 6 to 9 January 2027 at the Las Vegas Convention Center and across all of the show''s campuses in Las Vegas. Press and industry days beforehand (dates to be confirmed on ces.tech as the show approaches).
- CES 2026 results (independent CTA audit published on 31 March 2026): 148,392 attendees (+4% vs 2025), of whom 55,841 were international, from 141 countries, territories and regions, and more than 4,100 exhibitors across more than 2.6 million net square feet spread over 13 venues.
- Trade show reserved for professionals: closed to the general public, with badges subject to proof of activity in the consumer tech sector.
- Very broad sector coverage: AI, robotics, digital health, mobility, energy, immersive entertainment, quantum, accessibility.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Consumer electronics manufacturers and equipment makers, software publishers and AI platforms, carmakers and mobility players, digital health, robotics, energy, semiconductors. CES also hosts **Eureka Park**, the space dedicated to start-ups: around 1,200 young companies in 2026. The audience is strictly professional, with 52% senior executives and 189 public officials and decision-makers in 2026.

### Notable exhibitors

Exhibitor list and floor plan on the official site: [ces.tech](https://www.ces.tech/). The 2026 keynotes brought together leading executives: Lisa Su (Chair and CEO of AMD), Roland Busch (President and CEO of Siemens AG), Jensen Huang (Founder and CEO of NVIDIA), Athina Kanioura (Chief Strategy and Transformation Officer and CEO of PepsiCo Latin America) and Michael Kratsios (Adviser to the US President for Science and Technology) (source: ces.tech).

### Audience quality

- 148,392 audited attendees in 2026, of whom 55,841 were international (37.6%), from 141 countries, territories and regions (independent CTA audit compliant with UFI standards)
- 52% senior executives, 189 public officials and decision-makers in 2026
- Fast-growing themed hubs in 2026: AI (39,929 attendees, +22% year on year), robotics (19,605, +26%), marketing and advertising (13,433, +10%) (source: ces.tech)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

More than **1,400 speakers** took the floor across more than **400 conference sessions** in 2026. The programme covers AI, robotics, digital health, energy, enterprise solutions, immersive entertainment, mobility, quantum and accessibility. Keynotes from major brands set the rhythm of the week. The detailed programme and theme for the 2027 edition will be published as the show approaches (source: ces.tech).

### Awards and accolades

**CES Innovation Awards**: the CTA''s annual awards programme recognising the most innovative products and technologies presented at the show, by category. The 2026 winners were showcased at the Venetian. The 2027 categories and winners will be announced ahead of the edition (source: ces.tech).

### Community and networks

CES is run by the **Consumer Technology Association (CTA)**, the trade association representing the US technology industry. The **CTA Foundation** supports accessibility programmes ($700,000 in new grants announced around CES 2026). Eureka Park brings together the international start-up community, with numerous national pavilions (source: ces.tech).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Las Vegas Convention Center](/lieux/las-vegas-convention-center) listing. Note: CES 2026 spread across 13 venues in Las Vegas (three main campuses), beyond the Las Vegas Convention Center alone.

Specific to the show:

- **2027 dates:** 6 to 9 January 2027, with press and industry days beforehand (dates to be confirmed on ces.tech as the show approaches).
- **Visitor badge:** reserved for professionals with proof of activity in consumer tech. Online registration on ces.tech, opening several months before the show. The general public is not admitted.
- **Multiple venues:** plan for shuttles between the campuses (Las Vegas Convention Center, Venetian, other sites) given the size of the show.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published: the application to take part goes through a CTA sales contact via the official site [ces.tech](https://www.ces.tech/). Figures not publicly available.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with CTA sales, choose the campus and positioning (themed zone or Eureka Park for start-ups).
- 9 months out: submit an application for the CES Innovation Awards.
- 6 months out: prepare the stand, demos and multi-site logistics.
- 3 months out: press activation and media relations (high density of accredited journalists).
- 6 weeks out: confirm decision-maker meetings and sales briefing.

### For the decision-maker attendee

- Pre-register online on ces.tech with proof of professional activity in tech (access strictly professional).
- Arrange accommodation well in advance: Las Vegas is fully booked during CES.
- Plan ahead for travel between the 13 venues and organise your route by campus.
- Target keynotes and conferences in advance: the programme is dense and published several weeks before the show.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

For CES 2026, the CTA announced the **CES Green Grants** programme: $125,000 in support for two sustainable development projects in the city of Las Vegas (tree planting and street lighting upgrades towards high-efficiency solutions) (source: ces.tech).

Accessibility strand: accessibility is one of the show''s major themes, and the CTA Foundation supports dedicated programmes ($700,000 in new grants announced around CES 2026). No ISO 20121 certification mentioned to date (source: ces.tech).

## How the show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Attendees", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "2027 (upcoming)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" },
  { "edition": "2026", "visiteurs": "148,392", "exposants": "4,100+" },
  { "edition": "2025", "visiteurs": "142,465", "exposants": "4,500+" },
  { "edition": "2024", "visiteurs": "138,789", "exposants": "4,312" }
 ]}
 sources="ces.tech (independent audits compliant with UFI)"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

A sustained growth trajectory following the post-Covid recovery: from 138,789 audited attendees in 2024 to 148,392 in 2026 (+4% vs 2025), CES confirms its status as the world''s largest consumer tech trade show. The exhibitor base remains substantial, at around 4,100 to 4,500 depending on the edition, with a strong start-up component via Eureka Park. The 2026 momentum is driven by AI (+22% attendees year on year) and robotics (+26%). The 2027 edition, from 6 to 9 January at the Las Vegas Convention Center and across the Las Vegas campuses, extends this momentum. The 2027 theme and target figures will be published as the show approaches.', seo_title_en='CES 2027 Las Vegas: dates, exhibitors, programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='CES 2027 runs from 6 to 9 January at the Las Vegas Convention Center. The world''s largest tech trade show: 148,392 audited attendees in 2026, 4,100+ exhibitors, AI, robotics, mobility.' WHERE slug='ces-las-vegas';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='30th anniversary edition of the meeting point for suppliers to the food-processing industry, structured around 4 worlds (Ingredients & PAI, Equipment & Processes, Packaging, Food Safety). 2026 edition: 23,959 visitors (+1.4%) and 2,000 exhibitors, including 17% international, across 12 halls.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **30th anniversary edition** from 9 to 11 March 2027 at the Parc Expo Rennes Aéroport. CFIA celebrates its 30th anniversary in 2027 (created in 1997 with 360 exhibitors across 10,000 m²) (source: cfiaexpo.com).
- 2026 edition (29th): **23,959 visitors (+1.4% vs 2025)** and **2,000 exhibitors**, including 17% international, across **12 halls** (sources: cfiaexpo.com, agro-media.fr).
- A trade show **structured around 4 worlds**: Ingredients & PAI (Hall 4), Equipment & Processes (Halls 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8: the largest zone), Packaging & Conditioning (Halls 1, 10, 11), Food Safety (Hall 12, created in 2025).
- Organiser: **GL Events Exhibitions**. Exhibitor registration via [exposant.gl-events.com/cfia-rennes-2027](https://exposant.gl-events.com/cfia-rennes-2027/).
- A strong **Breton food-processing** anchoring: Brittany is the leading food-processing region in France and Europe, accounting for 11% of national food-industry turnover (source: Bretagne Développement Innovation).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A trade show for the entire supplier chain of the food-processing industry, structured around 4 worlds since 2025:

- **Ingredients & PAI** (Hall 4): ingredients, additives, flavourings, intermediate food products.
- **Equipment & Processes** (Halls 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8): machinery, production lines, automation, industrial utilities. This is the largest zone of the trade show.
- **Packaging & Conditioning** (Halls 1, 10, 11): materials, packaging machinery, primary and secondary conditioning. Halls 1 and 11 were redesigned in 2026.
- **Food Safety** (Hall 12): hygiene, food safety, quality control, traceability. Hall created in 2025 (around 100 exhibitors).

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is on the official website: [cfiaexpo.com](https://www.cfiaexpo.com/). The trade show gathered 2,000 exhibitors in 2026, including 17% international (source: cfiaexpo.com).

### Quality of attendance

- 23,959 visitors in 2026, up +1.4% vs 2025
- 2,000 exhibitors, including 17% international
- Access strictly reserved for food-processing industry professionals
- A high density of buyers, along with production, R&D, quality and procurement management from Breton and national food businesses

Source: cfiaexpo.com.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

Daily conferences across the 3 days of the trade show, organised by thematic world. The 2027 programme will be published in advance on cfiaexpo.com.

### Signature spaces

- **AI Village** (Hall 2, 2nd edition in 2026): **25 exhibitors (+30% vs 2025)**, daily pitches from 11:00 to 12:30, demonstrations of AI applied to formulation, traceability, line management and materials identification (source: cfiaexpo.com).
- **Reuse Village**: designed with the **Vrac & Réemploi** network, around 15 companies specialising in reusable packaging.
- **Food Factory of the Future** (Hall 6): a space for technology demonstrations and full-scale demonstrators for food-processing plants.
- **Food Talent** (4th edition on 12 March 2026): a day co-organised by **ABEA** (Association Bretonne des Entreprises Agroalimentaires), **Valorial** and **Bretagne Next**. A **job-dating event for 2,000 young people** with more than 40 Breton companies across 5 functions: R&D, production, maintenance, QHSE, support (source: abea.bzh).

### Awards & accolades

**CFIA Innovation Trophies**: 4 official categories in 2026.

- Ingredients & PAI
- Process, Conditioning, Equipment
- Packaging
- Quality, Hygiene, Safety

124 entries competing in 2026, 5 winners honoured (source: cfiaexpo.com).

2026 winners:

- **Saipol** "Empreinte by Saipol", Ingredients & PAI category (low-carbon programme for oilseed supply chains).
- **H.B. Fuller**, Packaging category (foamed adhesive for PET multipacks).
- **Sileane**, Process, Conditioning, Equipment category ("Replace In Place" robotic solution).
- **ATM Vision** (category to be confirmed).
- **Rescaset**, special mention from the jury (induction sealing for reuse).

### Community & networks

Institutional partners and networks: **ABEA**, **Valorial** (Breton food-processing competitiveness cluster), **Bretagne Next**, the **Vrac & Réemploi** network. Specialist press: Process Alimentaire, RIA, Agro-Media, Food Magazine.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Parc Expo Rennes](/lieux/parc-expo-rennes) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates:** 9 to 11 March 2027 (Tuesday to Thursday).
- **Pavilion locations:** 12 halls arranged according to the 4 worlds (Hall 4 Ingredients, Halls 2-3-5-6-7-8 Equipment, Halls 1-10-11 Packaging, Hall 12 Food Safety).
- **Visitor badge:** free with professional pre-registration via cfiaexpo.com. Access strictly reserved for food-processing industry professionals (proof of activity required).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published. Participation requests via the [exposant.gl-events.com/cfia-rennes-2027](https://exposant.gl-events.com/cfia-rennes-2027/) platform. The trade show has historically been tight on availability in the Ingredients & PAI and Food Safety zones: it is recommended to submit a request 12 months before the target edition. Figures not publicly available.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: submit your application on the GL Events platform, choosing your world (Ingredients & PAI, Equipment & Processes, Packaging, Food Safety).
- 9 months out: positioning within the corresponding hall and application to the thematic spaces (AI Village Hall 2, Reuse Village, Food Factory of the Future Hall 6).
- 6 months out: preparing the 2027 Innovation Trophies entry (4 categories: Ingredients & PAI, Process-Conditioning-Equipment, Packaging, Quality-Hygiene-Safety).
- 3 months out: activating ABEA, Valorial and Bretagne Next relays for upstream communication to Breton food businesses.
- 1 month out: finalising live demonstrations and briefing the on-site team.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free online badge pre-registration on cfiaexpo.com with proof of professional activity.
- Allow 2 full days to cover the 12 halls (1 day is not enough across 4 worlds).
- Prioritise the world matching your function: Hall 4 for R&D and formulation, Halls 2-3-5-6-7-8 for production and maintenance, Halls 1-10-11 for packaging, Hall 12 for QHSE.
- Block out the daily AI pitches at the AI Village (11:00 to 12:30, Hall 2) and the visit to the Food Factory of the Future (Hall 6).
- Getting to Rennes: TGV from Paris in 1 hr 30, then a road link to the Parc Expo Aéroport.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

CFIA''s CSR dimension is expressed through several documented levers. The Innovation Trophies include a **Quality, Hygiene, Safety** category that recognises advances in food safety and traceability. The **Reuse Village**, designed with the Vrac & Réemploi network, showcases around fifteen companies specialising in reusable packaging. The **Food Safety** hall created in 2025 structures a dedicated offering for hygiene, food safety and traceability. The low-carbon approach is championed by some recent winners (Saipol 2026 "Empreinte by Saipol" on oilseed supply chains, Rescaset on induction sealing for reuse). To date, CFIA does not publish a formalised CSR policy for the trade show itself.

## How the trade show has evolved

