### Trajectory analysis

CFIA celebrates its 30th edition in 2027 with a structurally growing trajectory: 360 exhibitors in 1997 across 10,000 m², 1,300 in 2015 across 8 halls, 1,700+ in 2025 across 12 halls, 2,000 in 2026. The addition of the **Packaging** world in 2000, then **Ingredients & PAI** in 2004, and finally **Food Safety** in 2025 (Hall 12), illustrates a strategy of gradually broadening the business worlds covered. The redesign of Halls 1 and 11 in 2026 across the packaging scope confirms the priority given to this world. The 30th edition in 2027 is a strong symbolic milestone: with attendance already at a high plateau (+1.4% in 2026), the growth potential lies more in the quality of the exhibitor mix (densifying the Food Safety and AI worlds) than in raw volume. Variables to watch: the capacity of the Parc Expo Rennes Aéroport across 12 saturated halls, and the renewal rate of Ingredients & PAI exhibitors.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='cfia-rennes';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Crossroads for suppliers to the food processing industry, South-West edition. Equipment, ingredients and services for the food industry.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- CFIA Toulouse is the South-West edition of the CFIA, the Crossroads for Suppliers to the Food Processing Industry, whose flagship edition is held in Rennes: [CFIA Rennes](/salons/cfia-rennes). It is run by **GL Events Exhibitions Industrie**.
- Next edition: 3rd edition, from 22 to 24 September 2026 at the [MEETT in Toulouse](/lieux/meett-toulouse) (Aussonne).
- A biennial trade show held in even years: inaugural edition in 2022, second edition in 2024, third edition in 2026.
- The trade show is structured around **3 complementary worlds**: Ingredients & food intermediates, Equipment & processes, Packaging and conditioning.
- Inaugural 2022 edition: close to 6,000 visitors (source: ria.fr). Recent editions bring together more than 350 exhibitors.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Suppliers to the food processing industry spread across the trade show''s three worlds: ingredients and intermediate food products (PAI), equipment and processes (processing, automation, maintenance, hygiene), packaging and conditioning. The trade show is aimed at professionals from the industrial hubs of the South-West: industrial management, production, R&D, quality, purchasing and maintenance managers within the food industry.

### Notable exhibitors

The trade show brings together more than 350 suppliers covering the needs of food industries in ingredients, processes, equipment and packaging. Details of the participants are available at [toulouse.cfiaexpo.com](https://toulouse.cfiaexpo.com/fr).

### Quality of the visitor base

- A regional positioning presented as an operational meeting point for South-West players, a region with a high density of food industries.
- Inaugural 2022 edition: close to 6,000 visitors (source: ria.fr).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The trade show offers a series of talks and conferences. Replays of the 2024 edition''s conferences are available online. Among the focus areas highlighted for the 2026 edition: CSR as an industrial lever (energy efficiency, reducing environmental impact, sustainable ingredients, eco-friendly packaging). The detailed 2026 programme is published in the run-up to the trade show (source: toulouse.cfiaexpo.com).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [MEETT in Toulouse](/lieux/meett-toulouse).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** reserved for professionals in the food processing industry, by prior online registration on the official website.
- **Dates:** 22 to 24 September 2026, Tuesday to Thursday.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
