### Trajectory analysis

Launched in 2022, CFIA Toulouse is the South-West edition of the CFIA, whose parent edition is held in Rennes: [CFIA Rennes](/salons/cfia-rennes). The choice of the South-West reflects the region''s high density of food processing industry. The inaugural 2022 edition brought together close to 6,000 visitors, and the trade show confirmed its foothold in 2024 for its second edition at the MEETT. The third edition, from 22 to 24 September 2026, continues this biennial rhythm in even years, drawing on the CFIA''s three complementary worlds: ingredients and food intermediates, equipment and processes, packaging and conditioning. The Toulouse region of the South-West also hosts other industrial gatherings such as [SIANE](/salons/siane-toulouse) and [SEPEM Toulouse](/salons/sepem-toulouse).', seo_title_en='CFIA Toulouse 2026: dates, exhibitors and visitor info (MEETT)', seo_description_en='CFIA Toulouse 2026, 3rd edition from 22 to 24 September at the MEETT. The South-West meeting point for suppliers to the food industry: ingredients, equipment and packaging. More than 350 exhibitors.' WHERE slug='cfia-toulouse';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- ChangeNOW is the major summit of solutions for the planet, held at the Grand Palais in Paris. The 2026 edition brought together **40,000 participants from 140 countries, 1,400 investors, 1,000 solutions, 10,000 companies and 500+ media outlets**.
- It gathers impact startups, investors, major groups and public decision-makers → an event for connecting and financing impact, not a sector-specific trade show.
- More than 200 conferences and 500 international speakers per edition (Johan Rockström, Jean-Marc Jancovici, Christiana Figueres…) → a strong summit dimension and high profile.
- Organised by ChangeNOW, on an annual basis.
- Next edition (10th anniversary): 26-28 April 2027, Grand Palais.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Impact startups, investors, major groups, public decision-makers and NGOs, on the themes of climate, biodiversity, the circular economy and inclusion.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of exhibitors and solutions is available on the official website: [changenow.world](https://www.changenow.world/).

### Quality of attendees

- 40,000 participants from 140 countries in 2026, **1,400 investors**, $9,000bn of AUM on the investor side (source: impact-report-2025)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

More than 200 conferences and 500 international speakers per edition. Themes: climate and decarbonation, biodiversity, the circular economy, resources, inclusion. Notable speakers: Johan Rockström, Kate Raworth, Jean-Marc Jancovici, Christiana Figueres.

### Awards & accolades

ChangeNOW prioritises hosting third-party events and programmes (investor forums, solution pitches, dedicated tracks) over running its own internal awards. Programme details and award winners can be found on the official website.

### Community & networks

An international impact platform, with the status of a **loi 1901 association** (RNA W942010521), holding **B Corp certification 2024 (score of 95)** and the **REEVE level 2 label**, the first major event to obtain it (source: changenow.world/sustainable-event).

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue:** Grand Palais, Paris.
- **Access:** paid event (online ticketing); Wednesday afternoon is open free of charge to the general public.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: quotes are available on request from ChangeNOW.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with ChangeNOW, submit an exhibitor/solution application.
- 6 months out: stand plan, pitch preparation.
- 3 months out: accreditations, accommodation.
- 6 weeks out: final brief, networking activation.

### For the decision-maker attending

- Paid ticket (Early Bird rates several months in advance); Wednesday afternoon free for the general public.
- Allow 2 days: 200+ conferences and a large solutions area, so target the keynotes in advance.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

ChangeNOW sets out its commitments on its [Sustainable event](https://www.changenow.world/sustainable-event/) page: B Corp certification (score of 95) and the REEVE level 2 label, 97.3% of materials reused and 100% vegetarian catering.

## How the trade show has evolved

