### Trajectory analysis

ChangeNOW has established itself as one of the world''s largest impact summits (40,000 participants, 140 countries in 2026). The 2027 edition marks its 10th anniversary at the Grand Palais. A distinctive feature: it is a paid event with a strong international and media dimension, halfway between a summit and a trade show.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='changenow-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='2026 edition at Paris Nord Villepinte, the second consecutive edition at the site following the move from the Porte de Versailles in 2025. A two-day, weekend-format event open to the general public, with tens of thousands of attendees in 2025.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 2026 edition of Comic Con France: **18 and 19 April 2026** at Paris Nord Villepinte, the second consecutive edition at the site following the move from the Porte de Versailles in 2025.
- Two-day weekend format: **Saturday 10am to 7pm, Sunday 10am to 5pm**, open to the general public, families and cosplayers.
- 2025 review (12 and 13 April, Villepinte): tens of thousands of attendees across two days, a successful repositioning of the trade show after the geographical move.
- Organised by the **Comic Con France team**, descended from Reed Expositions France (now RX France), the French division of the global pop-culture network **ReedPop**.
- General-public pricing: **€22.90 for a day pass, €39.99 for the weekend pass**, free for accompanied under-10s. Autograph sessions, photoshoots and VIP experiences available at an additional cost.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The trade show is structured around five main hubs, which cover most of the professional pop-culture verticals present in France.

- **Artist Alley**: guest illustrators, writers and colourists, mainly from the Marvel and DC stables, but also from European comics and manga.
- **Comics and manga publishers**: the leading French and international houses in the segment, who bring out their flagship authors for autograph sessions and previews.
- **Studios and platforms**: Disney via Lucasfilm and Marvel Studios, Warner for DC, Netflix, Sony Pictures and Amazon Prime Video depending on the year, present in their own right or through their licences.
- **Video games and TCG**: trading card game publishers, console demos, arcade cabinets and tournaments.
- **Geek Market**: premium and vintage figurines, limited editions, artist prints, pop-culture clothing and cosplay accessories.

### Notable exhibitors

On the comics and manga publishing side, the trade show has historically drawn **Panini Comics**, **Urban Comics**, **Glénat**, **Delcourt**, **Pika** and **Kana**. In Artist Alley, recent editions have welcomed the likes of **J. Scott Campbell**, **Salva Espin** (Deadpool vs Carnage) and **Andrea Broccardo** (Kanan). On the video games and TCG side, **Pokémon**, **Magic The Gathering** and **One Piece Card Game** run tournament and demonstration set-ups.

The 2026 exhibitor list is updated continuously on the official site as confirmations come in.

### Quality of the visitor base

Comic Con France caters to a predominantly general-public, family and enthusiast audience, with a significant share of cosplayers and seasoned collectors. For B2B exhibitors in the licensing, specialist retail and publishing segments, the audience remains qualified by its density of active fans and its strong prescriptive power, particularly among the 15-35 age group.

## Activities and community

### Guest line-up

The line-up of stars has been the pivot of the trade show since its inception. The 2025 edition brought together the likes of **Ian McDiarmid** (Emperor Palpatine, Star Wars), **Kevin McNally** (Mr Gibbs, Pirates of the Caribbean), **Jack Gleeson** (Joffrey Baratheon, Game of Thrones), **Robert Patrick**, **James Marsters**, **Lance Henriksen**, **Giancarlo Esposito** and **Brad Dourif**, as well as the **Charmed** cast assembled around **Rose McGowan**, **Holly Marie Combs**, **Brian Krause** and **Drew Fuller**.

The 2024 edition, still held at the Porte de Versailles, had welcomed **Temuera Morrison** (Boba Fett), **Anthony Daniels** (C-3PO), **Robert Englund** (Freddy Krueger), **Kevin Eastman** (co-creator of the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles) and **Raphael Luce**.

### Autograph sessions and photoshoots

Each guest operates according to a price list published by the organiser. In 2025, the **Ian McDiarmid** photoshoots were offered at **€90**, and the **Charmed** group photoshoot at **€230**. Advance purchase is explicitly recommended by the organiser to secure slots with the most sought-after guests.

### Cosplay

Cosplay is a defining dimension of the trade show, with a parade, a dedicated stage and themed shows. A conditional discount is offered to identifiable cosplayers at the entrance, according to the terms published by the organiser each edition.

### Stage programme

The main stage hosts panels, masterclasses, Q&A sessions with guests and previews of series and films. The full programme is published by the Comic Con France team in the weeks leading up to the trade show.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking, accommodation and the overall site plan: see the [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte) page.

Specific to this trade show:

- **2026 edition opening hours**:
  - Saturday 18 April: 10am to 7pm.
  - Sunday 19 April: 10am to 5pm.
- **Ticketing**: purchase online on the official site, advance booking strongly recommended for weekends and autograph sessions.
- **Accessibility**: the Villepinte site is wheelchair accessible, served by RER B at the Parc des Expositions station in the immediate vicinity.

## How much it costs to attend

General-public pricing confirmed for the 2026 edition:

- **1-day pass**: €22.90.
- **Weekend pass**: €39.99.
- **Free** for under-10s accompanied by a paying adult.
- **Cosplay**: conditional discount according to the organiser''s terms.

**Autograph sessions** and **photoshoots** are sold separately, with pricing specific to each guest. **VIP experiences** are also offered at certain editions, providing access to a dedicated welcome, goodies and priority autograph slots.

## Preparing your visit

### For the visitor

- 3 months out: keep an eye on the first guest announcements and the release of priority photoshoots.
- 6 weeks out: secure weekend passes and autograph sessions for the most sought-after guests.
- 2 weeks out: cosplay preparation, scouting the layout of the five hubs, identifying priority publisher stands and Artist Alley.
- On the day: arrive early in the morning to get in the autograph queue, bring cash and a card for the Geek Market.

### For the exhibitor or brand

Comic Con France is an activation ground for brands that address pop-culture communities: film and series licences, publishers, specialist retailers, streaming platforms and geek lifestyle brands. Exhibitor applications are made via the Comic Con France team. For licensing and retail players, it is one of the two major national events alongside Japan Expo.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" },
 { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" },
