 ]}
 rows={[
 { "edition": "2026 (upcoming)", "dates": "18-19 Apr", "lieu": "Paris Nord Villepinte", "format": "2 days" },
 { "edition": "2025", "dates": "12-13 Apr", "lieu": "Paris Nord Villepinte", "format": "2 days" },
 { "edition": "2024", "dates": "30-31 Mar", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles", "format": "2 days" }
 ]}
 sources="comic-con-france.com, rxglobal.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

Comic Con France was created in 2007 under the name **Kultima** by the founders of Japan Expo (JTS Participations), who made it the comics and American pop-culture counterpart to their manga trade show. The event was renamed **Comic Con Paris in 2009**, then taken over by **Reed Expositions France in 2015**, after a fallow year in 2014. The October 2015 edition was held at the Grande Halle de la Villette, before a spell at the Porte de Versailles.

The major turning point of recent years is twofold. First, the **return to Paris Nord Villepinte in 2025**, which brings the trade show geographically closer to Japan Expo and gives it greater hosting capacity. Second, the **shift in the calendar from October to April**, which positions it in a distinct slot from the other Parisian pop-culture events.

On the international stage, the trade show is part of the **ReedPop** network, the pop-culture division of RX (formerly Reed Exhibitions until June 2021), founded in 2006 by **Greg Topalian** and **Lance Fensterman**, and now the world''s leading producer of pop-culture events (New York Comic Con, Star Wars Celebration, PAX, MCM London Comic Con). This membership provides access to a sourcing pipeline of guests, licences and formats proven in other markets. The 2026 edition, the second consecutive one at Villepinte in the April slot, is set to confirm the repositioning trajectory begun in 2025.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='comic-con-france';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- "EUROPE''S LARGEST DENTAL CONGRESS": every late November, the Congrès ADF brings together the French and international dental profession around a dense scientific programme and an industry exhibition.
- Organiser: Association Dentaire Française (ADF).
- Upcoming edition: from 24 to 28 November 2026 at the [Palais des Congrès de Paris](/lieux/palais-des-congres-paris), Porte Maillot.
- 2026 theme: TOOTH_BEAT.
- Announced 2026 targets: ~28,000 participants, ~300 international exhibitors, 12,830 m² of exhibition space across 4 levels, nearly 100 sessions led by 400 speakers. These figures are organiser forecasts, not an audited report.
- Mixed format: the scientific congress (theoretical, hands-on and interactive sessions) runs from Tuesday 2 p.m. to Saturday midday; the exhibition is open from Wednesday to Saturday.
- Qualiopi-certified for continuing education.
- Scientific direction provided by a panel of experts renewed for each edition: a programme geared towards everyday clinical practice.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The exhibition gathers suppliers and distributors from the dental industry: manufacturers of equipment and chairs, imaging and radiology, implantology, CAD/CAM and digital workflow, consumables, hygiene and sterilisation, biomaterials, prosthetics laboratories, practice-management software publishers, training bodies and professional institutions. The visitor base is made up of dental surgeons, dental assistants, prosthetists, students and lecturers.

### Notable exhibitors

The official list of exhibitors for the edition is published by the organiser: [ADF exhibitor list](https://adfcongres.com/exposant/exposants/).

### Quality of the visitor base

The organiser announces a target of around 28,000 participants for 2026, drawn from a professional dentistry audience (practitioners, practice teams, prosthetists, students). This is an organiser projection, not an OJS-audited figure.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The heart of the congress is its scientific programme: nearly a hundred theoretical, hands-on and interactive sessions, led by around 400 speakers. Formats range from plenary lectures to practical workshops and clinical demonstrations, with a recurring focus on practice application. The programme runs from Tuesday 24 November (2 p.m.) to Saturday 28 November (midday). Some sessions are open to all participants without paid registration; details are published on the organiser''s website as the event approaches.

### Community & networks

The ADF is a federation of associations and bodies from the dental profession; the congress is its unifying annual gathering. Beyond the sessions, it serves as the yearly meeting point between learned societies, trade unions, manufacturers and practitioners. An official mobile app accompanies each edition for navigating the programme (available from September 2026 for the upcoming edition).

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the [Palais des Congrès de Paris](/lieux/palais-des-congres-paris) listing: the venue is served by metro line 1, the RER C and E (Porte Maillot station), the T3b tram and several bus routes, with around 1,000 parking spaces beneath the Palais.

Specific to the congress:
- Address: Palais des Congrès, 2 place de la Porte-Maillot, 75017 Paris.
- 2026 dates: congress from Tuesday 24 to Saturday 28 November; exhibition from Wednesday 25 (9 a.m.) to Saturday 28 November (2 p.m.).
- Exhibition hours: Wednesday to Friday 9 a.m.-7 p.m. (last entry 6 p.m.), Saturday 9 a.m.-2 p.m. (last entry 1 p.m.).
- Badges: registration for the scientific programme grants full access to the exhibition. Access to the exhibition alone is free for all healthcare professionals (children under 16 not admitted). Online registration opens in early June; student registration is online only.

## How much it costs to exhibit

The ADF does not publish a freely available stand pricing grid: exhibitor offers are detailed by the organiser''s Exhibitor Service ([ADF exhibitor offers](https://adfcongres.com/exposant/toutes-nos-offres/)). As a general industry guide, a presence at a major dental congress involves, beyond renting bare space, the usual cost items: stand fit-out and furniture, electricity and utilities, transport and logistics, staff and demonstrators, and team accommodation over 4 days. As no specific figures are published by the organiser, refer directly to the Exhibitor Service for a quote.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 to 6 months out: select the offer and book space with the Exhibitor Service, in line with the objective (product launch, brand awareness, recruiting partner practitioners).
- 4 to 3 months out: stand design across 4 exhibition levels, briefing of demonstrators, practitioner appointment-booking plan.
- 2 months out: logistics (transport, build-up), sales materials, product training for staff.
- 1 month out: client-base invitation campaign, scheduling of stand highlights (clinical demonstrations, workshops).

### For the decision-making visitor

Identify in advance the scientific sessions relevant to your practice and cross-reference them with a shortlist of exhibitors to see (CAD/CAM, implantology, practice software). Registering online early avoids queuing on site. Book accommodation early: late November is a busy period in Paris.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The ADF and Comident have jointly launched an environmental commitment charter aimed at optimising the ordering processes for dental products across the industry. In addition, the Palais des Congrès de Paris is managed by Viparis, which runs a structured CSR programme built around three pillars: Better for the Environment, Better Heritage, Better @Heart. As at the date of this listing, the organiser''s website does not feature a dedicated "Commitments" or "CSR" page for the congress detailing an ISO 20121 certification specific to the event; any additional sustainability initiatives should be confirmed directly with the organiser.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "participants", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2026 (upcoming)", "dates": "24-28 Nov. 2026", "lieu": "Palais des Congrès de Paris", "participants": "~28,000 (target)", "exposants": "~300 (target)" }, { "edition": "2025", "dates": "25-29 Nov. 2025", "lieu": "Palais des Congrès de Paris", "participants": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }]} sources="Figures announced by the organiser (targets), not OJS-audited." />

### Trajectory analysis

The Congrès ADF is a fixture of the European dental calendar: same venue (Palais des Congrès, Porte Maillot), same late-November slot, same annual rhythm. Its distinctiveness lies in its hybrid model, a leading scientific congress paired with an industry exhibition, which makes it at once a continuing-education event and a trade show. The volumes communicated by the organiser vary from one edition to the next depending on the scope cited (in the region of 300 to 400 exhibitors, 12,830 to 22,000 m² announced): these discrepancies stem from marketing communications rather than an audit, and call for treating these figures as orders of magnitude. The scientific direction and editorial theme are renewed each year, which keeps the programme attractive to practitioners.', seo_title_en='Congrès ADF 2026 Paris: dates, exhibitors, programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='Congrès ADF 2026: from 24 to 28 November at the Palais des Congrès de Paris. ~28,000 participants expected, ~300 exhibitors, 12,830 m². TOOTH_BEAT programme, Qualiopi certification.' WHERE slug='congres-adf-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='HR decision-makers and work transformation congress. Conferences, keynotes and workshops on the future of human resources.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The Congrès HR'' is the twice-yearly gathering of the French HR decision-maker community: two editions per year, in spring and autumn, at the [Pré Catelan](/lieux/le-pre-catelan) in the Bois de Boulogne (Paris 16th arrondissement).
- Organised by **Arcaneo** (AEF Info group), it brings together around 900 HR decision-makers around a packed format: 2 major debates, 10 themed sessions, 10 experiential workshops and 80 testimonials from human resources professionals.
- The 50th edition (anniversary edition) was held on 8 and 9 April 2026 on the theme of anticipating the future of the HR function.
- The next edition (51st) is announced for autumn 2026 at the Pré Catelan. Exact dates to be confirmed on the official website.
- A paid event focused on conferences and networking, with no traditional exhibition floor: this is a congress for leaders, not a trade show with stands.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The Congrès HR'' is not an exhibitor trade show in the classic sense: it is a congress for decision-makers. The audience is made up of group HR directors, HR directors, heads of training, talent and transformation, as well as invited experts and speakers. The community gathered numbers around 900 HR decision-makers per edition, drawn mainly from large companies and mid-cap firms.

Partners and sponsors (HR solution providers, consulting firms, training service providers) are present through partnerships and meeting spaces, rather than exhibition halls. The list of official partners is published at [congreshr.com/partenaires](https://www.congreshr.com/partenaires).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The editorial format is the heart of the Congrès HR'': **2 major debates**, **10 themed sessions**, **10 experiential workshops** and **80 testimonials** from human resources professionals per edition.

The 50th edition (8-9 April 2026) focused on anticipating the future of the HR function, with sessions covering the integration of AI into HR processes, health and mental health at work, employee engagement, mobility through skills, the evolution of leadership culture, managing transformations, the renewal and transfer of skills, and diversity, inclusion and pay equity.

The two major debates of this edition were led by Frédéric Encel, doctor (HDR) in geopolitics (Université Paris-VIII) and senior lecturer at Sciences Po Paris, and Gérald Bronner, professor of sociology (Université Paris-Diderot). The programme and theme of the 51st edition will be published as the event approaches (source: congreshr.com/programme).

### Community and networks

With 50 twice-yearly editions behind it, the Congrès HR'' has established itself as a recurring meeting point for the French HR community, with two appointments each year. The logic of the format is peer-to-peer experience sharing (HR director testimonials) rather than commercial demonstration.

## On site: what you need to know

Access and practical information: see the [Pré Catelan](/lieux/le-pre-catelan) listing, Route de Suresnes, Bois de Boulogne, 75016 Paris.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Format:** a two-day congress, alternating plenary sessions (major debates), themed sessions and experiential workshops.
- **Registration:** a paid event, advance registration via the official website. Reserved for HR decision-makers and professionals.
- **Organiser contact:** congreshr@arcaneo-group.com.

## Planning your visit

### For the HR decision-maker

- Target the themed sessions and workshops in advance according to your priorities (AI, health at work, skills, leadership, inclusion): the programme is published several weeks before each edition.
- Allow for both days: the format combines plenary sessions in the morning (major debates) with more focused themed tracks.
- Plan your networking: the value of the congress lies as much in peer-to-peer meetings as in the conference content.

### For the partner

- Get in touch in advance with Arcaneo regarding partnership and speaking formats (the terms are not published publicly).
- Prepare a testimonial or workshop angle: the congress favours concrete real-world feedback over product pitches.

## How the trade show has evolved

A twice-yearly fixture established over the past two decades, the Congrès HR'' follows a rhythm of two editions per year (spring and autumn). The recent sequence places the 49th edition in autumn 2025 (12-13 November 2025), the 50th edition (anniversary) on 8 and 9 April 2026, and the 51st edition in autumn 2026. The format has remained stable at around 900 HR decision-makers, 80 testimonials, 10 themed sessions and 10 experiential workshops per edition, making it one of the reference gatherings for the senior HR community in France. Audited attendance figures and the theme of the 51st edition will be announced as the event approaches.', seo_title_en='Congrès HR'' 2026 Paris: programme, dates and info | Agoris', seo_description_en='The Congrès HR'', the twice-yearly gathering of HR decision-makers at the Pré Catelan (Paris 16th). 900 decision-makers, 10 sessions, 80 testimonials. Organised by Arcaneo (AEF Info group).' WHERE slug='congres-hr-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Cosmetic formulation days. Meetings between formulators, ingredient suppliers and cosmetic brands.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- "Les Rencontres de la Formulation" (The Formulation Meetings): Cosmetagora is the technical and scientific gathering dedicated to cosmetic formulation, from ingredient sourcing to the development of textures.
- Organiser: the Société Française de Cosmétologie (SFC), a scientific association that runs the event directly, without any third-party event operator.
- Next edition: 19th Cosmetagora, on 12 and 13 January 2027 (9.30am-6pm), at the [Espace Champerret](/lieux/espace-champerret), Paris 17th.
- 2026 audience (organiser''s review): 5,510 visitors, 200 exhibitors, 245 stands across 7,000 m². A 100% professional audience: formulators, ingredient suppliers, subcontractors, evaluation laboratories, brands.
- Editorial highlight: the Prix de la Formulation (Formulation Award), whose 2027 theme is "AUDACE ET ART : QUAND LA COSMÉTIQUE DEVIENT CHEF-D''OEUVRE" (Boldness and Art: When Cosmetics Become a Masterpiece).
- Compact format: two days, a single venue, a strong scientific density (conferences, workshops, start-up area), in contrast to large generalist B2B trade shows.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The audience and the offer are centred on the formulation chain, not on the finished consumer product. You will mainly find suppliers and distributors of raw materials, specialists in textures and active ingredients, contract subcontractors, packaging designers, evaluation laboratories (safety, efficacy, toxicology) and testing service providers. On the visitor side: formulators, R&D and marketing managers, project leaders, brand founders and cosmetology students.

### Notable exhibitors

The official list of exhibitors is published on the organiser''s website. The 2026 edition brought together 200 exhibitors across 245 stands.

### Quality of the audience

According to the organiser''s review, the 2026 edition welcomed 5,510 visitors across 7,000 m². The audience is almost exclusively made up of professionals in cosmetic formulation and R&D, which makes it a trade show with a high proportion of decision-makers and technical profiles, rather than a volume-driven event.

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The programme is built around the core topics of the sector: raw materials, textures, new technologies, safety and efficacy evaluation testing, and formulation innovations. The detailed conferences and workshops for the upcoming edition are published by the organiser as the event approaches.

### Awards and accolades

The event presents the **Prix de la Formulation** (Formulation Award). The theme chosen for the 2027 edition is: "AUDACE ET ART : QUAND LA COSMÉTIQUE DEVIENT CHEF-D''OEUVRE" (Boldness and Art: When Cosmetics Become a Masterpiece). Two categories: Skincare, Hygiene and Haircare; Make-up and Suncare. A "Coup de Coeur" (Visitors'' Choice) award is also given by the visitors. This competition showcases the formulation creativity of the candidates, who are invited to draw inspiration from a work of art (painting, sculpture, photography) to design an innovative formulation.

### Community & networks

Cosmetagora is backed by the Société Française de Cosmétologie, the scientific community of cosmetology in France. A start-up welcome scheme is offered for innovative companies: a 3 m2 module, a team of 10 staff maximum, less than 2 years of existence, in the cosmetics or raw materials sector (contact: cosmetagora@sfcosmeto.fr).

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the venue page: [Espace Champerret](/lieux/espace-champerret) (Place de la Porte de Champerret, 75017 Paris; métro line 3, Porte de Champerret station; buses 84, 92, PC1, 165 at the Porte de Champerret stop; buses 93, 163, 164 at the L''Yser et la Somme stop; on-site car park).

Specific to the trade show: the 2027 edition is held on 12 and 13 January, from 9.30am to 6pm on both days. Entry is reserved for professionals by registration via the organiser''s website. The compact format (two days, a single exhibition level) makes a thorough visit possible over half a day to a day.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="No public pricing schedule is released by the organiser. The amounts below are indicative orders of magnitude for a professional trade show of this size and do not constitute the official Cosmetagora rates. Request the exhibitor pack from the SFC for the actual prices." rows={[{ "poste": "Stand (bare or fitted space, indicative)", "low": "3,000 €", "high": "9,000 €" }, { "poste": "Fit-out / furniture / signage", "low": "1,500 €", "high": "6,000 €" }, { "poste": "Samples, documentation, logistics", "low": "1,000 €", "high": "4,000 €" }, { "poste": "Staff, travel, accommodation", "low": "2,000 €", "high": "6,000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (indicative, 2 days)", "low": "~7,500 €", "high": "~25,000 €" }]} footer="A start-up scheme exists for innovative companies less than 2 years old (3 m2 module, 10 staff max). Actual rates to be confirmed with the SFC." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

Official 2026-2027 calendar (source: SFC Exhibitor Info page):

- 12 June 2026: stand allocation draw.
- 15 June 2026: publication of the allocation list online.
- 30 July 2026: deadline for the first deposit.
- 30 October 2026: registration close.
- 6 November 2026: deadline for submitting practical information.
- 27 November 2026: deadline for the balance of payment.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Target the relevant raw material suppliers and subcontractors in advance via the online exhibitor list.
- Identify the technical conferences and workshops as soon as the programme is published: this is the core value of the event.
- Set aside half a day to a day: the compact format makes it possible to cover all the stands without spreading them out.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

No dedicated "Commitments" or "CSR" page is published by the SFC for Cosmetagora, and the event does not hold its own ISO 20121 certification. Two tangible areas are nonetheless documented. On the venue side: the Espace Champerret is managed by Viparis, the world''s first operator certified ISO 20121 across all ten of its Parisian sites since 2014 (4th renewal cycle under way), covering waste management, energy efficiency, responsible purchasing and the fight against food waste. On the organiser side: the SFC includes CSR among its scientific communication priorities (alongside new technologies and AI) and has, since 2023, co-organised a Sustainability Challenge with L''Oréal Recherche & Innovation, open to start-ups and researchers proposing sustainable solutions for the cosmetics industry (3rd edition held in September 2025 during the IFSCC Congress in Cannes). This challenge, run by the same learned society that organises Cosmetagora, reflects a growing rooting of sustainability in the sector the trade show brings together. The start-up welcome scheme (3 m2 module, companies less than 2 years old) remains the only inclusive measure documented directly at the level of the event.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "19th (2027, upcoming)", "dates": "12-13 Jan. 2027", "lieu": "Espace Champerret, Paris", "visiteurs": "upcoming", "exposants": "upcoming" }, { "edition": "18th (2026)", "dates": "13-14 Jan. 2026", "lieu": "Espace Champerret, Paris", "visiteurs": "5,510", "exposants": "200" }]} sources="Société Française de Cosmétologie (sfcosmeto.fr)" />

### Trajectory analysis

Cosmetagora has established itself as the annual gathering point for cosmetic formulation in France, on a tight model: two days, a single venue (the Espace Champerret for several editions now), and an audience made up almost entirely of technical professionals. With 5,510 visitors and 200 exhibitors in 2026, the trade show remains mid-sized, but its value lies in the quality of its audience (formulators, R&D, ingredient suppliers) rather than in volume. The continuation of an annual theme for the Prix de la Formulation and of a start-up scheme reflects a desire to renew the scientific content from year to year while keeping a stable and legible format.', seo_title_en='Cosmetagora 2027 Paris: dates, exhibitors, programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='Cosmetagora 2027, on 12-13 January at the Espace Champerret (Paris). 19th edition of cosmetic formulation: 200 exhibitors, 5,510 visitors in 2026, Prix de la Formulation.' WHERE slug='cosmetagora-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='12th edition of the leading European B2B trade show dedicated to innovation in cosmetics and perfumery, held at the Carrousel du Louvre. Record 2025 edition: 5,800 visitors, 260 exhibitors including 36 start-ups, 75 countries represented.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Cosmetic 360 is presented as the leading European B2B trade show dedicated to innovation in cosmetics and perfumery, organised each year in Paris by **Cosmetic Valley**.
- 12th edition on **14 and 15 October 2026** at the [Carrousel du Louvre](/lieux/carrousel-du-louvre), 99 rue de Rivoli, Paris 1st arrondissement. Access strictly reserved for professionals.
- 2026 theme **"Regenerations"**: *repair, restore and revitalize* practices (regenerative agriculture, biotech, circular economy, skin repair).
- Record 2025 edition: **5,800 visitors** (vs ~5,000 at previous editions), **260 exhibitors** including 36 start-ups, **75 countries represented**, 17 international delegations, more than 5,000 international decision-makers. Top visitor countries: South Korea, Belgium, China, Italy, Switzerland.
- Organiser: **Cosmetic Valley**, an association founded in 1994, **awarded competitiveness cluster status since 2005**, the benchmark network for the French cosmetics and perfumery sector.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Cosmetic 360 brings together the entire upstream value chain of the cosmetics and perfumery industry:

- **Ingredients and raw materials**: active ingredients, biotech, functional ingredients, perfumery.
- **Formulation and contract manufacturing**: laboratories, OEM/ODM, subcontracting.
- **Packaging and filling**: containers, applicators, eco-design, recyclability.
- **Testing & analysis**: assessment laboratories, neuroscience, AI applied to testing.
- **Tech & industrial equipment**: automation, traceability, responsible production.
- **Distribution and retail tech**: in-store diagnostics, personalisation, customer journey.

### Notable exhibitors and 2025 winners

The **Cosmetic 360 Awards 2025** (theme *Predictions*) recognised six categories:

- **Raw Materials**: **Sparxell** for a structurally coloured cellulose pigment (an alternative to synthetic dyes).
- **Formulation**: **Technature** for a hydrogel mask that changes colour during use.
- **Testing & Analysis**: **Brain Impact** for an fMRI approach coupled with AI to identify purchase-decision markers.
- **Packaging & Packing**: **Nexdot** for **Parelux**, a nail varnish incorporating recyclable anti-UV *quantum dots*.
- **Brands & Retail**: **Byome Labs** for an in-store microbiome analysis solution in under 2 minutes.
- **Special Jury Prize "Predictions"**: **Cosmetopack**, a joint project by **Polymeris** and **Cosmetic Valley** for interactive modelling of container/content interactions.

On the start-up side, the **Village Beauty Tech Chartres** brings together 32 cosmetics start-ups less than 5 years old, backed by the Chartres métropole network and Cosmetic Valley, inspired by the French Tech model and hosted within the Start-up Village (not to be confused with the 36 exhibiting start-ups across the trade show overall).

### Quality of the visitor base

The trade show locked in a highly international and highly decision-making visitor base in 2025:

- 5,800 professional visitors (all-time record).
- 75 countries represented, 17 international delegations.
- More than 5,000 international decision-makers identified.
- Top 5 visitor countries: South Korea, Belgium, China, Italy, Switzerland.

## Programme & community

### Innovation Challenges 2026

Six major buyers lead the Innovation Challenges 2026, the trade show''s flagship initiative, which puts buyers and innovators directly in touch on precise specifications: **Chanel, L''Oréal, LVMH Recherche, Estée Lauder, Technature, Proya Cosmetics**.

### The 6 thematic strands for 2026

The 2026 editorial programme is organised around six strands:

1. **Predictive testing** (in vitro and in silico modelling).
2. **AI and modelling** applied to R&D and marketing.
3. **Tech & environment** (low-impact processes, impact measurement).
4. **Consumer diagnostics and personalisation**.
5. **Industrial efficiency** (productivity, automation, sourcing).
6. **Well-being and neuroscience** (sensory measurement, neuromarketing).

### Cosmetic 360 Week

Around the 2 days of the trade show, **Cosmetic 360 Week** opens up a week of sector meetings in Paris and across the regions, with a dedicated site at **cosmetic-week.com**. Recurring speakers announced: **L''Oréal, Dassault Systèmes, DSM Firmenich, Prose, Aptar Beauty**. The format expands the trade show into a genuine professional highlight of the post-summer beauty season.

### Biotech 2045 Anticipation Capsule

A striking piece of staging at the 2025 edition, the **Biotech 2045 Anticipation Capsule**, created by **Greentech**, projected visitors into a sector scenario 20 years ahead. This type of immersive feature is recurring and accompanies the annual theme: one to watch on the "Regenerations" side for 2026.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Carrousel du Louvre](/lieux/carrousel-du-louvre) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates and opening hours:** 14 and 15 October 2026, 2-day format.
- **Access:** strictly reserved for professionals (proof required), badge to be pre-registered online.
- **Digital platform:** included with the visitor badge, open before and after the trade show to prepare business meetings.
- **CEW France partnership offer:** preferential rate negotiated for CEW France members.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published to date: bespoke quote on request from the Cosmetic Valley team. Figure not publicly available.

Visitor rates: **€49 excl. VAT**, including access to the 2 days of the trade show and the digital networking platform. Historic progression of the rate: €40 in 2021, €45 in 2022, €49 excl. VAT today.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with Cosmetic Valley, identify your positioning (raw materials, formulation, packaging, testing, tech, retail).
- 9 months out: apply for the **Cosmetic 360 Awards** (6 categories) and the **Innovation Challenges** led by Chanel, L''Oréal, LVMH Recherche, Estée Lauder, Technature and Proya Cosmetics: a direct buyer-matching lever.
- 6 months out: align your messaging with the **"Regenerations"** theme (repair, restore, revitalize) to maximise visibility on visitor journeys.
- 3 months out: brief your team on the international delegations expected (South Korea, Belgium, China, Italy and Switzerland leading the way in 2025).
- 6 weeks out: make the most of **Cosmetic 360 Week** to schedule satellite conferences, site visits and off-stand business meetings.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online registration mandatory, professional proof to be provided.
- Badge rate **€49 excl. VAT**, digital platform included to prepare your meetings in advance.
- Prioritise the **Cosmetic 360 Awards** (6 categories) and the **Start-up Village** to scan early-stage innovations.
- Take advantage of **Cosmetic 360 Week**: a satellite programme bringing together L''Oréal, Dassault Systèmes, DSM Firmenich, Prose and Aptar Beauty.
- Carrousel du Louvre fully accessible to people with reduced mobility.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Cosmetic Valley has been structuring a CSR approach dedicated to the trade show since 2021, supported by the agency **COMMON GOOD CONSEIL**. The main levers:

- **Poplar plywood stands** sourced 100% from sustainably managed forests (France and Spain).
- **Algo® paints**, algae-based, **95% bio-sourced**.
- **Low-consumption LED lighting** across the entire site.
- Reuse and pooling of staging modules from one edition to the next.

The 2026 **"Regenerations"** theme extends this approach into an editorial topic: regenerative agriculture, biotech, circular economy, skin repair.

## How the trade show has evolved

