### Trajectory analysis

Launched in 2015, Cosmetic 360 passed the symbolic 10-year mark in 2024 and, in 2025, locked in its status as the benchmark European event: a record 5,800 visitors, 75 countries represented, 17 international delegations and more than 5,000 international decision-makers. The strength of the model rests on three levers: a structuring annual editorial theme (Predictions in 2025, Regenerations in 2026) that aligns exhibitors, awards and staging; Innovation Challenges led directly by major buyers (Chanel, L''Oréal, LVMH Recherche, Estée Lauder, Technature, Proya Cosmetics) that turn the trade show into a B2B marketplace; and a **Cosmetic 360 Week** that extends the physical event into a sector-wide highlight. The organising brand **Cosmetic Valley**, a competitiveness cluster since 2005, gives the trade show an institutional standing that is rare in the beauty ecosystem.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='cosmetic-360';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='58th edition of the world''s leading B2B cosmetics trade show at BolognaFiere, organised across 3 specialised sub-shows (Cosmopack, Cosmo Perfumery & Cosmetics, Cosmo Hair Nail & Beauty Salon). 2026 results: 255,000+ operators from 150 countries, 3,104 exhibitors from 68 countries.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Cosmoprof Worldwide Bologna is **the world''s leading B2B cosmetics trade show**: 58th edition from **18 to 21 March 2027** at **BolognaFiere** (Italy), organised by **BolognaFiere Cosmoprof S.p.A.** in partnership with **Cosmetica Italia**.
- 2026 results (57th edition, 26-29 March): **more than 255,000 operators** from over 150 countries, **3,104 exhibitors** from 68 countries, **10,000+ brands** represented, **33 country pavilions**, **170,000+ sq m of exhibition space**, of which 37% were first-time exhibitors. Sold out as soon as registration opened.
- Structured across **3 specialised sub-shows**: **Cosmopack** (raw materials, formulation, packaging, OEM/CDMO), **Cosmo Perfumery & Cosmetics** (selective perfumery, consumer brands, distribution) and **Cosmo Hair, Nail & Beauty Salon** (professional hairdressing, salon equipment, nail care, aesthetics).
- **French Pavilion** of 750+ sq m in Hall 16, organised by **Business France**, with support from **Bretagne Commerce International (BCI)** for micro-businesses and SMEs.
- For 4 days, Bologna becomes the world capital of beauty. Italy: the world''s 4th-largest cosmetics producer.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Cosmoprof Worldwide Bologna covers the entire cosmetics value chain, organised across 3 sub-shows with differentiated dates and schedules.

**Cosmopack (26-28 March 2027, Thursday-Saturday, 3 days)** brings together the upstream industrial segment:

- Active ingredients and raw materials (Roquette, BASF Pharma Solutions, DuPont).
- Excipients and formulation solutions.
- Contract manufacturers, OEM/CDMO and BioProduction (Lonza, Recipharm, Catalent, Fareva).
- Primary and secondary packaging (Schott, SGD Pharma, Gerresheimer, Stevanato).
- Machinery and production lines (IMA, Romaco, Syntegon formerly Bosch Packaging).

**Cosmo Perfumery & Cosmetics (26-28 March 2027, Thursday-Saturday)** brings together selective perfumery, consumer brands, distribution players and the finished product (FDF). International buyers and brands expected: L''Oréal, Estée Lauder, Sephora.

**Cosmo Hair, Nail & Beauty Salon (26-29 March 2027, Thursday-Sunday, 4 days)** is dedicated to professional hairdressing, salon equipment, nail care, aesthetics and training. Hair pro majors expected: TIGI, Wella, Schwarzkopf, Davines.

### Quality of attendance

Attendance in 2026 reached a benchmark level on the global B2B beauty market.

- **255,000+ professional operators** from over 150 countries.
- 3,104 exhibitors from 68 countries.
- 37% first-time exhibitors on the supply side.
- 2026 pre-registrations rose sharply across all regions: **Asia +53%, North America +28%, Middle East +23%, Africa +12%, Europe +11%** compared to 2025 (ITA pre-show data).

## Activities & community

### Cosmoprof & Cosmopack Awards

The 2026 Awards honoured **16 winners** plus a Lifetime Achievement Award at the ceremony on 27 March 2026. The editorial partnership is provided by **Beautystreams**, an international trend agency. Seven categories compete: Skincare, Make-up, Fragrance, Personal Care, Home Care, Hair Care, Packaging Design & Materials.

The packaging innovation awarded in 2026 illustrates the show''s momentum: the **Air Mist Gas-Free Spray System** by **Shinkwang M&P**, an atomisation system using air compression without propellant gas, winner in the Packaging Design & Materials category.

### International Cosmoprof Network

Cosmoprof Bologna is the parent brand of a network that is unique in the B2B beauty segment:

- **Cosmoprof North America Las Vegas** (main US edition).
- **Cosmoprof Asia Hong Kong**.
- **Cosmoprof India Mumbai**.
- **Cosmoprof CBE ASEAN Bangkok**.
- **Cosmoprof Miami** (launched in 2024, targeting LATAM).
- **Cosmoprof Sao Paulo**.

This "Cosmoprof Network" umbrella brand allows exhibitors to target regional markets with a shared editorial standard.

### French Pavilion

The **French Pavilion** extends over **more than 750 sq m in Hall 16**, organised by **Business France**. **Bretagne Commerce International (BCI)** specifically supports micro-businesses and SMEs from Brittany on the pavilion. A format well suited to French subcontractors, contract manufacturers, ingredient specialists and packaging suppliers targeting the international market.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [BolognaFiere](/lieux/bolognafiere) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates:** 18-21 March 2027 (58th edition). Cosmopack and Cosmo Perfumery & Cosmetics from 18 to 20 March (Thursday-Saturday), Cosmo Hair, Nail & Beauty Salon from 18 to 21 March (Thursday-Sunday).
- **Visitor hours:** 9:30 am-6:30 pm.
- **Exhibitor hours:** 8:30 am-7:00 pm.
- **Access:** strictly reserved for beauty professionals (proof of business activity required), online pre-registration mandatory at cosmoprof.com.
- **2026 Early Bird rates** (reference before publication of 2027 rates): **€30 per day**, **€50 for 2 days**, **€80 for 3-4 days** until 9 March 2026. Standard rate: €60 / €95 / €140. 2027 rates to be confirmed.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published to date: bespoke quote on request from BolognaFiere Cosmoprof S.p.A., varying according to the sub-show (Cosmopack, Cosmo Perfumery & Cosmetics or Cosmo Hair, Nail & Beauty Salon), the floor area, the location and the country pavilion. Figures not publicly available.

For French exhibitors, the French Pavilion option via **Business France** or **BCI** provides access to a turnkey format that is often more affordable than a bare stand, with logistical support and collective visibility.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: choice of target sub-show (Cosmopack vs Cosmo Perfumery & Cosmetics vs Cosmo Hair, Nail & Beauty Salon) according to product positioning.
- 10 months out: **French Pavilion** application to Business France or BCI (limited places, the event has historically sold out).
- 9 months out: application to the **Cosmoprof & Cosmopack Awards** in one of the 7 categories, with the Beautystreams editorial partnership amplifying press visibility.
- 6 months out: team briefing on pre-registrations by region (Asia, North America and Middle East growing strongly in 2026), adjustment of the stand''s language mix.
- 3 months out: alignment of the schedule with the specific dates of the sub-show (Cosmopack and Perfumery & Cosmetics 3 days, Hair & Beauty 4 days).
- 6 weeks out: leverage the Cosmoprof Network (Las Vegas, Hong Kong, Mumbai, Bangkok, Miami, Sao Paulo) for upstream communication with international buyers already registered for the regional editions.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online pre-registration mandatory, proof of professional status to be provided.
- Attractive Early Bird pricing if registering more than 15 days in advance (2026 reference: €80 for 4 days vs €140 standard).
- Prioritise the **Cosmoprof & Cosmopack Awards** (16 winners annually) and the country pavilions (33 in 2026) to scan emerging innovations.
- Allow at least 2 days on site: the **170,000+ sq m** format across 3 sub-shows calls for route planning.
- BolognaFiere is accessible by shuttle from Bologna Guglielmo Marconi airport (15 minutes) and Bologna Centrale station.

## CSR policy & initiatives

BolognaFiere and BolognaFiere Cosmoprof have built a consolidated CSR approach on several levels.

- **ISO 14001 certification** of BolognaFiere since 2019 (environmental management system), maintained across the Cosmoprof editions.
- **Gender Equality Certification UNI/PdR 125:2022** of BolognaFiere, a formalised gender equality approach.
- **HerConomy Award 2025**: a prize dedicated to diversity and inclusion in the sector, integrated into the Cosmoprof programme.
- **Green companies & brands area**: a space currently being developed to showcase exhibitors committed to the circular economy, recycling and eco-design.
- Partnership with **Cosmetica Italia** renewed in September 2025 through to 2029, anchoring the approach within the organised Italian sector.

## The trade show''s evolution

