/>

### Trajectory analysis

Founded in 1967 in Bologna under the name Cosmopack, Cosmoprof reached its 57th edition in 2026 and locked in its status as the **world''s leading B2B beauty trade show**. The strength of the model rests on four structural levers. First, a **structure of 3 sub-shows** (Cosmopack, Cosmo Perfumery & Cosmetics, Cosmo Hair, Nail & Beauty Salon) which allows every player in the chain, from the ingredient to the hair salon, to find its specific ecosystem without diluting the overall format. Next, an **international Cosmoprof Network** (Las Vegas, Hong Kong, Mumbai, Bangkok, Miami launched in 2024, Sao Paulo) that turns the Bologna event into an annual global hub. Third lever: the **institutional partnership with Cosmetica Italia**, renewed through to 2029, which anchors the show to the Italian cosmetics sector (the world''s 4th-largest producer). Finally, **2026 pre-registrations growing by double digits in 4 of 5 regions** (Asia +53%, North America +28%, Middle East +23%, Africa +12%, Europe +11%), confirming that the show is capturing the extra-European momentum just as global beauty pivots towards Asia and the Americas. For a French exhibitor, the **750+ sq m French Pavilion in Hall 16** organised by Business France is the most operational way in.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='cosmoprof-bologna';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='35th edition of the world''s largest trade fair for the pharmaceutical industry, at Fiera Milano with a pre-show Sustainability Summit on 5 October. 2025 Frankfurt results: 62,000+ visitors from 166 countries, 2,400 exhibitors, 260 speakers.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- CPhI Worldwide is presented as the world''s largest trade fair for the pharmaceutical industry, organised each year by **Informa Markets** on a rotation between Milan, Barcelona and Frankfurt.
- 35th edition on **6, 7 and 8 October 2026** at [Fiera Milano](/lieux/fiera-milano), Italy. Pre-show Sustainability Summit on 5 October. No Paris edition is scheduled: Paris hosted CPhI only once, in 2014.
- Record 2025 Frankfurt edition (28-30 October): **62,000+ visitors** (official CPhI Europe figure, up to 67,000 according to Messe Frankfurt), **2,400 exhibitors**, more than **166 countries** represented, 260 speakers, 250+ presenters. Leading countries: Germany, Switzerland, India, China, Italy, USA, Japan, South Korea, United Kingdom.
- 2024 Milan edition (8-10 October, 35th anniversary): 58,664 visitors (170 countries), 2,838 exhibitors (74 nations), 145,000 sq m mobilised.
- Organiser: **Informa Markets**, a division of Informa PLC listed on the London Stock Exchange. The **CPHI Global** umbrella brand claims 280,000+ professionals reached across the network.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

CPhI Worldwide covers the entire pharma value chain, historically structured into **6 co-located zones** under a single ticket:

- **CPhI Worldwide** (historic core): APIs, custom manufacturing, excipients, fine chemicals & intermediates, natural extracts.
- **FDF (Finished Dosage Formulations)**: finished forms, Big Pharma, CMOs, out-licensing opportunities.
- **ICSE (International Contract Services Expo)**: pharma outsourcing and contract services.
- **P-MEC + LabWorld**: pharmaceutical machinery, equipment and components, laboratory and analytical biotech.
- **InnoPack**: primary and secondary pharmaceutical packaging.
- **BioProduction**: bioprocessing and biopharma manufacturing.

The 2026 edition adds **4 new zones**: **AI & Tech**, **Cold Chain & Logistics**, **Contamination Control** and **Labelling**.

### Notable exhibitors and 2025 winners

The **CPHI Pharma Awards** are presented on the first evening, during the **CPHI Celebration**. There were 13 categories in 2025, expanded to around 15 categories for 2026. 2025 winners (Frankfurt):

- **API Development & Innovation**: **CordenPharma** for TAPS (TAG Assisted Peptide Synthesis).
- **Accelerating Innovation**: **NunaBio** for its cell-free synthetic DNA.
- **Manufacturing Excellence**: **Enzene** for **EnzeneX**, a continuous manufacturing platform.
- **CEO of the Year**: **Lars Petersen**, Fujifilm Biotechnologies.
- **Supply Chain Excellence**: **Cryoport Systems**.
- **Woman of the Year**: **Adriana Kiędzierska-Mencfeld**, RezonBio.
- **At the Heart of Pharma**: **CNX Therapeutics**.

On the recurring exhibitor side: APIs and active ingredients (Dr. Reddy''s, Aurobindo and Chinese players in force), excipients (DuPont, Roquette, BASF Pharma Solutions), CDMOs / CMOs (Lonza, Recipharm, Catalent, Fareva, CordenPharma, Flamma), packaging (Schott, SGD Pharma, Gerresheimer, Stevanato), biotech and bioproduction (Fujifilm Biotechnologies, Enzene), pharma machinery (IMA, Romaco, Bosch Packaging / Syntegon).

### Quality of attendance

In 2025 the show locked in its status as the world''s largest gathering for the pharmaceutical industry:

- 62,000+ professional visitors (official CPhI Europe figure, up to 67,000 according to the Messe Frankfurt press release).
- 166+ countries represented.
- 2,400 exhibitors present, 2,990+ announced on the initial programme.
- Top 9 exhibitor / visitor countries: Germany, Switzerland, India, China, Italy, USA, Japan, South Korea, United Kingdom.

## Activities & community

### Pre-Connect Congress and Sustainability Summit

CPHI now extends its in-person event over 4 days: **pre-show Sustainability Summit on 5 October 2026**, then the **Pre-Connect Congress** the day before opening, a premium-format day of conferences dedicated to strategy, BD and R&D leadership.

### Speakers Corner and conference programme

On the floor, the **Speakers Corner** runs a continuous programme over 3 days covering the industry''s major trends. The 2025 edition lined up 260 speakers and 250+ presenters: AI applied to R&D, continuous manufacturing, peptides and oligonucleotides, cold chain, GLP-1, India / China sourcing.

### The 4 new themed zones for 2026

The 2026 edition introduces 4 brand-new zones that structure the visitor journey:

1. **AI & Tech**: artificial intelligence applied to R&D, smart manufacturing, drug discovery.
2. **Cold Chain & Logistics**: cold chain, traceability, critical pharma logistics.
3. **Contamination Control**: contamination control, cleanrooms, controlled environments.
4. **Labelling**: labelling, serialisation, packaging regulatory compliance.

### The CPHI Network

CPhI Worldwide is the central European event of a global network structured by Informa Markets: **CPHI India + PMEC India**, **CPHI China** (Shanghai), **CPHI Japan**, **CPHI South East Asia**, **CPHI Americas Philadelphia** (launched 2024). The CPHI Global umbrella brand claims 280,000+ professionals reached across the entire circuit.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Fiera Milano](/lieux/fiera-milano) listing.

Specific to the show:

- **Dates and opening hours:** 6, 7 and 8 October 2026, 3-day format. Sustainability Summit on 5 October.
- **Access:** strictly reserved for professionals, badge to be pre-registered online. Free professional visitor badge with pre-registration.
- **Digital platform:** the **Events by CPHI** app (also known as the **CPHI Event Planner**) for pre-show matchmaking, business appointment booking and on-site navigation.
- **CPHI Celebration:** Pharma Awards ceremony evening on the first night, an essential networking moment.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published to date: bespoke quote on request from Informa Markets. Figures not publicly available.

Visitor rates: **free professional badge** with online pre-registration (proof of professional status required). The **Pre-Connect Congress** and the **Sustainability Summit** are subject to separate pricing not published to date.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with Informa Markets, choose the zone (CPhI core, FDF, ICSE, P-MEC + LabWorld, InnoPack, BioProduction, or the new AI & Tech, Cold Chain, Contamination Control, Labelling zones).
- 9 months out: enter the **CPHI Pharma Awards** (~15 categories in 2026): a strong visibility lever with Big Pharma buyers.
- 6 months out: brief the team on the top expected countries (Germany, Switzerland, India, China, Italy, USA, Japan, South Korea, United Kingdom).
- 3 months out: prepare appointments via the **Events by CPHI** app as soon as matchmaking opens.
- 6 weeks out: align your pitch with the 4 new 2026 zones if relevant (AI & Tech, Cold Chain, Contamination Control, Labelling) to capture curiosity traffic.
- 2 weeks out: confirm attendance at the **CPHI Celebration** (Pharma Awards evening) and the **Pre-Connect Congress** if you have a BD / strategy profile.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online pre-registration is mandatory, proof of professional status required, free badge.
- Download the **Events by CPHI** app to set up appointments in advance: matchmaking generally active from 6 weeks out.
- Prioritise the **CPHI Pharma Awards** (first evening) to identify the disruptive players in APIs, manufacturing and supply chain.
- Make the most of the **Pre-Connect Congress** (day -1) and the **Sustainability Summit** (day -2) for BD, sourcing and R&D profiles.
- Plan for 3 full days: 6 historic zones + 4 new zones = a typical 145,000 sq m to navigate.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Over several editions CPHI has structured a CSR approach integrated into the programme and the floor:

- **Sustainable Pharma Excellence Award**: a dedicated category for green chemistry, clean manufacturing and the circular economy.
- **Excellence with Purpose Award**: a category for social impact and patient-first thinking.
- **Sustainability Zone** on the floor: exhibitors aligned with the industry''s ESG challenges.
- **Pre-show Sustainability Summit**: a dedicated day on 5 October 2026 in Milan, ahead of the official opening.
- **At the Heart of Pharma** programme: a focus on inclusion, diversity and patient impact, with a dedicated Awards category (2025 winner: CNX Therapeutics).

## How the show has evolved

