A benchmark conference for developers in the Grand Ouest since 2012, DevFest Nantes has established itself as one of the largest French-speaking DevFests, with 3,500 attendees in 2025. The 2027 edition, from 11 to 12 March at the H Arena, is atypical on two counts: a change of venue linked to the renovation works at the Cité des Congrès, and a tightened calendar that makes the 2026-2027 vintage a one-off edition before the annual rhythm resumes. The programme, the call for papers and the 2027 target figures will be published as the event approaches.', seo_title_en='DevFest Nantes 2027: dates, programme and practical info', seo_description_en='DevFest Nantes 2027, the developers'' conference organised by GDG Nantes on 11 and 12 March 2027 at the H Arena. Programme, 2025 review and practical info.' WHERE slug='devfest-nantes';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for agri-food production dedicated to exports towards the Maghreb and Africa. Equipment, raw materials and packaging.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Djazagro is the leading trade show for agri-food production in North Africa, founded in 2003 and held every year in Algiers. It is operated by **Comexposium** (SIAL network), with its international sales activity relayed by the **Promosalons** network.
- 24th edition announced from **12 to 15 April 2027** at the Palais des expositions des Pins maritimes (Safex), Algiers (source: promosalons.com).
- 2026 actuals (23rd edition, 12 to 15 April): nearly 700 exhibitors from 28 countries, including around 150 Algerian companies and producers, with a strong international presence from Italy, Turkey, China and Germany (sources: algerie-eco.com, expressdz.dz).
- 2025 actuals (22nd edition, 7 to 10 April): 650 exhibitors from 36 countries and around 25,000 professionals, of whom 96% were Algerian, coming from 50 wilayas (sources: aps.dz, horizons.dz).
- A trade show geared towards export and sourcing: a majority of overseas exhibitors, serving a visitor base that is overwhelmingly Algerian and North African.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers of agri-food processing equipment and machinery, suppliers of raw materials, ingredients and additives, specialists in conditioning and packaging, players in bakery and pastry, in handling and storage, and in hospitality and catering. The trade show is dedicated exclusively to manufacturers. The visitor base is strictly professional, rooted in the Algerian and Maghreb agri-food sector.

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is available on the official website: [djazagro.com](https://www.djazagro.com/en/exhibitors-list). The 2026 edition brought together international pavilions from Italy, Turkey, China and Germany, as well as companies from several Arab countries (Saudi Arabia, Jordan, Lebanon, Sultanate of Oman, Tunisia) (source: maghrebemergent.news).

### Visitor quality

- Around 25,000 professionals welcomed in 2025, of whom 96% were Algerian coming from 50 wilayas, covering the entire national territory (source: horizons.dz)
- A visitor base targeted at export and sourcing: agri-food manufacturers, importers, distributors and processors seeking equipment and raw materials

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The **Agora des Experts** structures the show''s programme of conferences and professional panels, complemented by a training area and demonstrations. The 2026 edition notably hosted talks on CSR strategies in the packaging sector (source: maghrebemergent.news).

### Awards and accolades

The **Djaz''Innov** competition rewards the most innovative initiatives for the Algerian agri-food industry. From among the shortlisted projects, a jury of independent experts awards gold, silver and bronze medals, as well as a Jury''s Favourite prize and a Special Jury prize, during the official opening ceremony.

2026 winners (source: agro-media.fr):

- **Gold medal:** Goglio, "Fres-co System+" (packaging)
- **Silver medal:** Acinox, "Caniveau Hygienic Design" (hygiene and safety)
- **Bronze medal:** Selected Performance Ingredients, "Premium Gummies Formulations" (ingredients)
- **Jury''s Favourite:** Climatec Boulanaache, "Groupe frigorifique silencieux" (process)
- **Special Jury prize:** Promec srl, "Synchrojet Linear Combiblock" (process)

## On site: what you need to know

The trade show is held at the Palais des expositions des Pins maritimes (Safex), located to the east of Algiers, close to Houari Boumédiène airport. Access and accommodation to be arranged from Algiers.

Specific to the show:

- **Opening hours:** 10 am to 6 pm from Sunday to Tuesday, 10 am to 5 pm on Wednesday (source: djazagro.com - to be verified before publication, site returning a 403 error when this was written).
- **Visitor badge:** prior online registration on the official website, reserved for professional visitors.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with Comexposium or its Promosalons representative, choose your positioning among the zones (equipment and process, ingredients, packaging, bakery and pastry).
- 6 months out: prepare your stand and product demonstrations, submit an entry to the Djaz''Innov competition.
- 3 months out: organise import logistics (customs, shipping of equipment) and the commercial brief on the Algerian and North African markets.
- 6 weeks out: confirm buyer meetings and the Agora des Experts schedule.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free pre-registration on the official website with proof of professional activity.
- Target the international pavilions according to your needs (processing equipment, packaging solutions, ingredients).
- Follow the Agora des Experts and the Djaz''Innov awards ceremony to spot the prize-winning innovations.

## How the show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
   { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
   { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
   { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
   { "edition": "24th: 2027", "visiteurs": "to come", "exposants": "to come" },
