### Trajectory analysis

EGAST is a **senior regional trade show**: 40 years in 2026, 20 editions held, solid roots in the Grand Est and well-managed cross-border reach (Germany, Belgium, Switzerland). The model is stable: biennial in even years, 4 days, Parc Expo Strasbourg-Wacken, a strictly trade audience on a free badge.

The 2026 edition marked a qualitative step up on three fronts: a **denser programme** (12 competitions, including the new Inter-CFA and Meilleur Flan Pâtissier Grand Est formats), a **stronger CSR stance** (Charity Gala Dinner in aid of the Restos du Cœur, -80% carpeting, Régis Marcon''s patronage centred on transmission), and a **broader wine ecosystem** with the arrival of the European Red & Rosé Wine Contest alongside the Mondial des Vins Blancs Strasbourg.

The challenge for 2028: to hit the 25,000+ visitor target while maintaining a deliberately regional stance (no shift towards a national format like Sirha Lyon or Equip''Hotel Paris). The recurring pairing with the international wine competitions at the Palais de la Musique et des Congrès consolidates Strasbourg''s place as the Grand Est''s hospitality, catering and oenology rendezvous, without direct competition from the major national trade shows, which are held in odd years.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='egast-strasbourg';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='E-learning and digital training trade show. LMS platforms, learning content, serious games and virtual reality.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Leading digital training trade show in France, organised by **Infopromotions** (Weyou group) under the direction of **Florence de Courtenay**.
- Next edition: **9 and 10 June 2027** at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), opening hours 09:00-18:30 (day 1) and 09:00-18:00 (day 2).
- Figures announced by the organiser in 2025: **9,140 visitors** (+15% vs 2024) and nearly **250 exhibitors**. Organiser figures, not OJS-audited.
- Co-located with [Solutions RH](/salons/solutions-rh), Digital Workplace, Documation & iExpo and the Forum Cybersécurité, Cloud, IA: shared ticketing and a unified visitor journey. The brand has also historically gravitated around [Learning Technologies](/salons/learning-technologies-paris) within the digital learning market.
- Audience: training departments, L&D managers, HR directors and buyers of e-learning solutions, focused on LMS, authoring, bespoke content and assessment.
- Editorial highlight: the **Trophées du Digital Learning**, an awards ceremony built into the trade show (120+ entries submitted in 2025).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

LMS and LXP platform publishers, authoring tools, bespoke e-learning content production studios, assessment and certification players, virtual classroom and immersive training providers. The trade show addresses both large accounts and SMEs in the process of digitising their internal training.

### Notable exhibitors

The full list of exhibitors and the floor plan are published on the official page: [Innovative Learning exhibitors](https://www.innovative-learning.fr/exposants/). The positioning highlights platform publishers and content studios, the core target of French digital learning.

### Visitor quality

The announced visitorship is dominated by training decision-makers: training and L&D managers, HR directors, digital learning project leaders, solution buyers. The organiser claims 9,140 visitors in 2025 (+15% vs 2024), an in-house figure not audited by OJS, to be read as an order of magnitude of audience rather than a certified volume. Co-location with Solutions RH and the other trade shows in the HR-digital cluster mechanically broadens the pool of decision-makers present on site.

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The organiser announces more than 90 conferences and workshops with free access included in the visitor badge, spread across the two days. The programme covers the sector''s trends: AI applied to training, mobile learning, measuring the impact of solutions, instructional design. The detailed programme for the 2027 edition is published in the run-up to the trade show on the official website.

### Prizes and awards

The **Trophées du Digital Learning** reward the best digital training projects and solutions each year, with a ceremony built into the trade show. The organiser reports more than 120 entries submitted for the 2025 edition. The winners'' list can be consulted on the dedicated website [t-dl.fr](https://www.t-dl.fr).

### Community & networks

The trade show brings together the French digital learning community: publishers, studios, training departments and the HR ecosystem. Co-location with [Solutions RH](/salons/solutions-rh), Digital Workplace, Documation & iExpo and the Forum Cybersécurité, Cloud, IA makes it an annual meeting point for the HR-digital cluster at Porte de Versailles, in line with a digital learning market historically also driven by [Learning Technologies](/salons/learning-technologies-paris).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) page.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates and hours:** 9 and 10 June 2027, 09:00-18:30 on the first day and 09:00-18:00 on the second.
- **Hall:** no hall number is confirmed on the 2027 practical-information page at this stage, the website only mentions Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. To be checked on the official floor plan in the run-up to the trade show.
- **Visitor badge:** online registration, shared ticketing with the co-located trade shows (Solutions RH, Digital Workplace, Documation & iExpo, Forum Cybersécurité Cloud IA), a single badge for the entire cluster.
- **Conferences:** free-access programme included in the visitor badge.

## How much it costs to exhibit

