The trade show has undergone a recent rebrand: from eLearning Expo, the historic brand of French digital learning, to Innovative Learning by eLearning Expo, which retains the heritage while broadening the scope. The momentum announced by the organiser is one of growth, from around 7,950 claimed visitors in 2024 to 9,140 in 2025 (+15%), on a base of roughly 250 exhibitors. These volumes are in-house figures not audited by OJS, to be read as a trend rather than certified data. The positioning now rests largely on co-location with Solutions RH and the Porte de Versailles HR-digital cluster, which pools the decision-maker audience and places Innovative Learning within an annual event broader than digital learning alone.', seo_title_en='Innovative Learning eLearning Expo 2027 Paris | Agoris', seo_description_en='Innovative Learning by eLearning Expo 2027: 9-10 June in Paris Porte de Versailles. Nearly 250 exhibitors, 9,140 visitors announced in 2025, co-located with Solutions RH.' WHERE slug='elearning-expo-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International trade fair for renewable energy. Solar, wind, biomass, hydrogen and storage for the energy transition in the Mediterranean.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- EnerGaïa is the renewable energy forum for the greater south of France, in Montpellier. The 2025 edition brought together 22,600 participants and 560+ exhibitors (source: energaia.fr).
- Covers the entire renewables sector across 5 markets (energy, building, agriculture, industry, mobility) → a cross-cutting renewables trade show with a Mediterranean focus.
- 120 round tables and pitches per edition → a strong conference component, geared towards local acceptance and the rollout of projects.
- Organised by SPL Occitanie Events (ISO 20121 certified), backed by the Occitanie Region.
- Next edition: 9-10 December 2026, Parc des Expositions de Montpellier.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The entire renewable energy value chain: developers, energy companies, engineering consultancies, equipment manufacturers, local authorities and industrial players, across the energy, building, agriculture, industry and mobility markets.

### Notable exhibitors

Full list of exhibitors on the official website: [energaia.fr](https://www.energaia.fr).

### Quality of attendees

- 22,600 participants in 2025 across 7 halls (source: energaia.fr)
- Target audience: project developers, public and private decision-makers, local authorities, industrial players

## Events & community

### Conference programme

120 round tables and pitches per edition. Headline theme for 2025: local acceptance of renewable energy projects. Recurring themes: collective self-consumption, solar heat, geothermal energy, employment and training.

### Awards & accolades

EnerGaïa Innovation Trophies: annual list of winners on energaia.fr (Innovation Trophy Winners page).

### Community & networks

A forum backed by the Occitanie Region, with the economic development agency AD''OCC as a partner for engaging international decision-makers.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue:** Parc des Expositions de Montpellier.
- **Visitor badge:** free, reserved for professionals, registration required.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: quote on request from SPL Occitanie Events. As EnerGaïa offers shared regional pavilions, lower-cost formats are available for local players.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: request a quote from the organiser, book your space by market.
- 6 months out: stand plan, application for the Innovation Trophies.
- 3 months out: accreditations, accommodation.
- 6 weeks out: delivery of materials, final briefing.

### For the decision-maker attending

- Free professional badge upon registration.
- Allow 1 to 2 days: 5 markets across 7 halls, target the round tables in advance.

## CSR policy & initiatives

EnerGaïa sets out its commitments on its [An eco-responsible event](https://www.energaia.fr/un-evenement-eco-responsable/) page: an ISO 20121 certified organiser, a reuse partnership (Mas Réemploi) and six commitments to reducing the event''s footprint.

## How the trade show has evolved

