### Trajectory analysis

EnerGaïa has grown strongly over recent editions (from ~22,000 to 22,600 participants, 560+ exhibitors in 2025), driven by the acceleration of renewable energy projects in the greater south. One to watch for 2026: the impact of the municipal elections context on local acceptance, a central theme of the forum.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='energaia-montpellier';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Building energy efficiency day, Lyon edition. RE2020, energy renovation and decarbonisation of buildings.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- EnerJ-meeting Lyon is the day dedicated to the energy and environmental efficiency of buildings, the Lyon edition of the Paris event. A **Batiactu Groupe** event.
- Next edition: **Tuesday 15 September 2026** at the **Palais de la Bourse** (Place de la Bourse, 69002 Lyon), from 8:30 am to 6:30 pm. 4th Lyon edition.
- A condensed single-day format: 5 conference rooms, around one hundred announced speakers and an exhibition space of more than 1,000 m².
- Targets announced for 2026: around 2,000 decision-makers (project owners, project managers, government bodies, industry players, start-ups) and 100 leading exhibitors.
- 2026 theme: "BÂTIR 2050: SOBRIÉTÉ - EFFICACITÉ - DÉCARBONATION - ADAPTATION - DÉSIRABILITÉ".

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Industry players in climate engineering, building envelopes, bio-sourced materials, ventilation, solar and control systems; publishers and suppliers of technical services; sustainable construction start-ups. The exhibition is structured around solutions for sobriety, energy efficiency and the decarbonisation of buildings, targeting an audience of prescription decision-makers (project owners, project managers, government bodies).

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [lyon.enerj-meeting.com/exposants](https://lyon.enerj-meeting.com/exposants). Among the 50 industry players confirmed to date for 2026: Atlantic, GRDF, Wilo France, The Watch Dog (Platinum exhibitors); Chaffoteaux-Ariston-ELCO, Airzone, EDF, Saint-Gobain, Schüco, Hitachi Cooling & Heating, Wienerberger, K.Line, Kömmerling, Sobre Energie, Sylvania Group (Gold exhibitors); Distech Controls, Orange Business, Signify, Sika, SMABTP, Thermokon, Veka (early exhibitors).

### Audience quality

- A day positioned around prescription decision-makers: project owners, project managers, government bodies, industry players and start-ups
- An announced target of 2,000 decision-makers for 2026
- A matchmaking service connecting visitors with the prescription managers of the industry players present

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The format is built around **5 conference rooms** and around one hundred announced speakers, organised around the analysis of regulations and feedback from experience (REX). On-demand (VOD) access to all conferences is offered after the event. The detailed 2026 programme is announced as "coming soon" on the official website.

### Community and networks

The Lyon edition benefits from the high patronage of Mr Emmanuel Macron, President of the Republic, and the support of the Ministry of Ecological Transition, the Ministry of Territorial Cohesion, ADEME, the CSTB and the Plan Bâtiment Durable. It is also backed by more than 80 partners from the sector, with a network of institutional and professional players in building and energy across the region (press relays and sector calendars: Qualit''EnR, Cluster Eco-Bâtiment, Cerema).

## On site: what you need to know

The trade show takes place at the Palais de la Bourse, Place de la Bourse, 69002 Lyon (the peninsula, 2nd arrondissement).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 15 September 2026, from 8:30 am to 6:30 pm.
- **Access:** metro line A, alight at Cordeliers (direct access); from line B, alight at Charpennes and take line A. Rhônexpress from the airport towards Vaulx-en-Velin La Soie, then connect to metro line A. Cordeliers and Grolée car parks nearby. Limited-traffic zone on the peninsula: barriers lowered from 6 am to 1 pm, prior registration required for vehicle access in the afternoon.
- **Catering:** snacks available throughout the day, with organic and local produce.

## Planning your visit

### For exhibitors

- 9 months before: make contact with Batiactu Groupe, choose your positioning (industry players, start-ups, bio-sourced products, services and technical consultancies).
- 6 months before: prepare your stand and demonstrations, in line with the trade show''s low-carbon commitments (timber construction, plastic-free).
- 3 months before: activate the matchmaking service with prescription managers.
- 6 weeks before: confirm appointments with targeted decision-makers (project owners, project managers).

### For decision-maker visitors

- Pre-register at lyon.enerj-meeting.com (named badge reserved for building professionals).
- Single-day format: plan your conference itinerary in advance, as the programme is published as the trade show approaches.
- Anticipate vehicle access on the peninsula (limited-traffic zone in the afternoon) or favour public transport.
- Take advantage of on-demand (VOD) access to the conferences after the event to catch up on any sessions you missed.

## CSR policy & initiatives

EnerJ-meeting has pursued a stated low-carbon approach since its earliest editions and publishes a record of its footprint. Commitments relayed for the 2026 edition: stands built from timber, no plastic and short-circuit food sourcing (organic and local snacks). The trade show features an "Our low-carbon commitments" section on its official website.

The detailed figures on the carbon footprint and the environmental certifications of the Palais de la Bourse are not publicly verifiable to date on an accessible dedicated page (source: lyon.enerj-meeting.com).

## How the trade show has evolved

