### Trajectory analysis

Created by Batiactu Groupe, EnerJ-meeting has established itself as the annual gathering for the environmental performance of buildings, in a short, intensive format combining an exhibition with technical conferences over a single day. The 2026 edition, the tenth of its kind, brought together 4,100 professionals at the Carrousel du Louvre and generated 27,300 business connections, with an audience strongly oriented towards prescription (technical design offices, architects, local authorities). The 11th edition, on 23 February 2027 at the Carrousel du Louvre, extends this positioning, while the regional editions (Lyon, Marseille, Nantes) broaden the event''s territorial coverage.', seo_title_en='EnerJ-meeting Paris 2027: environmental performance of buildings', seo_description_en='EnerJ-meeting Paris 2027 takes place on 23 February at the Carrousel du Louvre. A day dedicated to the energy and environmental performance of buildings: 4,100 professionals, technical conferences and exhibitor villages.' WHERE slug='enerj-meeting-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The global meeting place for the automotive aftermarket, repair and mobility services, at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles on a biennial cycle. Record-breaking 2025 edition (50th anniversary): 91,500 visitors (+17%), 1,400 exhibitors (55% international from 35 countries), 100,000 sq m across 5 halls.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Equip Auto Paris 2027 is the global meeting place for the automotive aftermarket, repair and mobility services, scheduled from Tuesday 12 to Saturday 16 October 2027 at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), on a biennial cycle held in odd-numbered years (no 2026 edition in Paris).
- Record-breaking 2025 edition for the 50th anniversary: 91,500 trade visitors (+17% vs 78,280 in 2022), 1,400 exhibitors (55% international from 35 countries, 48% first-time exhibitors), 100,000 sq m across 5 halls, 18% international visitors from 118 countries, under the patronage of the President of the Republic.
- Trade show operated by Comexposium, jointly owned by FIEV (equipment manufacturers), FEDA (distributors) and CNPA Mobilians (automotive services), chaired by Philippe Baudin since April 2019.
- 14 areas of expertise covered (parts, workshop equipment, paint and bodywork, energy, IT, washing, tyres, recycling, training) plus a dedicated Circular Economy Village focused on reuse and reconditioned parts.
- The Pack Business One 2027 is listed at €4,017 excl. VAT for a fitted 9 sq m stand with Digital Community membership included, with early bird terms of a 30% deposit for commitments made before 31 December 2026, rising to 50% from 1 January 2027.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A structuring B2B trade show for the aftermarket and mobility sector. Full coverage of the services value chain: replacement equipment manufacturers, parts distributors and platforms, workshop tooling makers, paint and bodywork brands, energy operators and charging providers, DMS and diagnostics software publishers, washing equipment manufacturers, tyre makers, recycling and circular economy players, training organisations. Strictly professional audience: agent networks, independent repairers (MRA), car centres, independent and networked body shops, service dealerships, fleet managers, technical inspection, traders.

### Notable exhibitors (2025, 2027 baseline)

**Equipment and systems**: PHINIA via its Delphi brand (double Grand Prix in 2025 for its H2ICE hydrogen direct injection system manufactured at the Blois site, winner of the Innovation award and Special CSR Prize), Valeo (Grand Prix 2025 for its remanufactured DQ250 dual clutch), Schaeffler, BorgWarner, ZF, Bosch, Continental, NGK.

**Diagnostics and workshop equipment**: MAHA with the MAIA autonomous technical inspection robot (Grand Prix 2025, automated checking of lighting, geometry, ADAS), Carool with the ScanDrive tyre diagnostics bench requiring no vehicle immobilisation (Grand Prix 2025 for maintenance), Texa, Snap-on, Bosch Diagnostics, Hella Gutmann.

**Distribution and services**: Autodistribution, Alliance Automotive Group, Doyen Auto, Précisium, Top Garage, AD, Eurorepar Car Service, Speedy, Midas, the Norauto network, Feu Vert pro.

### Retention rate

A loyal core of long-standing exhibitors going back several decades (FIEV equipment manufacturers, FEDA distributors, Mobilians networks), with measured structural renewal in 2025: **48% first-time exhibitors**, reflecting the mass arrival of new players in electric mobility, the circular economy and digital. The 55% international split confirms the show''s position as a European aftermarket hub.

### Visitor quality

100% qualified professionals (named badges issued on proof of status). A mix of decision-makers: network technical departments, car centre buyers, heads of independent repair SMEs, fleet prescribers, trainers and schools, importers and exporters. Strong international qualification in 2025: 18% of foreign visitors from 118 countries, including structured delegations from North Africa, the Middle East, sub-Saharan Africa and Asia. The show is positioned as a venue for purchasing and signing annual contracts.

## Events & community

### Conference programme

Themed conference stages covering the 14 areas of expertise (independent repair, bodywork, mobility energy, technical inspection, tyres, recycling, IT and data, training, washing, paint, workshop equipment, parts and services, accessories). Technical workshops led by partner training organisations and live media stages. The detailed 2027 programme is published by the organisers in the run-up to the show.

### Awards & accolades

**Grands Prix Internationaux de l''Innovation Automobile**, created in 1985, celebrating their 40th anniversary in 2025 with 166 entries submitted and a jury of 100 specialist French and international journalists. 2025 winners:

- **PHINIA / Delphi**: H2ICE hydrogen direct injection system, winner of the Original Equipment award and the **Special CSR Prize** (double accolade), produced at the Blois site
- **Carool ScanDrive**: tyre diagnostics bench requiring no immobilisation, maintenance winner
- **MAHA MAIA**: autonomous automated technical inspection robot, technical inspection winner
- **Valeo DQ250**: remanufactured dual clutch, circular economy winner

The 2027 winners are announced by the organisers ahead of the show, with the awards presented during the week.

### Satellite events

**Equip Auto On Tour**, a touring format launched in 2024 with 3 confirmed stops: Montpellier on 8 June 2024, Reims on 29 June 2024, Rennes on 28 September 2024 (around 100 exhibitors and 1,000 professionals per stop, a regional local format). **Equip Auto Lyon Eurexpo**, an annual spin-off launched in 2023 (605 exhibitors and 25,500 visitors over 3 days for the inaugural edition), alternating with Paris. **Équipement Côte d''Ivoire** confirmed by FIEV for 26 to 28 November 2026, an African satellite event.

### Community & networks

Three associations own the show: **FIEV** (Fédération des Industries des Équipements pour Véhicules), **FEDA** (Fédération de la Distribution Automobile) and **CNPA Mobilians** (the professional organisation for automotive services). **Comexposium** operates the show. **Philippe Baudin** has chaired Equip Auto since April 2019 (then Managing Director of Schaeffler France and Vice-President Aftermarket at FIEV). Digital Community membership is included in the exhibitor pack: B2B matchmaking beforehand, contact tracking and post-show follow-up.

### What''s new in 2027

A benchmark 2027 edition building on the record 2025 results (50th anniversary, 91,500 visitors, 1,400 exhibitors). The **Circular Economy Village** is retained and expanded, focused on reconditioned parts, component reuse and the decarbonisation of the aftermarket. A strengthening of the mobility energy area is expected (charging, hydrogen, NGV, biofuels). A CSRD-aligned CSR programme with a target of **minus 30% carbon footprint vs 2022**: shared mobility for teams, responsible catering menus, removal of single-use plastic, eco-designed stands and real-time carbon assessment display. The detailed 2027 programme is to be confirmed.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), 100,000 sq m across 5 halls used in 2025
- **Transport access**: Metro L12 (Porte de Versailles), L8 (Balard). Trams T2 and T3a. RER C (Pont du Garigliano). October, trade show week: allow 30 to 45 minutes from central Paris by public transport.
- **Parking**: On-site and nearby car parks, heavily saturated mid-week. Favour public transport or park-and-ride sites on the outskirts. Shared mobility encouraged by the organisers as part of the CSR programme.
- **Accommodation**: The 15th arrondissement (Convention, Vaugirard, Balard) as a priority. Book 3 to 4 months ahead, as Equip Auto is one of the largest Paris trade shows in October (91,500 professionals concentrated over 5 days in 2025).
- **Opening hours & tickets 2027**: Tuesday 12 to Saturday 16 October, a strictly professional show requiring a named badge. Visitor registration online on the organisers'' official website from spring 2027.
- **Services**: Multiple catering points across the venue (responsible menus), VIP exhibitor areas, an international press room, live media stages, an official app, cloakrooms, left-luggage facilities and interpreting services for international delegations.

## What it costs to exhibit

