## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- M-18 (spring 2026): get in touch with Comexposium, position within an area of expertise, choose the hall, negotiate floor space
- M-12 (October 2026): commit before 31 December 2026 to benefit from the early bird rate (30% deposit vs 50% from 1 January 2027), enter the Grands Prix Internationaux de l''Innovation Automobile
- M-9 (January 2027): validate the scenographic concept, brief the agency and stand builder, plan On Tour participation if relevant
- M-6 (April 2027): final plans, order stand construction, logistics for materials and demonstrators
- M-3 (July 2027): team accreditations, accommodation, commercial brief, scheduling of B2B meetings via the Digital Community, press kits
- M-6 weeks (September 2027): delivery of materials, final team brief, activation of media campaigns and client invitations

### For the decision-making visitor

- Register as soon as 2027 professional ticketing opens (spring 2027): a free or preferentially priced named badge depending on the organiser''s schedule
- Favour Tuesday 12 or Wednesday 13 October for structuring supplier meetings, keeping Thursday for conferences and innovation stages
- Prepare your meetings via Equip Auto''s Digital Community beforehand (B2B matchmaking and built-in messaging)
- For international delegations: get in touch with the interpreting services and the areas dedicated to partner countries
- Allow 2 full days to cover the 14 areas of expertise and the Circular Economy Village

