### Trajectory analysis

Equip''Hôtel has established itself over several decades as Paris''s major biennial hospitality event. The 2024 edition ("Let''s dare!") confirmed a mature format: 1,200 exhibitors, 40% international from 40 countries, ~80,000 trade visitors from 114 countries. **The move to 4 days in 2026** (vs 5 in 2024) is the most interesting signal: RX France is tightening the show around the busiest professional days, while broadening the depth of its programme through the **HITEC Paris** co-location (1st European edition, 5 November 2026). The **"Plural Hospitality"** theme consolidates an editorial line begun with "Committed Hospitality" (2022) and "Let''s dare!" (2024): a path that embraces a gradual build-up around CSR and responsible innovation, without breaking from the brand image of its core hotel and catering audience.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='equip-hotel-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for windows, closures and solar protection. Joinery, glazing, blinds, shutters and architectural metalwork.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- EquipBaie-Métalexpo is no longer a standalone trade show: since 2024 it has been integrated into the Mondial du Bâtiment as the "Équipbaie-Métalexpo by Batimat" sector (source: Batiactu, Le Moniteur) → exhibiting here means having a presence within Batimat in the window, closure and façade sector, not at a dedicated trade show.
- 388 exhibitors confirmed in 2024 for the Équipbaie-Métalexpo sector (source: Mondial du Bâtiment press release, reported by Le Moniteur) → a sector well represented at the major building industry gathering.
- No attendance figure of its own: only the overall attendance of the 2024 Mondial du Bâtiment is published (more than 135,000 participants, across all trade shows, source: L''Écho de la baie) → do not attribute it to EquipBaie alone.
- Next edition: 28 September to 1 October 2026, Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, within the Mondial du Bâtiment, organised by RX France (source: Batirama).

## Who exhibits

