UPDATE salons SET description_en='Wood industry trade show. Machinery, tooling, timber materials, industrial joinery and timber construction for professionals.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Eurobois 2026 brought together 30,500 professionals and 600 exhibiting brands at Eurexpo Lyon (source: batiweb.com), up on 2024 (29,363 visitors, 523 exhibitors) (source: architecturebois.fr) → it is the benchmark trade show for the timber construction sector in France, with confirmed growth.
- 20% international visitors in 2026, 31% international exhibitors in 2024 (sources: elcia.com, architecturebois.fr) → the most internationalised regional construction trade show in France, the timber sector having a marked European dimension (Germany, Austria, the Netherlands).
- Strong growth by visitor segment in 2024: joinery +31%, fit-out +78%, framing +114%, architecture +139% (source: architecturebois.fr) → Eurobois is broadening its base beyond the "furniture-machinery-tooling" core towards timber construction and architectural specification.
- Organised by GL Events in Lyon (Eurexpo).
- **Next edition: 1-4 February 2028** (biennial rhythm, even years, source: eurobois-events.com).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers across the timber sector: machine-tool makers, timber construction suppliers, wood-energy, furniture, fit-out, digitalisation solutions for joinery workshops. Strong international presence (31% in 2024), with a notable weight of manufacturers from Central and Germanic Europe (source: architecturebois.fr).

### Notable exhibitors

Exhibitor list on the official website: [eurobois-events.com](https://www.eurobois-events.com).

### Visitor quality

- 30,500 professionals in 2026 (source: batiweb.com)
- Around 20% international in 2026 (source: elcia.com)
- Target profile: manufacturers, tradespeople (joiners, carpenters), architects, distributors, training bodies, timber prescribers (source: elcia.com)

## Events & community

### Conference programme

Main conference space "Wood Arena". 2026 themes: reuse of timber materials, standards (RE 2020 and beyond), digital fit-out, workshop digitalisation (source: architecturebois.fr).

### Community & networks

Confirmed industry partners: **EVOLIS** (equipment manufacturers). Presence of FIBOIS ("Bois Français & Design" exhibition). Eurobois Awards jury including CAPEB AURA members (source: eurobois-events.com/qui-sommes-nous). Specialist press: Architecture Bois, L''Atelier Bois, Forestopic, Le Courrier du Meuble.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** free with a badge or invitation obtained from an exhibitor; €40 incl. VAT without (source: elcia.com).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published: quote on request from GL Events. As Eurobois is a specialist timber-sector trade show with a strong international component (31% international exhibitors in 2024), the per-m² ranges are likely to sit between regional trade shows (Nordbat, Artibat) and national trade shows (Batimat).

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: request a quote from GL Events, book a space.
- 6 months out: order the stand from a builder.
- 3 months out: finalise the stand plan, build a timber-sector-focused pitch (provenance, PEFC/FSC certifications, RE 2020).
- 6 weeks out: accreditations, accommodation, equipment logistics.
- 1 week out: final brief, equipment check, stand delivery.

### For the professional visitor

- Obtain a free badge from an exhibitor or via the official website (€40 without an invitation, source: elcia.com).
- Identify the priority conferences at the Wood Arena, with the programme published in advance.
- Allow 1 to 2 days depending on the areas targeted (machine tools, timber construction, fit-out, furniture, design).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

CSR is at the heart of Eurobois''s positioning: timber is a low-carbon construction material, and the 2026 programme highlights the reuse of timber materials and RE 2020 compliance (source: architecturebois.fr). Sustainable forest management certifications (PEFC, FSC) are a structuring argument for exhibitors in the sector.

