### Trajectory analysis

A trade show created in 1968 on the initiative of the DGA to showcase French naval equipment, it became **Euronaval** in 1994 when it opened to foreign exhibitors and **SOGENA** (a GICAN subsidiary and event operator) was created. The show was held at the **Le Bourget exhibition park** from its creation until the 2022 edition. The 2024 edition marked the **move to Villepinte** (Hall 6), forced by the requisitioning of the Le Bourget site for the Paris 2024 Olympic Games and the modernisation works that followed.

The 2024 results structurally validate the new venue: +20% visitors vs 2022, greater capacity, broader catering, and direct RER B access from Paris and Paris-CDG (vs the more constrained access at Le Bourget). The 2026 edition consolidates this positioning with an overhaul of the EURONAVAL Awards around three operational axes (Engage / Transform / Sustain) that mirror the multi-domain doctrine of modern navies, and a structured pre-show conference programme with NATO, the Portuguese university hub FEUP and the think tanks Entanglement and S2IX. The 30th edition cements Euronaval as the European counterweight to competing shows (DSEI Maritime in London, Sea Air Space in Washington).', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='euronaval-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for packaging, materials handling and industrial process. Solutions for packing, internal logistics and automation.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Europack Euromanut CFIA** trade show was rebranded **Prod&Pack** in 2020-2021 by GL Events Exhibitions. The co-location with CFIA (Carrefour des Fournisseurs de l''Industrie Agroalimentaire) was discontinued at that point (sources: voxlog.fr, agro-media.fr).
- **Biennial** trade show: no 2026 edition. The 3rd Prod&Pack edition ran from 18 to 20 November 2025, and the **4th edition is announced for 16 to 18 November 2027** at Eurexpo Lyon, Halls 6 and 7 (source: prodandpack.com).
- 2025 edition (most recent reference): 15,931 visitors and more than 750 exhibitors (+20% vs 2023) (sources: prodandpack.com, agro-media.fr).
- Positioning as the "**packaged-product ecosystem**": production process and equipment, packaging and packing, materials handling, end-of-line, recycling and reuse. A trade show open to all industrial sectors (food, chemicals, cosmetics, pharma, e-commerce) (source: prodandpack.com).
- Organiser: **GLEX Industrie**, a subsidiary of GL Events Exhibitions (source: prodandpack.com/practical-informations).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers of packaging and packing machinery, suppliers of production equipment, makers of packaging materials (wood, plastic, glass, metal, paper and board), materials-handling and intralogistics service providers, and players in reuse and recycling.

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is on the official website: [prodandpack.com](https://www.prodandpack.com/). Confirmed at the 2025 edition: Groupe Lacroix (wood and board packaging), Pandobac (reusable crates and traceability), Groupe Emballage Technologies (ET-Pack), Flowcrete (industrial packaging flooring), Murin et Fouillat, PBH France, CS Pack, B2B France, Sidel (sources: groupe-lacroix.com, pandobac.com, et-pack.com, prodandpack.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

- A predominantly French professional visitor base, with strong regional roots in Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes
- Industrial buyers, packaging managers, production directors, R&D
- 15,931 visitors in 2025 (figure announced by the organiser, no published OJS certification)

## Events & community

### Conference programme

2025 themes carried over to 2027: reduction, reuse, recycling, traceability, AI applied to industry, industrial performance, innovation. More than 40 conferences announced (source: prodandpack.com/programme).

### Signature spaces

- **800 sq m showroom** with 5 working mini-factories presenting packaging materials (wood, plastic, glass, metal, paper and board) (source: agro-media.fr, lyon-entreprises.com)
- **Allée des Tendances Durables**: an immersive walkthrough on eco-design, created with designer Fabrice Peltier (source: agro-media.fr)
- **Village du Réemploi** in partnership with Réseau Vrac & Réemploi (around twenty companies)
- **Village IA**: demonstrations of AI applied to industrial design, sustainability and distribution (new for 2025)
- **La Pépinière**: a space for start-ups and incubators
- **Forum des Fédérations**: a round table of trade bodies, federations and institutions
- **Assises Nationales du Réemploi des Emballages** (3rd edition in 2025)

(Sources: agro-media.fr, prodandpack.com/programme-2025, lyon-entreprises.com)

### Community and networks

Official partner federations (partners page, prodandpack.com): **Elipso** (plastic packaging trade body), **Polyvia**, **Citeo**, **French Fab**, **CNE**, **Alliance Carton Nature**, **Fédération Industries du Verre**, Réseau Vrac & Réemploi (Village du Réemploi and Assises Nationales). Sources: prodandpack.com/partenaires.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon) listing.

Specific to this trade show:

- **Hall location:** Halls 6 and 7, Eurexpo Lyon.
- **Opening hours (2025 edition, to be confirmed for 2027):** Tuesday and Wednesday 9 a.m.-6 p.m., Thursday 9 a.m.-5 p.m. (source: prodandpack.com/practical-informations).
- **Visitor badge:** free with pre-registration via [pass.prodandpack.com](https://pass.prodandpack.com/).

## What it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: requests to take part go through the GL Events platform ([exposant.gl-events.com/prod-2025](https://exposant.gl-events.com/prod-2025/inscription)). The 2025 edition sold out with +20% more exhibitors than 2023, so it is advisable to submit a request 12 to 18 months before the target edition. Figures not publicly available.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- T-18 months: make contact with GL Events and request a booking (rapid saturation observed in 2025).
- T-12 months: choose a position among the 4 zones (packaging and packing machinery, production equipment, materials and containers, end-of-line and logistics).
- T-9 months: apply to the themed spaces (Village du Réemploi, Village IA, La Pépinière) to amplify press visibility.
- T-6 months: prepare live demonstrations (the 800 sq m showroom mini-factories have historically been the most visited).
- T-3 months: activate the partner federation channels (Elipso, Polyvia, Citeo, Adelphe) for upstream communications.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free online pre-registration of the badge at prodandpack.com.
- Target the live demonstrations in the 800 sq m showroom (often crowded in the afternoon).
- Plan the PPWR and AI conferences in advance.
- Allow at least 1 full day to cover the 2 halls.
- Access via the T5 tram or a shuttle from central Lyon, or Rhônexpress plus shuttle from Saint-Exupéry.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Information not available: as at the date of this listing, Prod&Pack does not publish a dedicated CSR commitments page for the organiser or for the trade show itself. The sustainability theme is handled editorially through the **Allée des Tendances Durables**, the **Village du Réemploi** and the **Assises Nationales du Réemploi des Emballages**, without a formalised public CSR policy for the trade show (source: agro-media.fr).

## How the trade show has evolved

