### Trajectory analysis

The 2020-2021 rebranding (Europack Euromanut CFIA to Prod&Pack) accompanied a strategic repositioning: dropping the CFIA co-location and broadening to all industrial sectors (beyond food alone). Volumes have remained stable at around 16,000 visitors across the old and new brands, but the number of exhibitors grew by 25% between 2023 and 2025 (+750 exhibitors), which saturated the halls and limited new registrations. The biennial rhythm (a shift in 2020 to one edition every 2 years) results from a deliberate trade-off to maintain a quality experience for exhibitors and visitors alike.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='europack-euromanut-lyon';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International trade show for land and air-land defence and security. The largest defence trade show in Europe.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Eurosatory 2026** is the **29th edition** of the world''s leading trade show for land and air-land defence and global security, from **15 to 19 June 2026** at [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte).
- A **biennial** trade show (even years), organised by **COGES Events**, a subsidiary of **[GICAT](/organisateurs/gicat)** (Groupement des Industries Françaises de Défense et de Sécurité Terrestres et Aéroterrestres). COGES Events is the event operator.
- The 2026 edition opens **Hall 4** and brings the exhibition space to more than **185,000 m²**, with a redesign of the demonstration zones (trench combat, 3D drone manoeuvres, close-quarters combat).
- 2026 targets communicated by the organiser: **2,300+ exhibitors** from **66 countries**, **42 national pavilions**, **330 official delegations**, **43,000+ visitors** from more than 150 countries, **450 speakers**, **120 conferences and round tables**.
- The 2026 programme is built around four themes announced by COGES: **multi-domain superiority** (cyber, space, AI, digital), **long-range combat and land manoeuvre with air mobility**, **global security and crisis management**, and **industrial resilience and a war economy**.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Eurosatory covers the whole of the land and air-land defence industry along with global security: land systems (armoured vehicles, artillery), soldier equipment, drones and robotics, C4ISR and communications, cyber defence, homeland security, ammunition, optronics, simulation, and MRO. The trade show brings together major prime contractors (Airbus Defence, Thales, KNDS, Nexter, MBDA, Dassault Aviation), equipment manufacturers, defence SMEs and mid-caps, deeptech start-ups (Eurosatory LAB) and government services.

### Notable exhibitors

The trade show, which is strictly reserved for professionals, hosts the leading French and international defence groups. The full list of exhibitors is published by the organiser on the 2026 exhibitors page of the official website: [eurosatory.com/en/exhibitors2026](https://www.eurosatory.com/en/exhibitors2026/). In 2024, 2,028 exhibitors from 61 countries were present, compared with 1,743 in 2022 (+16%).

### Visitor quality

A **strictly professional** trade show reserved for industry players, state authorities, armed and security forces, and accredited journalists. The 2024 edition brought together **355 official delegations** from **92 countries**, including chiefs of staff, ministers and senior institutional figures. Strong presence from the Defence and Interior ministerial offices, the DGA (Direction Générale de l''Armement) and the European Commission (Defence and Space).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2024 edition hosted **120 conferences** and more than **450 international speakers**. For 2026, COGES is announcing 120 round tables and 450 speakers. Confirmed 2026 speakers include **Catherine Vautrin** (Minister of the Armed Forces), **Patrick Pailloux** (Délégué Général pour l''Armement, DGA), **Andrius Kubilius** (European Commissioner for Defence & Space), **Lucas Philippe** (President of Interpol), as well as French, Belgian, British and Lithuanian military leaders.

### Awards & recognition

The **Concours Innovation GICAT** (official wording verbatim, organised by GICAT) recognises technologies that meet the operational needs of armed and security forces, across the fields of industrial start-ups, digital technologies (AI, cloud, quantum, space, cyber), electronics and robotics. Eurosatory also hosts the **Eurosatory Start-ups Challenge** (official wording): in 2024, more than **60 French and international start-ups** were present in the Eurosatory LAB (Hall 5A), with around twenty additional start-ups on the GICAT pavilion via the **GENERATE** programme (GICAT innovation accelerator).

### Satellite events

**Eurosatory LAB**: a space dedicated to start-ups and technology companies, a technology showcase for armed forces and institutional decision-makers. Official programme for 2026: more than 500 new solutions presented. **Live dynamic demonstrations** revamped for 2026: trench combat, 3D drone manoeuvres, close-quarters battle (CQB). **GENERATE** programme (GICAT accelerator).

### Community & networks

A global benchmark trade show for the land defence and security sector, Eurosatory brings together public procurement communities (DGA, foreign Defence ministries), industry players (the French defence technological and industrial base and allies), and armed and security forces. International specialist press coverage (Defense News, Janes, Air & Cosmos, Forces Opérations Magazine, Mer & Marine, La Tribune Défense). Official LinkedIn page: *Eurosatory*.

### What''s new in 2026

**Opening of Hall 4**, bringing the total space to **+185,000 m²**, making it the largest edition in the trade show''s history. Complete redesign of the **dynamic demonstration zones** (trench combat, 3D drone manoeuvres, CQB). A programme structured around the four themes: multi-domain superiority, long-range combat and mobility, global security, and the war economy. Target of **500+ new solutions** presented.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte), Halls 4, 5a, 5b and 6 plus outdoor dynamic demonstration zones. Hall 4 opening for 2026.
- **Transport access**: RER B, "Parc des Expositions" station (30 minutes from Gare du Nord, 8 minutes from Paris-CDG Airport). Direct metro/RER link from central Paris.
- **Parking**: 17,000 spaces available on site (Viparis figure).
- **Accommodation**: See the [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte) listing. In mid-June, hotel availability in Paris is very tight (summer festival, Roland-Garros has just finished, VivaTech the week before at Porte de Versailles). Book 4 to 6 months in advance.
- **Opening hours & badges**: Monday 15 to Thursday 18 June from 9am to 5pm, Friday 19 June from 9am to 3pm. **Access strictly reserved for professionals** (industry players, state authorities, armed and security forces, accredited journalists). Badge requests at eurosatory.mybadgeonline.com.
- **Services**: Business meeting zones, multiple catering options, press areas, Eurosatory LAB, outdoor demo zones.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with COGES Events, application file, location selection (Hall, space)
- 9 months out: application to the Concours Innovation GICAT, application to the Eurosatory LAB / GENERATE programme for start-ups
- 6 months out: stand brief, management of team accreditations (named professional badges only), requests for official delegation invitations
- 3 months out: logistics finalisation, meeting targeting via the business meetings platform, commercial demo brief
- 6 weeks out: B2B meeting scheduling, communications activation, team brief

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Professional badge request on the official platform (mandatory verification of professional profile, no general-public access)
- Identify priority industry players in advance (2,300+ exhibitors expected) via the official 2026 exhibitor list
- Allow at least 2 to 3 days to cover all the halls (4, 5a, 5b, 6) + dynamic demo zones + Eurosatory LAB
- The dynamic demonstrations (trench combat, 3D drones, CQB) run on a loop several times a day
- Main conferences: limited capacity, register in advance via the official programme

## CSR policy & initiatives

As of this listing''s date, Eurosatory does not publish a dedicated, structured "CSR commitments" page on its official website to the standards seen at comparable major trade shows. The trade show highlights its institutional grounding through GICAT and the Ministry of the Armed Forces, and the logistical streamlining of the Paris Nord Villepinte site (served by RER B, intermodal with Paris-CDG). This listing will be enriched as soon as a structured CSR section is published by COGES Events.

## How the trade show has evolved

