### Trajectory analysis

Eurosatory has shown steady growth since its move to Paris Nord Villepinte in 2002, with marked acceleration over the last two editions driven by the post-2022 geopolitical context (Ukraine, European rearmament, war economy). The 2024 edition (28th) broke all of the trade show''s historical records with 2,028 exhibitors and 75,000+ professional visitors, and the 29th edition in 2026 pushes the trajectory still further with the reopening of Hall 4 (+185,000 m² in total, the largest edition in history), 2,300+ exhibitors expected and 330 official delegations. The 2026 editorial positioning around the four themes (multi-domain, long-range combat, global security, war economy) reflects the agenda of the French Ministry of the Armed Forces and the European Commission (DG Defence & Space), with very high-level institutional mobilisation (Minister of the Armed Forces, DGA, European Commissioner for Defence). The start-up ecosystem (Eurosatory LAB, GICAT GENERATE programme) is taking on a growing role, reflecting the prominence of defence deeptech (military AI, drones, cyber, quantum) within the French and allied defence technological and industrial base.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='eurosatory-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Viticulture forum for technical and scientific exchange. Innovations in viticulture, oenology and wine marketing.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Euroviti is the **annual viticulture and oenology colloquium** organised by the [Institut Français de la Vigne et du Vin (IFV)](https://www.vignevin.com/conferences/euroviti/), through its Pôle Val de Loire Centre. It is a scientific and technical gathering, not a trade show with stands.
- The colloquium is held every January as part of the [SIVAL](/salons/sival-angers) trade show, at the Parc des Expositions d''Angers. The next occurrence is expected at SIVAL 2027, from 12 to 14 January 2027.
- Short format (one morning): the 2026 edition was held in the Salle Maine from 9.45 a.m. to 12.30 p.m., on the theme "Intra-varietal diversity in viticulture".
- Each edition addresses a single technical theme: intra-varietal diversity (2026), wines with no added sulphites (2025), integrated soil management (2024), resistant varieties (2022), vineyard decline and trunk diseases (2020).
- The proceedings of the main Euroviti editions since 2009 are available to download as PDFs on the IFV website.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

Euroviti is a thematic colloquium: each edition is built around a single technical subject, addressed over a morning of scientific presentations. The IFV mobilises its researchers and its research partners (notably INRAE) to share the most recent work with professionals across the sector.

Themes of recent editions: "Intra-varietal diversity in viticulture" (2026), "Wines with no added sulphites: how to make them?" (2025), "Integrated soil management in viticulture" (2024), "Resistant varieties, from creation to consumer" (2022), "Vineyard decline and trunk diseases" (2020). The theme of the 2027 edition will be published as SIVAL approaches (source: vignevin.com).

The proceedings of the main editions are put online as PDFs after each edition on vignevin.com.

### Community and networks

Euroviti is aimed at winegrowers, oenologists, cellar technicians, advisers and operators across the vine and wine sector. The colloquium is part of the vine and wine cluster of SIVAL, the trade show for specialised plant production that brings together each year in Angers the viticulture, arboriculture, market gardening, horticulture and seed sectors.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc des Expositions d''Angers](/lieux/parc-expo-angers).

Specific to the colloquium:

- **Format:** a one-morning colloquium. The 2026 edition was held in the Salle Maine from 9.45 a.m. to 12.30 p.m. (times and room to be reconfirmed for 2027 on vignevin.com).
- **Access:** as part of SIVAL, the trade show for specialised plant production. Registration for the colloquium and the programme are published in advance on the IFV website.
- **Proceedings:** the presentations from the main editions are put online as PDFs after the event on vignevin.com.

## Planning your visit

### For the professional

- Check the theme and programme of the upcoming edition on [vignevin.com/conferences/euroviti](https://www.vignevin.com/conferences/euroviti/), published a few weeks before SIVAL.
- Plan the morning of the colloquium within your SIVAL visiting schedule: the short format (one morning) combines with a tour of the exhibition aisles in the afternoon.
- To explore a past theme in more depth, download the proceedings of the available editions before your visit on vignevin.com.

## How the trade show has evolved

Euroviti is one of the oldest technical colloquia of the vine and wine sector in France: its proceedings have been documented since 2009 and it already existed under the aegis of ITV France (which became the IFV). Historically attached to [SITEVI](/salons/sitevi-montpellier) in Montpellier, the colloquium is today an annual fixture of SIVAL in Angers, organised by the Pôle Val de Loire Centre of the IFV. Each edition is devoted to a topical technical theme for the sector (varietal diversity, inputs, trunk diseases, soils, winemaking), making it a barometer of the scientific concerns of the moment rather than a commercial trade show. The theme and programme of the 2027 edition will be published as SIVAL approaches, from 12 to 14 January 2027.', seo_title_en='Euroviti 2027: IFV viticulture and oenology colloquium at SIVAL Angers', seo_description_en='Euroviti, the IFV''s annual viticulture and oenology colloquium, takes place in January at SIVAL in Angers. Programme, theme, format and history of the editions.' WHERE slug='euroviti-angers';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for the hospitality, catering and food-trade sectors of South-West France. Equipment, services and products for the café, hotel and restaurant industry.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Exp''Hôtel Bordeaux is the leading professional gathering for the Food & Hospitality sectors of South-West France, created and organised by **BEAM (Bordeaux Events And More)**, with the support of UMIH 33 and CMA Nouvelle-Aquitaine 33.
- A **biennial** trade show: the 7th edition was held from 23 to 25 November 2025 at the [Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux](/lieux/parc-des-expositions-de-bordeaux). The next edition has been announced for **21 to 23 November 2027**.
- 2025 results: **19,000 professionals** and **350 exhibitors** across three days, with 140 Michelin-starred chefs and MOF (Meilleurs Ouvriers de France) and 14 trade competitions.
- The offering is organised around five worlds: Food and Cuisine, Décor-Design and Fit-Out, New Technologies, Services, and Vehicles-Mobility.
- Official strapline: "Source, find inspiration, share".

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Equipment manufacturers and suppliers for the food trades, café, hotel and restaurant furniture and fit-out, digital solutions and service technologies, food and beverage wholesalers, professional vehicles and mobility, and service providers for cafés, hotels, restaurants, caterers and nightclubs. The trade show covers the full range of Food & Hospitality sectors, from artisans to hotel groups, with a strong South-West anchorage. Strictly professional visitor base.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of exhibitors is available on the official website: [exphotel.fr](https://www.exphotel.fr/). The 2025 edition brought together 350 exhibitors spread across the trade show''s five worlds. The artisan network is mobilised through CMA Nouvelle-Aquitaine 33 and UMIH 33, partners of the event.

### Visitor quality

- 19,000 professionals welcomed in 2025 (source: exphotel.fr).
- A visitor base made up of café, hotel and restaurant operators and decision-makers from South-West France: restaurateurs, hoteliers, café owners, caterers, head chefs.
- The presence of 140 Michelin-starred chefs and MOF, reinforcing the professional quality of the exchanges.

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The 2025 edition was chaired by chef **Stéphane Carrade** (2 Michelin stars, 1 green star). The trade show combines culinary demonstrations, trade workshops and highlights around the five worlds, with an emphasis on the transformation of the café, hotel and restaurant sectors and sustainable innovation.

### Awards and accolades

14 trade competitions were held in 2025, bringing together around a hundred candidates (professionals, apprentices, students). Among the distinctions awarded: the **Trophée Michel Guérard**, won by Théo Laussucq (Le Gabriel, Bordeaux), and the **Trophée David Campbell**, won by Camille Philippe (Newport Bay Club, Disneyland Paris) (source: tendancehotellerie.fr).

### Community and networks

The event is supported by UMIH 33 (Union des Métiers et des Industries de l''Hôtellerie) and CMA Nouvelle-Aquitaine 33 (Chambre de Métiers et de l''Artisanat), which mobilise the artisan and professional networks of the sector across the Gironde and beyond. Bordeaux Gironde CCI, FERRANDI Paris and Campus du Lac are also among the trade show''s institutional partners (source: exphotel.fr).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux](/lieux/parc-des-expositions-de-bordeaux).

Specific to the trade show:

- **2027 dates:** from Sunday 21 to Tuesday 23 November 2027.
- **Visitor badge:** reserved for professionals in the Food & Hospitality sectors, by prior registration.
- **Exhibitor registration:** via the dedicated area [exphotel.fr/exposez](https://www.exphotel.fr/exposez/je-souhaite-exposer).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor prices are not published on the official website. Participation requests and quotes are available via the exhibitor area ([exphotel.fr/exposez](https://www.exphotel.fr/exposez/je-souhaite-exposer)).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with the BEAM team, choose your world (Food and Cuisine, Décor-Design, New Technologies, Services, Vehicles-Mobility).
- 9 months out: stand positioning and possible entry into the trade competitions.
- 6 months out: prepare demonstrations and on-stand activations.
- 6 weeks out: confirm appointments with South-West café, hotel and restaurant decision-makers.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online pre-registration with proof of professional activity in the café, hotel and restaurant sector.
- Allow 1 to 2 days depending on the worlds you are targeting.
- Identify in advance the competitions and demonstrations by the Michelin-starred chefs and MOF.

## ESG policy & initiatives

Congrès et Expositions de Bordeaux (CEB), which operates under the BEAM brand, has been **ISO 20121** certified since July 2022 (AFNOR, certification for sustainable event management, covering event production and venue management). The 2025 edition placed the emphasis on ESG approaches, sustainable innovation and eco-responsible practices, with the responsible transition having become a structuring issue for the catering and hospitality sectors (sources: beam.fr, restauration21.fr).

## How the trade show has evolved

