/>

### Trajectory analysis

The Paris book event has lived through three major eras. **1981-1993 at the Grand Palais** as the original Salon du Livre. **1994-2020 at the Porte de Versailles**, a professional and general-public trade show format. **Covid cancellations in 2020 and 2021**, then a **complete overhaul in 2022** under the name Festival du Livre de Paris at the Grand Palais Éphémère, under the exclusive stewardship of the SNE via its subsidiary Paris Livres Événements (before 2022, the show was co-managed with Reed Expositions France). Successive guest countries: India 2022, Italy 2023, Québec 2024, Morocco 2025.

The 2026 edition (5th ed.) marked a **post-relaunch record of 121,000 visitors (+6% vs 2025)**, 1,800 authors and 12 stages, with the **comic strip (Bande Dessinée) as guest of honour** (echoing the cancellation of the 2026 Angoulême Festival) and a confirmed young attendance (around 50% under the age of 25). This momentum embeds the format for the long term and makes the 2027 edition (6th ed., 16-18 April, Grand Palais) a much-anticipated event, with a **European country as guest of honour** whose name has not yet been revealed. The multi-year programming beyond 2027 has not been officially communicated to date.', seo_title_en='Festival du Livre de Paris 2027: dates, programme, tickets', seo_description_en='Festival du Livre de Paris 2027: 6th edition on 16-18 April at the Grand Palais. Programme, Grand Prix RTL-Lire, Prix Gotlib, visitor prices and professional accreditations.' WHERE slug='festival-livre-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International cybersecurity forum. The European meeting point for digital security and trust.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Forum InCyber Europe 2027** (formerly FIC, rebranded in 2024) holds its **19th edition** from **Tuesday 9 to Thursday 11 March 2027** at [Lille Grand Palais](/lieux/lille-grand-palais), on the theme "**The agentic vertigo**: securing autonomous systems, towards autonomous cybersecurity?".
- The 2027 theme places **agentic AI** and autonomous systems at the centre: security of AI agents, automation of cyber defence, governance of self-deciding systems. The edition is held under the **High Patronage of the President of the Republic**.
- The edition is structured around **10 associated events** announced: European Cyber Cup (25 teams, 250 players announced), CFI - Cybersecurity for Industry, ID Forum, OSINT conference, Trust & Safety Forum, CoRIIN, INVEST INCYBER and Secure AI.
- **Sole organiser: Forward Global**, a group born from the split of Avisa Partners in 2023-2024. The exclusivity contract with Lille Grand Palais runs until 2029.
- A dense regulatory calendar: the 2027 edition extends the French transposition work on **NIS 2**, the application of the **AI Act** and **DORA**, with a ramping-up of topics around sovereignty, secure AI and post-quantum cryptography.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A B2B trade show covering the entire cybersecurity and digital trust chain: cyber publishers and integrators, IT services firms (ESN), telecom operators, hyperscalers, MSSPs, digital identity, OT/industrial security, AI security, blockchain and trust, digital defence, legal and compliance consulting (GDPR, NIS 2, DORA, AI Act). A mixed audience: private companies, public administrations, operators of vital importance (OIV), local authorities, security forces, academic research.

### Notable exhibitors

A long-standing presence from **Airbus Cyber**, **Orange Cyberdefense**, **Thales**, **Atos / Eviden**, **Capgemini**, **Sopra Steria**, **OVHcloud**, **Stormshield**, **HarfangLab**, **Tehtris**, **CrowdStrike**, **Microsoft**, **Google Cloud**, **Cisco**, **Palo Alto Networks**. Recurring institutional pavilions: European Commission, Europol, ANSSI, Gendarmerie nationale, Police nationale, ComCyber (Ministry of the Armed Forces). The 2027 exhibitor list is being built as registrations come in, open since 12 January 2026. Full up-to-date list on the [official exhibitors page](https://europe.forum-incyber.com/exposants/).

### Visitor quality

A markedly professional profile: CISOs, IT directors, CIOs, CTOs, compliance officers and data lawyers, complemented by sovereign forces (State services, defence, interior), research, specialised VC funds and international delegations. Recent editions have welcomed delegations from around a hundred countries (100 countries in 2025), with a pronounced cyber-diplomacy dimension (high-level summit, governmental plenary sessions).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

Each year the forum rolls out more than **200 conferences** (plenaries, round tables, masterclasses, technical demonstrations) and a high-level summit. The detailed programme and 2027 speakers are published progressively on the official portal. For reference, the 2026 edition had notably announced **Olivier Gavalda** (CEO, Crédit Agricole), **Neal Jetton** (Director of Cybersecurity, INTERPOL), **Octave Klaba** (founder, OVHcloud) and **Henna Virkkunen** (Vice-President of the European Commission), alongside the Director General of ANSSI **Vincent Strubel**. As headline speakers and chairs change with each edition, refer to the official 2027 programme for the up-to-date line-up.

### Awards & prizes

Three flagship prizes structure the forum (official Forward Global wording):

- **Cyber Start-up Prize**: 5 categories (President of the Republic Prize, Growth Prize, Operational Impact Prize, Research Prize, Jury''s Favourite Prize for start-ups less than 2 years old). 2025 winners: Patrowl (Grand Prix), Keyless (Operational Impact), enclaive (Growth), iliadata (Research), Cybi (Jury''s Favourite).
- **InCyber Book Prize**: 5 categories (general public, youth, academic research, cyberdefence, artificial intelligence). Awarded at a ceremony during the forum.
- **European Cyber Cup (EC2)**: a team competition (CTF, forensics, OSINT, hardware hacking, Battle Royale). The 2027 edition announces **25 teams and 250 players**. 2025 winners: ESNA, École 2600, Oteria Cyber School.

### Satellite events

The 2027 edition brings together around a dozen specialised villages and formats announced:

- **TechLab**: live technical demonstrations
- **CFI - Cybersecurity for Industry**: IT/OT and industrial security strand
- **ID Forum**: digital identity
- **OSINT conference**: open-source intelligence
- **Trust & Safety Forum**: platform trust and safety
- **CoRIIN**: congress on incident response and digital investigation
- **Secure AI**: track dedicated to the security of AI models
- **INVEST INCYBER**: investor / start-up networking sessions
- **CyberLeaders cocktail** and **TOP LEADERS one-to-one sessions**: executive networking
- **Crisis management masterclass**: C-level exercises

### Community & networks

The forum relies on an official matchmaking platform (more than 4,200 structured business meetings in 2025) and an official Forum InCyber app for managing one''s schedule, scanning contacts and accessing the programme. The specialist cyber press (INCYBER NEWS, Solutions Numériques, IT for Business, ZDNet France, ZATAZ, Le Mag IT) covers the event every year.

The Forum InCyber has gone international: **Forum InCyber North America** (Montreal, ~4,000 visitors in 2024), **Forum InCyber Japan** (Tokyo, launched December 2025 with ~900 participants), and an announced spin-off in San Antonio (Texas).

### What''s new in 2027

- **19th edition**, and the 4th under the Forum InCyber Europe banner (post-2024 rebranding).
- Central theme: "**The agentic vertigo**" (securing autonomous systems, automating cybersecurity, governing AI agents).
- **INCYBER IMPACT** initiative spotlighted.
- Programme structured around **10 associated events** announced, including Trust & Safety Forum and CoRIIN.
- Edition held under the **High Patronage of the President of the Republic**.
- 2027 regulatory framework: continuation of the NIS 2 transposition in France, the AI Act in application, DORA for the financial sector, post-quantum preparation.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Forward Global, organiser of the Forum InCyber, positions the forum on the theme of **digital trust serving businesses, citizens and future generations**, with a declared commitment to a secure and sustainable digital environment. Beyond this general guiding line, the organiser does not publish a detailed CSR report specific to the forum (event carbon footprint, zero-waste plan, soft mobility to Lille Grand Palais). The societal dimension is carried by the programme content: sessions on responsible cybersecurity, digital inclusion, cyber education (European Cyber Cup student challenges with EPITA, École 2600, Oteria Cyber School), and cyber diplomacy. Lille Grand Palais, the host venue, has its own environmental commitments, which can be consulted on the [venue page](/lieux/lille-grand-palais).

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Lille Grand Palais](/lieux/lille-grand-palais), 1 boulevard des Cités-Unies, 59800 Lille.
- **Transport access**: Lille Metro line 2, Lille Grand Palais station (direct exit). Lille is connected to Paris in 1 hr by TGV (Lille-Europe and Lille-Flandres stations, 10 min on foot from the palais), to Brussels in 35 min, to London in 1 hr 30 (Eurostar). Lille-Lesquin airport is 20 min away by taxi.
- **Parking**: Lille Grand Palais car park on site (heavily oversubscribed during the 3 days of the forum). Public city-centre car parks as an alternative. The train is preferable.
- **Accommodation**: Centre / Lille-Europe / Vieux-Lille districts as a priority. Book **3 to 4 months in advance**: early March sees strong hotel demand in Lille.
- **Opening hours & badges**: Tue 9 March to Thu 11 March 2027, access reserved for accredited professionals. Registrations open since 12 January 2026 on [the official portal](https://europe.forum-incyber.com/inscriptions/).
- **Services**: On-site catering, CyberLeaders VIP areas, radio/TV studios, official matchmaking platform, Forum InCyber app.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: submit exhibitor application via the official platform, choosing between an individual stand or a national / regional pavilion (Bpifrance, Choose France, French regional pavilions Hauts-de-France, Nouvelle-Aquitaine, Bretagne, etc.)
- 9 months out: apply for the Cyber Start-up Prize, enter a European Cyber Cup team
- 6 months out: stand brief, prospect targeting via the platform, request to speak in a conference or masterclass
- 3 months out: team accreditations, sales brief on product announcements, Lille accommodation logistics
- 6 weeks out: activate the Forum InCyber app, schedule business meetings, pre-qualify leads via matchmaking

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Register early: the professional capacity fills up fast
- Identify the 10 to 15 priority exhibitors in advance and schedule meetings via the official platform
- Allow **2 days minimum** to cover the palais + plenaries + thematic villages
- The governmental plenaries (ANSSI, ComCyber, European Commission) have limited capacity: pre-book
- The presence of sovereign forces (Ministry of the Interior, Ministry of the Armed Forces) makes it an annual entry point for sovereignty topics

## How the trade show has evolved

