## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with SEAE (05 62 34 87 44, 20 place du Foirail, Tarbes) to book a stand and obtain the up-to-date price list.
- 6 months out: choose the hall (Hall 1 livestock, Hall 3 institutional, Hall 4 thematic, halls 2 and 5 general) and brief on the stand.
- 3 months out: team accreditations, accommodation (book early, as March sees several events concentrated in Tarbes), and a brief on seasonal products.
- 6 weeks out: confirm logistics for machinery / animal deliveries (for the sectors concerned), register for competitions, and finalise stand activities.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Full-price pass €7 at the gate; online ticketing is available to avoid queuing at the weekend (Saturday and Sunday are the busiest days).
- Thursday is the quietest trade day: useful for machinery buyers, cooperatives and agricultural banking.
- Friday to follow the Ovinpiades and the sheep competitions (10am-2pm), Saturday for the organic-farming conference at 3pm and the draught-horse handling competition at 3pm.
- Allow 4 to 6 hours to cover the 24,000 m² (5 halls + ring), and at least half a day if your aim includes the competitions and the gourmet village.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The Salon Régional de l''Agriculture de Tarbes does not publish a dedicated CSR page on its official website. Its sustainability dimension is carried, in practice, by the show''s commitment to short supply chains: 60 farm producers and artisans present, the promotion of the Bienvenue à la ferme label (official partner), the Légumineuses d''Occitanie pavilion in Hall 4, and the organic-farming conference on the Saturday. The 2026 theme "International Year of Rangelands and Pastoralists" (UN) is integrated through the shepherd and herding-dog demonstrations and the educational game from the Département des Hautes-Pyrénées on mountain pastoralism. The 2026 decision to hold the show without presenting cattle, motivated by LSD health prevention, reflects a precautionary approach for the sector.

## How the show has evolved

