### Trajectory analysis

Since 1904 the Foire de Paris has established itself as Europe''s largest consumer commercial trade fair. Created on the initiative of the **CCI Paris** and professional organisations through the **Comité des Expositions de Paris** (a 1901-law association founded in 1903), driven by the jeweller **Gustave Sandoz** inspired by the Leipzig fair, the first edition was held on **17 March 1904 at the Carreau du Temple** with 500 exhibitors.

The 2025 edition confirmed solid commercial momentum: **400,000+ visitors (+5% YoY)** and **~1,250 exhibitors (+12% vs 2024)**, on a format stabilised at 12 days spanning the May bank holiday bridges. The 2026 edition marks a **structural shift** with the launch of **two new worlds (Auto Mobil Paris and Made in Paris)** that significantly broaden sector coverage beyond the historic home interiors and crafts core. Auto Mobil Paris shows **+65% floor space vs 2025** across 5,000 m² in Hall 5 with 6 manufacturers: a clear bet on mobility as a new attendance pillar. Made in Paris consolidates a Made in France editorial line over 15,000 m². The organiser **Comexposium** (born of the 2008 merger of Comexpo CCI Paris IDF and Exposium Unibail-Rodamco) is thus playing the card of diversifying its worlds without touching the calendar format or visitor pricing, two very stable parameters of the Foire de Paris.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='foire-de-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for technological innovation in hospitality and catering. Digital solutions, equipment and services for the hospitality and foodservice industry (HoReCa).', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **"The 100% HoReCa Tech & CSR trade show"**: Food Hotel Tech brings together developers of digital solutions and suppliers of equipment for the hospitality and catering sector (HoReCa), with a dual focus on technology and the sustainable transition.
- **Organiser: Easyfairs.** The trade show, founded by Karen Serfaty (CEO & Founder) in 2017, has joined the pan-European events group Easyfairs (acquisition announced on 15 April 2026). Karen Serfaty and her team remain at the helm of the event.
- **Next edition: the 10th, an anniversary edition, on 31 March and 1 April 2027**, at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), Hall 7.1. An anniversary evening is planned for the first night.
- **Audience (2026 figures): more than 8,700 visitors, 230+ exhibitors, 50+ start-ups and 36+ conferences.** Figures provided by the organiser (not OJS-audited).
- **2026 Awards presented**: Innovation Award, Startup Award, Customer Experience Innovation Award, Connected Kitchen Innovation Award.
- A compact two-day format, targeting HoReCa decision-makers (hoteliers, restaurateurs, groups, franchises) looking for tech and CSR solutions.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile
Developers of software and platforms for the HoReCa sector (PMS, booking, point-of-sale, management, marketing, data, AI), suppliers of connected kitchen and front-of-house equipment, payment, loyalty and HR management solutions, as well as players in the sustainable transition (waste management, energy, sourcing). The trade show combines large established developers and young start-ups (50+ start-ups in 2026), the latter competing for the Startup Award.

### Notable exhibitors
The list of exhibitors for the forthcoming edition is available on the [official website](https://www.foodhoteltech.com/en). At the 2026 edition, the award winners illustrate the exhibitor profile: Septeo (Witbooking AI), Unox, Châtaigne and Linkeat.

### Quality of the audience
2026 figures provided by the organiser: more than 8,700 visitors from the hospitality and catering industries. These figures come from the organiser''s own report and are not subject to public OJS certification. The audience is positioned in decision-making roles (management, operations, purchasing) on the side of HoReCa establishments and groups.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme
The 2026 edition offered 36+ conferences led by industry experts (technology, CSR, HoReCa operations), accompanied by innovation pitches and themed guided tours. The detailed programme of the 10th edition in 2027 is published on the organiser''s website as the event approaches.

### Awards and accolades
Food Hotel Tech presents several distinctions, the official titles recorded being: **INNOVATION AWARD**, **STARTUP AWARD**, **INNOVATION AWARD: CUSTOMER EXPERIENCE**, **INNOVATION AWARD: CONNECTED KITCHEN**. 2026 winners: Innovation Award to Septeo (Witbooking AI), Connected Kitchen to Unox, Customer Experience to Châtaigne, Startup Award to Linkeat.

### Community & networks
The trade show fosters a community of HoReCa decision-makers and tech suppliers, extended online via the event''s official accounts. The 10th edition is accompanied by an anniversary evening on the first night, in Hall 7.1.

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the venue page [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show: the 10th edition takes place on 31 March and 1 April 2027 in Hall 7.1 (the 2026 edition occupied Hall 4). Entry is by professional visitor badge, to be collected in advance on the organiser''s website. The short two-day format makes it advisable to plan your exhibitor meetings before attending.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="No public exhibitor pricing schedule is published for this edition. The amounts below are indicative sector benchmarks (2-day B2B tech trade show, Porte de Versailles), to be confirmed with Easyfairs/Food Hotel Tech." rows={[{ "poste": "Floor space + fitted stand (12-18 m²)", "low": "€6,000", "high": "€14,000" }, { "poste": "Fit-out, furniture, electricity", "low": "€1,500", "high": "€5,000" }, { "poste": "Logistics, transport, assembly", "low": "€1,000", "high": "€3,000" }, { "poste": "Staff, travel, accommodation", "low": "€2,000", "high": "€6,000" }, { "poste": "Communications, demos, giveaways", "low": "€1,500", "high": "€5,000" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (indicative)", "low": "~€12,000", "high": "~€33,000" }]} footer="Indicative sector estimate, excluding sponsorship/awards options. Request the official schedule from the organiser." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor
- **6 months ahead**: initial commercial contact with Easyfairs/Food Hotel Tech, choice of location in Hall 7.1, possible entry to the awards (Innovation, Startup).
- **3 months ahead**: finalisation of the stand, team brief, preparation of product demos and meeting bookings.
- **1 month ahead**: prospect invitation campaign, build logistics, communication materials.
- **2 days ahead**: build, demo rehearsals, finalising the meeting schedule.

### For the decision-making visitor
Registration and badge in advance, identifying relevant exhibitors and conferences (tech, CSR, operations), planning targeted meetings. The two-day format rewards a visit prepared around concrete projects (PMS overhaul, point-of-sale, AI, sustainability).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Food Hotel Tech is part of the Easyfairs group''s **Act for the Future** programme, launched in 2021: a commitment to carbon neutrality by 2050, a 50% reduction in greenhouse gas emissions by 2030 across all the group''s events, and membership of the **Net Zero Carbon Events** pledge (signed in October 2021). Easyfairs has also subscribed to the objectives of the **Science Based Targets (SBTi)** initiative and has reported a 34% reduction in its total CO2 emissions since 2019. These commitments apply in full to Food Hotel Tech since it joined the group in April 2026. On the editorial side, CSR is one of the trade show''s 11 solution themes (waste reduction, energy, sourcing, well-being at work), although no certification specific to the event or a carbon assessment specific to the Paris edition has been publicly documented to date. As for the venue, Paris Expo Porte de Versailles is operated by **Viparis**, the world''s leading operator certified **ISO 20121** across all its sites since 2014, and committed to the **BETTER EVENTS** strategy (2018-2030) along three axes: environment, territorial legacy and employee experience. In 2024, Viparis published a sustainability report compliant with the European **CSRD** directive.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "10th (2027, upcoming)", "dates": "31 Mar-1 Apr 2027", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles, Hall 7.1", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "9th (2026)", "dates": "14-15 Apr 2026", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles, Hall 4", "visiteurs": "8,700+", "exposants": "230+" }]} sources="Organiser''s website (foodhoteltech.com), Easyfairs press release (15 Apr 2026), Tendance Hôtellerie." />

### Trajectory analysis
Launched in 2017 by Karen Serfaty (CEO & Founder), Food Hotel Tech has established itself as the Paris event for technology applied to hospitality and catering, with a short two-day format at the Porte de Versailles. The major turning point dates to April 2026: the acquisition by the Easyfairs group (acquired alongside Tech For Retail), with the founder and her team retained at the helm of the event. The 10th edition in 2027 marks the trade show''s anniversary and its entry into a European development logic driven by its new operator. The move from Hall 4 (2026) to Hall 7.1 (2027) accompanies this step up. On the audience side, the organiser reports continuous growth (more than 8,700 visitors in 2026); these figures remain organiser data, not certified by an independent audit.', seo_title_en='Food Hotel Tech 2027 Paris: dates, exhibitors, awards | Agoris', seo_description_en='Food Hotel Tech 2027, 10th anniversary edition on 31 March-1 April at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles (Hall 7.1). 8,700+ visitors, 230 HoReCa tech & CSR exhibitors. Organised by Easyfairs.' WHERE slug='food-hotel-tech-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Annual gathering for franchising and organised retail in Lyon, organised by the CCI Lyon Métropole Saint-Étienne Roanne. Close to 160 brands recruit their future franchisees there in a single day. France''s second-largest event in the sector, behind Franchise Expo Paris.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Forum Franchise** is the annual gathering for franchising and organised retail in Lyon, organised by the **CCI Lyon Métropole Saint-Étienne Roanne**. It positions itself as France''s second-largest event in the sector, behind [Franchise Expo Paris](/salons/franchise-expo-paris).
- Next edition: 18th edition, on Thursday 8 October 2026 from 9 am to 5.30 pm at the [LDLC Arena](/lieux/ldlc-arena-lyon) in Décines-Charpieu.
- Close to 160 regional, national and international brands exhibit to recruit new franchisees, across all sectors.
- 2025 review (17th edition, the first at the LDLC Arena): 2,398 unique attendees (source: lyon-franchise.com/exposer).
- Free visitor entry with online registration.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Franchisors, organised retail brands and franchising experts. Every sector is represented: catering and food, automotive, banking and financing, beauty, health, fitness and hairdressing, specialist retail, home and building, property, fashion and accessories, business services and personal services.

The visitor base is made up of franchise candidates, project leaders and entrepreneurs looking to join a network, mostly from the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region.

### Notable exhibitors

Close to 160 brands exhibit at each edition. The exhibitor list is available on the official website: [lyon-franchise.com](https://www.lyon-franchise.com/). Brands that have exhibited at recent editions include: Brioche Dorée, Burger King (catering), Midas, Point S (automotive), Monoprix (distribution), Yves Rocher (beauty) (source: lyon-franchise.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

- 2,398 unique attendees in 2025, compared with 2,293 unique visitors in 2024 (sources: lyon-franchise.com/exposer, franchise-magazine.com)
- A predominantly regional visitor base: project leaders and franchise candidates from Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes
- Visitors'' main objectives: meeting targeted exhibitors, attending conferences and workshops, and finding out about setting up a franchise

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The Forum Franchise offers a programme of conferences and workshops led by sector experts (lawyers, financiers, network heads), covering financing, the legal framework of the franchise agreement and the franchise candidate''s journey. The detailed 2026 programme is published on the official website as the trade show approaches.

### Awards and prizes

The **Trophées Forum Franchise Lyon** spotlight the players who embody the dynamism and innovation of franchised retail. Three distinctions are awarded: **L''Ouverture de l''année**, **Le Développement de l''année** and **Le Coup de Cœur** (source: lyon-franchise.com/trophee-forum-franchise-2025/).

### Community and networks

The trade show brings together several partners, including the **Fédération française de la franchise**, the **Banque Populaire Auvergne Rhône-Alpes**, Fiducial and France Travail, alongside several specialist franchising media outlets.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and transport: see the [LDLC Arena](/lieux/ldlc-arena-lyon) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Thursday 8 October 2026, 9 am to 5.30 pm.
- **Visitor badge:** free with prior online registration via lyon-franchise.com.
- **Access:** tram T7 to Décines OL Vallée stop, bus 85, free P9 car park on site. 30 minutes from Lyon Part-Dieu station and 10 minutes by car from the airport and Lyon Saint-Exupéry station.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates published on the official website (excl. VAT):

<PricingTable
  columns={[
    { "key": "offre", "label": "Offer" },
    { "key": "prix", "label": "Price excl. VAT", "align": "right" }
  ]}
  rows={[
    { "offre": "Bare stand 12 m²", "prix": "2 700 €" },
    { "offre": "Standard pack 6 m²", "prix": "2 825 €" },
    { "offre": "6 m² pack, full customisation", "prix": "3 980 €" }
  ]}
  sources="lyon-franchise.com/exposer"
/>

These offers include a listing in the exhibitor directory, WiFi, access to the VIP club and two meals (source: lyon-franchise.com/exposer).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: making contact with the CCI Lyon Métropole, choosing the stand format from the published offers.
- 6 months out: preparing the franchisee recruitment pitch and the network''s presentation materials.
- 3 months out: applying for the Trophées Forum Franchise Lyon.
- 6 weeks out: confirming candidate meetings and briefing the sales team.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free online pre-registration at lyon-franchise.com.
- Set aside a day: the trade show takes place on a single day.
- Identify in advance the brands and conferences that match your project.
- Prepare your franchise candidate file (investment capacity, target sector, location area).

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
  columns={[
    { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
    { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Attendees", "align": "right" },
    { "key": "enseignes", "label": "Brands", "align": "right" }
  ]}
  rows={[
    { "edition": "2026 (18th, upcoming)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "enseignes": "~160" },
    { "edition": "2025 (17th)", "visiteurs": "2 398", "enseignes": "n/a" },
    { "edition": "2024 (16th)", "visiteurs": "2 293", "enseignes": "~160" }
  ]}
  sources="lyon-franchise.com, franchise-magazine.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

The Forum Franchise changed venue in 2025: after the Cité internationale des congrès de Lyon, its 17th edition moved for the first time to the LDLC Arena in Décines-Charpieu, a format it retains in 2026. The trade show is stabilising its audience at around 2,300 to 2,400 unique attendees and close to 160 brands, while remaining strongly anchored in the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes area. Its positioning as France''s second-largest franchising event, behind Franchise Expo Paris, makes it the benchmark gathering for organised retail in the south-east. The 18th edition takes place on 8 October 2026 at the LDLC Arena.', seo_title_en='Forum Franchise Lyon 2026: 18th edition at the LDLC Arena', seo_description_en='Forum Franchise Lyon, 18th edition on 8 October 2026 at the LDLC Arena. Close to 160 brands recruiting their franchisees. Organised by the CCI Lyon Métropole. Free entry.' WHERE slug='franchise-expo-lyon';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The trade show for franchising and business start-up. Brands, concepts and support for entrepreneurs.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 44th edition of Franchise Expo Paris: **14 to 16 March 2026** (Saturday to Monday) at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **Hall 1**.
- The oldest franchise trade show in Europe: created in **1981** by the **Fédération Française de la Franchise (FFF)**, operated since 2023 by **Infopro Digital** under FFF licence.
- Actual results from the 2026 edition: **31,937 visitors**, **550 exhibitors including 465 brands** (185 new exhibitors), **83 foreign exhibitors** from **23 nationalities**, **90 sectors** of activity represented.
- A 100% business-focused audience: average visitor age **39.6 years**, **48% have capital of more than €50,000** (17% above €150,000), **67% ready to launch within 12 months**, **2,000+ qualified meetings** generated on site.
- On the supply side: **338 brands** are looking for multi-franchisees, **130+** are opening under master franchise and **131** are accessible through takeover. A structuring international attendance: **1,677 professionals from 77 countries**.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Franchise Expo Paris brings together almost every model of independent organised retail: classic franchising, brand licensing, concession, partnership, commission-affiliation and cooperative. The 550 exhibitors in 2026 are spread across **90 sectors**, covering catering (fast food, themed, delivery), personal services, real estate, beauty and wellbeing, specialist retail (toys, flowers, sport, home decor), automotive mobility, hospitality, training and fashion.

The event attracts established network heads in the process of densifying their French coverage, foreign brands looking for a master franchisee for Europe, and emerging concepts validating their format before scaling up. **185 new exhibitors** at the 2026 edition, a sign of the continuous renewal of the offering.

### Confirmed brands 2026

The 465 brands in 2026 cover a broad sector range. Among the brands confirmed by the organiser and the specialist press:

- **Hospitality**: Accor, Fast Hotel, Brit Hotel.
- **Retail and lifestyle**: Monceau Fleurs, JouéClub, La Grande Récré.
- **Catering**: Pizza Cosy, Dreams Donuts.
- **Services and takeover**: Cash Express, Nestenn (real estate), Attila (roofing), Maclem.
- **Home and automotive**: Jotul, Norauto.

### Visitor quality

- **31,937 professional visitors** at the 2026 edition, a highly qualified candidate-investor profile.
- **48%** of visitors have personal capital of more than €50,000, of which **17%** above €150,000.
- **67%** state that they want to launch within 12 months of the trade show.
- An attendance made up mainly of executives in career transition, business founders and franchisees seeking a second network (multi-franchising).
- **1,677 international visitors** from **77 countries**, with a strong European presence (Belgium, Spain, Italy, United Kingdom) and the Maghreb.
- **2,000+ qualified meetings** arranged via the brand-candidate matching platform.

## Activities and community

### Trophées des Meilleures Franchises de France (TM2F)

**4th edition in 2026**, organised by **L''Indicateur de la Franchise** in partnership with **Caisse d''Épargne**, **Simon Associés**, **Franchise Management** and **In Extenso**. The ranking is built from a survey carried out directly with franchisees (with the prior agreement of the network heads), making it more of a barometer of network satisfaction than an editorial award. The winners benefit from strong visibility with the specialist press and candidates.

### Révélations de la Franchise

A competition dedicated to young, developing brands, a showcase for concepts beginning their national roll-out. A category distinct from the TM2F, with a jury of sector professionals.

### Pitch Auto and Pitch Restauration

Flash presentation sessions reserved for automotive mobility and catering brands. A short format (5 to 10 minutes per brand) before an audience of targeted candidates, a model calibrated to generate immediate meeting bookings.

### Conference programme

**178 conferences** scheduled over 3 days in 2026, led by **350 speakers** (network heads, chartered accountants, lawyers, financiers, franchisee witnesses). Almost **7,000 participants** counted across all the sessions. The programme covers the mechanics of applying, financing and capital, choosing a brand, building the business plan, post-signature support and the legal pitfalls of the DIP (Pre-contractual Information Document).

### Institutional partners

The French franchise ecosystem is structured around the **Fédération Française de la Franchise (FFF)**, the salon''s historic owner since 1981. The FFF brings together 2,035 networks representing **93,395 points of sale** and **€93.71 billion** in turnover in 2026, equating to more than **1 million jobs**. **Infopro Digital** has operated the trade show since 2023, succeeding RX France.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Hall**: 1 (main ground floor of Paris Expo Porte de Versailles).
- **Opening hours**: Saturday 14 and Sunday 15 March from 9.30am to 7pm, Monday 16 March from 9.30am to 6pm.
- **Weekend + Monday format**: a deliberate choice to allow employees in career transition to visit without taking time off, and managers to come on the Monday.
- **Visitor badge**: online pre-registration is required to benefit from preferential rates.

## What it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published publicly by the organiser. Quotes on request from **Infopro Digital** on behalf of the **FFF**. Several packages traditionally coexist: bare stand (floor space rental only), turnkey fitted stand, village spaces (young brands pooled in a compact format), and premium zones along the central aisle. As Hall 1 is the sole venue, competition for strategic locations (entrance, central aisle, proximity to conference stages) drives prices up.

### Visitor rates 2026

Official price list published by the organiser, which adjusts the price according to when you register:

- **September 2025 to 12 February 2026**: 1st badge **free**, additional badge **€15**.
- **13 February to 1 March 2026**: 1st badge **€15**, additional badge **€15**.
- **From 2 March 2026**: 1st badge **€30**, additional badge **€15**.
- **On site without pre-registration**: 1st badge **€34**, additional badge **€17**.

Exhibitor pricing data not publicly available at this date.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months before: make contact with Infopro Digital, choose location and stand format.
- 6 months before: apply for the **Trophées des Meilleures Franchises de France** or the **Révélations de la Franchise** depending on network profile.
- 4 months before: prepare the DIP, brief the sales team on candidate profiles (capital, geography, sector).
- 3 months before: integrate the matching platform to pre-qualify meetings (objective: fill the agenda for the 3 days).
- 6 weeks before: activate the specialist press (Officiel de la Franchise, Franchise Magazine, L''Indicateur de la Franchise), candidate materials, LinkedIn prospecting plan.

### For the candidate-investor visitor

- Free pre-registration before 12 February 2026: best rate on badges.
- **Prepare your financial file in advance**: a visitor with a documented capital file multiplies their chances of a quality interview with the network heads.
- Target a maximum of 8 to 12 brands out of the 465 present, otherwise you risk spreading yourself too thin.
- Attend 2 or 3 key conferences (financing, brand choice, DIP) before meeting the networks.
- **Monday = managers'' day**: a prime slot for in-depth meetings with founders and network directors, with fewer candidate crowds than at the weekend.

## CSR policy and initiatives

The organiser has structured its CSR approach around **5 concrete commitments**: reducing the environmental footprint of the trade show, encouraging eco-responsible transport, optimising the energy use of the installations, raising awareness among exhibitors and visitors, and producing educational content on responsible franchising.

Confirmed operational measures: **eco-designed badges**, **lanyards in recycled PET**, selective sorting deployed throughout the aisles and back office, reusable signage from one edition to the next, and a programme to raise exhibitor awareness on the design of eco-responsible stands.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" },
 { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "enseignes", "label": "Brands", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
 { "edition": "44th, 2026", "dates": "14-16 March", "visiteurs": "31,937", "exposants": "550", "enseignes": "465" },
 { "edition": "43rd, 2025", "dates": "16-18 March", "visiteurs": "32,000+", "exposants": "595", "enseignes": "472" },
 { "edition": "1st, 1981", "dates": "Parc Floral de Vincennes", "visiteurs": "", "exposants": "", "enseignes": "" }
