 sources="FFF, Infopro Digital, franchise-magazine.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

Franchise Expo Paris is the doyen of European franchise trade shows: created in 1981 by the FFF at the Parc Floral de Vincennes, it is today the **leading franchise trade show in Europe** and one of the three largest in the world alongside the North American IFA Convention. **44 cumulative editions** in 2026, with solid institutional roots since the transition to Infopro Digital operation in 2023.

The 2025-2026 trajectory reflects a slight, controlled contraction: **32,282 visitors in 2025** against **31,937 in 2026**, with the number of exhibitors falling from 595 to 550. The context is clear: the **municipal elections of 15 March 2026** mechanically reduced the participation of brands heavily dependent on local authorities, with the organiser having anticipated this decline as early as the commercial phase. The quality of the attendance remains excellent, with a preserved candidate-investor profile: 48% with capital above €50,000, 67% intending to launch within 12 months. The densification of the programme (178 conferences, 350 speakers in 2026 against 150 conferences and 73 experts in 2025) confirms Infopro Digital''s strategy of moving upmarket on content to offset the stabilisation in exhibitor volume.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='franchise-expo-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='B2B trade show for gas and electricity. Congress and exhibition for energy suppliers, distributors and network operators.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Gazelec** is an annual B2B congress dedicated to energy purchasing strategies (gas and electricity), organised by the agency **Content & Business**. It is a meeting point for buyer-consumers and suppliers, not a large-format exhibition.
- Next edition: 12, 13 and 14 October 2026 at the CNIT Forest, Paris La Défense.
- Hybrid format: two days of round tables and business sessions open to all, followed by a day of procurement training workshops reserved for buyers and energy managers.
- Announced 2026 figures (pre-event targets, unaudited): more than 1,000 participants, more than 300 buyers, 100 speakers, around sixty sponsors and around thirty specialist partners.
- Official strapline: *"Your annual meeting dedicated to energy purchasing strategies"*.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Energy suppliers and distributors, network operators and transmission system operators, brokers and aggregators, and providers of energy management solutions. On the demand side: procurement departments, energy managers, and energy officers from industrial and tertiary-sector companies across more than twenty sectors. The congress targets all the key players in the French and European energy industry.

### Notable exhibitors

The official website displays the logos of the current edition''s sponsors and partners without a usable named text list. For the exact line-up of sponsors and partners, see the [participants page on congresgazelec.com](https://www.congresgazelec.com/content/participants).

### Quality of the visitor base

- A congress geared towards procurement decision-makers: more than 300 buyer-consumers expected in 2026, out of a total of more than 1,000 participants (targets announced by the organiser)
- A day dedicated to buyers and energy managers, with procurement training workshops
- A cross-section audience of buyers and suppliers designed for qualified networking and business meetings

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The 2026 programme is built around 11 round tables and 12 business sessions over two days, followed by a day of training workshops reserved for buyers (6 working groups). The themes cover geopolitics and resilience in the face of the energy crisis, decarbonisation through electrification, the optimisation of supply strategies and the management of volatility, gas transmission costs, electricity market design, innovative contracts (PPAs), flexibility and storage, collective self-consumption, as well as the use of data and AI in energy management.

For reference, the 2025 edition featured a programme of 8 round tables, 6 working groups, 24 business sessions and 16 training sessions (source: filiere-3e.fr). The detail of the 2026 speakers is published on the official website.

### Community and networks

The congress draws on a network of media and professional relays within the energy industry.

The specialist energy press relays the event, in particular J3e / Filière 3e, which offered a partner rate for the 2025 edition (source: filiere-3e.fr).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and surroundings: see the [CNIT Paris La Défense](/lieux/cnit-la-defense) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Access:** metro line 1 and RER A, La Défense - Grande Arche stop (exit 4); tram T2 and Transilien lines L and U, La Défense stop; INDIGO car park, 19 av. de la Division Leclerc, 92800 Puteaux; nearby Vélib stations: Place Nelson Mandela, Avenue de l''Ark, Nanterre Université station.
- **Address:** Centre de Congrès CNIT Forest, 2 place de la Défense, 92092 Puteaux.
- **Registration:** with the organising team (inscriptions@contentandbusiness.fr, 01 83 64 12 58). Detailed opening hours are published on congresgazelec.com as the edition approaches.

## How much it costs to exhibit

The terms for sponsoring and partnership are not published on the official website. Sponsoring is handled directly with the organiser Content & Business (romain.dechaudat@contentandbusiness.fr). Figures not available publicly.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with Content & Business for sponsoring or partnership, and choose the speaking format.
- 6 months out: lock in the business sessions and round-table appearance, and prepare the procurement messaging.
- 3 months out: confirm buyer meetings, and brief the sales team on the year''s market issues.
- 6 weeks out: finalise the meeting schedule and the materials.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Pre-register with the organising team, specifying your profile (buyer-consumer or supplier).
- For buyers: target the procurement training workshop day, dedicated to energy roles.
- Prepare in advance the round tables to follow according to the current issues (PPAs, flexibility, market design, transmission costs).
- Book supplier meeting slots during the two days open to all.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "participants", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "acheteurs", "label": "Buyers", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
