### Trajectory analysis

Gazelec has established itself as the French meeting point for energy purchasing strategies, with more than 15 years of history: the specialist press mentioned its 15th anniversary in 2025. The congress has tracked market developments, from electricity market design questions post-ARENH to gas price volatility and long-term contracts (PPAs). The figures communicated (more than 1,000 participants, several hundred buyers) are targets announced ahead of the event and not audited results. The 2026 edition, from 12 to 14 October at the CNIT Forest in Paris La Défense, retains its hybrid congress-plus-procurement-training format, with a niche positioning around energy buyer-decision-makers.', seo_title_en='Gazelec 2026: energy procurement congress at CNIT Paris La Défense', seo_description_en='Gazelec 2026, the congress on energy purchasing strategies (gas and electricity), takes place from 12 to 14 October at the CNIT Forest, Paris La Défense. Programme, buyer profile, practical information.' WHERE slug='gazelec-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='France''s great industry gathering. Connected factory, subcontracting, measurement, materials and additive manufacturing.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Legacy slug**: this listing covers the **Global Industrie 2027** edition at [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon), from **15 to 18 March 2027** (the slug `global-industrie-lyon-2025` is kept for URL stability). The trade show has alternated between Paris (even years) and Lyon (odd years) since its creation: Lyon 2025, Paris 2026, Lyon 2027.
- Organiser: **GL Events Exhibitions**. Frequency: **annual**. Official verbatim slogan: *"La voix et les solutions de l''industrie"*. Under the high patronage of the President of the Republic.
- 2027 stated targets: 2,500 exhibiting companies, 60,000 industry professionals, 100+ startups, 3,000+ machines and robots in operation, 800+ speaking slots, 8,000 young people and jobseekers, 91 countries represented.
- The trade show was born from the **2018 merger of Midest, Industrie, Smart Industries and Tolexpo**, bringing together subcontracting, machine tools, smart industries and sheet metal processing into a single event.
- Four areas covered: robotics, digitalisation/AI, energy, environment, logistics, production and maintenance, services, defence, amounting to more than 50 aggregated industrial sectors.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Global Industrie is positioned as the largest industrial gathering in France and one of the most significant in Europe across the machine tool / subcontracting / robotics / smart industries scope. The exhibitor base is dominated by SMEs and mid-cap companies (85% in 2025): manufacturers in mechanical engineering, subcontracting, metal processing, robotics, automation, industrial digital, energy and defence. Strong presence of international pavilions (91 countries expected in 2027).

### Notable exhibitors

Official list on the [exhibitors page](https://www.global-industrie.com/liste-des-exposants) of the Global Industrie website. The trade show aggregates the historical communities of its four founding events: Symop (production machines and technologies), FIM (Fédération des Industries Mécaniques), Artema (mechatronics), UITS (surface technologies), Gimelec (electrical equipment), Cetim. International country pavilions structured around the 91 nations announced for 2027.

### Quality of the visitor base

The 2025 Lyon edition recorded 45,000 visitors (+20% vs the 2023 Lyon edition). 85% of exhibitors were SMEs / mid-cap companies. The 2026 Paris edition reported 2,500 announced exhibitors and a target of 60,000 professionals. The audience is made up of industry players (principals, subcontractors), production, purchasing, R&D, methods and maintenance managers, as well as international delegations and 8,000 young people and jobseekers through the GI Avenir programme.

## Features & community

### Conference programme

**Grande Scène**: the main stage, with more than 800 speaking slots announced for 2027 (500 speakers in 2024). The programme is structured around industry''s major challenges: reindustrialisation, energy transition, industrial AI, sovereignty, training. The trade show has historically hosted political keynotes (the 2018 edition was inaugurated by Emmanuel Macron, who at the time attended every Paris inauguration).

### Awards & accolades

**GI Awards** (Global Industrie Awards): *"Mettez en lumière vos savoir-faire"*. Around a hundred innovations enter each edition. Four categories worded verbatim from the organiser''s website:

- **Transformation technologique**: "Innovations liées aux nouveaux procédés, équipements, matériaux ou systèmes transformant les modes de production industrielle"
- **Industrie responsable**
- **Innovation numérique**: "Technologies digitales au service de la performance industrielle : data, IA, logiciels, cybersécurité, automatisation, connectivité"
- **Performance et efficience industrielle**

Two additional distinctions: **Startup "Jeune Pousse"** and **Prix spécial du jury**.

Three "Voix" awards in partnership with industrial communities: **Prix Bête de Meuf** (in partnership with Les Meufs de l''Industrie), **Prix Influstriel de l''année** (in partnership with Les Influstriels), **Prix Coup de cœur du jury**.

### Satellite events

- **GI Avenir**: an employment and training programme, with 8,000 young people and jobseekers expected in 2027.
- **Goldentech**: an industrial excellence competition.
- **Booster**: an acceleration space dedicated to supporting and financing industrial startups.
- **Entrepôt Connecté**: a feature dedicated to handling and logistics.

### Community & networks

Official **MyGI** app for networking and visit planning. The trade show is co-built with the historical professional federations: Symop, FIM, Artema, UITS, Gimelec, Cetim. Recurring institutional partners: Business France, Bpifrance, ADEME, La French Fab, Alliance Industrie du Futur.

Specialist press: L''Usine Nouvelle, Industrie & Technologies, Machines Production, Production Maintenance, CAO.fr.

### What''s new for 2027

A return to Lyon after the 2026 Paris edition. Announced target: 60,000 industry professionals and 91 countries represented. The "50 industrial sectors" programme is highlighted in the pre-event communication. An announced strengthening of the industrial AI and defence strands, continuing the themes carried by the 2026 edition.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking, accommodation and shuttles: see the venue listing for [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Eurexpo halls**: 6 halls used during the 2025 Lyon edition across around 100,000 m². 2027 configuration to be confirmed by the official floor plan published on global-industrie.com before opening.
- **Visitor badge**: prior online registration on the official website (professionals only).
- **Opening hours**: to be confirmed on the official website as the event approaches.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor prices are not publicly published by GL Events Exhibitions: quotes on request via the contact page of the official website. Budgets vary widely depending on the floor space, the hall, the country pavilion or the package (Startup Booster, federation pavilions, packaged stands vs bare space).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with GL Events Exhibitions, choose the hall and scope (machine tools, subcontracting, robotics, smart industries, processing, defence).
- 9 months out: apply for the GI Awards (Transformation technologique, Industrie responsable, Innovation numérique, Performance et efficience industrielle, Startup Jeune Pousse) and confirm your package.
- 6 months out: stand brief, integration into the federation pavilions (Symop, FIM, etc.) if relevant.
- 3 months out: team accreditations, accommodation in Lyon Est (strong hotel pressure around Eurexpo in March).
- 6 weeks out: activate the MyGI app, schedule meetings, finalise demo materials (the machines and robots in operation are a strong hallmark of the trade show).

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free professional badge on prior registration.
- Allow at least 2 of the 4 days to cover the 6 halls and more than 50 sectors.
- Identify the 10 to 20 exhibitors to target in advance via the official list and the MyGI app.
- The Grande Scène programme (800+ speaking slots) forces a trade-off: select the key sessions in advance.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Global Industrie communicates on the CSR front through two main strands: the **Industrie responsable** award category (rewarding industrial solutions with reduced impact) and the **GI Avenir** programme dedicated to training and the appeal of industrial careers (8,000 young people and jobseekers hosted at the trade show).

The official website does not publish a dedicated "CSR commitments" page for the event itself at the time of writing. One to watch: the possible publication of an eco-event charter by GL Events Exhibitions ahead of the 2027 Lyon edition.

## How the trade show has evolved

