/>

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with Deutsche Messe AG or the local representative, choose the exhibition category (Automation & Digitalization, Energy & Industrial Infrastructure, Research & Technology Transfer) and decide between an individual stand and a national group pavilion.
- 9 months out: book the floor space and hall, as placement in the flagship halls is decided early.
- 6 months out: design the stand, the live demonstrations and the logistics (handling, utilities, build-up).
- 3 months out: activate press and media relations (a high density of industrial journalists), and set up decision-maker meetings.
- 6 weeks out: brief the team, prepare the demos and the multilingual materials (a very international visitor base).

### For the decision-maker attendee

- Register online at hannovermesse.de, and allow time for badge validation and proof of professional status.
- Target one or two exhibition categories in advance rather than walking the whole site: the centre is vast.
- Schedule your meetings via the trade fair''s matchmaking platform before the event; walk-ins are not very effective at this scale.
- Book accommodation very early: Hannover is saturated during the trade fair.
- Identify the partner country''s pavilion (Spain in 2027) for the official highlights and international sourcing opportunities.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Industrial sustainability is a central editorial theme of HANNOVER MESSE: the trade fair showcases industry''s solutions for decarbonised production (electrification, digitalisation, automation, renewable energy and its storage, smart energy management, hydrogen and fuel cells, the circular economy). This is a **theme carried by the exhibitors**, that is, technologies presented on the stands, rather than a certification of the event itself (source: hannovermesse.de).

The environmental commitments specific to Deutsche Messe AG as organiser (green energy at the centre, carbon-neutrality targets for operations, any ISO 20121 certification) are not documented in a verifiable way in the public sources consulted. To be confirmed with Deutsche Messe AG.

## How the trade fair has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
