### Trajectory analysis

Since 2009, Heavent Meetings has established itself as the leading one-to-one meetings event for business tourism and the events industry in Europe, organised by Weyou Group. The model rests on qualification: pre-scheduled 15-minute meetings between service providers and Top Decision Makers with verified projects, where a classic trade show relies on footfall. The 2026 edition brought together 430 stands, around 4,400 attendees per day and 11,000 business meetings on La Croisette. The 2027 edition, from 2 to 4 March at the Palais des Festivals, extends this premium positioning by drawing on the dedicated TGV trains and the concentration of decision-makers over two full days. The figures and the 2027 programme will be confirmed as the trade show approaches.', seo_title_en='Heavent Meetings Cannes 2027: dates, exhibitors, visitor info', seo_description_en='Heavent Meetings Cannes 2027: the one-to-one event for business tourism and the events industry, from 2 to 4 March at the Palais des Festivals. Exhibitors, Top Decision Makers, Heavent Awards and practical info.' WHERE slug='heavent-cannes';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for the events, live and experiential communication industry. Solutions for event organisation.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 2026 edition of Heavent Paris: 17, 18 and 19 November 2026 at the Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **Hall 4**.
- The benchmark trade show for the French events industry, running for more than 25 years: **20,000 visitors and more** at the 2025 edition, **+23% new visitors** and **490 exhibitor stands**.
- Organised by **Weyou Group** (founded in 2009, present in France, Spain and the Netherlands), which also runs Heavent Meetings Cannes.
- A structuring events programme: **Heavent Awards** (18th edition in 2026), **Heavent Festivals Awards** (4th edition in 2025, 5th edition in 2026), AI conferences, the Green Village and sector-specific themed zones.
- Exhibitor pricing on bespoke quotation (form on weyou-group.com): no public rate card, with six themed villages to choose from.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Six themed zones organise the halls by sector: **Village Diffuseurs & Agents d''artistes** (broadcasters and artist agents), **Espace Services Festivals** (festival services), **Green Village** (players in eco-responsibility and the circular economy), **IMDA** (International MICE Destination Area), **Village Start-ups** and **Espace Digital & Nouvelles Technologies** (digital and new technologies).

Exhibitor categories represented: event agencies, organisers, technical service providers, set designers, producers, reception venues, caterers, DMCs, international hotels and institutional MICE players.

### Notable exhibitors

Full list on the official website: [heavent-paris.com/liste-exposants](https://www.heavent-paris.com/liste-exposants). The 2026 list is updated as registrations come in.

### Quality of visitors

- Strictly professional visitors (proof of employed or self-employed activity required).
- 20,000 visitors and more announced in 2025, including **23% new visitors**.
- Dominant profile: agency decision-makers, advertisers, communications and events departments, MICE buyers, festivals and cultural institutions.

## Activities & community

### Heavent Awards

The benchmark awards for the French professional events sector, **18th edition in 2025**. The 2026 edition is scheduled for **25 and 26 March 2026** at the Palais des Festivals in Cannes (paired with Heavent Meetings).

Results of the 18th edition: **154 entries submitted, 58 finalists, 33 winners**. The roll of honour is structured into 1st, 2nd and 3rd prizes per category (BtoC, Influence and Press Relations, BtoB, Internal Communications, Incentive Travel, Fashion Beauty Luxury, Exceptional Ceremony).

**Roll of honour, 18th edition (excerpts)**:

- **1st prize BtoC**: European premiere of *Avatar Fire and Ash* (Euphoriques for Disney).
- **2nd prize BtoC**: BMW iX3 showcase (Auditoire for BMW).
- **3rd prize BtoC**: Magnum Oasis Garden of Senses (Skudras Metropole for Unilever Baltic).
- **1st prize Influence and PR**: *Fragiles Impact* show at VivaTech (Havas Events for the Antoine Alléno association).
- **2nd prize Influence and PR**: 50 years of La Roche-Posay.

For the record, the 17th edition in 2025 honoured **Thierry Reboul** (artistic director of Creation, Branding and Ceremonies for Paris 2024) and **Paname 24** (a consortium of Auditoire, Double 2, Havas Events, Obo, Ubi) with a **Decade Award** for the Olympic Games opening ceremony.

### Heavent Festivals Awards

Awards dedicated to festivals (music, culture, sport, regional events), created in 2022. **4th edition in 2025**, **5th edition in 2026** at the show. The awards ceremony is scheduled for **Wednesday 18 November 2026 at 8:30 pm** as part of the official programme. Eleven categories spread across festival sizes, a Green prize, a VIP area, France and international scopes, and safety-prevention.

### Plenary conferences and AI programme

A conference programme featuring advertisers, agencies and specialists: content innovation, hybrid formats, digital, generative AI applied to events, sustainable stands and eco-design. The official programme is published by Weyou Group from the autumn preceding the show.

### Heavent Party

A **networking evening** held on **Wednesday 18 November from 7 pm** at the show. A long-standing Heavent Paris format and the anchor point for informal encounters between agencies, advertisers and service providers.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) page.

Specific to the show:

- **Hall location**: Hall 4.
- **2026 edition opening hours**:
  - Tuesday 17 November: 10 am to 10 pm.
  - Wednesday 18 November: 10 am to 7 pm, then the **Heavent Party from 7 pm**.
  - Thursday 19 November: 10 am to 5 pm.
- **Visitor badge**: free with online registration and proof of professional activity.
- **Organiser contact**: Weyou Group, contact@weyou-group.com.

## How much it costs to exhibit

No public rate card. Weyou Group sends a **bespoke quotation** via the form available on weyou-group.com, depending on the chosen themed village, the desired floor space and the level of fit-out (bare stand, equipped, package, start-up formula).

Formulas confirmed by the organiser:

- **Bare Stand** (floor space only).
- **Equipped Stand** (carpet, partitions, LED lighting).
- **Package Stand** (full fit-out).
- **Village Start-ups** (affordable rate, dedicated space).
- **IMDA** (DMCs, hotels, international MICE players).
- **Green Village** (eco-responsible stand).

A quotation request is recommended 9 to 12 months before the show to secure the best locations.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with Weyou Group, choose your positioning among the six themed villages.
- 9 months out: apply for the Heavent Awards (the call for entries calendar is published each summer).
- 6 months out: finalise your stand according to the chosen formula (Bare, Equipped, Package, Start-up, IMDA, Green Village).
- 3 months out: team briefing, programme of activities, preparation for Wednesday evening''s Heavent Party.
- 6 weeks out: activate digital materials, prospect mailings, book meetings via the official platform.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Online registration is mandatory, with proof of professional activity.
- Tuesday 17 November: the longest day (10 am to 10 pm), a busy slot for end-of-day networking.
- Wednesday 18 November evening: Heavent Party from 7 pm, Heavent Festivals Awards ceremony at 8:30 pm.
- Allow at least one full day to cover the six themed villages.

## CSR policy & initiatives

The show features a **Green Village** dedicated to players in eco-responsibility, the circular economy and low-carbon-footprint solutions for event production. The conference programme includes sessions on sustainable stands and eco-design. The Heavent Festivals Awards include a **Greenest Festival** prize.

Across Weyou Group, CSR/ESG partnerships are published on the websites of the group''s other events (notably Heavent Meetings Cannes). No specific ISO 20121 certification is mentioned to date for Heavent Paris.

## How the show has evolved

