HopitalExpo has evolved from a single-pavilion trade show dedicated to hospital equipment in 1985 into a thematic pavilion within a multi-sector umbrella (SantExpo). This integration has enabled the pavilion to capture a broadened visitor base (medico-social, digital health) while retaining its historic DNA: public hospital management, biomedical equipment suppliers, HIS. The Trophées Innovation Fonds FHF maintain strong editorial visibility for equipment and operating-theatre exhibitors, a direct legacy of the original Trophées HopitalExpo.', seo_title_en='HopitalExpo 2027 - SantExpo hospital pavilion at Paris Porte de Versailles', seo_description_en='HopitalExpo 2027: 25 to 27 May at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, Hall 1. The pavilion dedicated to public hospital management, biomedical equipment suppliers and HIS publishers, within SantExpo organised by the FHF and GL Events.' WHERE slug='hopital-expo-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Hydrogen trade show. Hydrogen technologies, fuel cells, energy storage and hydrogen mobility.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Hyvolution is the only trade show in Europe to cover the entire hydrogen value chain, from producers to industrial players, including local authorities and investors, all on a single floor.
- 41% of exhibitors at the 2025 edition were newcomers: the market is still taking shape, and first-time exhibitors are not lost in a crowd of established players.
- The official rate for an equipped stand in the collective pavilion is 825 € excl. VAT/m² (from 6 m²), plus 1,200 € excl. VAT in registration fees and 400 € excl. VAT per corner: public rates, a rarity in the sector.
- 25% of 2024 visitors were senior executives and 23% were international: a decision-maker visitor base, dense with high-authority contacts.
- 10th anniversary edition in 2026 (under the high patronage of the President of the Republic). 2025 attendance: **15,300 visitors**, i.e. **+3%** vs 2024 (11,503), with 12 international pavilions and 65 countries represented (source: organiser''s review press release).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A 100% sector-specific trade show, with no presence outside hydrogen. The exhibitor base covers the entire value chain: major industrial groups (Air Liquide, TotalEnergies, Engie, Plastic Omnium), specialised mid-caps and SMEs, deeptech startups, local and regional authorities, research bodies and federations. The 3 target markets (mobility, industry, energy production) are evenly balanced across the 6 thematic itineraries for 2026.

### Notable exhibitors

Air Liquide, TotalEnergies, Engie, Plastic Omnium, McPhy Energy, Linde, Nel Hydrogen, Symbio (Michelin/Faurecia), John Cockerill, Gaussin. 13 CAC 40 groups present in 2023.

### Retention rate

59% of exhibitors are returning (the inverse of the 41% newcomers). A strong foothold for long-standing players who regard Hyvolution as their must-attend annual fixture.

### Visitor quality

Exclusively professional, no general public. 25% senior executives and 23% international at the 2024 edition, with more than 10,500 participants in the conferences and workshops. A highly qualified visitor base, directly involved in the hydrogen value chain.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

4 high-level plenary conferences in 2025 (themes: Mobility, Industry, Financing, Market design) plus 120 exhibitor and partner workshops in a short 20-minute format. Format: Hyvolution Theater (plenaries) plus 3 thematic Forums.

### Awards & accolades

<DataMissing />

### Satellite events

Hyvolution Summit (3rd edition in 2025): a strategic summit bringing together the political and economic leaders of the sector. Exhibitor Happy Hour at the end of Day 2 (VIP Club). Employment and training campus (job dating, TV studio, jobs wall). Presentation of the European hydrogen index by EY.

### Community & networks

France Hydrogène (460 members): a structuring partner, with 14 regional delegations active throughout the year. 15 national hydrogen associations represented. Regional pavilions (Occitanie, Brittany, Île-de-France, etc.) and 12 international pavilions. Platforms: Hyvolution Connect (matchmaking), Hyvolution Hub (post-show replays). Official iOS/Android app.

### What''s new in 2026

Hyvolution Paris 2026: 27-29 January 2026, Porte de Versailles. Roll-out of the international network (France, Chile, Canada). 6 structured thematic itineraries: production, mobility, industry, infrastructure, carbon, optimisation.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **single Hall 1** (~25,000 m², a signature move for the 10th anniversary edition, source: organiser + CCI 77).
- **Transport access**: Metro L12 (Porte de Versailles) or L8 (Balard). Tram T2/T3a. January: allow for weather disruptions when travelling between halls.
- **Parking**: Parc des Expositions car park on site, paid. Viparis encourages soft mobility (CSR approach).
- **Accommodation**: Convention-Vaugirard (15th arr.) and Issy-les-Moulineaux area. January is a quieter period than June: booking lead times are less tight. Booking ahead is still advisable for the best rates.
- **Opening hours**: 9am-6pm across the 3 days. Set-up: to be confirmed with GL events (generally the day before and the morning of Day 1).
- **Services**: Catering on site. VIP Club (exhibitor access). Thematic Forum areas. Employment and training campus. Hyvolution Paris app (iOS/Android).

## How much it costs to exhibit

