### Trajectory analysis

Hyvolution is the fastest-growing of the three pilot listings, rising from 4,500 to 15,000 visitors in 3 years. This momentum is directly tied to the political and industrial acceleration of the hydrogen sector in Europe. Worth noting: the slight drop in exhibitor numbers between 2024 (572) and 2025 (550) deserves attention, possibly reflecting market consolidation or greater selectivity by the organiser. The 41% of new exhibitors offset this figure and confirm an active turnover.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='hyvolution-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Bathroom trade show. Design, equipment, wellbeing and innovations for the world of the bathroom.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Idéobain is the trade show for the bathroom and wellbeing, one of the shows within the Mondial du Bâtiment, co-located with Batimat and Interclima at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles → exhibiting at Idéobain means targeting the bathroom sector within a major construction event, with a shared badge.
- 166 Idéobain exhibitors in 2024, of which 83 were newcomers, a +36% increase vs 2022 (source: Batiweb) → strong renewal dynamics in the exhibitor offering for this segment.
- No attendance figure specific to Idéobain: the organiser only publishes the overall attendance of the Mondial du Bâtiment (135,944 visitors in 2024, across all shows combined, source: Batiweb, Le Moniteur) → do not attribute this figure to Idéobain alone.
- Organised by RX France, on a biennial rhythm in even years, with the afisb (the bathroom industry trade body) as co-organiser.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Bathroom and sanitaryware manufacturers, designers, architects, installers, distributors, specifiers and institutional bodies (source: ideobain.com).

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [ideobain.com](https://www.ideobain.com/fr-fr.html).

### Quality of the visitor base

Visitor base shared with the Mondial du Bâtiment (Batimat, Interclima), predominantly French and specifier-led. No breakdown specific to Idéobain published.

## Programme & community

### Conference programme

Forum Idéobain: pitches, conferences, workshops and round tables. 2024 themes: "step-free showers", "water savings, where do we stand?". Guided tours for architects and designers, a networking zone and an art exhibition (sources: ideobain.com, Sdbpro).

### Awards & accolades

Innovation Awards, bathroom category: 29 entries in 2024, 8 nominees, 3 winners (Gold: Burgbad, CleanFlow trap; Silver: Nobili; Bronze: Geberit, AquaClean Alba WC). Entries for 2026 now open (source: Sdbpro, Le Moniteur).

### Community & networks

Show integrated into the Mondial du Bâtiment alongside Batimat, Interclima and Renodays (2026 line-up). Specialist bathroom and sanitaryware press in attendance.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Show-specific:

- **Visitor badge:** show reserved for professionals, with shared access across the Mondial du Bâtiment shows (a single badge for Batimat, Interclima, Idéobain). Online registration recommended (source: batimat.com).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published: quote on request from RX France. As Idéobain is organised by RX France within the Mondial du Bâtiment, the per-m² ranges are likely close to those of Batimat (€250-400/m² for space only in 2026, source: cimbat.com via the Batimat lead), to be confirmed by a direct Idéobain quote.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 18 months out: initial contact with RX France, application for the Innovation Awards.
- 12 months out: stand concept sign-off, contractor brief.
- 6 months out: stand plan, build order.
- 3 months out: accreditations, accommodation (Mondial du Bâtiment demand is high, book early).
- 6 weeks out: delivery of materials, activation of the Mondial du Bâtiment app.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- The badge unlocks access to the Mondial du Bâtiment shows: plan your route accordingly (Idéobain + Batimat + Interclima).
- Target the Forum Idéobain and the products that won at the Innovation Awards.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Idéobain''s CSR focuses on water and materials: water saving (a recurring Forum theme, "water savings, where do we stand?"), economy of materials and adaptation to ageing (accessibility, step-free showers) were all highlighted in 2024.

The show sets out its commitments on its dedicated page [Our commitments](https://www.ideobain.com/fr-fr/le-salon/nos-engagements.html), underpinned by [RX''s sustainability policy](https://rxglobal.com/sustainability).

## How the show has evolved

<HistoryTable
