/>

### Trajectory analysis

Idéobain saw strong growth in its exhibitor offering in 2024 (166 exhibitors, +36% vs 2022, of which 83 were newcomers), a sign of renewed appeal for the bathroom segment within the Mondial du Bâtiment. The absence of attendance figures specific to the show limits how clearly the visitor dynamics can be read. One to watch for 2026: the impact of the "Mondial du Bâtiment" rebranding and of the new line-up (the arrival of Renodays) on Idéobain''s visibility.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='ideobain';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Professional travel trade show. Destinations, tour operators, airlines, hospitality and travel technology.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 48th edition of IFTM Top Resa: **15 to 17 September 2026** (Tuesday to Thursday) at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **Pavilion 1**.
- Opening hours: 9.30am to 7pm on Tuesday and Wednesday, 9.30am to 5pm on Thursday (early close).
- **Guest destination 2026: Uzbekistan**, a showcase programmed by the organiser RX France to capitalise on a trajectory that has risen from 2M international visitors in 2016 to **11.7M in 2025** (Samarkand, Bukhara and Khiva listed by UNESCO, the Afrosiyob train, Uzbekistan Airways flights from Paris, new Tashkent-Warsaw, Tashkent-Atyrau and Tashkent-New Delhi routes, and the Amirsoy and Beldersoy winter resorts).
- Editorial theme 2026: **"The value of travel: together, let''s reveal what creates impact"**, the common thread running through the conferences, workshops and awards.
- 2025 review (updated iftm.fr figures): **32,022 trade visitors**, **1,400 exhibitors**, **177 destinations**, **1,650 brands**, **16,725 business meetings** generated via the Everywhere matchmaking platform (+28% versus the 13,000+ initially announced).
- Editorial and strategic management: **Marie Allantaz** is leading the 2026 edition.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

IFTM Top Resa is the annual business gathering for leisure and business tourism in France. The offering is structured around **11 themed villages** that cover the entire travel value chain:

- **Destination France**: regional, departmental and territorial tourist boards.
- **Tour Operators**: generalist and specialist TOs, packagers, incoming agencies.
- **Cruise**: sea and river cruise lines.
- **Orchestra Start-Up Village**: travel tech startups (in partnership with Orchestra).
- **Parks**: theme parks, wildlife parks, leisure parks.
- **Media**: specialist press, B2B and B2C travel media.
- **Mountain**: resorts, ski operators, four-season tourism.
- **Business Club**: MICE, business travel, seminars, incentive.
- **Networks**: travel agency franchises and networks.
- **Coach Operators**: group coach tourism operators.
- **Sustainable Initiatives by mN''Organisation**: 300 m² dedicated to the sector''s transition.

### Quality of the visitor base

- **32,022 trade visitors** in 2025 (official iftm.fr figure).
- Decision-maker profiles: agency general management, TO production managers, MICE buyers, network and franchise executives, specialist journalists, tourism students in training (FFTST).
- Strictly trade-only visitor base, with online pre-registration requiring proof of activity.
- Strong international density: **177 destinations** represented in 2025, **1,650 brands**.

## Events and community

### National Group Tourism Convention

An unprecedented collaboration between **Atout France**, **FNTV** (Fédération Nationale des Transports de Voyageurs), **Destination Régions**, **Tourisme & Territoires** and **Offices Tourisme France**. A professional convention format focused on group tourism, a segment being repositioned after the Covid years.

### Travel Agents Cup and Travel Agents Cup Junior

The trade show''s emblematic competition, open to travel advisers. The junior edition is dedicated to tourism students in training. The event is hosted by **Sophie Jovillard** across the three days, in a highly visible stage format.

### Business Travel Awards

Awards produced by **Eventiz Media Group** and **Deplacementspros.com**, dedicated to the business travel segment (TMCs, business travel buying, suppliers). The **Marco Polo Grand Prize** honours the French business travel personality of the year.

### Startup Contest and Hackathon

Programming delivered by the **Orchestra Start-Up Village**. The Startup Contest rewards the most innovative young travel tech firm. The Hackathon brings together developers and product profiles around a challenge defined with the trade show''s technology partners.

### Business Club and Everywhere matchmaking

The **Business Club** structures the MICE and business travel dimension. The **Everywhere** platform orchestrates pre-scheduled business meetings: **16,725 meetings** generated in 2025, up 28% versus the previous edition (updated iftm.fr figure). It is the show''s most measurable ROI tool on the exhibitor side.

### Tourism Students'' Day

Co-organised with the **FFTST** (Fédération Française des Techniciens et Scientifiques du Tourisme). It brings together the cohorts of French tourism schools for a day dedicated to recruitment, careers conferences and orientation.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Pavilion**: 1.
- **Opening hours**: 9.30am to 7pm on Tuesday 15 and Wednesday 16 September, 9.30am to 5pm on Thursday 17 September (early close).
- **Visitor badge**: online pre-registration is mandatory, with progressive pricing depending on the purchase date (see below).
- **Free** for journalists, teachers and students on registration with supporting documentation.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published. Quotes are available on request from RX France via iftm.fr/exposer. The themed villages (Destination France, Tour Operators, Cruise, Orchestra Start-Up, Parks, Media, Mountain, Business Club, Networks, Coach Operators, Sustainable Initiatives) determine placement and the rate per m². Several formats traditionally exist: bare stand, fitted stand, turnkey packaged stand, and dedicated startup formats on the Orchestra Start-Up Village.

### Visitor rates 2026 (progressive)

- **€50 incl. VAT** until 31 May 2026.
- **€80 incl. VAT** from 1 June to 10 July 2026.
- **€130 incl. VAT** from 11 July to 14 September 2026.
- **€210 incl. VAT** on site, from 15 to 17 September 2026.
- **Premium Pass: €450 incl. VAT**, limited to 50 people. Includes inter-visitor business meetings, a half-day table and VIP Club access for 2 people.
- **Free** for journalists, teachers and students on registration.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: initial contact with RX France, choice of themed village from the 11 available.
- 9 months out: entry to the awards if relevant (Travel Agents Cup on the agency side, Business Travel Awards on the business travel side, Startup Contest on the travel tech side).
- 6 months out: finalising the stand, briefing the contractor, setting the Everywhere matchmaking strategy.
- 3 months out: opening of Everywhere business meetings on the schedule, preparation of trilingual sales materials.
- 6 weeks out: activating the partner network (Atout France, FNTV, ATD depending on profile), press materials, and a plan of pre-scheduled visits with targeted buyers.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Mandatory online pre-registration before 14 September to avoid the €210 on-site rate.
- Buy before 31 May to benefit from the entry rate of €50.
- 11 villages to explore: allow **2 days minimum** to cover your target and activate the Everywhere meetings.
- Thursday 17 September: a shorter day (close at 5pm), ideal for closing meetings.
- For business travel profiles: target the Business Club and the Business Travel Awards ceremony.

## Policy and CSR initiatives

The **Sustainable Initiatives Village**, a 300 m² space designed and run by **mN''Organisation**, structures the trade show''s CSR offering. It is made up of three recurring features:

- The **Durability Club**, a peer-club format focused on the operational side of the transition.
- The **Tree of Commitments**, a scenographic device for visitors and exhibitors to make pledges.
- The **Gaming Space**, a sustainable-practice self-assessment tool designed for TOs and agencies.

The village''s long-standing partner is **ATD** (Acteurs du Tourisme Durable), which runs 3 days of conferences at the venue. The organiser cites a framing figure: **71% of French people say they want to travel more responsibly**.

## The trade show''s evolution

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" },
 { "key": "theme", "label": "Theme or guest destination" },
