 ]}
 sources="iftm.fr, RX France"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

IFTM Top Resa has been the major annual business gathering for French tourism since 1979. Founded in Deauville under the name **Top Resa** in the tradition of the great American shows such as Pow Wow, it moved to **Paris Expo Porte de Versailles in 2008** and then took its current name, **IFTM Top Resa** (International French Travel Market), in **2009**. The 2025 edition confirmed a mature format: 32,022 trade visitors, 1,400 exhibitors, 177 destinations, 1,650 brands, and above all **16,725 business meetings** via Everywhere, up 28% versus the 13,000+ initially announced, a sign of matchmaking that is gaining substance. The 2026 edition builds on two levers. First, the **Uzbekistan guest destination**, a choice that reads clearly against the news (a sixfold rise in international visitors between 2016 and 2025, 11.7M in 2025, new air route openings, and an upgrade in hotel standards). Second, the **National Group Tourism Convention** in collaboration with Atout France / FNTV / Destination Régions / Tourisme & Territoires / Offices Tourisme France, which structures a group segment being repositioned post-Covid. The theme **"The value of travel: together, let''s reveal what creates impact"** consolidates a CSR editorial line already championed by the Sustainable Initiatives Village and the long-standing ATD partnership.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='iftm-top-resa';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International Luxury Travel Market: the world''s benchmark marketplace for luxury travel, by invitation only, structured around pre-scheduled business appointments between qualified buyers and premium brands. Organised by RX (Reed Exhibitions).', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **ILTM Cannes** (International Luxury Travel Market) is the world''s benchmark gathering for luxury travel: an annual, invitation-only marketplace entirely structured around pre-scheduled business appointments between qualified buyers and premium brands.
- Organiser and owner of the event: **RX** (Reed Exhibitions). Official tagline: "Live fast. Live big."
- Next edition: **30 November to 3 December 2026** at the [Palais des Festivals et des Congrès de Cannes](/lieux/palais-des-festivals-cannes). This is the 25th edition (the series began in 2002).
- Results from the 24th edition (1 to 4 December 2025, figures published by RX): nearly **10,000 participants**, more than **2,500 buyers** from 83 countries, more than **2,350 brands**, and more than **100,000 appointments** scheduled, a **12%** year-on-year increase.
- "The Sail": a pavilion dedicated to cruise, yachting and river travel, introduced at the 2025 edition.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Luxury hotels and resorts, cruise and yachting companies, tourist boards and destinations, destination management companies (DMCs), bespoke experience operators and premium lifestyle brands. On the demand side, the attendees are luxury travel buyers: advisers and agencies specialising in itineraries for very high-net-worth clients, alongside around a hundred editors and journalists from the luxury press.

ILTM Cannes operates as a closed marketplace: all participants (exhibitors, buyers, media) are pre-approved and registered by RX. It is not a trade show open to the general public.

### Notable exhibitors

Exhibitor list and online directory on the official website: [iltm.com/cannes](https://www.iltm.com/cannes). At the 2025 edition, more than 2,350 brands from luxury hospitality, destinations and experiences were present, with strong international representation.

### Quality of attendees

- More than 2,500 buyers from 83 countries at the 2025 edition, of which 44% were first-time participants
- To be accredited as a buyer, eligibility criteria are published on the official website ([iltm.com/cannes](https://www.iltm.com/cannes)): international activity in luxury travel and verifiable references with RX
- Strong presence of decision-makers: senior management, hotel owners and sales directors of premium brands

## Events & community

### Conference programme

ILTM Cannes offers a programme of conferences and educational sessions alongside the business appointments, including the Opening Forum devoted to the major trends in luxury travel. Recent themes have covered regenerative tourism, responsible travel, wellness and longevity, cruise and global hotel expansion. The detailed 2026 programme is published as the trade show approaches.

### Community and networks

The heart of the event rests on the pre-scheduled appointments: each buyer selects and ranks their preferences from among the exhibitors, and the system matches both parties'' choices ahead of the show to generate the confirmed appointments.

The programme is accompanied by networking events and evening receptions, and welcomes more than a hundred editors and journalists from specialist luxury media.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Palais des Festivals et des Congrès de Cannes](/lieux/palais-des-festivals-cannes).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Access:** invitation and prior accreditation only. Exhibitors, buyers and media must be approved by RX before the show.
- **Accommodation and transfers:** RX offers an accommodation booking service and free transfers for exhibitors.
- **Appointments:** the pre-scheduled appointments are generated by a preference-matching system; buyers select and rank the exhibitors to meet via the dedicated portal.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published on the official website. Participation is by application and approval by RX via the exhibitor portal ([iltm.com/cannes](https://www.iltm.com/cannes)). Figures not publicly available.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with RX and apply through the exhibitor portal, choose your positioning (hospitality, destination, cruise via the "The Sail" pavilion, experiences).
- 6 months out: prepare the stand and materials, sales brief on the priority buyer markets.
- 4 weeks out: finalise the schedule of pre-scheduled appointments once the RX matching is confirmed.
- 2 weeks out: confirm key appointments and prepare product demonstrations.

### For the buyer

- Buyer application on the official website, with supporting evidence of activity in luxury travel.
- Once accredited, select and rank the exhibitors to meet in the dedicated portal, within the set deadline.
- Allow for all four days of the show to maximise the number of pre-scheduled appointments.
- Target the Opening Forum sessions and the conference programme in advance.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

ILTM Cannes is part of RX''s sustainability approach, framed by the **RX Sustainability Roadmap**. RX is a founding member of the Net Zero Carbon Events initiative and is committed to reaching **Net Zero by 2040**.

RX works with its suppliers and exhibitors to embed sustainability at every stage of the event. The detail of the focus areas and quantified commitments is available at [rxglobal.com/sustainability](https://rxglobal.com/sustainability). No ISO 20121 certification specific to ILTM Cannes is mentioned to date.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "exposants", "label": "Brands", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
 { "edition": "2026 (25th, upcoming)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" },
 { "edition": "2025 (24th)", "visiteurs": "~10,000", "exposants": "2,350+" }
 ]}
 sources="iltm.com, traveldailynews.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

The 2025 edition, the 24th, set a record for the event: nearly 10,000 participants, more than 2,500 buyers from 83 countries and more than 100,000 appointments scheduled, up 12% year on year. This momentum confirms ILTM Cannes''s position as the leading global hub for luxury travel at year end. The 2026 edition, marking the 25th anniversary, will take place from 30 November to 3 December at the Palais des Festivals et des Congrès de Cannes, building on the "The Sail" cruise pavilion introduced last year. Target figures for 2026 will be published as the show approaches.', seo_title_en='ILTM Cannes 2026: global luxury travel marketplace (30 Nov-3 Dec)', seo_description_en='ILTM Cannes 2026, 25th edition from 30 November to 3 December at the Palais des Festivals. The global luxury travel marketplace organised by RX: qualified buyers, pre-scheduled appointments, premium hospitality and cruise.' WHERE slug='iltm-cannes';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Robotics zone within SIDO Lyon, France''s meeting point for the convergence of IoT, AI, XR and robotics. SIDO 2025 review (Innorobo relaunch): 380 exhibitors, ~9,000 trade visitors, 60 conferences.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Innorobo by SIDO is **the dedicated robotics zone within SIDO Lyon**, France''s meeting point for the convergence of IoT, AI, XR and robotics. Not a standalone trade show: since the 2025 relaunch, Innorobo has been integrated into the SIDO village and addresses industrial, mobile and collaborative robotics as well as embedded AI.
- 2026: **16 and 17 September 2026** (Wednesday-Thursday) at the [Centre de Congrès de Lyon - Cité Internationale](/lieux/centre-de-congres-de-lyon), 50 quai Charles de Gaulle, 69006 Lyon. Consolidated SIDO-wide targets: **8,000 trade visitors**, **300+ exhibitors**, **70 conferences**, **210 experts** over 2 days.
- 2025 edition review (relaunch, 17-18 September, 11th SIDO edition): **380 exhibitors**, **~9,000 trade visitors**, **60 conferences**, **200+ speakers**. First Innorobo by SIDO edition after a 6-year Innorobo hiatus.
- 2026 co-location confirmed: **SIDO** (IoT, AI, XR, robotics), **IMPACT by SIDO** (responsible digital technology), **Lyon Cyber Expo** (cybersecurity). A density unmatched in France: industry + IoT + AI + cyber + responsible digital + robotics over 2 days.
- Organiser: **Infopro Digital Trade Shows (IPDTS)**. Infopro Digital acquired Innorobo''s assets in 2018 to preserve its legacy, then relaunched the brand in 2025 under the SIDO Lyon umbrella.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Innorobo by SIDO addresses the entire robotics and embedded-AI value chain, with an industrial convergence angle:

- **Articulated robots** and industrial manipulator arms.
- **Cobotics**: collaborative robots for industry, assembly and logistics.
- **Mobile robots**: AMRs, AGVs, service robotics, intralogistics.
- **Critical components**: actuators, motors, sensors, vision, gripping, geared motors.
- **Integrated intelligent systems**: robotics integrators, digital twins, simulation, MES.
- **Embedded AI (Edge AI / Physical AI)**: embedded vision, lightweight models, real-time inference, sensor fusion.

On the applications side, the Innorobo zone targets: **manufacturing**, **logistics**, **medical**, **mobility**, **retail** and the **public sector**. By design, the SIDO co-location broadens the audience to IoT, AI, cybersecurity and responsible-digital decision-makers, that is, the entire technology stack of a smart-factory project.

### Notable exhibitors in the 2025 Innorobo zone

Identified during the 2025 relaunch:

- **AICA**: intelligence for adaptive industrial robotics.
- **Maxon**: precision motorisation and drives, a long-standing benchmark in robotics.
- **Enchanted Tools**: humanoid service robotics, a French start-up with international visibility.
- **OnRobot**: grippers and tooling for cobots, an open ecosystem.
- **Faulhaber**: precision micromotors and miniature drives.
- **Innodura**: industrial robotics solutions.

Confirmed ecosystem partners: **Coboteam** (French cobotics network), **Robotics Valley** (robotics cluster), **pôle CIMES** (competitiveness cluster for engineering, mechatronics and systems).

### Quality of the visitor base

SIDO 2025''s visitor base was announced at ~9,000 professionals, with a 2026 target raised to 8,000 trade visitors consolidated across the entire village (SIDO + Innorobo + IMPACT + Lyon Cyber Expo). Dominant profile: **industrial players** (factory, methods, maintenance and R&D management), **robotics integrators**, **technical management** (IT, OT, automation), **industrial purchasing**, **technical executives** at SMEs/mid-caps, **academic research** and **robotics start-ups**. The convergence with SIDO and Lyon Cyber Expo additionally attracts IoT, AI and industrial cybersecurity profiles (ISA/IEC 62443, OT security), who are the natural counterparts for a connected-robotics project.

## Activities & community

### 2026 conference format

The programme unfolds across the 4 co-located events, with an overall target of **70 conferences** and **210 experts** on the SIDO 2026 side. The Innorobo zone''s themes extend SIDO''s editorial threads on:

1. **Industrial robotics and cobotics**: factory deployment, ROI, integration into existing lines.
2. **Mobile robotics and logistics**: AMRs/AGVs, intralogistics, service robotics.
3. **Embedded AI and Physical AI**: vision, sensor fusion, lightweight edge models, sim-to-real transfer.
4. **Critical components and integrated systems**: actuators, sensors, digital twins.

Mixed formats: plenary conferences, industrial case studies, on-stand demos, start-up sessions, integrator workshops.

### Convergence with SIDO, IMPACT and Lyon Cyber Expo

This is the specificity claimed since the 2025 relaunch: a single badge grants access to all of the content.

- **SIDO**: convergence of IoT, AI, XR and robotics. It is the benchmark French trade show for Industry 4.0 technologies.
- **IMPACT by SIDO**: responsible digital technology, eco-design, frugality, life cycle. Relevant for CSR and responsible-purchasing functions.
- **Lyon Cyber Expo**: OT and IT cybersecurity, a critical topic for any connected robotics.

The takeaway: no other French robotics trade show offers this density of industry + IoT + AI + cyber + responsible digital + robotics over 2 days.

### Partners and ecosystem

The ecosystem underpinning the Innorobo zone relies on recognised sector bodies: **Coboteam**, **Robotics Valley**, **pôle CIMES**. This foundation sets Innorobo by SIDO apart from more generalist robotics events by giving it a French sector anchoring (notably in Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes, France''s leading industrial basin for mechatronics).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Centre de Congrès de Lyon - Cité Internationale](/lieux/centre-de-congres-de-lyon).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates and opening hours**: 16 and 17 September 2026 (Wednesday-Thursday), 2-day format.
- **Venue**: Centre de Congrès de Lyon - Cité Internationale, 50 quai Charles de Gaulle, 69006 Lyon. The site adjoins the Parc de la Tête d''Or and the Rhône, 15 minutes from the Part-Dieu centre.
- **B2B visitor access**: **free with professional pre-registration** (online badge at sido-lyon.com). **€50 excl. VAT** without pre-registration. Proof of professional activity required (industry, IT/OT, innovation).
- **Official website**: sido-lyon.com (canonical). The former sido-event.com domain redirects.
- **Digital platform**: programme, floor plan and matchmaking on sido-lyon.com.

