### Trajectory analysis

Innov-Agri Ondes 2026 is the 33rd edition of a benchmark French agricultural-machinery trade show, launched 35 years ago according to NGPA. The "open-field" model (80 ha of real-world demonstrations) remains the differentiating feature compared with indoor-hall trade shows (SIMA, now redeployed in an intermittent format). The Outarville / Ondes rotation, established for more than 15 years, structures two distinct farming basins: cereal production in the Centre-Loiret and mixed crop-livestock farming in the South-West.

The 33rd edition is part of a period of strategic expansion led by Hervé Noiret (CEO, Groupe NGPA): the launch of the Hauts-de-France format in Essigny-le-Grand in June 2025, a return to Saint-Quentin in 2027, then a broader rotation to other regions from 2028 onwards. The Ondes format remains the South-West benchmark within this expanded calendar, with a focus on agroecology, robotics and new-energy issues already deployed in 2024 and repeated for 2026.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='innov-agri-ondes';
