UPDATE salons SET description_en='International trade fair for lingerie, swimwear and apparel fabrics. Sourcing of raw materials, lace and embroidery.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Interfilière Paris** is the leading international trade show for sourcing materials, accessories and textile innovations for lingerie, swimwear and activewear. Founded in **1963**, it is owned by **Eurovet** (jointly held by the Fédération de la Maille, de la Lingerie & du Balnéaire and the Comexposium group) and operated by **Groupe WSN** since 2022, under the "Eurovet by WSN" banner.
- **Biannual** rhythm: two editions per year, one in January and one in September, at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles.
- Next edition: **5 to 7 September 2026** at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. The following edition is announced for 16 to 18 January 2027.
- The trade show is co-located with WSN''s fashion and lingerie ecosystem at Porte de Versailles: [Who''s Next](/salons/whos-next-paris) and [Bijorhca](/salons/bijorhca-paris) for the fashion and accessories segment are co-located across both cycles (September and January); Curve Paris for the lingerie and swimwear segment is co-located during the September cycle.
- Strictly trade-only audience: buyers, collection managers, designers and design studios from lingerie, swimwear and fashion brands.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Interfilière brings together **upstream suppliers** from across the industry: lace and embroidery manufacturers, weavers and knitters, suppliers of technical fabrics and elastics, accessory makers (underwires, hooks, cups, ribbons), threads, dyes and finishes, as well as sourcing and manufacturing service providers. Since 2025, the offering has broadened to include more suppliers for the fashion and accessories sectors.

Not to be confused with a finished-brand trade fair: lingerie and swimwear brands (Chanel, Calvin Klein, Hermès, Victoria''s Secret, Skims, among others cited by the organiser) are here as **trade buyers**, not exhibitors.

### Notable exhibitors

Exhibitor list and floor plan on the official website: [interfiliere.com](https://www.interfiliere.com). The number of exhibitors is not officially published by the organiser; no figure is reproduced here.

### Quality of the visitor base

- Strongly international visitor base: the official website reports more than 16,000 professionals at the January edition, a figure combined with the co-located Salon International de la Lingerie, of which around 60% are international.
- Decision-making profiles on the upstream side: materials buyers, collection managers, designers, design studios and specialist journalists.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The trade show offers a programme of conferences, technical workshops, trend forums and networking spaces, built around materials innovation, responsible sourcing and seasonal trends. The detailed 2026 programme is published in the run-up to the show on the official website.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** reserved for industry professionals, by prior online registration via the official website. Proof of professional activity is required.
- **Co-location:** a single badge grants access to the co-located trade shows of the Eurovet by WSN ecosystem over the same period (to be confirmed for each edition on interfiliere.com).

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with the WSN teams, choose your positioning (materials, lace and embroidery, accessories, sourcing).
- 6 months out: prepare collections and material samples to present to design studios.
- 3 months out: schedule meetings with buyers and collection managers.
- 6 weeks out: finalise the stand and the commercial brief for your target markets (lingerie, swimwear, activewear, fashion).

### For the decision-making visitor

- Pre-register online at interfiliere.com with proof of professional status.
- Identify the trend forums and conferences in advance to structure your sourcing visit.
- Make the most of the co-location to cover both the upstream side (Interfilière) and the downstream side (Salon International de la Lingerie, Curve Paris) in a single trip.

## How the trade show has evolved

Founded in 1963, Interfilière established itself as the international sourcing event for lingerie and swimwear, then expanded into activewear and, since 2025, into a broader fashion and accessories scope. Operational management was entrusted by Eurovet to Groupe WSN in 2022, with Eurovet remaining the owner of the brand. The trade show retains its rhythm of two editions a year, in January and September, at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, at the heart of the fashion and lingerie ecosystem brought together by WSN.', seo_title_en='Interfilière Paris 2026: lingerie, swimwear & textile sourcing', seo_description_en='Interfilière Paris, the international trade show for materials sourcing in lingerie, swimwear and activewear. Next edition 5 to 7 September 2026 at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. Organiser, exhibitors, practical information.' WHERE slug='interfiliere-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Intermat 2024 brought together 127,500 visitors over 4 days, of whom 21% were international, coming from 130 countries (source: Le Moniteur Matériels, Construction Cayola) → this is the benchmark event for construction and civil engineering equipment in France, with a strong international dimension.
- 1,065 exhibitors in 2024, the majority of them international according to the organiser (source: Le Moniteur Matériels) → a trade show where the world''s machinery manufacturers exhibit, not a regional one.
- The frequency has become triennial (2018, 2024, 2027) following a change to the calendar → exhibiting or visiting must be planned on a 3-year cycle, not a 4-year one.
- Intermat Demo zone: around 200 machines on outdoor demonstration, with hybrid and electric powertrains in the spotlight (source: intermatconstruction.com) → the appeal of the trade show is seeing the machines in operation, not just on a stand.
- **Next edition: 21-24 April 2027** at Paris Nord Villepinte (source: intermatconstruction.com/infos-pratiques).
- Organised by **Comexposium in partnership with Evolis and Seimat** (source: intermatconstruction.com/présentation-du-salon).
- Co-located with **World of Concrete Europe** (4th edition in 2027), a forum on concrete decarbonisation (source: intermatconstruction.com).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Construction machinery manufacturers, equipment suppliers, hire companies, civil engineering and construction firms. Sectors covered: earthmoving, roads, building, mining and quarrying, materials. A highly international professional attendance.

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [intermatconstruction.com](https://www.intermatconstruction.com/fr-FR/intermat/presentation-du-salon).

### Quality of attendees

- 127,500 admissions in 2024, of which 21% were international, from 130 countries (source: Le Moniteur Matériels, Construction Cayola)
- Profile: civil engineering firms, hire companies, equipment management departments, international buyers

## Events & community

### Conference programme

Intermat Demo zone: around 200 machines on demonstration every 10 minutes outdoors. Intermat Academy space (employment, training) and the World of Concrete Europe Forum (concrete decarbonisation).

### Awards & accolades

Intermat Innovation Awards (9th edition in 2024), 4 categories plus special prizes. Gold winners 2024: Dynaset (earthmoving), Bomag (roads), Betolar (concrete), Tenstar Solution (new technologies). Start-up Prize: Heracles Robotics and Muodim (source: intermatconstruction.com, Construction Cayola).

### Community & networks

An international trade show attached to the construction and civil engineering equipment industry. Specialist press in attendance: Le Moniteur, Construction Cayola, Chantiers de France.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte) page.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** €39 incl. VAT online, €69 incl. VAT on site. Free for students (with proof) and children under 12. Strictly a trade-only event (source: Intermat 2024).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: quote on request from Comexposium via the official website. As Intermat is an international heavy-equipment trade show with often large stands and machinery on display, exhibitor budgets are among the highest in the sector.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 18 months out: make contact with Comexposium, book your space (machinery areas are reserved very early).
- 12 months out: machinery transport logistics, application for the Innovation Awards.
- 6 months out: stand plan and demo zone, team briefing.
- 3 months out: accreditations, accommodation (international turnout, book early).
- 6 weeks out: machine delivery, final briefing.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- €39 badge online (vs €69 on site): register ahead of time.
- Allow 1 to 2 days: the outdoor Demo zone and the halls cover a large area.
- Target the machinery demonstration slots (every 10 minutes) in advance via the programme.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The decarbonisation of construction machinery is the central CSR focus of Intermat: electric, hydrogen, biofuel (HVO) powertrains and retrofitting were at the heart of the 2024 edition (source: Le Moniteur). For 2027, the organiser is structuring the trade show around three pillars: environmental, societal and economic sustainability (source: Construction Briefing).

## How the trade show has evolved

