### Trajectory analysis

Intermat 2024 confirmed its status as a major international event for construction equipment (127,500 visitors, 130 countries). The shift to a triennial rhythm (next edition 2027) tightens the cycle compared with the historical four-yearly cadence. Variable to watch for 2027: the machinery decarbonisation momentum, which is reshaping the exhibitor offering and the demonstrations.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='intermat-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- "The Power of Solutions": ISH is the world''s leading trade show for water (sanitation, bathrooms) and building energy (heating, ventilation, air conditioning, renewable energy, building management).
- Organiser: Messe Frankfurt Exhibition GmbH. Frequency: biennial, odd-numbered years.
- Next edition: ISH 2027, from 15 to 19 March 2027, at the [Messe Frankfurt](/lieux/messe-frankfurt) (Frankfurt am Main, Germany).
- Post-event report ISH 2025 (Messe Frankfurt): 163,157 visitors from 150 countries and 2,183 exhibitors from 54 countries, including 72% international exhibitors.
- The trade show is organised around two worlds: ISH Water (bathrooms, drinking-water hygiene, water-efficient sanitation solutions) and ISH Energy (heating, renewables, energy efficiency, smart buildings).
- Headline themes announced for 2027: green roofs and façades, swimming pools and spas, integrated solutions to address building complexity.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile
Manufacturers and distributors of taps and fittings, sanitary ceramics, bathroom furniture, heating systems (heat pumps, boilers, solar thermal), ventilation, air conditioning, building management technology and water-treatment solutions. The trade show covers the entire chain, from the industrial component to the bathroom fit-out.

### Notable exhibitors
The full list and the hall-by-hall plan can be consulted on the [official exhibitor page](https://ish.messefrankfurt.com/frankfurt/en/exhibitor-search.html). At the 2025 edition, the bathroom sector brought together names such as Axor, burgbad, Bette, Duravit, Hansgrohe, Hewi, Ideal Standard, Kaldewei, VitraBad and Villeroy & Boch within the Pop up my Bathroom space.

### Quality of the visitor base
Post-event report ISH 2025: 163,157 visitors from 150 countries. 94% of visitors said they were satisfied with the edition and 96% rated the exhibitors'' offering as very high quality. The visitor base brings together installers, engineering consultancies, architects, specialist distributors, wholesalers and construction-sector decision-makers.

## Events & community

### Conference programme
ISH runs a programme of forums and technical conferences spread across the two Water and Energy worlds, complemented by demonstration and trends areas. The detailed programme for the 2027 edition is published on the official website in the run-up to the trade show.

### Awards and accolades
"Designplus Award by ISH": an award recognising products that combine innovation, sustainability and design quality in the fields of HVAC and water. At the 2025 edition, 13 winners were recognised from more than 160 entries, with the ceremony held on the first day of the trade show at the Design Plaza (hall 3.1). The "Pop up my Bathroom" space also showcases forward-looking bathroom concepts.

### Community & networks
ISH fosters an international professional community, notably relayed through its [LinkedIn showcase](https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/ish-frankfurt) and across Messe Frankfurt''s digital platforms between editions.

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the [Messe Frankfurt](/lieux/messe-frankfurt) listing.

Specific to the trade show: ISH 2027 runs from 15 to 19 March 2027 (Monday to Friday). The show occupies several halls split by world (Water and Energy), with dedicated thematic areas (bathrooms, heating, renewables, building management). Registration and the access badge are arranged through the official website''s online ticketing, which also offers a digital platform for exhibitor search and appointment booking.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="Pricing schedule not publicly published for ISH 2027: indicative sector ranges for a leading international trade show of this size. Request the official quote from Messe Frankfurt." rows={[{ "poste": "Bare floor space rental (m²)", "low": "10,000 €", "high": "35,000 €" }, { "poste": "Fitted stand (design, furniture)", "low": "15,000 €", "high": "60,000 €" }, { "poste": "Logistics, utilities, services", "low": "5,000 €", "high": "20,000 €" }, { "poste": "Staff, travel, accommodation", "low": "8,000 €", "high": "25,000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (international stand)", "low": "~40,000 €", "high": "~140,000 €" }]} footer="Indicative estimate excluding communications and stand activation. The actual budget depends on the surface area, the location within the hall and the level of fit-out." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor
- 12 months out: book the floor space and choose the hall/world (Water or Energy) according to your offering.
- 6 months out: stand design, service-provider brief, ordering of utilities and technical services.
- 3 months out: complete the online exhibitor listing, book appointments via the digital platform, press plan.
- 1 month out: logistics, team accreditations, multilingual sales materials.

### For the decision-making visitor
Target in advance the halls matching your priorities (sanitation/bathrooms on the Water side, heating/renewables on the Energy side), pre-book the key conferences and organise your supplier meetings via the official platform. Allow at least two days on site given the size of the trade show.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Sustainability is a defining theme of ISH, whose "The Power of Solutions" positioning highlights water- and energy-efficient solutions (energy efficiency, renewables, drinking-water hygiene and conservation). The organising group Messe Frankfurt runs a formalised sustainability programme (EMAS validation, Net Zero Carbon Events commitment signed in 2022, carbon-neutrality target for the Frankfurt site by 2040) applied to its venues and events. The specific CSR commitments for the 2027 edition are detailed on the official website in the run-up to the trade show.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2027 (upcoming)", "dates": "15-19 March 2027", "lieu": "Messe Frankfurt", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "2025", "dates": "21-25 March 2025", "lieu": "Messe Frankfurt", "visiteurs": "163,157", "exposants": "2,183" }]} sources="Messe Frankfurt, ISH 2025 final report." />

### Trajectory analysis
ISH retains its status as the world''s leading trade show for water and building energy, with a highly international visitor base (150 countries in 2025) and a predominantly foreign exhibitor base (72%). The editorial trajectory is shifting markedly towards decarbonisation: heat pumps, renewables, energy efficiency and smart building management on the Energy side, water conservation and hygiene on the Water side. The new focuses announced for 2027 (green roofs and façades, swimming pools and spas, integrated solutions) confirm the show''s broadening towards a holistic approach to sustainable buildings.', seo_title_en='ISH 2027 Frankfurt: dates, exhibitors, programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='ISH 2027, the world''s leading trade show for water (sanitation) and energy (HVAC), from 15 to 19 March 2027 at the Messe Frankfurt. 2025 edition: 163,157 visitors from 150 countries, 2,183 exhibitors.' WHERE slug='ish-francfort';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Annual business convention for the IT & Tech Channel: two days of business meetings between manufacturers, software vendors, wholesalers, operators and the distribution network (resellers, integrators, MSPs, IT services firms).', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- IT Partners is the annual business convention of the **IT & Tech Channel** in France: two days of business meetings between upstream players (manufacturers, software vendors, wholesalers, operators) and downstream IT distribution (resellers, integrators, MSPs, IT services firms).
- Organised by **RX France** (Reed Exhibitions). Official baseline: "Where the leaders of the IT & Tech Channel meet".
- Next edition (21st): 3 and 4 February 2027 at [Paris La Défense Arena](/lieux/paris-la-defense-arena), in Nanterre. This is the second consecutive year at this venue following the move from Disneyland Paris.
- Review of the 2026 edition (20th edition, early February 2026): around 240 exhibitors, nearly 6,600 visitors, and approximately 25,500 contacts generated through the ITP Connect and Colleqt tools (source: itforbusiness.fr).
- Published environmental commitments: signatory of the Net Zero Carbon Events Pledge and the Climate Pledge, with a detailed [commitments page](https://www.itpartners.fr/fr-fr/decouvrir-itp/nos-engagements.html).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

On the exhibitor side: manufacturers, software vendors, wholesalers and value-added distributors, telecoms operators and cybersecurity experts. On the visitor side: integrators, MSPs and providers, IT resellers, IT services firms, telecoms service providers, consultants and office-equipment specialists. The fabric is overwhelmingly made up of micro-businesses (65% of companies with 1 to 50 employees), supplemented by 12% SMEs and 23% large enterprises.

IT Partners stands apart from consumer-facing digital trade shows such as [VivaTech](/salons/vivatech) through its tightly focused business-convention format, centred on the commercial development of the distribution network rather than on technology demonstration.

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is available on the official website: [itpartners.fr](https://www.itpartners.fr/fr-fr/qui-participe/liste-exposants.html). The 2027 list is published online and updated as the trade show approaches.

### Visitor quality

- 50% of visitors hold management positions (CIO, purchasing, general, technical, sales or marketing management)
- Geographic breakdown 2026: 54% from the Paris region, 41% regional visitors, 5% international (source: itforbusiness.fr)
- Visitor-to-stand contact rate up 12% in 2026 compared with 2025 (source: itforbusiness.fr)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The programme comprises conferences, workshops and keynotes spread over two days, with replays available after the trade show. In 2026, the **Channel Arena** and **Cyber Arena** spaces brought together more than 1,400 participants, up 44% from one edition to the next (source: itforbusiness.fr). The full 2027 programme is published as the trade show approaches on itpartners.fr.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris La Défense Arena](/lieux/paris-la-defense-arena) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Address:** 99 Jardin de l''Arche, 92000 Nanterre. Access via the RER A (La Défense or Nanterre Préfecture), metro line 1, the T2 tram and numerous RATP bus routes.
- **Parking:** Q-Park at the Westfield shopping centre (P1/P2), roughly a 7-minute walk from the venue.
- **Visitor badge:** prior online registration, reserved for IT & Tech Channel professionals.
- **Travel from the regions:** a Pack Wagon service has been set up to make it easier for regional visitors to attend (source: distributique.com).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with RX France, choose your positioning and stand format.
- 6 months out: prepare your business meeting plan and product demos.
- 3 months out: activate the ITP Connect and Colleqt tools to qualify and schedule meetings in advance.
- 6 weeks out: confirm meetings with target resellers and integrators, sales briefing.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Pre-register online at itpartners.fr with proof of professional activity in the IT & Tech Channel.
- Allow 1 to 2 days depending on the scope covered (distribution, cybersecurity, telecoms, infrastructure).
- Target the conferences and the Channel Arena and Cyber Arena spaces in advance.
- Prepare your business meeting schedule using the trade show''s matchmaking tools.

## CSR policy & initiatives

IT Partners details its commitments on its [Our commitments](https://www.itpartners.fr/fr-fr/decouvrir-itp/nos-engagements.html) page. The trade show is a signatory of the Net Zero Carbon Events Pledge and the Climate Pledge, with a stated objective of halving its greenhouse gas emissions by 2030 and reaching carbon neutrality by 2040.

On responsible production: application of the UNIMEV energy-efficiency plan, removal of single-use plastic consumables, water fountains made available, cardboard materials and coated fabrics for common areas and signage, alternatives to red meat with a vegetarian offering. On waste: a target of a 5% increase in recovery and reuse and a 10% reduction in waste at each edition.

On inclusion and accessibility: guaranteed wheelchair access on every stand, accommodation of speakers'' specific needs, code of conduct and RX inclusive events guide, diversity in panels. No ISO 20121 certification mentioned to date (source: itpartners.fr/decouvrir-itp/nos-engagements).

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "2027 (21st, upcoming)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" },
  { "edition": "2026 (20th)", "visiteurs": "~6,600", "exposants": "~240" }
 ]}
 sources="itpartners.fr, itforbusiness.fr, distributique.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

The 2026 edition, the 20th, was held in early February at Paris La Défense Arena, the second year at this venue following the move from Disneyland Paris. It brought together around 240 exhibitors and nearly 6,600 visitors, with a decline of around fifty exhibiting brands compared with 2025, which the organiser attributes to a tough economic context for the IT sector. The trade show nevertheless improved business intensity per stand (+12% contact rate) and the audience for its Channel Arena and Cyber Arena conference spaces (+44%). The 2027 edition (21st), on 3 and 4 February at Paris La Défense Arena, confirms the trade show''s foothold at its new venue and its positioning as the benchmark business event for the French IT & Tech Channel.', seo_title_en='IT Partners 2027: the IT & Tech Channel trade show, 3-4 February, Paris La Défense Arena', seo_description_en='IT Partners 2027 (21st edition), the IT & Tech Channel business convention, takes place on 3 and 4 February at Paris La Défense Arena (Nanterre). Exhibitors, visitor profile, programme and practical info.' WHERE slug='it-partners-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The world''s largest travel trade show at Messe Berlin, a consolidated 3-day B2B format since 2023. Partner country 2027: Maldives. 2026 edition (60th anniversary): around 97,000 trade visitors, 5,601 exhibitors, 166 countries represented, 47bn euros in transactions generated.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- ITB Berlin 2027 is the world''s largest travel trade show, scheduled from Tuesday 16 to Thursday 18 March 2027 at [Messe Berlin](/lieux/messe-berlin) (Berlin ExpoCenter City, Messedamm 22, 14055 Berlin). Three days of strictly B2B trade show, a consolidated format since the 2023 reform.
- **Partner country 2027: Maldives**, with a focus on luxury tourism, sustainability and marine conservation. Following Angola in 2026 and Albania in 2025.
- 2026 edition (3 to 5 March, 60th anniversary): around 97,000 trade visitors, 5,601 exhibitors, 166 countries represented, 47 billion euros in transactions and purchasing decisions generated, 96% visitor satisfaction.
- Trade show run by Messe Berlin GmbH since its creation in 1966 by Professor Manfred Busche (first edition: 9 exhibitors, 5 countries: Egypt, Brazil, West Germany, Guinea, Iraq).
- Halls organised by geographic destinations and by market segments: Adventure Tourism, Business Travel, LGBTQ+ Travel, Luxury Travel, Medical Tourism, Travel Technology. eTravel Stage in hall 6.1, Blue Stage in hall 7.1b for the sustainable destination management forum.
- 2027 exhibitor rates not yet published as of June 2026, exhibitor registration deadline set for 1 September 2026.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A fully B2B professional trade fair covering the entire value chain of global tourism: national and regional tourism offices (NTOs and RTOs), hotel groups, airlines, tour operators and travel companies, cruise lines, inbound agencies, OTAs, TravelTech publishers, GDS, training bodies, media and professional associations. An exclusively professional audience since the B2B transition confirmed in 2023.

### Notable exhibitors (2026, 2027 reference base)

**Tourism offices and destinations**: Angola (2026 partner), Maldives (2027 partner), Albania, Germany, Atout France, Visit Britain, ENIT Italy, Turespaña, Saudi Tourism Authority, Visit Qatar, Dubai DET, Singapore Tourism Board, Brand USA, Japan National Tourism Organization, Tourism Australia.

**Hospitality**: Accor, Marriott, Hilton, IHG, Hyatt, Radisson, Meliá, NH Hotel Group, Deutsche Hospitality, Kempinski, Mandarin Oriental, Four Seasons, Soneva (Maldives luxury benchmark), Six Senses.

**Aviation and cruise**: Lufthansa Group, Air France-KLM, Emirates, Qatar Airways, Singapore Airlines, Turkish Airlines, TUI Group, DER Touristik, MSC Cruises, Costa Cruises, Royal Caribbean.

**Distribution and technology**: Amadeus, Sabre, Travelport, Booking Holdings, Expedia Group, Trip.com Group, HRS, HBX Group, Trivago. TravelTech startups grouped within the Business France **France Tourisme Tech** programme.

### Retention rate

A core of national and hospitality exhibitors loyal for several decades (European tourism offices, major hotel groups, long-standing GDS). Significant structural renewal driven by TravelTech, new emerging destinations and vertical segments (Adventure, LGBTQ+, Medical, Luxury). A stable French presence around the **France Tourisme Tech** pavilion run by Business France, complemented by occasional participation from regional tourism committees (CRT).

### Visitor quality

100% qualified professionals (named badges issued on proof since the B2B switch in 2023). A mix of decision-makers: tour operator sales and purchasing management, MICE buyers, destination marketing management, hotel general management, hospitality investors, specialist journalists. 166 countries represented on the exhibitor side in 2026, a predominantly European visitor mix complemented by structured delegations from Asia, the Middle East, Africa and the Americas. A defining purchasing event for seasonal contracts and annual tour operator negotiations.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**ITB Berlin Convention**, presented by the organisers as the "epicenter for transformative knowledge", is the world''s leading B2B tourism congress: more than 400 speakers across the three days. Structural themes: generative AI applied to tourism, sustainability and decarbonisation, transformation of distribution models, geopolitics of travel, vertical segments (luxury, adventure, medical, LGBTQ+). **eTravel Stage** in hall 6.1 for TravelTech, **Blue Stage** in hall 7.1b for the sustainable destination management forum and the Green Destinations + ITB Earth Award presentations. The 2027 programme is published in the run-up to the trade show.

### Awards & accolades

**Green Destinations Top 100 Story Awards**: 100 sustainable tourism initiatives recognised each year, presented on the Blue Stage. **ITB Earth Award 2026**: won by **Fernando de Noronha** (Brazil) for the Golfinho Rotador / Spinner Dolphin marine conservation project. **People''s Choice 2026**: **Selçuk** (Ephesus Field Life Village, Turkey), elected by more than 20,000 public votes. **PATWA International Travel Awards** also presented during the trade show. The 2027 winners will be announced beforehand by the organisers, with the awards presented across the three days.

### Satellite events

Regional editions of the ITB portfolio run by Messe Berlin: **ITB Asia** (Singapore, October), **ITB China** (Shanghai, May), **ITB India** (Mumbai, September). The **France Tourisme Tech** TravelTech programme run by Business France, which brings together a collective French startup pavilion at ITB Berlin each year. Occasional side events in Paris and Lyon ahead of the trade show (preparation days, CRT sector briefings).

### Community & networks

A single organiser since 1966: **Messe Berlin GmbH**, operator of the Berlin ExpoCenter City. Trade show created by **Manfred Busche** (Professor Doctor) in 1966 with 9 exhibitors and 5 countries (Egypt, Brazil, West Germany, Guinea, Iraq). The full B2B switch was confirmed in 2023 and has become permanent: ITB Berlin no longer hosts the general public. Defining institutional partnerships: UNWTO, WTTC, IATA, Skift, ITB Berlin Pioneers Network (alumni). The structured French presence draws on **Atout France**, **Business France** (France Tourisme Tech programme) and participating **CRT**.

### What''s new for 2027

**Maldives** as partner country 2027: luxury, sustainability, marine conservation. Continuing the 2026 momentum (97,000 visitors, 5,601 exhibitors, 166 countries, 47bn euros in transactions). An expected strengthening around generative AI applied to distribution, CSRD compliance for European players, and regenerative tourism. **Messe Berlin CSR commitment**: signatory of the **Net Zero Carbon Events Pledge** and the **Climate Pledge**, with a target of minus 50% greenhouse gas emissions by 2030 and carbon neutrality by 2040. **Sustainable Tourism Zone** and **Blue Stage** renewed in hall 7.1b.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Messe Berlin](/lieux/messe-berlin), Berlin ExpoCenter City, Messedamm 22, 14055 Berlin, Germany. A historic site run by Messe Berlin GmbH since 1966.
- **Transport access**: S-Bahn S3, S9, S41, S42, S46 (Messe Süd or Messe Nord/ICC stations). U-Bahn U2 (Kaiserdamm station). Bus M49. BER airport (Berlin Brandenburg) around 45 minutes away by S-Bahn. March period, professional trade show: increased intra-European rail traffic, prioritise public transport.
- **Parking**: Car parks on site and around the Berlin ExpoCenter City, heavily saturated across the three days. Prioritise public transport or park-and-ride facilities on the outskirts.
- **Accommodation**: Charlottenburg, Wilmersdorf and Westend districts as a priority (immediate proximity to the Messe). Mitte and Kreuzberg for those seeking urban centrality. **Book 4 to 6 months in advance**, as ITB Berlin is one of the three annual hotel peaks in the German capital (alongside IFA and the Berlinale).
- **Opening hours & badges 2027**: Tuesday 16 to Thursday 18 March, a strictly professional trade show on named badge. Online visitor registration on the organisers'' official website from autumn 2026.
- **Services**: Multiple catering points across the entire venue (sustainable menus aligned with the CSR commitment), exhibitor VIP areas, an international press room, media platforms, an official app, cloakrooms, left luggage, and interpreting services for international delegations (English, German, Spanish, Mandarin, Arabic).

## How much it costs to exhibit

