## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out (spring 2026): make contact with Messe Berlin GmbH or with Business France (France Tourisme Tech programme) for TravelTech startups, hall and market segment positioning
- 9 months out (summer 2026): commitment before 1 September 2026 (official exhibitor registration deadline), application for the Green Destinations Top 100 Story Awards and the ITB Earth Award for eligible destinations
- 6 months out (autumn 2026): validation of the scenography concept, agency and stand builder brief, scheduling of B2B meetings via the ITB Berlin matchmaking tool
- 3 months out (December 2026): final plans, stand construction order, equipment logistics, team accreditations
- 6 weeks out (February 2027): delivery of materials, final team brief, activation of media campaigns and client invitations, ITB Berlin Convention planning
- 15 days out: accommodation confirmation (bookings secured 4 to 6 months ahead), final commercial brief, press kits

### For the decision-making visitor

- Register as soon as the 2027 professional ticketing opens (autumn 2026): named badge issued on professional proof
- Prioritise Tuesday 16 March (day 1) for defining commercial meetings and tour operator negotiations, keep Wednesday for the Convention (400+ speakers) and Thursday for targeted prospecting
- Prepare your meetings via the official ITB Berlin matchmaking tool beforehand (B2B introductions and integrated messaging)
- For international delegations: get in touch with the interpreting services and the national pavilions (2027 partner country Maldives, Germany, Atout France for the French delegation)
- Allow all 3 full days to cover the halls by geographic destination and by vertical segment (Adventure, Business, LGBTQ+, Luxury, Medical, Travel Technology)
- Book accommodation 4 to 6 months in advance (high hotel pressure on Berlin during ITB)

