### Trajectory analysis

ITB Berlin emerges from its 2026 60th anniversary reinforced as the world''s leading travel trade show: 97,000 trade visitors, 5,601 exhibitors, 166 countries and 47 billion euros in transactions generated over three days, 96% visitor satisfaction. Three structural indicators validate the trajectory: **unrivalled geographic coverage** (166 countries, ITB retains its lead over WTM London and FITUR Madrid), **B2B switch confirmed since 2023** (the end of the general public has strengthened visitor qualification), **ITB Berlin Convention** consolidated as the world''s leading B2B tourism congress with 400+ speakers. The trajectory of partner countries (Albania 2025, Angola 2026, Maldives 2027) confirms the opening to emerging destinations. **The 2027 edition plays a post-anniversary consolidation role**: Maldives as a luxury-sustainability-marine conservation showcase, a strengthened generative AI and CSRD programme, and CSR commitment to the Net Zero Carbon Events Pledge and the Climate Pledge. Over 60 years (1966 to 2026), ITB Berlin has accompanied every disruption in the sector: European aviation liberalisation, the emergence of OTAs, the mobile-first switch in distribution, and the rollout of generative AI.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='itb-berlin';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='25th edition "25th Impact" of Europe''s premier gathering for Japanese popular culture, at Paris Nord Villepinte over 4 days. 2025 results: 230,000 visitors, more than 800 exhibitors, 671 guests and 674 events across 35 stages.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **25th edition "25th Impact"** of Japan Expo, from **9 to 12 July 2026** at Paris Nord Villepinte, over **4 days**.
- A **predominantly B2C trade show with an integrated Village Pro**: Europe''s premier gathering for Japanese popular culture, and the largest French trade show for the 15-25 age bracket since 2008 (134,467 visitors certified by Infora for the first Villepinte edition).
- 2025 edition results (24th, 3-6 July): **230,000 visitors**, **more than 800 exhibitors** (835 cited by ecostylia.com), 140,000 m², 671 guests, 674 events spread across 35 stages. First French presidential visit to the trade show (Emmanuel Macron).
- Organised by **SEFA Event** (founded in 2007 by Jean-François Dufour, Sandrine Dufour and Thomas Sirdey, co-managers), a company part of the **Iconik Global** group.
- Four structuring hubs: **Hall 5A** manga and publishing, **Hall 6** gaming, **Hall 7** cosplay and stages, **Hall 4** traditions and J-music. Integrated Village Pro at the entrance of Hall 5A.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Four families of exhibitors announced by the organiser (source: japan-expo-paris.com):

- manga publishers and licences (rights holders, agencies, distributors),
- video game publishers and studios (consoles, mobile, platforms),
- lifestyle and merchandising brands (figurines, goodies, street/kawaii fashion, Japanese food),
- traditional cultural players (crafts, martial arts, J-music, Japan tourism, language schools).

### Notable exhibitors

**Hall 5A manga (2025 edition)**: Glénat (E154), Pika Édition (G152), Ki-oon (B170), Kana, Kurokawa, Panini Manga, Kazé, Akata, Ototo, Taifu, Mangetsu, Nobi Nobi, Black Box, Vega-Dupuis (sources: publisher websites, 2025 edition feedback).

**Hall 6 gaming (2025 edition)**: **SEGA** (Shinobi: Art of Vengeance, Demon Slayer: Sweep the Board), **Bandai Namco** (Arknights Endfield), **Nintendo Switch 2** with Pokémon Legends Z-A, Mario Kart World, Metroid Prime 4 Beyond, Donkey Kong Bananza, Super Mario Party Jamboree, **Cygames** (Granblue Fantasy, Umamusume Pretty Derby), **JP Universe** (Hajime Tabata, No Straight Roads 2). **Crunchyroll Hall 6 stand F628 (400 m² in 2025)**: panels for Gachiakuta, To Your Eternity season 3, Demon Slayer with Takahiro Sakurai, Dr STONE SCIENCE FUTURE. **Toei Animation** hosted Eisaku Inoue (animator on Saint Seiya, One Piece) and Keiichi Ichikawa.

Full list on the official website: [japan-expo-paris.com](https://www.japan-expo-paris.com).

### Visitor quality

- A predominantly general-public audience, core target 15-35 years, the leading French trade show for the 15-25 age bracket since 2008 (Infora).
- **230,000 visitors** over 4 days in 2025 (organiser self-reported).
- Integrated Village Pro (entrance of Hall 5A) for B2B meetings between publishers, rights holders, licensing and distribution.
- 671 professional guests in 2025 (mangaka, character designers, voice actors, studios, publishers).

## Activities & community

### Events programme

**674 events spread across 35 stages** in 2025: J-pop and J-rock concerts, orchestral live shows, fan conventions, cosplay demonstrations, mangaka and studio talks, animation screenings, signings, video game panels, demos of upcoming games, martial arts and traditional demonstrations (tea ceremony, ikebana, calligraphy).

### Guests of honour and exhibitions

The 2025 edition was marked by the "**Nightmares & Obsessions**" exhibition by mangaka **Junji Itō** (horror, Uzumaki, Tomie), the visit of the disciples of **REDICE STUDIO** for Solo Leveling (first appearance in France) and of **Kazuhiko Torishima**, the historic tantō (editor) of Akira Toriyama (sources: press feedback from the 2025 edition).

### Awards and competitions

National and international cosplay competitions, **Japan Expo Awards** by category (manga, animation, video game), J-music showcase launchpads. The 2026 programme will be published in spring 2026 by the organiser.

### 2025 presidential visit

First visit by a President of the French Republic to the trade show: **Emmanuel Macron** came in 2025 to acknowledge the place of Japanese pop culture in the French creative economy and the Japan-France cultural reach.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte) page.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Hall locations:** Hall 4 (traditions, J-music), Hall 5A (manga, publishing, Village Pro), Hall 6 (gaming), Hall 7 (cosplay, stages).
- **Opening hours (2026 edition):** Thursday 9 July opening **from 3 pm** with a dedicated Anniversary Discovery Ticket, Friday 10, Saturday 11 and Sunday 12 July standard hours (full programme published by the organiser in May-June 2026).
- **Audience:** open to all, ticket required. Village Pro accessible by accreditation.

## What it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published: application to take part via the organiser portal (sefa-event.com / japan-expo-paris.com/exposer). Figures not publicly available.

**Visitor rates, Genin Rate** (until 2 July 2026, source: japan-expo-paris.com):

| Category | Price |
|---|---|
| Anniversary Discovery Ticket Thursday (from 3 pm) | €14 |
| 1-Day Pass | €27 to €36.90 |
| 4-Day Pass | €96.30 (€95.30 Fnac) |
| FastPass Thursday | €37 |
| FastPass Friday | €35 |
| FastPass Saturday | €46 |
| FastPass Sunday | €39 |
| Zen Badge 4 Days | €169 |

The **Jōnin Rate** (premium early bird) is sold out to date for 2026.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- M-12: initial contact with SEFA Event, choice of hall (5A manga, 6 gaming, 7 cosplay, 4 traditions/J-music) and possible Village Pro positioning.
- M-9: application for panels, guest talks, themed exhibitions. Request for a stage slot (35 stages in 2025).
- M-6: stand finalisation, upstream communication plan across video game and manga communities (social networks, specialist press, creators).
- M-3: team briefing, preparation of signings, guest panels, game demos, general-public activities and evening programme.
- W-6: leveraging the Japan Expo and Iconik Global network (sister events, media, influencers relays).

### For the decision-making visitor

- **Thursday 9 July** (Anniversary Ticket €14, from 3 pm): the quietest day, ideal for scouting publisher stands and planning the following 3 days.
- **Friday 10 July**: the most intense professional day for Village Pro networking with publishers / licensing.
- FastPass recommended to target major guest talks (Crunchyroll, Toei, mangaka panels) given the visitor density on Saturday-Sunday.
- Zen Badge 4 Days (€169): relevant if the aim is to cover manga + gaming + cosplay + J-music without time constraints.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Japan Expo draws on the **"Second Life Events"** scheme run by Iconik Global: an online platform for the reuse of furniture and event items from one edition to the next and between the group''s events. No detailed public CSR charter at trade-show level to date, and no ISO 20121 certification mentioned. Impact figures (energy, waste, transport) not published.

## How the trade show has evolved

