## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out (spring 2025): make contact with JEC Group; the strategic spaces (aerospace pavilions, country hubs) go early even at an annual show
- 9 months out: enter the JEC Composites Innovation Awards (a demanding technical submission), and the Start-up Booster for young companies
- 6 months out: validate the stand concept, brief the contractor, order the semi-finished products and demonstration parts
- 4 months out: commit to the matchmaking programme to prepare the pre-scheduled business meetings (target of 17,000 in total)
- 3 months out: team accreditations, accommodation, sales brief, lead targets quantified by application category
- 6 weeks out: deliver materials, activate the JEC World app, schedule meetings, and run upstream communications around the JEC World Premiere on 12 January 2026

### For the decision-making visitor

- Badge at €85 incl. VAT as early bird from 19 January to 9 March 2026, an immediate saving versus €110 incl. VAT on site
- Conference programme and SAMPE sessions published in advance on jec-world.events; identify priority sessions by application
- Allow a minimum of 2 days; 78,000 m² and 1,350+ exhibitors are impossible to cover in a single day
- First-Time Buyers Program: free access for eligible first-time buyers, with applications via JEC Group several weeks before the show
- Activate matchmaking via the official app to set up pre-scheduled business meetings in advance

## CSR commitment

JEC Group has not to date published an ISO 20121 charter or a detailed event carbon assessment specific to JEC World. The sustainability narrative is carried mainly by the composites themselves: the lightweighting of aerospace and automotive structures (reducing consumption and emissions), next-generation wind turbine blades, hydrogen storage, recycling and the circular economy. Editorially, this translates into two flagship programmes: the "Circularity & Recycling" Innovation Awards category and the Start-up Booster Sustainability Award (€2,500). For exhibitors, entering these categories is a free CSR visibility lever recognised by the sector.

## How the trade show has evolved

