### Trajectory analysis

The JFR are the benchmark annual event for French-speaking radiology, structured around a scientific congress and an industrial exhibition. The 2025 edition brought together 11,877 visitors and 180 exhibitors on the exhibition side, with 76 countries represented (source: jfrexpo.com). Note: the overall scientific congress, which includes those registered for sessions and workshops beyond the exhibition alone, reports more than 13,000 participants across all categories for 2025 (source: jfr.plus/jfr-2025). The figures in the HistoryTable above correspond to the exhibition scope (visitors with access to the industrial stands), which is more directly comparable from one edition to the next. The 2026 edition, the 74th, is targeting more than 12,000 participants and puts the United Kingdom and Colombia in the spotlight, confirming the international dimension of the congress.', seo_title_en='JFR 2026 - Journées Francophones de Radiologie | 8-11 October, Paris', seo_description_en='The Journées Francophones de Radiologie (JFR) 2026, 74th edition, from 8 to 11 October at the Palais des Congrès de Paris. Medical imaging congress and exhibition organised by the SFR. Exhibitors, practical information and programme.' WHERE slug='jfr-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International trade fair for immersive technologies and virtual reality. The benchmark event for VR, AR and XR technologies.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Laval Virtual is Europe''s benchmark trade fair for immersive technologies (VR, AR, MR, XR), created in 1999 by the town of Laval and the Mayenne département (source: laval-virtual.com).
- Next edition (29th): 7 to 9 April 2027 at the Espace Mayenne, Laval (source: laval-virtual.com).
- A rare hybrid format in Europe: 3 strictly professional days in April, complemented by general-public days and by the **Recto VRso** digital art festival in November.
- Post-Covid volumes: around 5,000 to 6,000 professional visitors (a third of them international, from 37 nationalities) and 160 to 180 exhibitors. The historical figure of 18,000 visitors dates back to the 2018 edition and no longer reflects the event''s current size (sources: 3dvf.com, planeterobots.com).
- Strong academic roots: the permanent **Laval Virtual Center** third place hosts Clarté (a VR/AR/AI resource centre), the Arts et Métiers Laval Institute and the School of Design (source: agglo-laval.fr).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

VR/XR hardware, development platforms, industrial integrators, content studios, academic research centres and R&D laboratories, XR startups. A strongly B2B profile with a notable share of institutional exhibitors (CEA, Inria, engineering schools).

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [laval-virtual.com](https://laval-virtual.com/en/exhibitors-laval-virtual/). Regular presence of HTC VIVE, Varjo, Pico, SenseGlove, Manus (hardware); Unity Technologies, Unreal Engine, Innoactive (platforms); Dassault Systèmes, Sopra Steria, SKYREAL, CEA List, Immersion (industrial integrators); OptiTrack, Clarté, Gracia AI (tracking and research) (source: 3dvf.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

- A strictly professional audience over the 3 trade days, complemented by separate general-public days - Around a third international: 37 nationalities represented in 2024 (source: planeterobots.com)
- A technical and decision-making audience: R&D, innovation, training, XR procurement
- OJS-audited figures not published to date (R2)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

B2B conferences organised over 3 days around 5 themes: XR and AI / LBE, Media & Museums, Industry & Defence, Training & Education, Health & Wellbeing. Sessions of 45 minutes to 1 hour 30, mainly in English with simultaneous translation (source: laval-virtual.com/conferences-en).

### Awards and accolades

**Laval Virtual Awards**: ceremony on the Thursday, with around 300 entries reviewed each year. **6 official categories**: XR Devices and Interactions Products, Developer & Authoring Tools, XR for a Cause (positive impact), Enterprise & Productivity Solution, Education & Training, Consumer Experience & Entertainment. Special competitions: #Experiences, #StartUps, #Students, #ReVolution (source: laval-virtual.com/general-categories).

**#ReVolution**: a competition dedicated to research laboratories and R&D departments experimenting with XR. The winner is invited to exhibit at SIGGRAPH the following year. International jury including Inria, Meta, École des Mines Paris (source: laval-virtual.com/revolution).

### Satellite events

**Recto VRso**: an associated digital art festival, with its 9th edition in November 2026 at the Le Quarante venue in Laval, free admission (source: recto-vrso.com). **LBE Area** (Location-Based Entertainment) extended to 500 m² in 2026 for collective immersive experiences (source: techniques-ingenieur.fr).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Espace Mayenne](/lieux/espace-mayenne) listing.

Specific to the trade fair:

- **Opening hours (2026 edition, to be confirmed for 2027):** 3 trade days with morning and afternoon sessions, plus the Laval Virtual Party on the Wednesday evening.
- **Professional visitor badge:** paid (see pricing below), a named badge is required for the 3 trade days.
- **App:** programme and floor plans available from the website and the official app.

## What it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published: quote on request from Maxime Leroy, sales manager (mleroy@laval-virtual.org). This figure is not publicly available.

Published visitor rates (2026 edition, to be confirmed for 2027):

- **Full Pass**: €390 excl. VAT, full access to the halls (Mayenne, Pégase, LBVR Area), conferences, tech-talks, doctoral consortium, LV Party evening, Awards ceremony
- **Discovery Pass**: €145 excl. VAT, access to the exhibition with conference and evening options
- **Student Pass**: €30 incl. VAT, access to the exhibition with conference options
- **General public**: €4.90 full rate, €3.50 reduced, free for under-12s

(Source: laval-virtual.com/ticketing, grandpublic.laval-virtual.com)

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact at mleroy@laval-virtual.org and request a stand quote.
- 9 months out: enter the Laval Virtual Awards via laval-virtual.awardsplatform.com to boost visibility.
- 6 months out: prepare hands-on demos (the format is very much product-trial oriented, with little room for "showcase" stands).
- 3 months out: brief the team, prepare 5 to 10-minute demo scripts, recruit translators if needed.
- 6 weeks out: push your invitations to international contacts (a third of the visitor base).

### For the decision-making visitor

- Distinguish between the 3 trade days (7-9 April 2027) and any general-public days (2027 programme to be confirmed on grandpublic.laval-virtual.com).
- Full Pass recommended to make the most of the B2B conferences, the Laval Virtual Awards and the LV Party.
- Schedule a detour via the **Laval Virtual Center**, a permanent third place in Laval, if the trip warrants an extended visit (source: agglo-laval.fr).
- TGV access from Paris: 1 hour 10 to Laval, then 15 minutes to reach the Espace Mayenne.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Information not available: as at the date of this listing, the Laval Virtual Association does not publish a dedicated CSR commitments page or any identifiable "eco-responsible event" label. The association''s profile on the Zei platform mentions no formalised commitments (source: zei-world.com/pro/2429).

## How the trade fair has evolved

