### Trajectory analysis

Laval Virtual has undergone a deliberate post-Covid repositioning: dropping the mass-event format (18,000 visitors in 2018) in favour of a tighter, more B2B and more international event (a third from abroad, 37 nationalities). The 2024-2026 editions stabilise a size of 5,000-6,000 professionals and 160-180 exhibitors. A notable feature: the 2026 edition sharpened its focus on the "industrialisation of XR" and immersive AI, which matches the expectations of major integrators (Dassault Systèmes, Sopra Steria, CEA) and aligns the trade fair with the R&D budgets of large accounts rather than the general-public market (sources: itsocial.fr, techniques-ingenieur.fr).', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='laval-virtual';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The largest French trade show for digital learning and professional training, co-located with HR Technologies France. LMS and LXP, e-learning, microlearning, serious games, AI applied to learning.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Learning Technologies France is the largest French trade show dedicated to digital learning and professional training. It is organised by **CloserStill Media**, which took over the iLearning Forum in 2017 and launched the first edition under the name Learning Technologies France in 2018 (source: closerstillmedia.com).
- Next edition: 20 and 21 January 2027 at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, Hall 4.
- The trade show is co-located with **HR Technologies France**: a single badge grants access to both exhibition spaces and their conferences.
- 2026 edition (28-29 January, Hall 6): 410+ exhibitors, 550 speakers, 350+ conferences and sessions (figures announced, source: learningtechnologiesfrance.com), with AI in training running as the common thread through more than half the programme.
- Free conference programme for professional visitors, in French and English.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

LMS and LXP platform vendors, e-learning and microlearning production studios, serious game and educational virtual reality specialists, training bodies, providers of AI applied to learning, and instructional design consultancies. Attendees include training departments, L&D managers, HR directors, digital transformation managers and buyers of training solutions.

Co-location with HR Technologies France broadens the audience to HR and talent management decision-makers. The trade show is part of the French training and HR ecosystem alongside trade shows such as [eLearning Expo](/salons/elearning-expo-paris) and [Solutions RH](/salons/solutions-rh-paris) in Paris, or [RH](/salons/rh-lyon) in Lyon.

### Notable exhibitors

Full list of exhibitors on the official website: [learningtechnologiesfrance.com](https://www.learningtechnologiesfrance.com/exposants). Sponsors highlighted at the recent edition: 360Learning, Apolearn, Bealink, Edflex, Firstgroup, Kwark, Rise Up, Septeo Education, Teach Up, Very Up (Platinum sponsors); Cegid, CEGOS, Cornerstone, CrossKnowledge, Didask, Docebo, Dokeos, iSpring, Speexx, Training Orchestra (Gold sponsors, partial list); Busuu, Learnlight, Synthesia, Tosa, Arts et Métiers (Silver sponsors).

### Quality of attendees

- More than 16,000 training, HR and talent management professionals gather each year across the combined Learning Technologies France and HR Technologies France footprint (figure announced, learningtechnologiesfrance.com).
- A single badge granting access to both co-located trade shows, targeting training departments, L&D managers, HR directors and digital transformation managers.
- A decision-maker-focused programme, with more than 50% of exhibitors and speakers addressing AI in training at the 2026 edition.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2026 edition brought together 550 speakers for 350+ conferences and sessions, in French and English, accessible free of charge to professional visitors (source: learningtechnologiesfrance.com). Artificial intelligence in training is the central theme: ethical use of generative AI, dependence on economic and technological models, and responsible uses for trainers and learners. Replays of conferences from previous editions are available online. The detailed 2027 programme will be published as the trade show approaches.

### Prizes and awards

The trade show presents the **Learning Impact Awards**, which recognise high-impact training projects. Categories and winners to be confirmed ahead of each edition on the official website.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. on both days (2027 edition: Wednesday 20 and Thursday 21 January).
- **Visitor badge:** free with prior online registration, reserved for professionals. The badge is sent by email before the trade show and can be printed at home or via the terminals available in the hall.
- **Dual access:** the badge opens access to the entire exhibition space and to the conferences of both Learning Technologies France and HR Technologies France.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published on the official website: stand booking is done via the "Réserver un stand" button on [learningtechnologiesfrance.com](https://www.learningtechnologiesfrance.com/exprom/exposer-au-salon). Specific figure not publicly available, to be requested directly from CloserStill Media.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months before: get in touch with the CloserStill Media sales team, choose the location and stand format.
- 6 months before: prepare product demos, in line with the show''s AI and training common thread.
- 4 months before: apply for the Learning Impact Awards if relevant, finalise the conference and session plan.
- 6 weeks before: activate L&D and HR decision-maker meetings, brief the stand team.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free pre-registration on learningtechnologiesfrance.com, badge received by email before the trade show.
- Allow one to two days to cover both Learning Technologies France and HR Technologies France with a single badge.
- Target conferences in advance: the free programme is published several weeks before the trade show.
- Focus your research on AI applied to training, the programme''s dominant common thread.

## How the trade show has evolved

