### Trajectory analysis

Learning Technologies France was born in 2018, following CloserStill Media''s acquisition of the iLearning Forum in 2017, as the French spin-off of the London trade show Learning Technologies, the European benchmark for workplace learning. The trade show settled at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles with an annual rhythm in January and grew in scale around its co-location with HR Technologies France, which today brings together more than 16,000 training and HR professionals. The 2027 edition, on 20 and 21 January, extends this positioning by placing AI applied to training at the centre of the programme. The final figures and the 2027 programme will be published as the trade show approaches.', seo_title_en='Learning Technologies France 2027: digital learning and training in Paris', seo_description_en='Learning Technologies France 2027, on 20 and 21 January at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. The largest French trade show for digital learning and training, co-located with HR Technologies France. Organised by CloserStill Media.' WHERE slug='learning-technologies-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Annual gathering of cybersecurity decision-makers. Conferences, workshops and B2B meetings for CISOs and CIOs.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Les Assises de la cybersécurité is the leading annual gathering of digital security decision-makers in France (CISOs, CIOs, technical directors, risk managers), held each autumn in Monaco. Official tagline: "The gathering of cybersecurity experts".
- Next edition (26th): from 7 to 10 October 2026 at the [Grimaldi Forum](/lieux/grimaldi-forum) in Monaco.
- Organiser: DG Consultants, a subsidiary of the Comexposium group. The event runs on a model of pre-scheduled, qualified one-to-one meetings between cybersecurity leaders from major accounts and solution providers.
- 2025 review (25th edition, 8 to 11 October 2025): 3,349 participants, 180 partners, 12,000 one-to-one meetings, 21 startups at the Startups Village and more than 60 highlights (keynotes, round tables, conferences, pitches). Post-review theme: "Cybersecurity in the service of the common good, founded on trust, cooperation and transformation" (source: monacocyber.mc).
- Distinct from the [Forum InCyber Europe](/salons/fic-lille) (formerly FIC, Lille): Les Assises targets invitation-only business meetings for cyber decision-makers, whereas the Forum InCyber is a broader, open trade show.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Cybersecurity solution providers: security software vendors, integrators, infrastructure and managed services providers (MSSPs), specialists in detection and response, identity management, compliance and digital sovereignty. The audience is made up of decision-makers: CISOs, CIOs, technical directors, infrastructure, network and telecoms managers, risk managers. Participation is by selection and invitation, in a format of pre-scheduled one-to-one meetings.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of partners is available on the official website: [lesassisesdelacybersecurite.com](https://www.lesassisesdelacybersecurite.com). The 2025 edition brought together 180 partners, including 21 startups at the Startups Village (source: monacocyber.mc).

### Quality of the audience

- 3,349 participants in 2025, a community of cybersecurity decision-makers from major French accounts
- 12,000 one-to-one meetings organised in 2025, the heart of the event''s model
- An invitation-only format with profile selection, ensuring a qualified audience of decision-makers

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2025 edition offered more than 60 highlights (keynotes, round tables, conferences and pitches). Replays of the 2025 edition are available online. The 2026 programme and theme will be published as the edition approaches.

The Les Assises ecosystem extends beyond the Monaco gathering with community formats such as Le Cercle (networking evenings) and Le Before (preparatory strategic session).

### Awards and accolades

The **Prix de l''Innovation des Assises** is awarded each year to a cybersecurity startup. Applications for the 2026 edition opened ahead of the event. The details for the 2026 edition (jury, winner) will be published by the organiser.

### Community and networks

Les Assises brings together the community of cybersecurity leaders from major French accounts around peer-to-peer networking moments: lunches, dinners and evening events. The event connects these decision-makers with the most advanced solution providers on the cyber market.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Grimaldi Forum](/lieux/grimaldi-forum) in Monaco.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Format:** participation by selection and invitation, built around pre-scheduled one-to-one meetings between decision-makers and partners.
- **Badge:** prior registration required, with detailed conditions and arrangements on the official platform [lesassisesdelacybersecurite.com](https://www.lesassisesdelacybersecurite.com).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months before: get in touch with DG Consultants for partnership and positioning.
- 6 months before: for startups, apply for the Prix de l''Innovation des Assises (closing mid-April for the October edition).
- 3 months before: build your one-to-one meeting agenda, targeting priority decision-makers.
- 6 weeks before: prepare the demos and case studies to present in conference.

### For the decision-maker attendee

- Prior registration at lesassisesdelacybersecurite.com, participation subject to profile selection.
- Build your one-to-one meeting agenda in advance, the central format of the event.
- Target the conferences and keynotes according to your priorities (sovereignty, AI, compliance, resilience).
- Plan for the networking moments (lunches, dinners, evening events) that are an integral part of the format.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Les Assises provides an eco-gestures guide encouraging participants to limit their environmental footprint during the event. Beyond this initiative, the event''s structured CSR commitments are not detailed publicly on the official website to date.

## How the trade show has evolved

