### Trajectory analysis

Les Thermalies has accumulated **44 years of history as of 2026** according to official SPAS Organisation communications, placing the first edition around 1982. The exact founding date is not publicly documented as at the date of this listing.

The trade show has maintained its historic positioning at the Carrousel du Louvre: an urban, central, 4-day format, free by invitation, targeting a mainly female, buyer-focused visitor base. The recent trajectory confirms a plateau of around **25,000 visitors / 250 to 300 exhibitors** for the Paris edition, with the regional Lyon edition gaining ground (9,000 visitors in 2025, 8th edition in 2026).

The strategic developments led by the trade show''s management (Karelle Geyer) focus on broadening the theme beyond thermal spa treatments in the strict sense: **Longévité** (launched in 2026) and **Patient Associations** reposition the event around overall preventive health, a growth segment in the silver-economy and medicalised-wellness market. The Paris + Lyon pairing in January locks in the start-of-year calendar for the French wellness sector.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='les-thermalies-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International trade show for luxury packaging. High-end packaging for cosmetics, fragrances, wines and spirits.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Luxe Pack Monaco** is the world''s benchmark gathering for luxury packaging: creative, high-end packaging solutions for cosmetics, perfumery, wines and spirits, tableware and premium spirits.
- A trade show organised by **IDICE MC** (Infopro Digital group, publisher of Emballages Magazine), held annually at the **Grimaldi Forum** in Monaco.
- Next edition: **28 to 30 September 2026** at the Grimaldi Forum. The edition''s tagline: "Unbox your vision. Lead the change."
- 2024 review (closed on 2 October): 10,300 visitors, 52% of whom were international, coming from more than 80 countries, and 450 exhibitors including 55 newcomers (sources: usinenouvelle.com, premiumpack.fr).
- A structured CSR approach built around the **LUXE PACK in Green** competition and the Grimaldi Forum''s ISO 20121 certification: [CSR approach page](https://www.luxepackmonaco.com/fr/demarche-rse).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers and designers of premium packaging, specialists in materials (glass, metal, paper and board, sustainable plastics), decoration and embellishment, packaging design, and printing and personalisation technologies. The visitor base is strictly professional: packaging, purchasing, development and marketing departments of the major luxury, beauty, fragrance, spirits and tableware houses.

### Notable exhibitors

Exhibitor list on the official website: [luxepackmonaco.com](https://www.luxepackmonaco.com/en/exhibitors-list). The 2024 edition brought together 450 exhibitors, including 55 newcomers (source: usinenouvelle.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

- 10,300 visitors at the 2024 edition, 52% of whom were international from more than 80 countries, with a notable rise in German, Emirati, Turkish and Indian participants (source: usinenouvelle.com)
- An audience geared towards packaging decision-makers from luxury and beauty houses
- A trade show historically ranked among the highest attendance figures in its sector: 10,420 visitors in 2023, the highest level since its creation (source: luxepackmonaco.com)

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The trade show offers a programme of conferences and round tables on the major challenges of luxury packaging: sustainable materials, eco-design, disruptive innovation, design and brand experience. The detailed 2026 programme will be published in the run-up to the show on luxepackmonaco.com.

### Awards and accolades

**LUXE PACK in Green**: a competition run for 14 years in partnership with **INFINITY GLOBAL**, recognising exhibitors'' best responsible solutions and initiatives, with a dedicated space, conferences and an awards ceremony (source: luxepackmonaco.com/fr/luxe-pack-in-green/).

The trade show also runs initiatives to showcase innovation, such as **Innovation Unpacked**.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Grimaldi Forum](/lieux/grimaldi-forum) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** by prior online registration on luxepackmonaco.com, reserved for sector professionals.
- **Dedicated areas:** since the expansion of the Grimaldi Forum, the show has introduced new areas, including **The Portal**, devoted to sustainable and transformative packaging technologies.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with IDICE MC, choose your positioning and book a stand.
- 6 months out: prepare product launches and demonstrations, brief the team.
- 4 months out: enter the LUXE PACK in Green competition for eco-responsible solutions.
- 6 weeks out: confirm meetings with the packaging departments of your target houses.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Pre-register online on luxepackmonaco.com with proof of professional activity.
- Allow 1 to 2 days depending on your scope (materials, decoration, printing technologies, sustainability).
- Identify the conferences and the LUXE PACK in Green area in advance for CSR matters.
- Plan accommodation ahead: the Principality and the French Riviera are in high demand in late September.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Luxe Pack Monaco sets out its commitments on its [CSR approach](https://www.luxepackmonaco.com/fr/demarche-rse) page. The Grimaldi Forum, which hosts the trade show, is certified **ISO 20121** (sustainable events) and **ISO 14001**: 100% green energy supply since 2019 (2,470 sq m of photovoltaic panels), 16 waste-sorting streams, 40 tonnes of carpet recycled per year, eco-certified cleaning products and large-format printing on recycled PVC (source: luxepackmonaco.com/fr/demarche-rse).

The **LUXE PACK in Green** competition, run in partnership with INFINITY GLOBAL, showcases exhibitors'' best responsible solutions and initiatives through a dedicated exhibition space, conferences and an awards ceremony.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
   { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
   { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
