### Trajectory analysis

Luxe Pack Monaco has settled its attendance above 10,000 visitors since 2023 (10,420 visitors, its highest level since creation), with an international share exceeding half of the visitor base. The 2024 edition confirmed this footing with 10,300 visitors and 450 exhibitors, in a dynamic of internationalisation (more than 80 countries represented). From 2025, the show embarked on a scaling-up driven by the expansion of the Grimaldi Forum and new areas such as The Portal. The 2026 edition, from 28 to 30 September, extends this trajectory around sustainability and packaging innovation, under the tagline "Unbox your vision. Lead the change."', seo_title_en='Luxe Pack Monaco 2026: dates, exhibitors and practical info', seo_description_en='Luxe Pack Monaco 2026 takes place from 28 to 30 September at the Grimaldi Forum. The world''s trade show for luxury packaging: exhibitors, key figures, CSR and how to prepare your visit.' WHERE slug='luxe-pack-monaco';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Autumn edition of the world''s reference trade fair for decoration, design and the art of living, at Paris Nord Villepinte. January 2026 edition: 67,300 visitors from 148 countries, 2,300 exhibiting brands including 500 newcomers, 50% international attendance.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Maison&Objet Paris Pulse**, autumn 2026 edition: **10 to 14 September 2026** at Paris Nord Villepinte. Complementary **Premier** edition scheduled from 14 to 18 January 2027.
- The world''s reference trade fair for decoration, design and the art of living, organised by **SAFI** (Salons Français et Internationaux), a subsidiary jointly owned by **Ateliers d''Art de France** and **RX France**, chaired by Vincent Lhoste.
- Most recent edition (January 2026): **67,300 visitors from 148 countries**, **2,300 exhibiting brands including 500 newcomers**, 50% international attendance, 65% foreign exhibitors, around **€200m in economic spin-offs for the Île-de-France region** (source: maison-objet.com).
- Designer of the Year 2026: **Harry Nuriev** (Crosby Studios, New York), with his "Transformism" manifesto. Curatorial theme for 2026: "**Past Reveals Future**", developed across 4 manifestos (Metamorphosis, Mutation, Revisited Baroque, Neo-Folklore).
- Year-round 365-day B2B digital platform **MOM (Maison&Objet and More)**: **5,000+ brands**, **30,000 products**, **480,000+ international professionals** including 300,000 in the EU, 1.5 million social media followers.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Maison&Objet Paris structures its offering around six thematic sectors aligned with the 2026 curatorial theme "Past Reveals Future". The event covers the entire value chain of the home and the art of living: decoration, furniture, lighting, tableware, textiles, home fragrance, gift and jewellery. A balanced mix of **French heritage houses** (crystal, porcelain, art furniture), **international contemporary design publishers**, **emerging young designers** and **craft artisans** showcased via the **Craft** sector run by Ateliers d''Art de France.

The **Village Manufactures d''Excellence**, a 2026 signature, brings together around twenty heritage companies from the French industrial fabric. A new **Pet Square** introduces the pet lifestyle vertical, in response to the structural rise of this market on the premium retail side.

### Iconic brands (January 2026 edition)

The autumn edition follows on editorially from January 2026, which had brought together notably (source: maison-objet.com):

- **Lalique**: immersive installation "Air de Lalique" and reissue of the Tourbillons vase designed by Suzanne Lalique.
- **Baccarat**: collaboration with Harry Nuriev around the reinterpreted Zénith chandelier.
- **CFOC** (Compagnie Française de l''Orient et de la Chine), **Alain Ellouz** (alabaster lighting), **Galerie Negropontes**.
- **Ateliers d''Art de France**: Craft hub for fine craftsmanship, an institutional showcase of exceptional savoir-faire.

### Quality of attendance

- **67,300 visitors** in January 2026 (148 countries), 50% international, **+30% Chinese visitors**, confirmed growth in the Italian, Belgian and Spanish markets (source: maison-objet.com).
- Permanent volume claimed: **300,000 international buyers/year** consolidated across the two Premier and Pulse editions, **1,500 accredited journalists/year**.
- Decision-maker profiles: purchasing departments of department stores and concept stores, premium independent retailers, hoteliers and restaurateurs (contract purchasing), interior architects, decoration/design press influencers, international agents and distributors. **Strictly professional attendance**, named non-transferable badge, proof of activity required.
- Pulse edition September 2025 (reference for the 2026 vintage): **51,500 unique visitors** including 10,400 newcomers, **2,125 exhibitors** (626 new) from 58 countries, 138 countries on the visitor side, **€111m in economic spin-offs** (source: maison-objet.com).

## Events and community

### Designer of the Year and curatorial theme

The most closely followed distinction on the design press side, the **Designer of the Year 2026** goes to **Harry Nuriev**, founder of Crosby Studios (New York). "Transformism" manifesto. The annual curatorial theme **"Past Reveals Future"** is developed across **4 manifestos** that structure the scenography and product selections: **Metamorphosis**, **Mutation**, **Revisited Baroque**, **Neo-Folklore**. This interpretive framework serves as a guide for the press and buyers (source: maison-objet.com).

### The Talks

**25 conferences over 5 days** bringing together designers, publishers, journalists and futurists. The 2026 programme is centred on the **influences of French design in the United States**, **AI applied to culture and creation**, the evolution of premium retail and new forms of residential hospitality.

### Village Manufactures d''Excellence and Pet Square

- **Village Manufactures d''Excellence**: 20 selected French heritage companies, a showcase of exceptional industrial savoir-faire.
- **Pet Square**: new 2026 sector dedicated to the premium pet world (furniture, accessories, lifestyle).

### Institutional partners and ecosystem

- **Ateliers d''Art de France**: co-shareholder of SAFI, leads the Craft hub.
- **RX France**: co-shareholder of SAFI, operational and international contribution (Reed Expositions affiliation).
- **MOM (Maison&Objet and More)**: year-round 365-day B2B digital platform that extends the physical trade fair, 5,000+ listed brands, 30,000 products, 480,000+ active professionals.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte) listing.

Specific to the trade fair:

- **Pulse dates**: Thursday 10 to Monday 14 September 2026.
- **Visitor badge**: early pre-registration from **€35**, free during the promotional window, rising to **€80** on the day, **€30 to €40** on-site, **student** rate **€15 to €20** on proof of status.
- **Named non-transferable badge**, professional proof required at registration.
- **Next Premier edition**: 14 to 18 January 2027, the reference winter format on the buyer-volume side.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published publicly. Quotes on request from **SAFI** via the application form on maison-objet.com. Several packages traditionally coexist: bare stand (floor space rental only), turnkey equipped stand, packages for young brands and emerging designers (notably via the Craft hub of Ateliers d''Art de France). Placement by thematic sector determines the rate per m².

Figures not publicly available to date.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: contact SAFI, choose the thematic sector aligned with the 4 manifestos for 2026 (Metamorphosis, Mutation, Revisited Baroque, Neo-Folklore).
- 9 months out: submit an application for the curatorial selections (Rising Talents, Craft, young designers).
- 6 months out: finalise the stand according to the chosen package, brief the contractor, plan MOM communications (digital platform listing).
- 3 months out: team accreditations, press content, scheduling of meetings with international influencers.
- 6 weeks out: activate the partner network, specialist decoration/design press, plan of pre-scheduled visits with priority buyers.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Early pre-registration strongly recommended (rate **€35** vs €80 on the day).
- 5-day trade fair: **allow at least 2 to 3 days** to cover the 6 sectors and the curatorial manifestos.
- Identify in advance the Designer of the Year (Harry Nuriev), Village Manufactures d''Excellence and Pet Square selections to pace your visit.
- Digital complement: the **MOM** platform extends the trade fair 365 days a year for sourcing between editions.

## Policy and CSR initiatives

Maison&Objet applies an **Eco-Green Charter** structured around sustainable sourcing, the "less is more" principle on the scenography side, and respect for people and the environment (source: maison-objet.com). The trade fair relies on an ecosystem of operational partners:

- **Les Canaux** (City of Paris, social and solidarity economy): support for reuse and second-hand.
- **Re''up**, **Emmaüs Défi**: upcycling and reuse channels for post-fair materials.
- **Fab City Grand Paris**: **Sustain''Lab** programme dedicated to upcycling stand elements and décor.

This CSR line is consistent with the positioning of the Craft hub and the Ateliers d''Art de France anchorage, which embrace a heritage-focused, low-carbon approach to fine craftsmanship.

## The trade fair''s evolution

