### Trajectory analysis

Maison&Objet was born in **1995** from the merger of six Parisian trade fairs (Paas, Moving, Tex''styles, Mic, Scènes d''Intérieur, Parallèles), with a first edition of 1,250 exhibitors and 38,000 visitors, run by **Blenheim** (the future Reed Expositions) and the **Ateliers d''Art de France** via SAFI. More than thirty years later, the trade fair shows **roughly three times as many exhibitors** and **nearly double the audience** at its Premier edition, with 67,300 visitors in January 2026. The dual governance of **Ateliers d''Art de France + RX France** remains structuring: it combines a fine-craftsmanship hub with strong French legitimacy and the international reach of a global trade fair operator. The **Premier (January) / Pulse (September)** split has established itself as the reference framework of the decoration-design sector, complemented by a **MOM** digital platform that now covers 365 days of B2B activity. The 2026 vintage "Past Reveals Future" and the choice of Harry Nuriev confirm an editorial line that embraces a close dialogue between heritage savoir-faire and the international avant-garde.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='maison-objet-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show dedicated to make-up formulation and packaging. Product innovations, colours and make-up trends.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- MakeUp in Paris is presented by the organiser as **the only 100% B2B European trade show dedicated to the make-up world**, broadened since 2019 to hybrid skincare, haircare and nutricosmetics.
- 2026 edition: 17 and 18 June 2026 at the **Carrousel du Louvre** (Salles du Carrousel, 99 rue de Rivoli, Paris 1er), from 10 am to 6 pm (source: makeup-in-paris.com).
- Co-located with **Édition Spéciale by LUXE PACK**: a single badge grants access to both trade shows on the same dates and at the same venue.
- More than **150 exhibitors** announced for 2026 (vs 145 in 2025 for the 15th anniversary edition). Attendance expected at around 4,000 professionals (source: premiumbeautynews.com).
- Organised by **Beauteam**, an agency founded in 2008 that became part of the **Infopro Digital** group in 2017 (sources: infopro-digital.com, cci-paris-idf.fr).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Three broad categories of upstream/supplier exhibitors:

- **Subcontractors (façonniers) and Full Service**: formulators, contract manufacturers, OEM/ODM.
- **Make-up packaging suppliers**: primary packaging, secondary packaging, applicators.
- **Ingredient and accessory suppliers**: pigments, fragrances, trend agencies.

### Notable exhibitors

Partial list confirmed for 2026 (source: makeup-in-paris.com/exhibitors): COSMAX, CHROMAVIS FAREVA, COSMESIT, DKSH France, Schwan Cosmetics, Taiki, Nippon Shikizai, Icons Beauty Group, A&H Cosmetics (subcontractors / Full Service); Century Box Mainetti, Brivaplast Group, Choebe Packaging, Dingrong, Alliance Étiquettes (packaging).

At the 2024 edition, exhibitors included: Geka, MS BeautiLab, Ancorotti Cosmetics, Anjac Health & Beauty, Fiabila, Faber-Castell, Art Cosmetics, HCT, IL Cosmetics, MPlus Cosmetics, Lumson, Libo Cosmetics, CTK, KDC One (source: premiumbeautynews.com).

### Quality of attendance

- Access strictly reserved for beauty industry professionals (proof required)
- Around 4,000 trade visitors expected
- Main targets: marketing/product directors, purchasing, R&D and formulation teams within beauty brands
- OJS data not published to date (R2)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

For 2026 the organiser announces **15 conferences** built around three pillars: **Beauty & Identity**, **Formulation & Innovation**, **Experience & Wellbeing**, with more than 30 speakers (trend agencies, dermatologists, luxury economists, journalists) (source: makeup-in-paris.com/program-animations).

### Innovation & Trends Awards (IT Awards)

Main 2026 categories: Formulation & Ingredients, Contract Manufacturing / Private Label / OEM / ODM, Packaging, Accessories. Two special 2026 prizes: **Ready-to-Market IT Award** and **Full Service IT Award**. Worth noting: the public''s Coup de Cœur (which existed in 2025) **is not being held again in 2026**. More than **100 entries** assessed by a jury of around ten international professionals (source: makeup-in-paris.com/it-awards).

### Beauty Talks, Trend Partners Spaces, activities

- **Beauty Talks**: 5 sessions of 30 minutes led by independent experts.
- **Trend Partners Spaces**: 7 dedicated trend agencies (the named 2026 list is not published by the organiser; recurring agencies in the network: Peclers Paris, NellyRodi, Beautystreams, Asia Cosme Lab, Spate).
- **ESSENTIA**: AI-driven lash diagnosis for personalised mascara recommendation (exclusive 2026 feature) (source: makeup-in-paris.com/program-animations).
- 2025 edition: **Beauty Tank** for emerging brands and start-ups, **Pop-up Ingredients and Lab** on raw materials (source: premiumbeautynews.com).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Carrousel du Louvre](/lieux/carrousel-du-louvre) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** 10 am-6 pm on 17 and 18 June 2026.
- **Visitor badge:** free with online registration, badge to be printed before arrival to speed up access. Registration contact: logan.tharpe@infopro-digital.com (source: makeup-in-paris.com).
- **Bonus:** the same badge grants access to **Édition Spéciale by LUXE PACK** on the same dates and at the same venue.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published: bespoke quote on request from Beauteam / Infopro Digital. No figure available publicly.

Visitor rates: **free** with professional pre-registration.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with Beauteam / Infopro Digital, request a stand quote.
- 9 months out: enter the **IT Awards** (record of 100+ entries in 2026: strong visibility with the international jury, press, and exposure at the Carrousel).
- 6 months out: prepare a short pitch focused on a new formula/packaging innovation (a human-scale format of ~150 stands that prioritises the quality of the buyer contact).
- 3 months out: brief the team for the Awards ceremony (usually day 1, 6 pm) and the networking cocktail that follows.
- 6 weeks out: tap into the MakeUp in network (New York, Los Angeles) for upstream communication on international exhibitors.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Online registration is mandatory, badge to be printed before arrival.
- Arrival recommended from 9 am to make the most of the trade show from opening.
- Take advantage of the co-location with **Édition Spéciale by LUXE PACK** (a single badge for two trade shows).
- Target the **Trend Partners Spaces** (7 trend agencies) and the **IT Awards** ceremony to scan the year''s trends.
- Venue is fully accessible to people with reduced mobility (lift, wheelchair available on site).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

No dedicated CSR commitments page is published to date on makeup-in-paris.com. Sustainability is addressed editorially through one-off operations (**"MakeUp in… Sustainable"** in 2022: a call for entries with 10 formulators and 12 packaging suppliers), through the **Ocean Beauty** prize created in 2025 on the environmental theme, and through a 2022 CSR round table bringing together the CSR directors of L''Oréal, Chanel Parfums Beauté, Guerlain and Yves Rocher. No formalised CSR policy from the trade show itself has been identified to date (sources: makeup-in.com, premiumbeautynews.com).

## How the trade show has evolved

