### Trajectory analysis

The trade show has settled into a human-scale format (~150 exhibitors) that prioritises the quality of the buyer contact over volume. The official broadening to hybrid skincare and haircare in 2025 (15th anniversary edition) marks an editorial shift: MakeUp in Paris is no longer confined to make-up alone and captures the cross-functional packaging and formulation directors of beauty brands. The co-location with **Édition Spéciale by LUXE PACK** over several editions amplifies attendance without diluting the specialisation. The IT Awards trajectory (from ~60 entries to more than 100 in 2026) is the most visible indicator of the trade show''s momentum.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='makeup-in-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Official baseline: "A unique event in Europe for innovation partnerships and investment rounds in MedTech, Diagnostics and Digital Health".
- A European business convention for early-stage partnering in MedTech, in vitro diagnostics and digital health: built around one-to-one meetings, startup pitches and investment rounds, rather than a conventional stand-based trade show.
- Organisers: Eurasanté, together with the Clubster NHL, Medicalps and BioValley France clusters. A travelling edition (Lille, Grenoble, Marseille depending on the year).
- 10th edition on 10 and 11 December 2026 at the [Parc Chanot](/lieux/parc-chanot-marseille) in Marseille, co-located with BioFIT to bring biotech and medtech players together on the same site.
- Stated target: 700+ international players from the sector (promotional figure from the organiser, official registration page).
- Standout themes for 2026: four conference tracks (R&D Collaborations, Licensing, Investment, Animal Health) and a partnering format structured around qualified meetings.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

MedFIT is not a consumer-facing trade show but a B2B business convention: its "exhibitors" are first and foremost partnering participants. The profiles listed for the most recent edition are, verbatim:

- "Start-ups: Medical devices – IVD – Imaging – Digital Health (≤ 5 years old)"
- "Mature companies: Medical devices – IVD – Imaging – Digital Health"
- "Investors"
- "Consulting companies / Law firms / Other service providers"
- "TTOs – Research institutions – Incubators – Academia"
- "Associations / Clusters / Public organisations"
- "Suppliers and subcontractors"

### Notable exhibitors

The list of participants and exhibitors for the edition is kept up to date on the official page: [MedFIT participants](https://www.medfit-event.com/2025-participants/). The format relies on medtech companies, diagnostics laboratories, investment funds and technology transfer organisations, rather than major consumer brands.

### Quality of the attendees

The stated target for 2026 is 700+ international players from the sector. This figure is a promotional objective communicated ahead of the event, not an audited result. The core audience is made up of medtech startup executives, business development leads, investors and technology transfer managers looking for early-stage partnerships and funding.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2026 programme is built around four tracks (official labels):

- "T.1 - R&D COLLABORATIONS": hospital-industry partnerships, large-group engagement with startups, academic entrepreneurship.
- "T.2 - LICENSING": due diligence strategies, digital health market dynamics.
- "T.3 - INVESTMENT": family offices, the evolution of capital, the impact of regulation on funding.
- "T.4 - ANIMAL HEALTH".

A plenary session has been announced on the theme: "Innovation under pressure: Strategic levers for validation, capital access and healthcare systems integration".

### Awards and accolades

The event schedules pitch sessions under the "Start-up Slams" format, a dedicated platform for young companies to present their projects to investors and industrial partners.

### Community & networks

MedFIT draws on the ecosystem of French health clusters (Clubster NHL, Medicalps, BioValley France) and the Eurasanté incubator. Co-location with BioFIT extends the network to biotech and life sciences players. Discussions continue on the event''s LinkedIn account.

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the [Parc Chanot](/lieux/parc-chanot-marseille) listing, Rond-point du Prado, 13008 Marseille.

Specific to MedFIT 2026:

- Dates: Tuesday 10 and Wednesday 11 December 2026, opening from 8.30am each day.
- Access: proof of identity (ID card or passport) is required at the entrance.
- Badge: the conference badge must be worn at all times, including during the evening reception. Badges are sent by email ahead of the event and can be printed at the welcome desk.
- Security: bags and luggage are checked at the entrance.
- Platform: partnering relies on a schedule of one-to-one meetings arranged in advance.

## What it costs to exhibit

MedFIT offers several exhibition and registration packages, priced according to profile and registration date. As of 19 June 2026, the regular rate is in effect (early bird closed on 18 June 2026; late registration from 2 October 2026).

<BudgetTable warning="Rates published on the official website as at the date of writing. All prices are exclusive of VAT. The rate shown in the ''low'' column corresponds to the super early bird (before 12 March 2026, now closed), and the ''high'' column to the regular rate (from 19 June 2026). Contact the organiser for bespoke options." rows={[{ "poste": "Start-up Corner 4 m² (company ≤ 5 years old)", "low": "1 550 €", "high": "1 824 €" }, { "poste": "Fitted stand 6 m²", "low": "2 570 €", "high": "3 024 €" }, { "poste": "Fitted stand 9 m²", "low": "3 590 €", "high": "4 224 €" }, { "poste": "Fitted stand 12 m²", "low": "4 344 €", "high": "5 110 €" }, { "poste": "Fitted stand 18 m²", "low": "5 850 €", "high": "6 882 €" }, { "poste": "Full delegate pass (startups/SMEs)", "low": "450 €", "high": "635 €" }, { "poste": "Full delegate pass (TTO / universities / research)", "low": "467 €", "high": "660 €" }, { "poste": "Full delegate pass (large company)", "low": "929 €", "high": "1 254 €" }, { "poste": "Full delegate pass (service providers)", "low": "1 254 €", "high": "1 693 €" }, { "poste": "Visitor pass (without partnering platform access)", "low": "450 €", "high": "450 €" }, { "poste": "Investor pass", "low": "Free", "high": "Free" }]} totals={[{ "label": "Stand + pass range", "low": "2 000 €", "high": "7 000 € +" }]} footer="Prices exclusive of VAT, super early bird / regular rate range. Source: medfit-event.com/exhibition/book-your-stand/ and medfit-event.com/register/registration-fees/." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 4 months out: confirm your participation package and your profile on the partnering platform.
- 3 months out: complete your company listing and your matching criteria to optimise one-to-one meetings.
- 2 months out: prepare your pitch (in particular if applying for the Start-up Slams) and identify priority targets.
- 1 month out: confirm your schedule of arranged meetings and prepare your materials.

### For the decision-maker attending

- Define your objectives in advance: sourcing early-stage projects, seeking funding, licensing or R&D partnerships.
- Activate your meetings schedule as soon as the platform opens to secure slots with the profiles you are targeting.
- Identify the relevant sessions across the four tracks and the plenaries on funding and market access.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

As at the date of writing, the official MedFIT website carries no Commitments/CSR page or any publicly verifiable dedicated event certification. The organiser Eurasanté is an economic development group (GIE) for the health sector, but no CSR programme specific to the event can be sourced as things stand. Information to be confirmed with the organiser before making any claim.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "participants", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "10th (2026, upcoming)", "dates": "10-11 Dec. 2026", "lieu": "Parc Chanot, Marseille", "participants": "700+ (target)" }, { "edition": "9th (2025)", "dates": "8-9 Oct. 2025", "lieu": "Grenoble", "participants": "~600 (organiser reference, 2 editions)" }, { "edition": "2024", "dates": "n/a", "lieu": "Lille", "participants": "n/a" }]} sources="Official MedFIT website (medfit-event.com)." />

### Trajectory analysis

MedFIT confirms its model as a travelling business convention, anchoring the event in turn within France''s major health ecosystems (Lille, Grenoble, Marseille). The format remains centred on early-stage partnering and investment in medtech, diagnostics and digital health, as opposed to a conventional stand-based trade show. The 10th edition in 2026 marks two shifts: the return to Marseille at the Parc Chanot and co-location with BioFIT, bringing the biotech and medtech communities together on a single site to increase opportunities for cross-sector meetings. The target of 700+ participants places the event in a tighter, more qualified format, where value is measured by the number and relevance of business meetings rather than by footfall.', seo_title_en='MedFIT 2026 Marseille: dates, partnering, programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='MedFIT 2026, the 10th edition of the medtech/diagnostics/digital health business convention, on 10-11 December at the Parc Chanot in Marseille. 700+ participants expected, one-to-one meetings, Start-up Slams.' WHERE slug='medfit-marseille';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- A B2B business convention dedicated to medical devices and health technologies, held in Lyon in early July.
- Organised by Proximum SAS (a subsidiary of the Comexposium group), with the support of the long-standing co-founders David Bilman and Xavier Kessous. Lyonbiopole, BioValley France, Eurobiomed and Medicen are partners, under the Enosis Santé alliance.
- 14th edition on 1 and 2 July 2026 at the [Centre des Congrès de Lyon](/lieux/centre-de-congres-de-lyon), Cité Internationale.
- A convention format: qualified one-to-one meetings, innovation showrooms and expert conferences, rather than a classic stand-based trade show.
- 2025 edition: 1,250 participants, 130 exhibitors, 60 speakers, 30 conferences (organiser figures).
- Announced theme for 2026: the place of AI throughout the life cycle of the medical device.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile
Medi''Nov Connection brings together the players across the medical device value chain: medtech manufacturers and industrial firms, healthcare establishments, e-health experts, subcontractors and technical service providers, investors and financial backers. The model is that of a business convention: participants come for one-to-one meetings scheduled in advance, not to walk the aisles of stands.

### Notable exhibitors
The list of the edition''s exhibitors and partners is published on the [official participants'' platform](https://medinov.vimeet.events/fr/list/second). On the ecosystem side, the event draws on the health competitiveness clusters Lyonbiopole, BioValley France, Eurobiomed and Medicen, brought together within the Enosis Santé alliance.

### Quality of the audience
For the 2025 edition, the organiser reports 1,250 participants and 130 exhibitors. The one-to-one format favours the qualification of meetings: appointments are scheduled according to the profiles and projects declared, which orientates the event towards business matchmaking rather than mass attendance.

## Events & community

### Conference programme
The programme combines plenary conferences, Flash Conferences, thematic round tables and an experimentation space, the Medi''Nov LAB. For 2026, the organiser announces a guiding thread centred on artificial intelligence in the life cycle of the medical device, with two round tables and seven plenary conferences on this theme. The detailed programme is put online on the dedicated congress page as the event approaches.

### Awards and prizes
The event runs an innovation competition, which selects 8 start-ups to pitch before the medtech community during a session of 5 minutes each. The vote is split between the public (75%) and a jury (25%), with the ceremony on the evening of 1 July. The 2026 edition notably features feedback from previous winners.

### Community & networks
Medi''Nov Connection is part of the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes health ecosystem and beyond, through its cluster partners (Lyonbiopole, BioValley France, Eurobiomed, Medicen) gathered under the Enosis Santé alliance. Thematic guided tours and visits organised by Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes Entreprises are also offered around the event.

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the listing for the [Centre des Congrès de Lyon](/lieux/centre-de-congres-de-lyon), located at 50 Quai Charles de Gaulle, in the Cité Internationale (Lyon Part-Dieu station around 15 min away, Lyon Saint-Exupéry airport around 30 min away, underground car park with charging points).

Specific to the edition: on 1 and 2 July 2026, announced opening hours are 9am to 6pm on 1 July and 9am to 5pm on 2 July. Registration and appointment booking are done on the event''s digital platform (medinov.vimeet.events), which serves as the matching tool for the one-to-one meetings.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Medi''Nov Connection is a business convention with no classic stand model: participation is organised around exhibitor or participant packages giving access to the scheduled one-to-one meetings, the innovation showrooms and the conferences, rather than to a surface area in square metres. The price lists are not published in open access: they are obtained from the organiser via the exhibitor page. The total cost depends on the package chosen (number of meetings, visibility, sponsorship) and on the additional costs of travel and accommodation in Lyon.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor
- 4 to 3 months before: validate your participation package with the organiser and complete your profile on the platform (offering, projects, target audiences sought).
- 2 months before: prepare your showroom materials and your value proposition for the one-to-one matching.
- 3 to 2 weeks before: confirm your schedule of booked meetings and identify the conferences to follow.
- 1 week before: confirm logistics, access to the Centre des Congrès and accommodation.

### For the decision-maker visitor
Register in advance on the platform to activate the matching, set out your needs precisely (sourcing, technical partnerships, financing), then build your schedule of meetings and select the relevant conferences before the event. As the format is centred on scheduling, the value is captured above all by preparing your meetings in advance.

## CSR policy & initiatives

No structured CSR policy specific to the event is publicly documented on the website to date. As the event is organised by Proximum SAS (Comexposium group) and hosted at the Centre des Congrès de Lyon (operated by GL Events), sustainability commitments at the level of the organising group and the venue may apply, but are not detailed at the level of the convention.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "participants", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "14th (2026, upcoming)", "dates": "1-2 July 2026", "lieu": "Centre des Congrès de Lyon", "participants": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "2025", "dates": "n/a", "lieu": "Lyon", "participants": "1,250", "exposants": "130" }]} sources="Official website medinov-connection.com, Comexposium." />

### Trajectory analysis
Launched in 2013, Medi''Nov Connection has established itself as the benchmark medtech business event in the Lyon region, capitalising on the density of the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes health ecosystem. The event approaches its 14th edition in a context of operational transition: historically run by the agency First Connection, it is now organised by Proximum SAS, a subsidiary of the Comexposium group, with co-founders David Bilman and Xavier Kessous supporting the handover. This attachment to a major events operator may broaden the convention''s resources and reach, while retaining its differentiating format of one-to-one meetings, set apart from the stand-based trade show model embodied by the major European medtech events.', seo_title_en='Medi''Nov Connection 2026 Lyon: dates, programme, B2B meetings | Agoris', seo_description_en='Medi''Nov Connection 2026: 14th medtech business convention, 1-2 July at the Centre des Congrès de Lyon. 1,250 participants, 130 exhibitors, one-to-one meetings, innovation competition.' WHERE slug='medi-nov-connection-lyon';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **MEDICA** is the world''s leading trade fair for medical technology and healthcare, held every year in Düsseldorf by **Messe Düsseldorf GmbH**. Its official title: *International Trade Fair for Medical Technology and Healthcare*.
- Next edition: 16 to 19 November 2026 (Monday to Thursday) at the [Messe Düsseldorf](/lieux/messe-dusseldorf). Hall 9 is undergoing a complete refurbishment in 2026-2027 and will not be available as exhibition space for this edition.
- Latest fully reported edition (2024, post-show figures published by Messe Düsseldorf): around 80,000 professional visitors from 165 countries and 5,800 exhibiting companies from 72 nations, MEDICA and COMPAMED combined, of whom more than 90% were decision-makers.
- MEDICA runs alongside **COMPAMED**, the trade show dedicated to the supplier industry of medical technology (subcontracting, components), on the same dates and at the same venue.
- For 2026, the trade fair adopts a new thematic structure across five areas: Clinical Diagnostics & Therapeutic Technologies, Digital Medicine, Data & Artificial Intelligence, Integrated Care, Rehabilitation & Homecare, Healthcare Infrastructure, Manufacturing & Quality, and Healthcare Systems, Education & Global Health.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers of medical and imaging devices, developers of digital health solutions, laboratory and diagnostics, electromedical and physiotherapy equipment, consumables and single-use devices, medtech start-ups, distributors and prescribers. The visitor base is strictly professional and strongly international: the share of visitors travelling from abroad traditionally exceeds two thirds, with a marked presence from Asia (China, South Korea, India, Japan, Taiwan), Europe and the United States.

### Notable exhibitors

Exhibitor listing on the official website: [MEDICA exhibitor directory](https://www.medica-tradefair.com/vis/v1/fr/directory/p). The 2025 edition brought together 5,300 exhibiting companies from 70 nations. The companies present cover the entire medical technology value chain, from major international equipment makers to the component suppliers found on the COMPAMED side.

### Quality of the visitor base

- Strictly professional visitor base, with more than 90% decision-makers at the 2024 edition and a satisfaction rate above 90%
- Strong internationalisation: 165 countries represented in 2024, 160 countries in 2025, with 75% international visitors in 2025
- Presence of buyers, technical management, clinicians and distributors coming to source medtech innovation on a global scale

## Events & community

### Conference programme

MEDICA rolls out a programme of forums and thematic conferences covering artificial intelligence, robotics, digitalisation and connected care, issues placed at the heart of the sector''s transformation. The programme is built around recurring platforms (forums dedicated to digital health, the laboratory, physiotherapy and start-ups). The detailed programme and the campaign theme are published as each edition approaches on medica-tradefair.com.

### Community and networks

The event brings together the global medical technology ecosystem: manufacturers, suppliers, distributors, clinicians and start-ups.

The 2025 edition''s campaign was carried by the strapline "Meet Health. Future. People." Messe Düsseldorf also runs an international network of offices and national pavilions that structure the participation of foreign delegations.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Messe Düsseldorf](/lieux/messe-dusseldorf) listing.

Specific to the trade fair:

- **Opening hours:** Monday to Wednesday from 10am to 6pm, Thursday from 10am to 4pm.
- **Accommodation:** a dedicated hotel booking platform set up by Messe Düsseldorf with Kuoni Tumlare Congress, offering room allocations close to the exhibition grounds.
- **Co-location:** the ticket and logistics cover joint access to COMPAMED, held at the same venue on the same dates.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- T-12 months: make contact with Messe Düsseldorf and choose your positioning among the five 2026 thematic areas, or on the COMPAMED side for suppliers.
- T-9 months: book your stand and register for the forums and special programmes.
- T-6 months: prepare product demonstrations and brief your sales teams on the international delegations expected.
- T-3 months: activate your communications via the online exhibitor directory and the national pavilions.
- T-6 weeks: confirm buyer meetings and prepare logistics (transport, set-up).

### For the decision-making visitor

- Register online at medica-tradefair.com with proof of professional activity.
- Allow at least one to two days given the scale of the trade fair (several halls, Hall 9 unavailable in 2026).
- Target the five thematic areas and the relevant forums in advance: the programme is published several weeks before the show.
- Arrange accommodation early via the official platform, as hotel demand in Düsseldorf is very high during the show week.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

MEDICA''s CSR commitments are part of the sustainability strategy of its organiser Messe Düsseldorf. The operator has reduced its event-specific electricity consumption by 52% (over the 2010-2019 period) and its heating requirements by 30% compared with 2000. Messe Düsseldorf states that it has avoided around 19,500 tonnes of CO2 compared with 2011 (Scope 1 and 2). The exhibition grounds are fitted with photovoltaic panels (550,000 kWh/year) and certified ISO 50001 for energy management.

Messe Düsseldorf is among the first signatories of the "Net Zero Carbon Events Pledge" and offers a support guide for exhibitors aimed at more sustainable participation.

## How the trade fair has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
