  { "edition": "2024", "visiteurs": "~80,000", "exposants": "5,800" }
 ]}
 sources="medica-tradefair.com, messe-duesseldorf.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

MEDICA confirms edition after edition its status as the world''s largest B2B medical trade fair, with a stable base of around 5,000 to 5,800 exhibitors and 78,000 to 80,000 professional visitors from more than 160 countries. The MEDICA and COMPAMED figures are often reported in aggregate by Messe Düsseldorf, which calls for caution when reading the totals: the 2024 total of 5,800 exhibitors includes around 750 suppliers on the COMPAMED side. The 2026 edition, from 16 to 19 November, adopts a new thematic structure across five areas and will be held without Hall 9 (undergoing a complete refurbishment). The target figures and the detailed 2026 programme will be published as the show approaches.', seo_title_en='MEDICA 2026 Düsseldorf: dates, exhibitors, practical info | Agoris', seo_description_en='MEDICA 2026, the world''s leading medical technology trade fair, runs from 16 to 19 November at the Messe Düsseldorf. Dates, exhibitors, new thematic structure, COMPAMED and tips for exhibiting or visiting.' WHERE slug='medica-dusseldorf';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Official positioning: "Information, inspiration and networking around the development and manufacture of medical technology" (medteclive.com).
- Organiser: MedtecLIVE GmbH (a subsidiary of NürnbergMesse, registered office Messezentrum 1, 90471 Nuremberg). The MedtecSUMMIT congress is tied to the Innovation Expo editions in Nuremberg (reduced format, odd-numbered years); it is not associated with the Stuttgart edition.
- Next edition (main trade show): 2-4 May 2028 at [Messe Stuttgart](/lieux/messe-stuttgart). The flagship show takes place in Stuttgart in even-numbered years; odd-numbered years see an Innovation Expo in Nuremberg (reduced format).
- Reference figures (2026 edition, Stuttgart): more than 4,000 trade visitors (post-show press release 8 May 2026, organiser figure, not OJS-audited); around 300 exhibitors expected according to pre-show forecasts.
- Positioning: European spring trade show dedicated to the development and manufacture of medical devices (processes, components, materials, services).
- Decision-maker audience: medical device manufacturers, subcontractors, component and material suppliers, regulatory and industrial service providers.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

MedtecLIVE brings together the upstream side of medical device manufacturing: subcontracting and contract production, plastics processing and microtechnology, components and materials, production machinery and equipment, cleanrooms, medical electronics, sterilisation, as well as the associated services (regulatory affairs, quality, consulting). It is a value-chain trade show, geared towards engineering and production rather than finished products.

### Notable exhibitors

The official exhibitor list and floor plan are published on the organiser''s website: see the [MedtecLIVE exhibitor list](https://www.medteclive.com/en). Several networks and clusters are recurring partners of the show: Medical Mountains, VDMA, Bayern Innovativ, VDWF, Kunststoff-Netzwerk Franken, Swiss Medtech and BVMed (partners cited for the 2026 edition).

### Quality of the visitor base

For the 2026 edition in Stuttgart, the organiser confirmed more than 4,000 trade visitors. Among the delegations expected in 2026 were notably visitors from the Czech Republic, the Netherlands and Ireland (announced pre-show). Italy was represented by a collective pavilion of more than ten exhibitors; Switzerland, via Swiss Medtech, with more than fifteen companies. The visitor base is mostly made up of technical and procurement decision-makers from the medical device industry, with an international dimension.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The trade show is built around a lively conference programme across two forums on the exhibition floor, covering innovation, regulation and trends in medtech manufacturing. The detailed 2028 programme will be published as the edition approaches on the official website.

### Prizes and awards

No prize or award presented during the show is confirmed verbatim on the official website as at the date of writing. This section will be completed if the organiser publishes an honours list for the 2028 edition.

### Community and networks

MedtecLIVE relies on a dense network of medtech clusters and federations (Medical Mountains, BVMed, Swiss Medtech, VDMA, VDWF) that run collective stands and networking sessions. The brand communicates around bringing technical contacts directly together, serving the entire value chain.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking, accommodation and transport: see the venue page [Messe Stuttgart](/lieux/messe-stuttgart). The exhibition centre is adjacent to Stuttgart Airport, served by the S-Bahn.

Show-specific: the 2028 edition is announced for 2 to 4 May 2028 at Messe Stuttgart (Messepiazza 1, 70629 Stuttgart). Opening hours confirmed on the official website: Tuesday 2 May 9am-5pm, Wednesday 3 May 9am-5pm, Thursday 4 May 9am-4pm. The halls, floor plan and badge accreditation arrangements will be published on the official website when registration opens. Worth noting for multi-year planning: the Innovation Expo offshoot takes place in Nuremberg in odd-numbered years (reduced format, associated with the MedtecSUMMIT).

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="Indicative sector ranges. The official rate card (price per sqm, bare vs equipped stand, charges) is not published as at the date of writing: refer to the MedtecLIVE exhibitor pack for the exact amounts." rows={[{ "poste": "Bare floor space (per sqm, indicative)", "low": "210 €", "high": "300 €" }, { "poste": "Turnkey equipped stand (12-20 sqm)", "low": "6 000 €", "high": "14 000 €" }, { "poste": "Fit-out, furniture, signage", "low": "3 000 €", "high": "12 000 €" }, { "poste": "Logistics, utilities, cleaning, registration fees", "low": "1 500 €", "high": "5 000 €" }, { "poste": "Staff, travel, accommodation (3 days)", "low": "3 000 €", "high": "10 000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (12-20 sqm stand, indicative)", "low": "~18 000 €", "high": "~50 000 €" }]} footer="Indicative estimate for a medium-sized stand. The collective stands run by the partner clusters (Medical Mountains, Swiss Medtech) offer a lower-cost way in." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 to 12 months out: book the floor space, decide between an own stand and a collective cluster stand (Medical Mountains, Swiss Medtech).
- 6 months out: finalise the fit-out, brief the team on the decision-maker targets, plan business meetings.
- 3 months out: settle the logistics, declare machinery and demonstrators, prepare regulatory and technical materials.
- 1 month out: confirm accreditations, follow up with qualified contacts, organise the stand schedule.

### For the decision-maker visitor

Target the relevant value-chain exhibitors in advance via the official list and floor plan, book meetings with subcontractors and component suppliers, and block out the sessions of the two forums on regulatory and process topics. Favour the collective stands to map out a segment quickly (plastics processing, microtechnology, cleanrooms).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

As at the date of writing, MedtecLIVE does not publish a dedicated Commitments/CSR page for the event. At organiser level, NürnbergMesse pursues structured and verifiable sustainability commitments: ISO 50001 certification (energy management) since 2014, renewed for the period running to 2027; an ISO 14001 process (environmental management) underway since 2023, valid until 2026; DGNB Platinum for halls 3A and 3C; photovoltaic generation (5.2 GWh in 2025) that has saved 4,340 tonnes of CO2 since the system was commissioned; a show ticket that doubles as a public transport pass; signatory of the fairpflichtet initiative and of the Charta der Vielfalt. No ISO 20121 certification specific to the MedtecLIVE event is publicly documented.

## How the show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2028 (upcoming)", "dates": "2-4 May 2028", "lieu": "Messe Stuttgart", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "2026", "dates": "5-7 May 2026", "lieu": "Messe Stuttgart", "visiteurs": "> 4,000 (post-show)", "exposants": "~300 (pre-show forecast)" }]} sources="Official website medteclive.com (event pages and post-show press release May 2026)." />

### Trajectory analysis

MedtecLIVE was born in 2019 from the coming together of NürnbergMesse and UBM (Informa Markets since the 2018 acquisition), merging the former Medtec Europe and MT-CONNECT trade shows. In 2022, MedtecLIVE GmbH absorbed Messe Stuttgart''s T4M (Technology for Medical Devices) show, giving rise to the "MedtecLIVE with T4M" format for its first combined Stuttgart edition. The show now operates on an annual rhythm with alternation: in even-numbered years, a major show at Messe Stuttgart; in odd-numbered years, a reduced-format Innovation Expo in Nuremberg (associated with the MedtecSUMMIT). This page covers the Stuttgart edition, the show''s main showcase, whose 2026 edition drew more than 4,000 trade visitors.', seo_title_en='MedtecLIVE 2028 Stuttgart: dates, exhibitors, programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='MedtecLIVE with T4M 2028: 2-4 May at Messe Stuttgart. Over 4,000 trade visitors (2026 edition). Medical technology trade show, organised by MedtecLIVE GmbH (NürnbergMesse).' WHERE slug='medteclive-stuttgart';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International trade show for microtechnologies and precision engineering. The benchmark event for watchmaking, medical, aerospace and micro-nanotechnologies.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Micronora 2026 runs from **29 September to 2 October 2026** at [Micropolis Besançon](/lieux/micropolis-besancon), the leading international trade show for microtechnologies, precision engineering and nanotechnologies. Held biennially in even years, organised by the Micronora association (a dedicated entity, distinct from the Pôle des Microtechniques, which remains an industrial partner).
- 2024 edition results: **14,500 trade visitors and 750 exhibitors** across **25,000 m²**, a return to pre-Covid levels. Exhibitor breakdown: 30% regional, 28% national, 32% international from 21 countries.
- 2026 target: **800 exhibitors** across 25,000 m², with **85% of space sold by April 2026** (505 exhibitors already announced at that date, of which 21% were newcomers). Growth expected compared with 2024.
- **2026 Zoom focus on aerospace, space and defence (ASD)**, the show''s first ASD theme since 2000. The programme is run with the ASD cluster of the Pôle des Microtechniques, supported by GIFAS, the DGAC and the Ministry of the Armed Forces. A dedicated ASD Day takes place on 30 September.
- Announced launch of **Micronora Americas** at the Palais des Congrès de Montréal from **14 to 16 September 2027**: 120 exhibitors targeted (50% European, 50% North American), an industrial gateway between Europe and North America.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A B2B trade show covering the entire microtechnology value chain: R&D, subcontracting and production technologies. The scope spans micromechanics, micro-machining, additive manufacturing, micro-electronics, MEMS, optics, instrumentation and nanotechnologies (open to nano since 2006). Historical applications: watchmaking, medical, luxury goods, automotive. Growing applications: aerospace, space, defence and telecoms.

### Notable exhibitors

Regional and international exhibitors cited for 2026: Aurea Technology, Dixi Microtechniques, Axon''Nanotech, STSI, Exail, SKF. The major names of the Franche-Comté and Swiss microtechnology fabric of the Jura Arc have a long-standing presence. The 2026 and 2024 exhibitor lists are available on the [official exhibitors page](https://micronora.com/en/exhibitors-2024/).

### Visitor quality

A decision-maker industrial visitor base: technical management, R&D, design offices, buyers, SME and mid-cap executives, and prime contractors (aerospace, medical, luxury watchmaking, automotive, defence). A strong international component: 21 countries represented on the exhibitor side in 2024. Long-standing influence across the Jura Arc (France, Switzerland).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

A cycle of conferences, round tables and Agora sessions over the 4 days. 2026 edition: a talk by Philippe Croizon on resilience and human innovation. ASD Day on 30 September 2026, with contributions from institutional partners (GIFAS, space agencies). Fabrique 4.0 activities (mobile training unit).

### Awards & accolades

**Micronora Awards**: an innovation competition reserved for exhibitors, co-exhibitors, brands and firms represented at the show. **Three official categories** (verbatim labels):

- **Machines & capital equipment**
- **Microtechnology components & sub-assemblies**
- **Intelligent systems & software**

Three award tiers: **Micron d''Or**, **Micron d''Argent**, and **special jury mentions**. Notable 2024 winners: Chiron (Micron d''Or Machines for the Micro5 machining centre), Silmach (Micron d''Or Components for the Silicon Core), Percipio Robotics (Micron d''Or Intelligent Systems for Digital Twin), Nidec (Micron d''Argent Machines for the Cut and Weld System), Laser Cheval (special mention for Quartz Géode).

### Satellite events

**15th edition of the Micro Nano Event**: international B2B business meetings organised alongside the show. Exhibitors'' evening. The exhibition "From watchmaking expertise to the technologies of the future" sets the Franche-Comté watchmaking heritage against emerging technologies. 2026 demonstrations: omnidirectional drones, aircraft cockpit displays (linked to the ASD Zoom).

### Community & networks

**Micronora Informations** magazine: a quarterly publication distributed to 15,000 industrial decision-makers across the French-speaking area (France, Switzerland, Belgium).

Institutional partners: Région Bourgogne-Franche-Comté, Grand Besançon Métropole, CCI Bourgogne-Franche-Comté, Bpifrance, UNIMEV, FIM Mecallians, Pôle des Microtechniques (PMT).

### New for 2026

**Aerospace, space and defence Zoom** (the first ASD Zoom since 2000), with dedicated demonstrations and an ASD Day on 30 September. Announcement of the launch of **Micronora Americas** in Montréal in September 2027, the show''s first international extension. A reinforced presence of micro-nanotechnologies for European industrial sovereignty.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Micropolis Besançon](/lieux/micropolis-besancon), Besançon Exhibition Centre, Bourgogne-Franche-Comté.
- **Access and logistics**: see the [Micropolis Besançon](/lieux/micropolis-besancon) page for transport, parking and accommodation.
- **Opening hours**: from Tuesday 29 September to Friday 2 October 2026 (4 days).
- **2026 edition highlights**: ASD Day on 30 September, Fabrique 4.0 demonstrations, watchmaking-technologies exhibition.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: get in touch with the Micronora association, choose your stand location (the show was 85% sold as early as April 2026, so submit your application early for future editions)
- 9 months out: enter the Micronora Awards (relevant category: Machines & capital equipment / Components & sub-assemblies / Intelligent systems & software), brief your stand
- 6 months out: register for the 15th Micro Nano Event (B2B meetings by schedule), brief your international team (32% of exhibitors are international, so plan for FR/EN support)
- 3 months out: accreditations, accommodation in Besançon (limited availability, plan ahead)
- 6 weeks out: prepare your ASD pitch if you are involved in the Zoom, target aerospace-space-defence prime contractors

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Identify the 10 to 20 priority exhibitors in advance via the official exhibitors page (the Pôle des Microtechniques offers sector-specific itineraries)
- Schedule your Micro Nano Event B2B meetings in advance (structured 30-minute format)
- The ASD Day on 30 September is the one to prioritise for aerospace-space-defence buyers
- Allow 2 days to cover the 25,000 m² plus conferences and demonstrations

## CSR policy & initiatives

At the time of writing, the official Micronora website does not feature a publicly structured "CSR commitments" page. The identified elements with a sustainability dimension relate more to the content on display than to a show-level policy: the presence of nanotechnology R&D in biocompatible materials, micro-sensors for medical and environmental applications, and a 2024 focus on intelligent microtechnologies (22 research institutions, projects such as Smart BRA for early breast cancer detection). The Micronora association is also a member of UNIMEV, the professional body that runs the sector CSR framework for events in France.

## How the show has evolved

