### Trajectory analysis

In 2025 Milipol Paris consolidates its status as the world''s leading event for state homeland security and safety, with massive internationalisation (+44% foreign visitors, 160 nationalities, 163 official delegations) and an exhibitor base that is 67% international. The structuring into five Innovation Awards categories (cyber and AI, first responder, drone and counter-drone, crisis management, CSR) reflects two underlying shifts: the convergence of physical security and cybersecurity driven by force employment doctrine (drones, operational AI, information warfare), and an unprecedented integration of CSR across this perimeter. The **Milipol Network** (Qatar, Singapore MTX, India launching) secures a quarterly presence in the zones with the highest public security purchasing power (the Gulf, Asia-Pacific, the Indian subcontinent). A variable to watch for 2027: the capacity of the Villepinte site to absorb a fresh wave of exhibitor growth if the 2025 momentum continues, and the evolution of delegation access conditions in a tense geopolitical context.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='milipol-paris';
