## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- T-18 months (autumn 2026): make contact with Alpexpo, thematic positioning, booking of a strategic location near the collective pavilions if relevant
- T-12 months (spring 2027): confirm surface area and hall, apply for the Mountain Innovation Awards, apply for the Grenoble Alpes or French Tech Alpes Start-up Village collective pavilions
- T-6 months (October 2027): final stand plan, builder brief, equipment and demonstrator logistics, team accreditations
- T-3 months (January 2028): Grenoble accommodation, commercial brief and lead targets, scheduling of B2B meetings with resort operators
- T-6 weeks (March 2028): delivery of materials, final team brief, activation of client invitation campaigns, badge pre-registration

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free pre-registration required in advance, personalised badge on proof of professional activity
- Identify priority conferences in advance among the many events offered over the 3 days
- Allow a minimum of 2 days to cover the 60,000 sq m and the collective pavilions
- If possible, combine the visit with a trip to a neighbouring Alpine resort (Chamrousse, Sept Laux, Vercors) for complementary operational meetings

## CSR policy & initiatives

Alpexpo and Mountain Planet set the event within an approach to reducing its environmental footprint: low-carbon mobility prioritised to the site (direct tram A from the station), pooled catering and logistics, promotion of short supply chains and the region via the local collective pavilions. Natural risk management and the climate resilience of mountain territories are also a recurring editorial theme of the trade show, in connection with ANENA. The detail of the edition''s commitments is specified by the organiser as the trade show approaches.

## How the trade show has evolved

