### Trajectory analysis

Mountain Planet confirms, edition after edition, its status as the world''s largest mountain trade show by size. Following the 2024 fiftieth anniversary (23,604 visitors, 462 exhibitors, around 900 brands, 67 countries, +17% vs 2022), the 2026 edition recorded +4.5% trade visitors vs 2024 (i.e. ~24,650 visitors) and 460 exhibitors across 60,000 sq m, with the opening of a second hall: momentum that durably anchors the event among the world''s sector benchmarks.

Three structural indicators explain this consistency. First, **industrial continuity**: POMA, Doppelmayr, Leitner, Kässbohrer, Prinoth, TechnoAlpin and MND Group form a base of exhibitors present for several decades within the Grenoble ecosystem. Next, **editorial diversification**: the trade show has broadened its scope beyond ski-area equipment alone towards sport-health, natural risk management and climate resilience, which are matters of society and public policy. Finally, **institutional anchoring**: distinct partnerships with ANEM and ANENA, collective pavilions led by Grenoble Alpes Métropole and French Tech Alpes, and operation by a Société Publique Locale backed by the metropolitan authority.

The 2028 edition, scheduled from 11 to 13 April at Alpexpo Grenoble, takes place two years out from the 2030 Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games awarded to the French Alps. It promises to be one of the most strategic of the decade for those working in mountain planning, mobility and hospitality, as the Alpine region prepares for an Olympic horizon that will shape investment and infrastructure.', seo_title_en='Mountain Planet 2028 - Global mountain development trade show | Grenoble', seo_description_en='Mountain Planet 2028: the global gathering for the mountain sector, 11-13 April 2028 at Alpexpo Grenoble. Ski lifts, snowmaking, climate resilience. A pivotal edition 2 years out from the 2030 Olympic Winter Games.' WHERE slug='mountain-planet';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The Mobile World Congress (MWC) is the world''s largest trade show dedicated to the mobile telephony industry. Organised by the GSM Association (GSMA), it brings together the sector''s leading players every year. The GSMA gathers more than 850 mobile operators and nearly 250 companies from the telecommunications ecosystem worldwide.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- MWC Barcelona (Mobile World Congress) is the world''s largest gathering for connectivity and telecoms, organised by the **GSMA**, the association that brings together more than 750 mobile operators worldwide.
- The 2026 edition, which marked the trade show''s **20th anniversary** in Barcelona, was held from 2 to 5 March 2026 at the [Fira Barcelona Gran Via](/lieux/fira-barcelona-gran-via) under the theme "Infinite AI".
- Next edition announced: **MWC27, from 1 to 4 March 2027**, at the same venue, under the theme **"The IQ Era"**.
- 2026 review (post-show GSMA figures): nearly **105,000 attendees** from 207 countries and territories, **2,900 exhibitors, sponsors and partners**, more than 1,700 speakers and 2,600 accredited journalists and analysts. Estimated economic impact for Barcelona: 588 million euros (source: gsma.com).
- The startup trade show **4YFN**, also organised by the GSMA, is co-located and included within the same ecosystem.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Mobile operators, network equipment makers, chipmakers, device manufacturers, software publishers and cloud players, corporate IT departments, AI and connectivity players, as well as government delegations and regulatory authorities. The attendee base is strictly professional and strongly international: 207 countries and territories represented in 2026, and 58% of attendees coming from industries adjacent to the core of the mobile ecosystem (source: gsma.com).

The co-located startup trade show **4YFN** brings together more than 1,000 startups and exhibitors, as well as investors representing over 70 billion euros in funds (source: 4yfn.com).

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [mwcbarcelona.com](https://www.mwcbarcelona.com/). The trade show gathers the world''s leading connectivity names: operators, network equipment makers, device manufacturers, chipmakers and cloud platforms. The precise composition by edition is published on the official exhibitors page.

### Quality of the attendee base

- Nearly 105,000 attendees in 2026, from 207 countries and territories
- Strong institutional presence: the GSMA Ministerial Programme brought together 188 government delegations, 54 ministers and 118 heads of regulatory authorities in 2026 (source: gsma.com)
- 58% of attendees from adjacent industries (automotive, finance, healthcare, media), a sign of the trade show''s cross-sector reach

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

More than **1,700 speakers and thought leaders** took the floor at the 2026 edition, around the theme "Infinite AI". The programme covers the major challenges of connectivity: next-generation networks, artificial intelligence, FinTech, digital inclusion and public policy. The MWC27 theme, "The IQ Era", has been announced by the GSMA. The detailed programme will be published as the trade show approaches.

### Awards and recognition

The **Global Mobile (GLOMO) Awards** are presented on site each year. The 2026 GLOMO Awards were handed out at MWC26, with more than 30 prizes spread across six categories and judged by a panel of more than 200 independent experts. The new 2026 categories reflect the priority given to AI and inclusion: Best AI-Powered Network Solution, AI-Enabled Customer Experience, FinTech & Digital Commerce Innovation, Marketing for Good, Best Device <$150 and Digital Inclusion & Usage-Gap Impact (source: gsma.com). 2027 categories and winners to be confirmed as the trade show approaches.

### Community and networks

The trade show is run by the GSMA, which represents more than 750 mobile operators worldwide and also produces the MWC editions in Las Vegas, Shanghai, Kigali and Doha. The startup competition and entrepreneurial ecosystem are run by the co-located trade show 4YFN, which generated more than 700 curated business meetings in 2026, of which more than 60% were between startups and investors (source: 4yfn.com).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Fira Barcelona Gran Via](/lieux/fira-barcelona-gran-via) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Venue:** Fira Gran Via, Av. Joan Carles I, 64, 08908 L''Hospitalet de Llobregat, Barcelona.
- **Visitor badge:** prior online registration on the official website, reserved for professionals. Several categories of paid passes depending on the access level.
- **Co-location:** access to 4YFN is via the North entrance of the Fira Gran Via.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: making contact with the GSMA, choosing positioning and hall.
- 9 months out: applying for the Global Mobile (GLOMO) Awards if relevant (submission before the closing date).
- 6 months out: preparing the stand, product demos and the business meeting plan.
- 3 months out: activating press relations, a large contingent of journalists and analysts (2,600+ accredited in 2026).
- 6 weeks out: confirming meetings with operators and decision-makers, sales briefing.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Online registration on mwcbarcelona.com with proof of professional activity.
- Allow 2 to 4 days depending on the scope covered (networks, devices, AI, startups via 4YFN).
- Target the conferences and keynotes ahead of time: programme published several weeks before the trade show.
- For startup sourcing and investment, build 4YFN into the itinerary.

## How the trade show has evolved

