### Trajectory analysis

Natexpo is part of a long history: a first dietetics trade show appeared in **1957**, renamed **Dietexpo** in the late 1980s at Porte de Versailles. The show took its current name, **Natexpo**, and adopted its 5-sector structure in **2003**. It was for a long time a biennial Paris event, before being made **annual** with the introduction of Lyon in even years to better capture Southern Europe.

The current rhythm is now settled: **Lyon in even years** (compact 2-day format, 350-400 exhibitors), **Paris in odd years** (3-day format, 600-650 exhibitors). The 2024 Lyon edition was a successful test of the condensed format; the 2025 Paris edition confirmed the return to Porte de Versailles with an attendance level comparable to 2022 (10,843 visitors vs ~10,000) despite a context of an organic sector under pressure.

The historical organiser remains **SPAS Organisation**, an independent company founded in 1979, owned since 2010 by Patricia Berthomier-Massip. No acquisition by a major events operator (Comexposium, GL Events, RX) has been documented to date, unlike other French sector trade shows. The co-organiser **La Maison de la Bio** (renamed in 2024, formerly Fédération Natexbio) anchors the event''s institutional legitimacy within the supply chain.

The 2026 editorial positioning remains faithful to the official strapline, verbatim, *"Natexpo, l''éclaireur des Bio-tendances"*: a strictly professional trade show, rooted in the supply chain, positioned as the reference gathering for organic buyers and decision-makers in France and Southern Europe.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='natexpo-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Construction trade show for the north of France. Materials, equipment, fit-out and renovation for building and construction professionals.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Nordbat is the benchmark construction trade show for the Hauts-de-France region: 18,140 visitors in 2026, +7% vs 2024 (sources: nordbat.com, lebatimentperformant.fr) → the commercial target for exhibiting is regional (Hauts-de-France, Nord-Pas-de-Calais, Picardie, the Belgian cross-border area), not national.
- 400+ exhibitors across 20,000 m² in 2026 (sources: nordbat.com, lechodelabaie.fr) → a compact format compared with Batimat, but a higher visitor/exhibitor density (around 45 visitors per exhibitor): a stand receives more footfall.
- Reserved exclusively for professionals, free entry on pre-registration (source: nordbat.com) → no general-public dilution, and qualified traffic.
- 80 talks and associated events in 2026 over 3 days → strong editorial density for a trade show of this size, centred on renovation, summer comfort and new regulations.
- Hauts-de-France region: 130,000 construction-sector employees, 37,000 businesses (source: lechodelabaie.fr) → a significant addressable regional market.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Building-industry manufacturers, producers and distributors, and service providers to regional building and construction trades. Lille''s proximity to Belgium and the Benelux explains a share of cross-border exhibitors.

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is available on the official website: [nordbat.com](https://www.nordbat.com/fr/preparez-votre-visite/liste-des-exposants-2026/).

### Visitor quality

- Exclusively professional visitors (mandatory pre-registration with supporting documentation) (source: nordbat.com)
- Main target: building trades, regional construction business owners, specifiers, project managers, distributors
- 18,140 visitors in 2026, growing steadily since 2024 (16,953) (sources: nordbat.com, lechodelabaie.fr)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

2026 edition: 80 talks and associated events structured around 3 themes: "Renovation in service of regional appeal", "Summer comfort: building design and equipment choices", "Building differently: reuse versus regulation" (sources: nordbat.com, Le Moniteur).

### Satellite events

2026 edition: sourcing sessions with social housing providers, a first for the trade show (meetings scheduled across 2 slots) (source: nordbat.com).

### Community & networks

A trade show rooted in the regional professional fabric of Hauts-de-France. Partnerships with regional building and construction federations and the trade press (Le Moniteur, Batiweb, Le Bâtiment Performant).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Lille Grand Palais](/lieux/lille-grand-palais) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours (2026 edition, to be confirmed for 2028):** Wednesday 10am-7pm, Thursday 10am-9pm (late opening), Friday 10am-6pm (source: nordbat.com).
- **Visitor badge:** free on invitation, mandatory pre-registration at nordbat.com. Proof of professional activity required at the entrance.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: quotes on request from Expo Conseil (organiser, contact via nordbat.com). As Nordbat is a more compact regional trade show than the national ones (20,000 m² vs 100,000 m² for Batimat), the per-m² ranges are likely to be more accessible.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: request a quote from Expo Conseil, book your space.
- 6 months out: order your stand from a stand builder.
- 3 months out: final stand plan, team brief, activity programme.
- 6 weeks out: accreditations, accommodation, equipment logistics.
- 1 week out: final brief, equipment check, stand delivery.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Mandatory pre-registration at nordbat.com with proof of professional activity.
- Identify priority conferences among the roughly 80 on offer; the programme is published several weeks in advance.
- Allow 1 day: the compact 20,000 m² format can be covered in a single well-planned day.
- Lille city centre is a 10-minute walk away: it is possible to combine a trade-show visit with business meetings on the same day.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Nordbat''s CSR dimension is expressed mainly through its programming: the "reuse versus regulation" and "energy renovation of regions" themes are at the heart of the 80 talks and associated events of the 2026 edition, alongside sourcing sessions dedicated to social housing providers (source: nordbat.com).

## How the trade show has evolved

