### Trajectory analysis

Steady growth in visitor traffic over the last two editions (16,953 in 2024 → 18,140 in 2026, +7%), with a stable exhibitor count of around 400 (sources: nordbat.com, Le Moniteur). The trade show has found its regional equilibrium size and is capitalising on its rising editorial quality (80 talks and associated events in 2026, the first social-housing-provider sourcing sessions). One to watch for 2028: whether this momentum holds in a strained building and construction climate, and the impact of the calendar shift (February 2026 → March 2028).', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='nordbat-lille';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Cybersecurity and ethical hacking convention in the south of France. Technical talks, CTF and hands-on workshops.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The URL `numeriquest-toulouse-2026` actually covers the **Toulouse Hacking Convention (THCon)**, a French cybersecurity convention founded in 2017. No trade show named "Numeriquest" exists in Toulouse: this is the name of a company exhibiting at a different, unrelated trade show (source: editorial research).
- 10th edition: **5 and 6 May 2026** (talks) + 7 May 2026 (CTF) at the **Auditorium Marthe Condat, Université Paul Sabatier**, Toulouse (source: thcon.party/program).
- A **convention/conference + CTF** format: this is not a trade show with exhibitor stands, but an academic and professional cyber event. There is no classic exhibitor-visitor journey.
- The organiser **reports up to 1,800 international participants** (2022 figure) with a mixed audience of amateurs, professionals and researchers. The CTF brings together more than 600 competitors from 12 countries (sources: thcon.fr, thcon.party).
- Cyber recruiting sponsors: Orange Cyberdefense, ITrust, Sopra Steria, Synacktiv, Epsilon, ESGI (source: thcon.party/sponsors).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

THCon does not have exhibitor stands as such. Instead, the format is built around:

- **Institutional and industrial sponsors** (Gold, Silver, Bronze) who recruit or source cyber talent.
- **Partner schools** (ENSEEIHT, ENAC, INSA Toulouse, Université Paul Sabatier).
- **Research laboratories** (LAAS-CNRS, ANSSI) and academic speakers.

### Notable sponsors (2026 edition)

**Gold** sponsors: Orange Cyberdefense, ITrust, Epsilon, ESGI, Sopra Steria.
**Silver** sponsors: Root-Me PRO, Lyra, Holberton Actual Digital School, Viveris, MISC, Never Hack.
**Bronze** sponsors: Eurecia, Synacktiv, IMS Networks, G Echo (source: thcon.party/sponsors).

### Quality of the audience

- A mixed audience of amateurs, cybersecurity professionals, academic researchers and students
- A strong international component: a CTF with competitors from 12 countries, 4 continents in 2022
- Up to 1,800 participants announced (2022 figure, organiser declaration)
- No published OJS report (R2)

## Programme & community

### Conference programme (2026 edition)

**Pre-event** on Monday 4 May 2026 (2 pm-5.45 pm): "Security for and by hardware", at the Jacques Herbrand auditorium, IRIT, Université de Toulouse.

**Talks** on Tuesday 5 and Wednesday 6 May 2026, in a keynote + short (20 min) and long (30 min) presentation format. Themes covered: reverse engineering, vuln research, malware analysis, crypto attacks, offensive AI, 5G security, infostealers, space security (sources: thcon.party/program).

Announced keynotes: **Aurelien Francillon** (Eurecom) on smartphone backdoors; **Michael Schwarz** (CISPA) on CPU architecture exploits.

### Capture The Flag (CTF)

Thursday 7 May 2026 (1 pm-9 pm) at **ENSEEIHT**, extended online over 24 h. Separate on-site and online leaderboards. The online CTF is free, the on-site CTF is paid with a limited number of places (source: thcon.party).

### Call for Papers

CFP opened in November 2025, deadline 12-19 January 2026, notifications 13-20 February 2026. Three categories: regular papers, industry papers, student papers. Language: English (source: thcon.party/cfp).

### Community and networks

THCon is run by a **volunteer team** of cyber professionals, students and researchers from across France. The Toulouse academic ecosystem (Paul Sabatier, ENSEEIHT, ENAC, INSA, LAAS-CNRS) forms the academic foundation of the event (source: thcon.fr).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Université Paul Sabatier](/lieux/universite-paul-sabatier-toulouse).

Specific to the convention:

- **Talks location:** Auditorium Marthe Condat, reachable via line B of the Toulouse metro, Université Paul Sabatier station.
- **CTF location:** ENSEEIHT (Toulouse city centre) on 7 May.
- **Times:** Tuesday 5 and Wednesday 6 May, full days; Thursday 7 May 1 pm-9 pm for the CTF.
- **Registration:** online ticketing on thcon.party (see prices).

## How much it costs to exhibit

The THCon format does not offer a classic exhibitor stand: visibility comes through **sponsoring** (Gold, Silver, Bronze). Sponsor quote requests via thcon.party. Figures not publicly available.

Published visitor prices (2026 edition):

- **Conference (2 days, meals and evening included):** €95 without t-shirt, €100 with t-shirt
- **Student rate:** €30 without t-shirt, €35 with t-shirt (ID verification required)
- **Online CTF:** free
- **On-site CTF:** paid, limited number of places

(Source: thcon.party/tickets)

## Preparing your visit

### For the sponsor

- 9 months out: get in touch with the THCon team to apply to the Call for Sponsors.
- 6 months out: choose the tier (Gold, Silver, Bronze) based on recruitment objectives and budget.
- 3 months out: prepare a short pitch (an academic, not commercial, presence), prepare recruitment material.
- 6 weeks out: brief the team on the target profiles (researchers, cyber engineering students, reverse/offensive professionals).

### For the cyber visitor

- Register online on thcon.party, payment required (€95 pro, €30 student).
- Allow 2 to 3 days depending on the scope (CTF included or not).
- Prepare an application for the on-site CTF if the goal is the competition.
- Identify the relevant talks in advance from the ~25 talks over 2 days (programme published ahead of time).
- A strong networking component in the evenings: the social gathering is a highlight.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Information not available: as at the date of this listing, THCon does not publish a dedicated CSR commitments page or any identifiable eco-responsible charter on its official sites.

## How the trade show has evolved

