## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out (November 2025): preparing the application file, choosing the sector (Main, Editions, Emergence, Voices, Digital), putting together the artistic programme
- 9 months out (February 2026): submitting the application to RX France, selection by the committee of international gallerists
- 6 months out (May 2026): confirmation of the selection, negotiation of area and location, signing of the exhibitor contract
- 4 months out (July 2026): finalising the artistic programme, scenography brief, transport logistics and artwork insurance
- 2 months out (September 2026): collector and press invitations, team accreditations, communications plan
- 1 month out (October 2026): final adjustments, artwork loans, validation of labels and hanging

### For the decision-making visitor

- Buy your ticket online on parisphoto.com (B2C ticketing exclusively online)
- Photographers and art professionals: request the **Pro Pass** for unlimited access from 13 to 16 November and access to the VIP previews
- VIP preview on Wednesday 12 November from 2pm: by invitation only, with priority for collectors and curators
- Favour Thursday 13 or Friday 14 November for gallery meetings, and the weekend for the off programme and signings
- Allow 1.5 to 2 days to cover the five sectors and the talks in the conference programme
- Carte Blanche Étudiants: 2026 deadline on 8 June, Saif grant of 3,000 euros for the winner

## How the trade fair has evolved

