### Trajectory analysis

In 2025 Paris Photo confirmed its status as the largest international fair dedicated to photography, with a new attendance record of 87,275 visitors and a solid editorial foundation (170 galleries from 25 countries, 1,385 artists). The return to the renovated Grand Palais in 2024, after the editions held at the Grand Palais Éphémère during the 2021-2023 renovation works, marked a turning point: the fair recovered its historic setting and its full volumes. **The 2026 edition plays three cards at once**: the Bicentenary of Photography 2026-2027 celebrated in France, which places the 29th edition at the heart of a national cultural moment; the objective of reaching 220+ exhibitors and 75,000 visitors with 30% new exhibitors to confirm the renewal dynamic; and the consolidation of structural commitments (Elles x Paris Photo having risen from 20% to 39% female artists since 2018, the Net Zero Carbon Events Pledge and the Climate Pledge backed by the RX / RELX group). Under the direction of Anna Planas and Florence Bourgeois, Paris Photo confirms a trajectory of measured growth, anchored in curatorial quality and the diversification of collector audiences.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='paris-photo';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The trade show for connected commerce. E-commerce, retail, omnichannel, payment and customer experience.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **NRF 2026: Retail''s Big Show Europe** (formerly Paris Retail Week, rebranded in 2025) holds its 2nd edition under the new brand from **Tuesday 15 to Thursday 17 September 2026** at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), halls 4 & 6 (2025 layout repeated).
- Event **co-organised by Comexposium and the NRF (National Retail Federation)**: a strategic partnership announced in 2024 to create the European spin-off of the New York Retail''s Big Show. Comexposium remains the on-site operator.
- 2025 review (1st NRF edition): **12,500 visitors**, **500 exhibitors**, **200 speakers**, **100 international startups**, **58 countries represented**, **25,000 sq m of exhibition space**. The first European edition was broadly praised by the retail trade press.
- 2026 targets stated by the organisers: **12,500+ professionals, 525 exhibitors, 4,200 brands represented, 200+ speakers, 60+ countries, 100+ exclusive sessions**. Edition theme: **"The Next Now"** (transformations in European and global retail).
- 2015 launch: Paris Retail Week was born from the merger of **E-commerce Paris** and **Equipmag** (two Comexposium trade shows). The NRF rebranding in 2025 marked the 10th edition. Equipmag has remained integrated since 2024 within the overall retail / e-commerce / point-of-sale scope.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

An omnichannel retail trade show covering five major exhibitor areas: **IT for commerce & logistics**, **e-logistics and supply chain**, **payment solutions**, **retail tech and digital in-store**, **marketing, data, customer relations**. The exhibitor profile is dominated by SaaS vendors, integrators, digital agencies, payment solution providers, last-mile logistics operators, store equipment suppliers and retail tech startups.

### Notable exhibitors

The 2025 edition brought together 500 exhibitors including 100 international startups. No 2026 list has been published at this stage: refer to the [official exhibitor list](https://www.nrfbigshoweurope.com/) as the event approaches. The 2025 international pavilions included delegations from the Netherlands, the United Kingdom, Turkey, Poland, the Czech Republic and Israel (via Promosalons).

### Visitor quality

The 2025 edition welcomed 12,500 retail decision-makers from 58 countries. Target profile: retailers (CEOs, e-commerce directors, store operations directors, IT/digital directors, logistics directors, marketing data), large European and international distributors, pure-play e-tailers, DTC brands, shopping centre property companies. Qualified retailers benefit from a specific **Free Expo Pass** (named registration).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

More than **100 exclusive sessions** announced for 2026 (target of 200 speakers): keynotes, breakout sessions, expert talks. The programme is structured around eight themes: **seamless unified retail, store design innovation and technology, logistics and supply chain, CSR and ESG, marketplace growth, payments innovation, CRM systems, intelligent use of digital data**. The 2026 editorial theme is "The Next Now".

### Awards & accolades

The **Retail''s Big Show Europe Awards** are presented on 16 September (day 2) and reward the most innovative solutions. For the 2026 edition, the organiser''s website announces **9 categories** (vs 8 in 2025). 2025 winners (8 categories, official labels verbatim):

- **Seamless Unified Retail Store**: New Black
- **Store Design, Innovation, and Technology**: Vusion Group
- **Logistics and Supply Chain**: IF Returns
- **Expansion of Marketplaces**: Mirakl
- **Payment Innovations**: Lyzi
- **CRM Systems**: Loyaltee
- **Intelligent Use of Data**: Live Crew
- **Startup/Innovation**: Claim.me

### Satellite events

Three flagship experience zones within the trade show: **Innovators Showcase**, **Startup Hub**, **House of Innovation Pavilion**. The event remains a convergence point for the Parisian pop-up stores activated by exhibiting brands during the week, with no official co-organised pop-up programme at this stage.

### Community & networks

A structuring strategic partnership: **NRF (National Retail Federation, the world''s largest retail association, based in Washington) + Comexposium (the historic organiser of Paris Retail Week)**. The event is part of the **NRF Global Network** alongside the Retail''s Big Show New York (January) and the Retail''s Big Show Asia Pacific (Singapore). International exhibitor recruitment via Promosalons.

Retail trade press: LSA, e-marketing, Republik Retail, FashionUnited, Mind Retail, A1 Retail, Retail Times.

### What''s new in 2026

- 2nd edition under the NRF brand, following a 2025 first edition judged a success by the trade press
- Target of **9 award categories** (vs 8 in 2025)
- **"The Next Now"** theme centred on AI transformations, consumer expectations and sustainability imperatives
- Confirmed presence in Paris despite competition from European retail events (Shoptalk Europe, EuroShop)

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), halls 4 & 6 (2025 layout repeated, to be checked against the official practical information as the event approaches).
- **Dates and opening hours**: Tuesday 15 to Thursday 17 September 2026, three fully professional days (no general public opening).
- **Visitor passes**: **Free Expo Pass** reserved for qualified retailers (named validation by the NRF depending on company type and job role). **Non-Retailer All-Access Pass at €1,950 excl. VAT**: access to keynotes, breakouts, Exhibitor Big Ideas, expo, Startup Hub, Innovators Showcase. Prices and conditions to be confirmed on the [official registration page](https://www.nrfbigshoweurope.com/en/attend/pass-types/eligibility-registration).
- **Transport, parking and accommodation logistics**: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles page](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles). Mid-September in Paris is a less stretched week than June (Roland-Garros, VivaTech, Tour de France), but still allow 3 to 4 months'' lead time for accommodation in the 15th arrondissement.

## How much it costs to exhibit

