## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with the Comexposium / NRF sales team, choose your scope (Startup Hub, Innovators Showcase, international pavilion, standard stand)
- 6 months out: apply for the Retail''s Big Show Europe Awards (9 categories in 2026), validate package and location
- 4 months out: stand brief, targeting of visiting retailers, matchmaking activation on the official platform
- 2 months out: team accreditation, accommodation booking in the 15th arrondissement, product demo brief
- 3 weeks out: scheduling of B2B meetings, sales demo brief, finalisation of collateral and signage

### For the decision-maker visitor

- **Retailers**: check your eligibility for the Free Expo Pass as soon as registration opens (named NRF validation required, do not wait until the final weeks).
- **Non-retailers** (vendors, agencies, consultancies): All-Access Pass at €1,950 excl. VAT, to be weighed up depending on the value of the keynotes / breakouts compared with the expo alone.
- Identify your 10 to 15 priority exhibitors among the 500+ present in advance. Map your route by theme (payment, logistics, data, store tech).
- Allow **2 days minimum** to cover the expo + keynotes + Startup Hub. Three days for those targeting the ESG / data breakouts.
- Cross-reference with the European retail calendar: Shoptalk Europe (June, Barcelona) and EuroShop (triennial, Düsseldorf) are the two other structuring fixtures of the ecosystem.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The 2026 edition lists **"CSR and ESG"** as one of the **eight major thematic strands** of the conference programme, reflecting a sustainability positioning claimed by the organisers. The 2025 trade press noted that the sustainability issue was central to the show''s keynotes (retail climate tech, circular economy, low-carbon supply chain).

No structured, publicly available CSR programme specific to the trade show (such as a Net Zero Carbon Events charter or a published carbon footprint) has been identified to date on the official website. The dedicated CSR award category that existed in 2024 under Paris Retail Week (2024 winner: Save Your Wardrobe) does not appear as such in the 2025 NRF honours list, the ESG topic now being addressed transversally across the programme.

## The trade show''s evolution

