### Trajectory analysis

A trajectory in deep transformation: 10 editions under the Paris Retail Week brand (2015-2024) peaking at around 40,000 visitors in the best years, then a shift in 2025 to a more tightly focused, more international event under the NRF Retail''s Big Show Europe brand. The 12,500-visitor figure for 2025 is below the historic Paris Retail Week peak, but the event embraces a repositioning towards a target of **international retail decision-makers** (58 countries) rather than a broader B2B general audience. The 2026 edition retains the format and the target. The Comexposium / NRF partnership is part of an NRF Global Network strategy (New York January, Singapore autumn for Asia, Paris September for Europe) that now structures the global retail calendar.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='paris-retail-week';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for landscaping and outdoor design. Green spaces, urban greening, sustainable landscape management and maintenance equipment.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Paysalia 2027** takes place at [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon) from **Tuesday 30 November to Thursday 2 December 2027**: the 10th edition of France''s leading landscaping trade show, on a biennial odd-year cycle since its creation in 2009.
- **Institutional organiser**: [Unep, Les Entreprises du Paysage](https://www.lesentreprisesdupaysage.fr) (Union Nationale des Entreprises du Paysage). **Event operator**: [GL Events](https://www.gl-events.com), via the GreenTech+ platform. The trade show is explicitly "co-produced" by the two entities.
- The 2025 edition (2-4 December 2025) drew **41,500 professional visitors** (+9% vs 2023), **1,019 exhibitors** showcasing nearly **1,900 brands** (25% international) and **60 visitor nationalities**: a record turnout and the largest edition since 2009.
- Co-located with **Rocalia** (the natural stone trade show, same halls, same dates): a single combined Paysalia + Rocalia visitor pass, already in place across the 2023 and 2025 editions.
- Flagship competitions expected in 2027: the **Carré des Jardiniers** (the "Maître Jardinier" title, in partnership with VALHOR), the **Paysalia Innovation Awards** (5 prizes plus a special prize for French plant production plus the Startup Village Favourite), as well as the Concours National de Reconnaissance des Végétaux (Unep) and the Employment & Training Village.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A leading B2B trade show for landscaping, gardens and sports facilities in France. The full sector is covered: landscaping contractors, nurseries and horticulturists, equipment and powered-tool manufacturers, irrigation and water management, landscaping machinery, urban furniture, outdoor lighting, soil treatment, sports equipment and sports surfaces. The 2025 edition counted 1,019 direct exhibitors representing nearly 1,900 brands on site, of which 25% were international exhibitors.

### Notable exhibitors

The full exhibitor list is published on the [official Paysalia page](https://www.paysalia.com/fr/liste-exposants) as the trade show approaches. The 2025 edition brought together the big names in landscaping machinery, seed producers, nurseries and irrigation manufacturers, as well as the start-ups of the Startup Village (2025 winner: Filae with Rupa, an urban greening support made from recycled fishing nets).

### Visitor quality

Core profile: landscaping contractors (Unep''s historic target audience), specialist distributors, landscape architects, local authorities (green spaces, highways and sports departments), engineering consultancies, and public and private buyers. 60 visitor nationalities in 2025 (Switzerland, Italy, Belgium, Spain, Portugal, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Germany, Turkey and Morocco leading the way).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**92 conferences** scheduled in 2025 across the whole trade show, including **13 conferences dedicated to the Employment & Training Village**. Recurring 2025 themes carrying over to 2027: adapting to climate change, water management and responsible irrigation, urban greening, biodiversity, sustainable gardens, and the ecological transition of landscaping businesses. The Agora (Hall 6) and the Forum (Hall 7) host the main sessions.

### Awards & accolades

- **Carré des Jardiniers**: the show''s flagship competition, with [VALHOR](https://www.valhor.fr) as official partner. The winner receives the **"Maître Jardinier"** title. 2025 winner: **Ludovic Orain** with "L''écrin méditerranéen", crowned "Maître Jardinier 2025" under the jury presidency of Jean Mus.
- **Paysalia Innovation Awards**: 5 prizes in 2025 (rewarding products, services, equipment, plants and processes with tangible benefits and environmental commitment). 2025 winners: Koppert France, CAPILLUM, Moasure, Minier Professional Solutions / Hortival Diffusion & Verdia (Éditeur Végétal), AKOA SYSTEM. **Special prize for French plant production**: Synfolia (Synfoplant). **Startup Village Favourite**: Filae (Rupa).
- **Concours National de Reconnaissance des Végétaux**: launched in 2011 by Unep, co-organised with VALHOR and the Ministère de l''Agriculture, with the final historically held at Paysalia.

### Satellite events

**Rocalia**, the natural stone trade show, co-located at Eurexpo on the same dates since 2017 (also organised by GL Events / GreenTech+): a single badge gives access to both trade shows. The **Journée Ville Verte** is a format dedicated to local authorities. The **Employment & Training Village** brings together training centres, landscaping schools and recruiting businesses.

### Community & networks

Unep (Les Entreprises du Paysage) is the representative trade body for landscaping businesses in France and the institutional co-producer of the trade show since its creation. The show is part of GL Events'' **GreenTech+** portfolio (alongside Rocalia, BePositive and Eurobois).

Specialist press in attendance: Le Lien Horticole, Matériel Paysage, Maison et Jardins Actuels, Architecture Bois, Secteur Vert, Enjeux Piscine, Light ZOOM Lumière, Archi.

### What''s new for 2027

The 10th edition of the show (Paysalia was created in 2009, on a biennial odd-year cycle). The detailed programme is published progressively on the [official Paysalia website](https://www.paysalia.com) as the trade show approaches.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon), Chassieu (eastern Lyon). In 2025, Paysalia + Rocalia occupied **Halls 4 to 7** at Eurexpo, with the Agora in Hall 6 and the Forum in Hall 7. The 2027 layout is to be confirmed as the trade show approaches.
- **Dates**: Tuesday 30 November, Wednesday 1 December, Thursday 2 December 2027 (3 days).
- **Badges**: a strictly professional trade show. Single Paysalia + Rocalia badge. Registration in advance on the official website.
- **Access and general logistics**: see the [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon) page (T3 and T5 tram lines, shuttles, car parks, accommodation in eastern Lyon and the city centre).

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: initial commercial contact with GL Events / GreenTech+, checking eligibility for the themed villages (Biodiversity & Environment, Startup, Employment & Training)
- 9 months out: applications for the Paysalia Innovation Awards and the Carré des Jardiniers (finalist selection file, tight calendar constraints)
- 6 months out: stand booking, hall selection (4 to 7), briefing the team on the expected CSR themes (water management, biodiversity, circular economy)
- 3 months out: team accreditations, accommodation in eastern Lyon (Chassieu, Bron, Saint-Priest) or the city centre depending on budget
- 6 weeks out: activating visitor matchmaking tools, briefing the sales team on demos, preparing conferences if speaking

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free Paysalia badge for professionals in landscaping, gardens and sports (advance registration required)
- Allow at least 2 days to cover Paysalia + Rocalia without cutting the conferences short
- Identify your 10 to 15 priority exhibitors in advance via the official list (1,900 brands, a dense line-up)
- Schedule the Carré des Jardiniers finals and the Paysalia Innovation Awards ceremony (usually mid-show)
- Eastern Lyon in December: allow a 30 to 45 minute margin from the centre of Lyon (T3 + T5 or car), and book accommodation 3 to 4 months in advance given the Rocalia co-location

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Paysalia explicitly positions itself as an "eco-responsible trade show" and structures its ESG commitments around three stated pillars: reducing its carbon footprint, limiting consumables, and developing diversity.

Actions documented by the organiser for the 2025 edition:
- Printed communications on recycled paper, digital badges, roll-up recovery by Ecopack Solutions
- Fit-out using recyclable materials (wood, cardboard), furniture hire, recyclable carpeting
- Sorted waste collection in the halls, a partnership with **Valdelia** for material recovery, a partnership with **Le Chaînon Manquant** against food waste
- Contracted green electricity, progressive LED lighting, presence detectors in washrooms
- 24 electric vehicle charging points on site, encouragement of car-sharing and tram access
- Installation of 3 beehives on site
- Support for the **Plantons pour l''Avenir** fund (replanting: 2.35 million trees and 2,120 hectares contributed according to the organiser).

The CSR theme also runs through the show''s editorial content: the Biodiversity & Environment Village, the central CSR criterion of the Paysalia Innovation Awards, and a conference programme geared towards water management, urban greening and climate adaptation.

## How the trade show has evolved

