### Trajectory analysis

Paysalia was created in 2009 by GL Events and Unep with a clear positioning: to become the leading landscaping trade show in France, on a biennial odd-year cycle at Eurexpo Lyon. The trajectory has been one of continuous growth, with a clear jump in 2025: +9% in visitors compared with 2023 and more than 41,500 professionals welcomed, making it the largest edition since its inception. Co-location with Rocalia (the natural stone trade show) since 2017 has strengthened its appeal, broadening the visitor audience to include hard-landscaping specifiers. Its integration into GL Events'' GreenTech+ portfolio (with BePositive, Eurobois and Rocalia) anchors Paysalia in the sustainable outdoor-design segment. The 2027 edition is anticipated as the 10th-edition anniversary: at 18 months out, the organisers have yet to communicate any specific format or quantified targets, beyond confirmation of the 30 November - 2 December 2027 dates and the Eurexpo venue.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='paysalia-lyon';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='40th anniversary edition of the only generalist community pharmacy trade show in France, at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles Hall 7.2. 2026 figures: 9,000 to 13,000 professionals, 350 to 400 exhibitors, 100 conferences and 75+ hours of training.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Pharmagora Plus is the **only generalist community pharmacy trade show in France**. The other French pharma trade shows (CPHI, Pharmapack) target the upstream pharmaceutical industry, not the community pharmacy.
- **40th anniversary edition on 13 and 14 March 2027** at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), **Hall 7.2**. Opening hours: Saturday 9am-6.15pm, Sunday 9am-5pm.
- 2025 figures (38th ed., 8-9 March): **8,000+ visitors**, including **5,400 pharmacy owners** (+5% vs 2024), and **400+ exhibitors and sponsors**.
- 2026 edition (39th ed., 14-15 March): between **9,000 and 13,000 professionals** announced, around **350 to 400 exhibitors**.
- Organiser: **CloserStill Media** (British group), which acquired Pharmagora in April 2014 then rebranded it "Pharmagora Plus" in March 2015. Show director: **Adrien Collilieux**.
- Extensive programme: **100 conferences, 75+ hours of training**, dedicated streams for owners, employed pharmacists, dispensers and students. Some conferences are eligible for DPC (continuing professional development) via Atoopharm.
- **Free admission with prior registration**, strictly reserved for community pharmacy professionals.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Pharmagora Plus brings together the entire supplier chain of the French community pharmacy:

- **Generic and originator laboratories**: Biogaran, Mylan/Viatris, Teva, Sandoz.
- **Dermo-cosmetics and hygiene**: La Roche-Posay, Avène, Bioderma, Uriage.
- **Food supplements and nutrition**: Super Diet and other OTC brands.
- **Buying groups and banners**: PHR, Giphar, Pharmacie Lafayette, Pharmavie, Univers Pharmacie, Pharmabest.
- **Pharmacy software publishers (LGO)**: LGPI/Pharmagest, Smart Rx, Winpharma, OCP Pharmagora, Crystal.
- **Team management and back-office solutions**: Skello (scheduling, pharmacy HR) and equivalent players.
- **CSR and anti-waste solutions**: Pharmagreen and the emerging green pharmacy ecosystem.

### Quality of the visitor base

The trade show''s central argument rests on the decision-making density of its visitor base:

- 8,000+ visitors in 2025, including **5,400 pharmacy owners** (the community pharmacy purchasing decision-makers).
- A +5% increase in owners between 2024 and 2025.
- A diverse audience: owners, employed pharmacists, pharmacy dispensers, pharmacy students.
- A 100% French-speaking audience, with national reach and a strong presence from the Île-de-France region and major cities.

### Institutional support

Pharmagora Plus is backed by all the representative organisations of the community pharmacy, making it a sector trade show in the strict sense:

- **USPO** (Union des Syndicats de Pharmaciens d''Officine), chaired by Pierre-Olivier Variot.
- **FSPF** (Fédération des Syndicats Pharmaceutiques de France), chaired by Philippe Besset.
- **ANEPF** (Association Nationale des Étudiants en Pharmacie de France), with Noémie Chantrel-Richard representing students.
- **Atoopharm**: educational partner for the 11th consecutive year (since 2015-2016), DPC operator.
- **Le Moniteur des Pharmacies**: long-standing media partner.
- **Leem** (Les Entreprises du Médicament), represented by Frédéric Lavie.
- **Federgy** (Fédération des Groupements de Pharmaciens), chaired by Alain Grollaud.
- **Proximité e Santé**, with Cécile Morvan.

## Activities & community

### Trophées de la Pharmacie

The **Trophées de la Pharmacie** recognise, each year, the pharmacies and players that innovate in the field, across **6 categories**:

1. **Health & Prevention**
2. **Communication of new missions**
3. **Patient communication**
4. **Social and environmental responsibility (CSR)**
5. **Use of digital technology in healthcare**
6. **Student Prize**

The jury is **co-chaired by Cécile Morvan** (founder of the Trophées, Proximité e Santé) and **Alain Grollaud** (president of Federgy).

### 5 specialised programmes

The 2026 editorial content, set to be renewed in 2027, is organised around five thematic programmes:

- **Mental Health and Well-being**: patient advice, early identification, coordinated care pathway.
- **Women''s Health**: 4 structuring themes: female leadership in the profession, gender-based medicine, inequalities in access to care, and life-cycle care management.
- **Professional Set-up**: in partnership with **ANEPF**, a pathway for creating and taking over a pharmacy aimed at students and young owners.
- **Dermatology**: dermo-cosmetic advice, common skin conditions, chronic pathologies.
- **Digital and AI**: digitalisation of the pharmacy, AI integration, ethics and data security.

### Conference programme

100 conferences, more than 75 hours of training, with streams by profile:

- **Owners**: economic management, new missions, agreement negotiations.
- **Employed pharmacists**: expert advice, continuing training, career development.
- **Dispensers**: over-the-counter advice, products, demeanour.
- **Students**: setting up, choice of specialism, first professional experiences.

Some conferences are eligible for **DPC (continuing professional development) via Atoopharm**, the long-standing educational partner.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking, accommodation and catering: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates and times**: Saturday 13 March 2027 from 9am to 6.15pm, Sunday 14 March 2027 from 9am to 5pm.
- **Hall**: Hall 7.2 of the exhibition centre.
- **Access**: strictly reserved for community pharmacy professionals (owners, employed pharmacists, dispensers, students), with proof to be presented.
- **Registration**: free and compulsory online ahead of the event.
- **Weekend format**: 2 condensed days on Saturday-Sunday, designed to allow pharmacy teams to attend without closing during the week.

## How much it costs to exhibit

- **Professional visitors**: free admission with prior registration. No badge fee charged.
- **Exhibitors**: prices on personalised quote (floor space, location within Hall 7.2, technical constraints, sponsorship pack). Figures not published publicly; contacting the organiser directly is recommended.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with CloserStill Media, identify the relevant stream (laboratory, dermo, OTC, buying group, LGO, CSR).
- 9 months out: apply for the **Trophées de la Pharmacie** (6 categories) if your pharmacy innovation fits, a lever for visibility with the sector jury.
- 6 months out: align your messaging with the **5 specialised programmes** (mental health, women''s health, set-up, dermatology, digital/AI).
- 3 months out: brief your team on the visitor profiles (owners, employed pharmacists, dispensers, students) and prepare DPC materials where relevant.
- 6 weeks out: coordinate with the institutional supporters present (USPO, FSPF, ANEPF, Federgy) on the conference highlights.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online registration compulsory, professional proof to be provided.
- Weekend format: allows you to attend with part of the pharmacy team without closing the pharmacy.
- Prioritise the **5 specialised programmes** and the **DPC Atoopharm** conferences to make the most of the visit as continuing training.
- For newly established practitioners and students: focus on the **Professional Set-up** pathway co-run with ANEPF.
- Make use of Hall 7.2 to map out the LGO, dermo and buying-group offering side by side in a single day.

## CSR policy & initiatives

CSR is an emerging editorial theme of the trade show, gradually structured since 2024-2025:

- A **"green pharmacy and commitment" round table** scheduled in 2025, signalling the subject''s rising prominence.
- A **dedicated CSR Trophy category** among the 6 categories of the Trophées de la Pharmacie.
- A **Net Zero page** driven by the CloserStill Media / RELX group at corporate level, applied to the trade show.
- The presence of specialist players such as **Pharmagreen** (pharmagreen.fr), an anti-waste solution for medicines in the pharmacy.

The subject remains a work in progress compared with B2B trade shows that are more mature on CSR, but the combination of a dedicated Trophy, conference programming and specialist exhibitors establishes a defined theme for 2027.

## How the trade show has evolved

