/>

### Trajectory analysis

Première Vision was born in **1973 in Lyon**, at the initiative of around fifteen silk makers who sought to organise a shared commercial gathering ahead of the collections. More than fifty years later, the trade show has become the world''s benchmark for upstream fashion sourcing, now held at Paris Nord Villepinte and backed by a leading industrial operator. The ownership trajectory has been gradual: **GL Events** entered the capital in **2007** with a 24.5% stake, rose to 49% in **2010**, then acquired full control in **2023** for the trade show''s fiftieth anniversary. This move to 100% made it possible to align Première Vision with the international strategy of GL Events Exhibitions and to secure long-term investment momentum.

The appointment of **Florence Rousson** as Chair of the Executive Board in **February 2024**, succeeding Gilles Lasbordes, marked a new editorial chapter: a strengthened anchoring of the **biennial Craftsmanship & Know-How (February) / Innovation & Technology (September) cycle**, a deliberate return to a mid-September calendar in 2025, the announcement of the **opening towards the Beauty sector** and the consolidation of the **Smart Creation** scheme begun in 2015. The September 2026 vintage, the second "Innovation & Technology" instalment of the cycle, extends this line with a forward-looking emphasis on materials, processes and the broadening of the worlds covered.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='premiere-vision-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for occupational risk prevention and workplace safety. Equipment, training and solutions for occupational health.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Préventica is the benchmark event for occupational health and safety and quality of working life (QWL) in France, under the patronage of the Ministry of Labour and the Ministry of Health.
- Lyon 2026 edition (organiser forecast): **15,000 participants, 550 exhibitors, 180 conferences and workshops, 750 experts** (source: preventica.com/salon/lyon-2026).
- Twice-yearly format: two regional sessions a year. In 2026: Rennes (16-18 June) then Lyon Eurexpo (6-8 October).
- 180 conferences and workshops with free access at each session, so the bulk of the visitor value lies in the programme, not just the stands.
- Organised by Communica Organisation, free entry for visitors.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Prevention bodies, PPE manufacturers, and players in ergonomics, training, HR/QWL consulting, security and crisis management (source: preventica.com).

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [preventica.com](https://www.preventica.com/salon/lyon-2026/visiter).

### Quality of the visitor base

- Company directors, HR directors, prevention officers, QHSE managers, occupational health and medicine professionals, facilities management, procurement, security
- 15,000 participants expected for the Lyon 2026 edition (source: preventica.com)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

180 conferences and workshops with free access, led by experts. Themes: the future of work, mental health, prevention of musculoskeletal disorders, social dialogue, the health of care workers, the digitalisation of prevention, CSR and QWL, women''s health at work, One Health. Structuring partners: Présanse, Assurance Maladie, MSA, OPPBTP, MASE, CNRACL-FNP (source: preventica.com).

### Awards and recognition

Prix du Management Inspirant (formerly "Leader Bienveillant"), awarded since 2019: recognises managerial practices in health, safety and QWL (5 organisations honoured in Paris 2025). An Innovation Award is also presented.

### Community and networks

Patronage of the Ministry of Labour and the Ministry of Health. The trade show is anchored in prevention and QWL networks, with a specialist QHSE and occupational health press.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon).

Specific to the show:

- **Visitor badge:** free registration, conferences with free access.

## What it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: quote on request from Communica Organisation.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: request a quote from Communica Organisation, book your space.
- 6 months out: order your stand, apply for the conferences (the programme is a lever for visibility).
- 3 months out: stand plan, team briefing.
- 6 weeks out: accreditations, accommodation, logistics.
- 1 week out: final briefing, stand delivery.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free registration, conferences with free access: build your route around the programme (180 sessions).
- Allow 1 to 2 days depending on the themes you are targeting (occupational health, QWL, security).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

CSR is at the heart of Préventica: occupational health and safety and quality of working life are the very subject of the trade show, with "CSR and QWL" as an explicit conference theme (source: preventica.com). The Prix du Management Inspirant rewards responsible managerial practices. The social dimension of CSR (working conditions, mental health, social dialogue) is central to it.

## How the show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "participants", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "conferences", "label": "Conferences", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
 { "edition": "Lyon 2026 (national, upcoming)", "participants": "target 15,000", "exposants": "target 550", "conferences": "180" },
 { "edition": "Paris 2025 (national)", "participants": "14,000", "exposants": "550", "conferences": "180" }
 ]}
 sources="Préventica"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

Préventica maintains a stable format of around 14,000-15,000 participants per session, with a dense conference programme (180 sessions) that makes it as much a congress as a trade show. The 2026 session is held at Lyon Eurexpo (6-8 October), preceded by a session in Rennes (June). Variable to watch: the rise of mental health and QWL topics, which is broadening the visitor base beyond the historical QHSE core.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='preventica-lyon';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show on the prevention of occupational risks and workplace safety. Paris edition for businesses in the Île-de-France region.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Préventica is the benchmark congress and trade show for **occupational health, safety and quality of working life**. A travelling brand created in 1997 in Bordeaux by Éric Dejean-Servières, it is organised by **Communica Organisation** (Lormont, Gironde) and is held under the patronage of the Ministry of Labour, Health and Solidarity and the Ministry of Public Action, the Civil Service and Simplification (sources: preventica.com/qui-sommes-nous, echos-judiciaires.com).
- The brand organises **two congresses and trade shows per year in different cities**. The most recent Paris edition was held from **10 to 12 June 2025** at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles). No Paris edition is scheduled for 2026: the next French stops are Rennes (16 to 18 June 2026) and [Préventica Lyon](/salons/preventica-lyon) (6 to 8 October 2026). The next Paris edition has not yet been announced.
- The 2025 Paris edition was announced with **600 exhibitors, 180 conferences and workshops, 750 experts and 15,000 attendees expected** (source: preventica.com/salon/paris-2025).
- Paris entered the rotation in **2017** (first Paris edition, 20 to 22 June 2017) and then hosted the trade show in 2019, 2021, 2023 and 2025: a biennial rhythm in odd-numbered years, with the 2021 edition having been pushed back to late November by the health crisis but still kept in an odd-numbered year (sources: cramif.fr, gpomag.fr).
- **Préventica Innovation Award**: 20 winners recognised in Paris in 2025, across two categories.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Eight exhibition sectors structure the offering: workspace design, hygiene and cleaning, road safety and eco-mobility, site safety and first aid, HR management and quality of working life, consultancy and training, production and worksite safety, and personal protective equipment (source: preventica.com/salon/paris-2025/exposants).

### Notable exhibitors

The full list of 2025 exhibitors is available on the official website: [preventica.com/salon/paris-2025/exposants](https://www.preventica.com/salon/paris-2025/exposants). These included AFNOR, Abbott, the Agefiph and 360SkillVue, the 2025 winner of the Innovation Award for its solution detecting and preventing musculoskeletal disorders (MSDs) and psychosocial risks (PSRs) (sources: preventica.com, faceaurisque.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

- More than 15,000 decision-makers expected at the 2025 Paris edition (source: bati.zepros.fr)
- Professional visitor base: company directors, HR directors, HSE/QHSE managers, prevention officers, occupational health services, and public and private buyers
- Three mid-week days (Tuesday to Thursday), a congress-and-trade-show format that draws attendees as much for the conferences as for the exhibition

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**180 conferences and workshops** delivered by **750 experts** featured in the 2025 Paris edition programme, around some twenty major issues: mental health, prevention of MSDs and occupational wear and tear, social dialogue, the digitalisation of prevention, the impact of climate disruption on work, the transformation of occupational medicine, and the health of company directors (source: preventica.com/salon/paris-2025).

### Awards and recognition

**Préventica Innovation Award**: 20 winners recognised in Paris in 2025, split across two categories: "Support and services for prevention policies and the management of quality of working life" (7 winners, including Companioncare, GAE Conseil and Reverto) and "Equipment and technologies for comfort and safety at work" (13 winners). The awards are presented on the first day of the trade show (sources: preventica.com/salon/paris-2025/actualites, faceaurisque.com).

### Community and networks

Préventica runs a year-round online platform (magazine, webinars, supplier directory, podcasts) used by a community of 100,000 users each year (source: preventica.com/qui-sommes-nous).

The congress and trade show is held under the patronage of the Ministry of Labour, Health and Solidarity and the Ministry of Public Action, the Civil Service and Simplification.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the page for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** free with online registration, a personalised badge to be printed before your visit. The trade show is intended for professionals in prevention and occupational health.
- **Opening hours recorded at the 2025 Paris edition:** 9 a.m.-6 p.m. on Tuesday and Wednesday, 9 a.m.-5 p.m. on Thursday (source: preventica.com/salon/paris-2025/infos-pratiques).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published on the official website. Participation (stand, conference, partnership) goes through the official request form: [preventica.com/demande-participation.php](https://www.preventica.com/demande-participation.php).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- As soon as the cities and dates are announced: submit a participation request via the official form, as stands are reserved early for the Paris editions.
- Ahead of the trade show: apply for the Innovation Award, presented on the first day and relayed by the specialist prevention and safety press.
- Note: the brand organises two events per year in different cities; with no Paris edition announced, [Préventica Lyon](/salons/preventica-lyon) (6 to 8 October 2026) is the next major stop for reaching a national visitor base.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free online pre-registration on the official website to obtain your personalised badge.
- Target the conferences in advance: the programme (180 sessions at the most recent Paris edition) is published several weeks before opening.
- Plan your exhibition route around the eight sectors: PPE, worksite safety, and quality of working life and HR management are not in the same aisles.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

CSR and ecological transformation are among the trade show''s programming pillars: a "CSR Policy" information space, conferences dedicated to companies'' CSR approaches and to the impact of climate on working conditions (source: preventica.com). The organiser does not, to date, publish a page setting out the eco-responsible commitments specific to the production of the event itself.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Paris edition" },
 { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Attendees", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
 { "edition": "2025 (10-12 June)", "visiteurs": "15,000 expected", "exposants": "600 announced" },
 { "edition": "2023 (23-25 May)", "visiteurs": "15,000 expected", "exposants": "550 announced" },
 { "edition": "2021 (30 Nov-2 Dec)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "~380 announced" },
 { "edition": "2019 (21-23 May)", "visiteurs": "10,000 expected", "exposants": "400" }
 ]}
 sources="preventica.com, bati.zepros.fr, gpomag.fr, smartintegrationsmag.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

Created in 1997 in Bordeaux under the name "Qualité des lieux de travail" at the request of the Carsat, Préventica built its model on the road: two congresses and trade shows a year touring France''s major cities, complemented by an international edition in Casablanca. Paris entered the rotation in 2017 and has returned every odd-numbered year since: 2019, 2021 (an edition pushed back to late November by the health crisis), 2023 and 2025. The Paris edition has established itself as the brand''s densest format: from 400 exhibitors and 10,000 visitors expected in 2019 to 600 exhibitors and 15,000 attendees expected in 2025, following the scaled-back 2021 edition (around 380 exhibitors). With Rennes and Lyon on the 2026 calendar, the Paris return will happen in 2027 at the earliest, with no official announcement to date.', seo_title_en='Preventica Paris 2025: occupational health, safety and quality of working life congress', seo_description_en='Preventica Paris, the occupational health and safety congress and trade show at Porte de Versailles: 600 exhibitors, 180 conferences and 15,000 attendees expected in 2025. Next editions: Rennes and Lyon 2026.' WHERE slug='preventica-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The trade show for the players and solutions of sustainable development and CSR. ESG, climate, circular economy and impact.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Produrable is the benchmark trade show and conference for CSR and corporate sustainable development, in Paris. Official 2026 figures: **15,000 visitors, 350 partners and 800 speakers** (source: produrable.com).
- 19th edition in 2026 on the theme **"Cultivating balance"**, structured around 6 thematic tracks: agriculture/health/biodiversity, production/consumption/circularity, housing/mobility/energy/climate, finance/reporting/governance, technology/AI/R&D, social/knowledge/communication.
- Organised by Groupe AEF, under the high patronage of the Ministry for the Ecological Transition, Biodiversity, Forests, the Sea and Fisheries.
- Next edition: 30 September and 1 October 2026, Palais des Congrès de Paris.
- Concrete CSR trajectory: 2025 carbon footprint = **168.60 t CO₂** (vs 416 t in 2024, -60%), Palais des Congrès certified ISO 20121, FSC kraft cardboard badges, 85% French suppliers (source: produrable.com/un-evenement-ecoresponsable).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

CSR service providers and solutions, consultancy, impact measurement and responsible procurement, targeting the CSR departments, executive management and procurement functions of large companies and mid-sized firms.

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [produrable.com](https://www.produrable.com/).

### Quality of the visitor base

- Decision-maker visitor base, CSR/sustainable development departments, executive management and procurement functions - 50/50 gender parity among the 800 speakers
- Claimed community: 50,000 decision-makers across the CSR ecosystem

## Events & community

### Conference programme

250 conferences and workshops per edition (24 major conferences + partner workshops). 2025 themes: CSR backlash, review of the Paris Agreement and the Green Deal, adaptation.

### Awards & accolades

Grand Prix de la Marque Engagée (9th edition in 2026, 9 categories, 21 Gold/Silver/Bronze winners) and the Talents for the Planet Awards, presented during the trade show (source: produrable.com).

### Community & networks

The benchmark trade show for the French CSR community, under the high patronage of the Ministry for the Ecological Transition.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Palais des Congrès de Paris](/lieux/palais-des-congres-paris).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** personalised badge via the trade show''s online ticketing.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published: quote on request from Groupe AEF.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months before: request a quote from the organiser, book your space.
- 6 months before: stand layout, application for speaking slots (the programme is a lever for visibility).
- 3 months before: accreditations, accommodation.
- 6 weeks before: final brief, delivery of materials.

### For the decision-maker visitor

