- Allow 1 to 2 days depending on the targeted CSR themes.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Produrable details its commitments on its [An eco-responsible event](https://www.produrable.com/un-evenement-ecoresponsable) page: ISO 20121 certified venue, published carbon footprint (168.6 t CO₂ in 2025, declining), FSC kraft cardboard badges and predominantly French furniture.

## The trade show''s evolution

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
 { "edition": "19th: 2026 (upcoming)", "visiteurs": "", "exposants": "" },
 { "edition": "18th: 2025", "visiteurs": "14,000+", "exposants": "300" }
 ]}
 sources="organisateur"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

Produrable confirms its leadership over the French CSR community (15,000 visitors announced for 2026, 800 speakers at 50/50 parity). The content-rich conference format makes it as much a strategic content event as a commercial one. One to watch for 2026: the effect of the "CSR backlash" context on the engagement of large companies.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='produrable-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='IT and digital business convention. A B2B meeting point between IT decision-makers, CIOs and technology solution providers.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Ready For IT is the One-to-One business convention for IT and cybersecurity decision-makers, organised by **Comexposium**. The principle: individual meetings pre-arranged and qualified in advance between decision-makers leading projects and solution providers.
- Next edition: 7th edition, from 2 to 4 June 2026 at the [Grimaldi Forum](/lieux/grimaldi-forum) in Monaco.
- The 2025 edition (6th edition, Monaco) reported a satisfaction rate of 80% and a recommendation rate for the One-to-One meetings of 98% (source: numerique360.banquedesterritoires.fr).
- Strictly professional audience: CIOs, CISOs, CTOs and innovation directors on the decision-maker side, software vendors and integrators on the provider side.
- Business convention format: 30-minute One-to-One meetings via a dedicated platform, exhibitor village, conferences, keynotes and expert workshops.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

On the provider side: software vendors, integrators, cloud operators, cybersecurity and digital transformation specialists. On the invited decision-maker side: CIOs, CISOs, CTOs and innovation directors from companies and mid-sized firms leading IT projects.

The mutual pre-selection via the meetings platform sets Ready For IT apart from an open trade show: decision-makers and partners are matched on the basis of qualified needs and offerings.

### Notable exhibitors

List of partners on the official website: [ready-for-it.com](https://www.ready-for-it.com/).

### Quality of the visitor base

- Strictly qualified invited decision-makers: CIOs, CISOs, CTOs, innovation directors leading projects
- Recommendation rate for the One-to-One meetings of 98% reported for the 2025 edition (source: numerique360.banquedesterritoires.fr)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

Beyond the One-to-One meetings, the programme offers conferences, keynotes, round tables and expert workshops. The major themes set out for 2026 cover the industrialisation of generative and agentic AI, cybersecurity and cyber-resilience strategies, the European sovereign cloud, the governance of AI agents and trust in data.

### Community and networks

Coverage by the specialist IT press: LeMagIT, IT for Business, Silicon.fr.

Ready For IT sits within the ecosystem of IT and cybersecurity meetings held in Monaco and across France, alongside the [Assises de la Sécurité](/salons/les-assises-de-la-securite-monaco) and the [Forum InCyber](/salons/fic-lille).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Grimaldi Forum](/lieux/grimaldi-forum) in Monaco.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Access format:** decision-makers take part by invitation and prior registration, with One-to-One meetings scheduled via the dedicated platform ahead of the event.
- **Duration:** three days, with a schedule of 30-minute individual meetings complemented by the content programme.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- Get in touch with Comexposium for the partner package and positioning on the meetings platform.
- Provide a precise solution profile to optimise matching with decision-makers leading projects.
- Prepare the 30-minute One-to-One meetings: target needs, short and qualified demonstrations.

### For the visiting decision-maker

- Apply for invited decision-maker status and qualify the IT project or projects under way.
- Select the partners to meet in advance via the meetings platform.
- Identify the conferences and keynotes linked to the 2026 issues: agentic AI, cyber-resilience, sovereign cloud.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
   { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
