### Trajectory analysis

Ready For IT has established itself as a benchmark One-to-One meeting point for IT decision-makers, built on the business convention model rather than the open trade show. The satisfaction (80%) and meeting recommendation (98%) rates reported for the 2025 edition confirm the relevance of the qualified matchmaking format. The 7th edition, from 2 to 4 June 2026 at the Grimaldi Forum in Monaco, places the emphasis on the industrialisation of generative and agentic AI, cyber-resilience and the sovereign cloud. The 2026 review figures will be published as the event approaches.', seo_title_en='Ready For IT 2026 Monaco: One-to-One convention for IT leaders', seo_description_en='Ready For IT 2026, 7th edition from 2 to 4 June at the Grimaldi Forum in Monaco. The One-to-One convention for CIOs, CISOs and CTOs around AI, the sovereign cloud and cybersecurity. Organised by Comexposium.' WHERE slug='ready-for-it-monaco';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Annual trade show dedicated to the equipment, training and practices of physiotherapy and massage therapy, organised under the slogan "Rééduca, la rééducation en mouvement".
- Organiser: RX France (Reed Exhibitions Limited, RELX group).
- 2026 edition: Thursday 17 to Saturday 19 September 2026, at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), Halls 5.2 and 5.3. Free entry with a badge, reserved for rehabilitation professionals and accredited students (group requests via a tutor).
- Audience: the 2025 edition (9-11 October) drew around 5,500 visitors, 130 exhibitors and 233 brands. For 2026 the organiser is targeting 6,000 visitors, 110 exhibitors and 262 brands across 42 sectors.
- 2026 theme: "La performance du soin dans toutes ses dimensions", with a conference programme, six certifying courses eligible for DPC funding and several professional competitions.
- Highlights to watch: the Massage Masters by Rééduca competition, the Massage Academy Challenge, the Rééduca Innov'' awards and the Octobre Rose initiative at Rééduca.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile
Manufacturers and distributors of rehabilitation equipment, software publishers and practice management solutions, training bodies, sports-health and textile brands, and connected-health start-ups. The offering is structured around four families: products and technologies, equipment and materials, services, and specialised practices.

### Notable exhibitors
The official list of brands present is published on the [show''s exhibitor page](https://www.salonreeduca.com/fr-fr/Exposants/liste-des-exposants.html). The 2025 edition brought together 233 brands; the organiser is announcing 262 for 2026.

### Quality of the visitor base
The visitor base is made up of physiotherapists, osteopaths, directors and managers of healthcare establishments, doctors and surgeons, nurses, as well as sports-health professionals (coaches, instructors). According to the organiser''s visitor survey, 61% of attendees come looking for services, 60% for equipment and materials and 58% for products and technologies.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme
The programme is built around a Conference Area led by medical and paramedical experts, an Innovation Village with start-up pitches, and six certifying courses for the assessment of professional practices, eligible for DPC funding. The detailed 2026 programme is published by the organiser in the run-up to the event.

### Awards and prizes
- Massage Masters by Rééduca: a professional massage competition, complemented by the Massage Academy Challenge (both scheduled for Friday 18 September 2026).
- Rééduca Innov'': an award recognising the major product and service innovations in the rehabilitation sector, with the prize-giving on 17 September 2026.

### Community & networks
The show draws on community-driven activities: Octobre Rose at Rééduca (conferences and workshops dedicated to breast cancer awareness, in partnership with the Réseau des Kinés du Sein, Rose Up and Ruban Rose), the Espace Talents Santé (meetings with physiotherapists and osteopaths active on social media, with a signing area across the three days) and the Spot-Sport-Santé (the AVIROSE Challenge indoor rowing relay, run in support of the Réseau des Kinés du Sein).

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the show: Rééduca 2026 takes place from 17 to 19 September 2026, in Halls 5.2 and 5.3, from 9.30am to 6.30pm. Entry is free with a badge to be collected online. Address: 1, place de la Porte de Versailles, 75015 Paris.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="No price schedule is published by the organiser. The ranges below are indicative for a stand at a mid-sized health/paramedical trade show in Paris and are not binding on RX France." rows={[{ "poste": "Space rental (bare stand, ~9 to 18 m²)", "low": "4 000 €", "high": "11 000 €" }, { "poste": "Fit-out and equipped stand", "low": "3 000 €", "high": "10 000 €" }, { "poste": "Logistics, utilities, handling", "low": "1 500 €", "high": "4 000 €" }, { "poste": "Communication, staff, travel", "low": "2 500 €", "high": "8 000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (indicative)", "low": "~11 000 €", "high": "~33 000 €" }]} footer="For a firm price schedule, request the exhibitor pack from RX France." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor
- 6 months out: book the space with RX France and choose the hall (5.2 or 5.3).
- 4 months out: finalise the stand and scenography, and apply for Rééduca Innov'' if relevant.
- 2 months out: prepare the product demonstrations and line up meetings with prescribers.
- 3 weeks out: confirm the installation logistics and brief the team.

### For the decision-maker attending
Collect your free badge online in advance. Prioritise the Innovation Village and the Conference Area, identify the slots for the certifying DPC courses and plan the equipment demonstrations across the three days.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Rééduca is held at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, a site operated by Viparis, the world''s leading events operator certified ISO 20121 across all its sites since 2014, and committed to the Better Events 2030 approach (three pillars: Better for the Environment, Better Heritage, Better at Heart). RX France, the organiser, belongs to the RELX group, which publishes a sustainability policy (the Sustainability section on rxglobal.com). No CSR commitments page specific to the Rééduca event is published to date: the elements above relate to the venue and the organiser, not to a CSR scheme specific to the show.

## How the show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2026 (upcoming)", "dates": "17-19 Sept. 2026", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles (Halls 5.2-5.3)", "visiteurs": "6,000 (target)", "exposants": "110 (target)" }, { "edition": "2025", "dates": "9-11 Oct. 2025", "lieu": "Porte de Versailles", "visiteurs": "~5,500", "exposants": "130" }]} sources="2025 review: milo-kine.fr (post-event, 15 October 2025) and salonreeduca.com. 2026 targets: official site salonreeduca.com (pre-event marketing data)." />

### Trajectory analysis
Rééduca has established itself as the annual fixture of physiotherapy in France, anchored at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. The continuity of the format can be read in the stability of the venue and the growing strength of its professional activities: the Massage Masters competition, launched in 2025, returns in 2026 and is extended with the Massage Academy Challenge. The shift in the calendar from October 2025 to September 2026 is worth noting for exhibitors who plan their commercial cycle around it. The 2026 figures put forward by the organiser (6,000 visitors, 262 brands) are marketing targets to be weighed against the audited post-event review, with the 2025 actual figure standing at around 5,500 visitors.', seo_title_en='Rééduca 2026 Paris: dates, exhibitors, physio programme | Agoris', seo_description_en='Rééduca 2026: 17-19 September at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles (Halls 5.2-5.3). 2025 actual: ~5,500 visitors, 130 exhibitors, 233 brands. 2026 target: 6,000 visitors. Trade show for rehabilitation and physiotherapy, RX France. Free entry with a professional badge.' WHERE slug='reeduca-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='14th edition of France''s leading B2B proptech trade show, held at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, Pavilion 6, dedicated to technologies and services for transactional, rental and management real estate. 2025 results: 11,500+ professional visitors, 400 exhibitors including around a hundred startups, 120+ conferences.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 14th edition of **RENT (Real Estate & New Technologies)**: **4 and 5 November 2026**, Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **Pavilion 6** (architecture by Jean Nouvel).
- **France''s leading B2B proptech trade show**, dedicated to technologies and services for transactional, rental and management real estate.
- 2026 strapline: "Real estate moves from the screen to invisible AI". A direct continuation of the 2025 thread "AI, best friend or worst enemy?".
- 2025 results (13th edition, 5 and 6 November): **11,500+ professional visitors**, **400 exhibitors** including around a hundred startups, **120+ conferences, workshops and pitches**, **1,500 meeting requests** on the MySITL Connect platform.
- **"Festival de la PropTech" evening event** renewed: Wednesday 4 November from 7 pm to 9.30 pm, giant blind test, convivial atmosphere.
- Leadership: founded in 2013 by **Hervé Parent** (former chair of FF2i 2003-2013, manager of HP Conseils). Acquired outright by **Figaro Classifieds** in January 2019. General management held since that date by **Stéphane Scarella**.
- Main editorial partner: **Le Figaro Immobilier**.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

400 exhibitors in 2025 spread across **7 visitor trails** signposted by the organiser, covering the entire value chain of an estate agency or real estate operator:

- **Property transaction**: agency CRM, prospecting, valuation, electronic signature.
- **Rental management and property administration**: managing-agent software, rental management, dematerialisation.
- **Digital marketing**: real estate SEO, social ads, automation, marketing CRM.
- **Visibility and distribution**: listing portals, syndication, lead scoring.
- **Real estate fintech**: crowdfunding, online brokerage, creditworthiness scoring, payment.
- **Sector software**: drafting of deeds, transaction, managing-agent, management (Septeo, Modelo, etc.).
- **Technology**: data, AI, virtual tours, drone photo and video, virtual home staging (IACrea, Hoqi), construction and BIM, smart building.

Around a hundred startups exhibit each year, some of them on the spaces dedicated to innovation. The international editions **RENT Swiss (Lausanne)**, **RENT Madrid** and **RENT Casablanca** extend the brand beyond France.

### Notable exhibitors

Full list of exhibitors on the official website: [rent-event.com](https://rent-event.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

- **11,500+ professional visitors** in 2025.
- Profiles: estate agents, mandated agents, property administrators, managing agents, developers, social landlords, notaries, brokers, network executives, real estate CIOs, investors.
- Online pre-registration is mandatory, with proof of activity required for profiles not visible in the sector databases.
- Students on real estate training programmes: free on presentation of a student card.

## Activities and community

### Festival de la PropTech (evening event)

A 2025 innovation renewed in 2026. **Wednesday 4 November, 7 pm to 9.30 pm**, at the show. Giant blind test format, convivial atmosphere, open to registered exhibitors and visitors. The stated aim: to make the show a social moment, not just a business one. The event extends day 1 without detracting from day 2.

### Proptech Sweet Awards

Official awards for the 2026 edition, in partnership with **MySweetImmo**. Jury made up of **Ariane Artinian** (founder of MySweetImmo), **Jean-Pierre Domingo** (Managing Director of Septeo Solutions Immobilières) and **Stéphane Scarella** (Managing Director of RENT). **3 official prizes**:

- **Pépite Sweet Award**: innovation or new solution of the year.
- **Proptech Very Sweet Award**: social and environmental impact.
- **Proptech Sweet Ladies Award**: female leadership in proptech.

Past competitions have notably brought to light **Flatsy**, winner of La Startup RENT Orpi 2021.

### RENT Channel

A TV set installed at the show, with live recordings of the highlights (keynotes, exhibitor interviews, product demonstrations). Broadcast live and on replay across the RENT and Le Figaro Immobilier channels.

### Proptech Marketplace

A structured business development space designed to facilitate exhibitor / buyer introductions, complementing the MySITL Connect algorithmic matchmaking.

### Conferences, workshops and pitches

**120+ sessions** in 2025 over 2 days: panel discussions, inspiring keynotes, technical workshops, startup pitches. The 2026 strapline "Real estate moves from the screen to invisible AI" structures the editorial through-line, in continuity with "AI, best friend or worst enemy?" carried in 2025.

### MySITL Connect platform

A pre-show matchmaking tool. **1,500 meeting requests** generated at the 2025 edition, a sign of established usage among exhibitors as well as decision-making visitors.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the show:

- **Pavilion**: 6 (architecture by Jean Nouvel).
- **Dates**: Wednesday 4 and Thursday 5 November 2026.
- **Evening event**: Festival de la PropTech on Wednesday 4 November, 7 pm to 9.30 pm.
- **Visitor badge**: online pre-registration mandatory at rent-event.com.
- **Free** for students on real estate training programmes on presentation of a card.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published. Quote on request from the organiser via rent-event.com (exhibitor area). Placement and the per-square-metre rate vary according to the chosen trail (transaction, management, digital marketing, visibility, fintech, sector software, technology) and the stand format (bare, fitted, packaged, startup format on the spaces dedicated to innovation).

### Visitor rates (2025 reference)

- **2-day pass**: €390 excl. VAT.
- **Early bird**: 50% off the 2-day pass (closing date announced on the official website).
- **Free** for students on real estate training programmes on presentation of a card.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 10 months out: get in touch with the RENT sales team, choose your trail from the 7 (transaction, management, digital marketing, visibility, fintech, sector software, technology).
- 7 months out: apply for the Proptech Sweet Awards (Pépite, Very Sweet, Sweet Ladies) if relevant.
- 6 months out: contract the stand, brief the contractor, finalise the MySITL Connect matchmaking strategy.
- 3 months out: prepare product materials, open up business meetings in the diary.
- 6 weeks out: activate your network (Le Figaro Immobilier, MySweetImmo, targeted agency networks), press materials, pre-scheduled visit plan.
- 1 week out: brief the team on product demonstrations, the Wednesday evening event and the confirmed meetings.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online pre-registration mandatory before the eve of the show.
- Activate the early bird if the window is still open (50% off the 2-day pass).
- For estate agents and mandated agents: target the transaction, digital marketing and visibility trails.
- For property administrators and managing agents: target rental management, sector software and fintech.
- For CIOs and tech profiles: target the technology trail (data, AI, BIM, smart building) and the hundred or so exhibiting startups.
- Plan for the Wednesday evening event: a social moment, useful for extending conversations started during the day.

## CSR policy and initiatives

RENT has not formalised a separate CSR charter at show level. CSR topics are integrated into the editorial programme through the conferences (energy renovation, energy performance ratings, environmental certifications, low-carbon transition of the property stock) and through the **Proptech Very Sweet Award**, which specifically recognises solutions with a social or environmental impact. This trajectory is distinct from **SIBCA** (Salon Immobilier Bas Carbone), which is positioned on the low-carbon construction and operation value chain.

## How the show has evolved

