 ]}
 sources="foiredebordeaux.com, BEAM, Chambre régionale d''agriculture Nouvelle-Aquitaine"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

The Salon de l''Agriculture de Nouvelle-Aquitaine has established itself as the region''s largest consumer-facing agricultural gathering, by attaching itself to the Foire Internationale de Bordeaux to share audience, ticketing and the infrastructure of the Parc des Expositions. This integration enables it to reach a far wider audience than a stand-alone agricultural trade show, while retaining a strong identity around the triptych of livestock, wine-growing and gastronomy from the South-West.

The 2026 edition marks several shifts. A **new two-hall layout** makes the show easier to read: beef cattle and gastronomic produce in Hall 1, equine and breeds to be conserved in Hall 4. The arrival of a **new general commissioner, François Trignol**, a farmer in the Dordogne, signals a strengthened sector grounding. The consolidation of the **Trophée Aquitanima Junior** (5 agricultural colleges) confirms the priority given to the next generation, in connection with the careers-of-the-future zone run by the DRAAF.

The organiser **BEAM**, formerly CEB (Congrès et Expositions de Bordeaux), steers the CSR approach with **ISO 20121 certification** and the **Foires de France label**, two markers that position the show among the most advanced regional trade fairs in terms of responsible management. The slogan **"Le rendez-vous made in Sud-Ouest"** sums up the positioning: a resolutely regional agricultural trade show, a showcase for the Nouvelle-Aquitaine sectors, attached to the largest commercial trade fair in the South-West.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='salon-agriculture-nouvelle-aquitaine';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Professional trade show for wood energy and biomass. Boilers, stoves, pellets, cordwood and district heating networks.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Salon Bois Énergie** is the French professional gathering of the biomass heating sector: wood boilers and heating plants, stoves and pellets, forest wood chips, district heating networks and associated services.
- Organiser: **BEES SAS (BioEnergie Événements et Services)**, an operator based in Lyon. Long-standing local partners of the Nantes edition: **Atlanbois / FIBOIS Pays de la Loire** and **ADEME** (information stand), without co-organiser status.
- Next edition: **3-4 February 2027** (Wednesday-Thursday), at the [Parc des Expositions de Nantes](/lieux/parc-des-expositions-de-nantes) - La Beaujoire. Edition number not confirmed by the organiser.
- Audience of the Bois Énergie component: in the region of **3,000 trade visitors** and **~125 exhibitors**, with companies from around a dozen European countries (orders of magnitude as communicated, not OJS-audited).
- A structural point worth knowing: the Bois Énergie brand is integrated into the umbrella event **Bio360 Expo** (bringing together the bioenergy, bioeconomy and decarbonisation sectors), at the same venue and on the same dates. Wood-energy visitors therefore gain access to a broader bioeconomy scope.
- A trade show anchored in Nantes since 2021 (with Nantes already hosting in 2015 and 2022) following an itinerant history: Besançon (2011), Saint-Étienne (2012, 2014), Nancy (2016), Grenoble/Alpexpo (2018-2020).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile
Manufacturers and distributors of wood boilers and heating plants (logs, wood chips, pellets), stoves and inserts, producers and packagers of fuels (pellets, forest wood chips, cordwood), thermal engineering consultancies, district heating network integrators, equipment suppliers (silos, augers, filtration, control systems) and players in the sector''s financing and support.

### Notable exhibitors
The exhibitor list for the upcoming edition is kept up to date by the organiser. Consult the official list on the [Salon Bois Énergie website](https://www.bois-energie.fr).

### Quality of the visitor base
A visitor base geared towards decision-makers and prescribers: local authorities and energy syndicates, district heating network operators, installers and heating engineers, public project owners and social landlords, biomass-heated industrial sites, engineering consultancies. The organiser communicates an order of magnitude of around 3,000 trade visitors and a presence of companies from around a dozen European countries. These volumes are communicated figures, with no public OJS audit at this stage.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme
The event draws on a cycle of professional conferences, business meetings and technical site visits depending on the edition. The detailed programme for the 2027 edition is published as the event approaches on the official website.

### Awards and accolades
An innovation competition has historically accompanied the event. The official title and rules for the 2027 edition are to be confirmed on the organiser''s website before any citation.

### Community & networks
The trade show brings together the French wood-energy sector and its regional inter-professional bodies (including FIBOIS Pays de la Loire / Atlanbois on the Nantes side), alongside the institutional players of the energy transition. Its integration into Bio360 Expo connects it to the broader bioeconomy community (biogas, biochar, bio-sourced materials).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc des Expositions de Nantes](/lieux/parc-des-expositions-de-nantes) - La Beaujoire.

Specific to the trade show: a two-day edition, on 3 and 4 February 2027. The event is held jointly with Bio360 Expo on the same site, which broadens the scope of the visit. The reception hall, the access badge and the business meeting scheduling platform are detailed on the official website when registration opens.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="Pricing schedule not published at this stage for the 2027 edition. The amounts below are indicative orders of magnitude for a B2B professional trade show of this format (2 days, national/European scope) and do not replace a quote from the organiser." rows={[{ "poste": "Bare floor space (stand ~9 to 18 m²)", "low": "3 000 €", "high": "8 000 €" }, { "poste": "Fit-out / equipped stand", "low": "2 500 €", "high": "9 000 €" }, { "poste": "Logistics, furniture, utilities", "low": "1 500 €", "high": "5 000 €" }, { "poste": "Staff, travel, team accommodation", "low": "2 500 €", "high": "8 000 €" }, { "poste": "Communication, leads, goodies", "low": "1 500 €", "high": "6 000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (indicative, excluding options)", "low": "~11 000 €", "high": "~36 000 €" }]} footer="Request the official schedule and stand formats from the organiser (BEES SAS) via the trade show website." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor
- 6 months out: confirm the space reservation and stand format with BEES SAS, set the budget.
- 4 months out: finalise the stand fit-out, product demonstrations and the delivery logistics for heavy equipment (boilers, machinery).
- 2 months out: schedule business meetings via the platform, prepare materials and the pitch for a visitor base of prescribers and local authorities.
- 1 month out: brief the team on the targets (district heating networks, local authorities, project owners) and confirm accommodation in Nantes.

### For the decision-maker visitor
Pre-register your badge online, identify in advance the exhibitors relevant to your project (heating plant, district heating network, fuel supply) and book your meetings. The co-location with Bio360 Expo means you can cover both the upstream biomass side and related bioeconomy topics in a single visit.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The umbrella event Bio360 Expo displays a section of environmental commitments ("Nos engagements Verts") consistent with its energy transition theme. The detail of the measures applied specifically to the Salon Bois Énergie (waste management, mobility, catering, carbon footprint) is not publicly documented separately at this stage and remains to be confirmed with the organiser.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2027 (upcoming)", "dates": "3-4 February 2027", "lieu": "Parc des Expositions de Nantes - La Beaujoire", "visiteurs": "~3,000 (announced)", "exposants": "~125 (announced)" }, { "edition": "2026", "dates": "11-12 February 2026", "lieu": "Parc des Expositions de Nantes", "visiteurs": "~3,000", "exposants": "~125" }, { "edition": "Earlier editions", "dates": "since 2011", "lieu": "Itinerant (Besançon, Saint-Étienne, Nancy, Grenoble, Nantes since 2021)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }]} sources="Official site bois-energie.fr ; Bio360 Expo (bio360expo.com) ; NTradeShows (ntradeshows.com) ; FIBOIS Pays de la Loire (fibois-paysdelaloire.fr, 2020 edition review)." />

### Trajectory analysis
The Salon Bois Énergie is one of the oldest gatherings of the biomass heating sector in France, present since 2011 and historically itinerant in order to serve different forestry and industrial regions. The standout trajectory of recent years is its consolidation in Nantes: present as early as 2015 at the CCI de Nantes, it has been continuously anchored there since 2021 (Parc des Expositions - La Beaujoire). The Bois Énergie brand has, moreover, been integrated into the umbrella event Bio360 Expo, operated by BEES SAS. For the wood-energy sector, this means an unchanged core target (heating plants, district heating networks, fuels) but a visiting environment broadened to the whole bioeconomy. The 2027 edition, anchored in Nantes on 3 and 4 February, confirms this geographic stabilisation.', seo_title_en='Salon Bois Énergie 2027 Nantes: dates, exhibitors, info | Agoris', seo_description_en='Salon Bois Énergie 2027: 3-4 February at the Parc des Expositions de Nantes. Biomass heating plant sector, pellets, district heating networks. ~125 exhibitors, ~3,000 trade visitors.' WHERE slug='salon-bois-energie';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='B2B trade show for property co-ownership and real estate management. Managing agents, property administrators, energy renovation and technical management.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Salon de la Copropriété et de l''Habitat** is the benchmark event dedicated to the management and renovation of co-owned properties: managing agents, co-ownership boards, energy renovation, legal obligations and building works. It is organised by **Beyond Event**.
- Next edition: Wednesday 4 and Thursday 5 November 2026 at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), Halls 5.2 / 5.3.
- For more than thirty years, the trade show has brought together professionals and decision-making co-owners in a compact two-day format. Latest figures available (2024 edition): 9,493 participants and 272 exhibitors (source: monimmeuble.com).
- For 2026, the organiser is announcing nearly 300 exhibitors and 10,900 visitors expected (pre-show projections).
- The trade show is divided into 8 themed areas, with three highlights: the Professional Co-ownership Congress, the Co-ownership Grand Prix Awards and a networking evening.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Professional managing agents and property administrators, architects, engineering firms, works companies (energy renovation, façade restoration, roofing, maintenance, fit-out), lawyers, start-ups and providers of technical and digital solutions for building management. The offering is spread across 8 themed areas: Automation - Digital - AI, Banks - Insurance - Financing, Energy - Water - Waste, Mobility Infrastructure and Equipment, Common Areas - Maintenance - Hygiene, Security - Comfort Solutions, Managing Agents - Experts - Professional Organisations, Works - Renovation - Maintenance.

### Notable exhibitors

Full list of exhibitors on the official website: [copropriete-habitat.com/exposants](https://copropriete-habitat.com/exposants/). Among the exhibitors present at recent editions (2025): EDF, Engie, Enedis, Dalkia, Bouygues Construction, Bureau Veritas, Century 21, Caisse d''Épargne IDF, the Fédération des Ascenseurs and Fain Ascenseurs (energy, construction, lifts, real estate and co-ownership services).

### Quality of the audience

- The audience is made up of co-ownership professionals (managing agents, property administrators) and decision-making co-owners: chairs and members of co-ownership boards, multi-property co-owners.
- 9,493 participants welcomed in 2024 (source: monimmeuble.com), 10,900 visitors expected for 2026.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

At the 2025 edition, more than 80 conferences, keynotes, workshops and training sessions were held, led by co-ownership managers, company directors, co-owners and professional organisations. The themes covered financial management and new regulations, co-ownership governance, new uses and digital platforms, quality of life in co-owned buildings and the energy transition. The Professional Co-ownership Congress addresses sector-specific topics: artificial intelligence in management tools, HR policy, comprehensive energy renovation, reduction of charges and CSR. The 2026 programme has not yet been published.

### Awards and accolades

The **Co-ownership Grand Prix Awards**, organised in partnership with the magazine Copropriété et Travaux, reward the women and men who help the sector progress. The categories include: Sustainable development and low-carbon solutions, Connected co-ownership and digital services, Co-ownership professions, Mobility, Co-ownership partners, Works, maintenance and upkeep, Special Jury Prize, Special Magazine Prize and 2nd Special Prize from the magazine Copropriété et Travaux.

### Community and networks

Institutional partners present at the trade show: FNAIM du Grand Paris (FNAIM du Grand Paris Village, which runs several conferences with the École Supérieure de l''Immobilier), UNIS Île-de-France and Century 21.

A friendly, professional evening extends the first day until 10 pm, dedicated to networking.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Wednesday 4 November 9 am-10 pm (with the networking evening at the end of the day), Thursday 5 November 9 am-6 pm.
- **Halls:** 5.2 / 5.3.
- **Visitor badge:** prior online registration, with separate pathways for co-ownership professionals and for co-owners.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published on the official website: requests to take part via the dedicated form ([copropriete-habitat.com/devenir-exposant](https://copropriete-habitat.com/devenir-exposant/)) or by email to contact@copropriete-habitat.com. Figures not publicly available.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact with Beyond Event, choose your themed area from the show''s 8 worlds.
- 6 months out: prepare the stand plan and brief the team on the institutional partnerships (FNAIM Grand Paris, UNIS IDF).
- 3 months out: enter the Co-ownership Grand Prix Awards in conjunction with the magazine Copropriété et Travaux.
- 6 weeks out: confirm meetings with managing agents and co-ownership boards, sales briefing.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Pre-register online at copropriete-habitat.com, choosing the professional or co-owner pathway.
- Allow half a day to a full day depending on your scope (works, energy, legal, digital).
- Identify in advance the conferences of the Professional Co-ownership Congress and the technical workshops (energy renovation, charges control).

## The trade show''s evolution

