### Trajectory analysis

Since 2023 the Salon du Chocolat Paris has been consolidating a mixed format that draws both 90,000-96,000 general-public visitors and a B to B Village structured for manufacturers and artisans. The Comexposium partnership signed in March 2024 marks a new cycle: Event International retains operational control while Comexposium brings its Passions Division, its SIAL/Vinexposium network and its logistics, marketing and digital capabilities. The visible consequence was already apparent at the 2025 anniversary edition: 40% new exhibitors and the expansion to the Cake Time and Bean to Bar spaces. The 2026 edition (the 31st) marks the first full year of the partnership at cruising speed.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='salon-du-chocolat-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show on energy and home renovation. Insulation, heating, solar power, heat pumps and eco-construction.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key facts

- The **Salon Énergie Habitat** is the major annual home and habitat event for the Grand Est region, focused on energy-efficient renovation, construction and home improvement. Official strapline: "LE rendez-vous de l''habitat du Grand Est!".
- 45th edition from 20 to 23 March 2026 at the [Parc des Expositions de Colmar](/lieux/parc-expo-colmar), in halls 2, 3 and 4.
- A trade show organised by **Colmar-Expo** (SA Colmar-Expo), the operator of the exhibition centre, held annually each March.
- Nearly 180 regional exhibitors covering renewable energy (heat pumps, solar photovoltaics, wood heating), construction and renovation, joinery and home improvement, as well as advice and financing.
- Paid admission (5.50 euros, with concessions and free entry), alongside a programme of conferences and free expert consultations on energy-efficient renovation and 2026 grants.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Whole-house renovation and construction firms (timber-frame homes, thermal insulation), installers of energy solutions (heat pumps, geothermal, photovoltaics, wood and pellet heating), joiners (windows, doors, shutters, verandas, pergolas), interior and exterior design professionals, and advice and financing providers. The trade show combines commercial exhibitors with public support bodies, drawing a visitor base made up mainly of private individuals with home improvement projects in the Grand Est region.

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is available on the official website: [energiehabitat-colmar.com](https://www.energiehabitat-colmar.com/fr/liste-des-exposants-2026.html). The 2026 edition brings together regional players such as Alsace Géothermie, JA Energies, Groupe France Habitat, Maisons Erbat and Schmidt, alongside public support bodies offering advice (France Rénov'', ADIL 68, CAUE d''Alsace).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The trade show offers a series of daily conferences centred on energy-efficient renovation and its financing. The 2026 programme includes: "Rénovation énergétique et adaptation du domicile : mieux vivre dans son logement" (CITIVIA and CICAT68), "Travailler avec l''architecte" by Etienne Rohrer (Ordre des Architectes Grand Est), "Bien préparer ma copropriété à la rénovation énergétique" (ADIL 68), "Mon parcours rénovation énergétique et son financement" (Caisse d''Épargne Grand Est Europe and Leroy Merlin), "Le vrai du faux des aides à la rénovation énergétique en 2026" (Collectivité Européenne d''Alsace), as well as talks on geothermal energy and photovoltaics.

The trade show also offers "RDV Coaching Déco" sessions: 30 minutes free with architects and interior designers, plus free expert consultations with advice bodies.

### Community and networks

Partners and advice bodies in attendance: ADIL 68, Ordre des Architectes Grand Est, CAUE d''Alsace, IMEOS, France Rénov'', Collectivité Européenne d''Alsace, Caisse d''Épargne Grand Est Europe, CICAT68 and Citivia SPL.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc des Expositions de Colmar](/lieux/parc-expo-colmar).

Specific to this trade show:

- **Halls:** halls 2, 3 and 4 of the exhibition centre.
- **Opening hours:** Friday, Saturday and Sunday from 10 a.m. to 7 p.m., Monday from 10 a.m. to 6 p.m.
- **Admission prices:** 5.50 euros full price, 4.50 euros concession (students, people with disabilities), free for children (see conditions on site), and free for over-60s on Monday. Free invitations can be downloaded online via the official ticketing service.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with Colmar-Expo about placement in halls 2, 3 or 4.
- 6 months out: prepare the stand and demonstrations (energy equipment, joinery, home improvement).
- 3 months out: apply to take part in the conference programme or the expert consultations.
- 6 weeks out: commercial briefing on the target audience of private individuals with renovation and home improvement projects.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Prepare your project in advance (energy-efficient renovation, heating, insulation, home improvement) to target the right exhibitors.
- Book an "RDV Coaching Déco" (30 minutes free) or an expert consultation with the advice bodies (France Rénov'', ADIL 68, CAUE).
- Identify the conferences on 2026 renovation grants and their financing before your visit.
- Allow half a day to a full day depending on the scope of your project.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Édition" },
  { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "45e / 2026", "dates": "20-23 mars 2026" },
  { "edition": "44e / 2025", "dates": "14-17 mars 2025" },
  { "edition": "43e / 2024", "dates": "15-18 mars 2024" }
 ]}
