 ]}
 sources="letudiant.fr, viparis.com, region-academique-idf.fr"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

In 2026, the Salon de l''Étudiant Île-de-France reaches its **40th edition**, a sign of editorial longevity that is rare on the French guidance trade show market. Created in 1986 in Paris, the format spread as early as 1988 to Lille, Lyon and Marseille, then to some twenty French cities, reaching nearly 120 shows a year today.

The 2026 regional calendar illustrates this density: **Bordeaux** (9 to 11 January, 37th edition), **Lyon Eurexpo** (9 to 11 January), **Lille** (15 to 17 January, 38th edition), **Marseille** (16 and 17 January, 37th edition) and **Paris Île-de-France** (30 January to 1 February, 40th edition). The year closes in spring with the specialist shows (Grandes Écoles, apprenticeships) and in June with Cap sur la Rentrée for the Parcoursup supplementary phase.

Three structural factors explain the trade show''s dominant position: L''Étudiant''s free editorial mission (the legacy of founders **René Silvestre**, **Guy Pessiot** and **Benoît Prot**), strong institutional grounding with the Île-de-France academic region and ONISEP, and exhaustive coverage of Île-de-France post-baccalaureate provision, from BTS to the Grandes Écoles. The end of the print version of the magazine in February 2019 accelerated the group''s shift towards all-events and digital, without affecting the momentum of the physical trade shows, which remain sixth-form pupils'' main point of contact with their future institutions.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='salon-etudiant-ile-de-france';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for construction, renovation and home improvement. Solutions for private individuals and building trade professionals.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Salon Habitat & Déco de Bordeaux** is the regional public-facing event for home construction, renovation, fitting-out and decoration. It returns for its **5th edition** at the Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux, Hall 3.
- 2026 edition: from **6 to 8 March 2026** (Friday to Sunday), 10 am to 7 pm, at the Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux, Hall 3.
