## How the trade show has evolved

5th edition in 2026. Annual trade show organised by LÉO at the Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux. Attendance figures and a detailed review of previous editions have not been published publicly to date.', seo_title_en='Salon Habitat & Déco de Bordeaux 2026: dates, exhibitors, practical info', seo_description_en='Salon Habitat & Déco de Bordeaux 2026: 5th edition from 6 to 8 March 2026 at the Parc des Expositions, Hall 3. 250 exhibitors in construction, renovation, fitting-out and decoration. Organised by LÉO.' WHERE slug='salon-habitat-bordeaux';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='A trade show for the home, interior decoration and interior design. Furniture, lighting, coverings and decorative objects.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key facts

- The **Salon Habitat & Design** in Saint-Étienne is the annual consumer event devoted to the home: construction, renovation, indoor and outdoor fitting-out, decoration, design and gardening. It is organised by **Saint-Étienne Évènements**, operator of the [Parc Expo de Saint-Étienne](/lieux/parc-expo-saint-etienne) and a subsidiary of the GL Events group.
- Next edition announced: **12 to 14 March 2027** at the Parc Expo de Saint-Étienne.
- The 2026 edition (from 6 to 8 March, presented as the fourth edition) marked a turning point: for the first time, the Salon de l''Habitat and the Salon de l''Immobilier were brought together in a single hall, the latter strand being organised in partnership with the magazine **Le 42 Immo**.
- More than **130 exhibitors**, local and regional, in 2026, over 90% of which were based in the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region, along with more than 50 property professionals (developers, builders, financial advisers, notaries).
- Free entry with registration. A regional consumer-facing event, not a B2B professional trade show.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Building trades, energy-renovation specialists, manufacturers and distributors of kitchens, windows, verandas, pergolas, stoves and heating solutions, landscapers and gardening professionals, decorators and furniture retailers. On the property side: developers, individual-home builders, agencies, financial advisers and notaries.

The trade show shows strong regional roots: more than 90% of the 2026 exhibitors were based in Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes.

### Notable exhibitors

Link to the list of exhibitors: [salonhabitatdesign-saintetienne.com](https://www.salonhabitatdesign-saintetienne.com/liste-exposants). The 2026 edition notably featured an apartment created by **Conforama** as part of the **La Maison Confo** activation.

### Quality of the visitor base

- A regional consumer visitor base, with projects in construction, renovation, decoration or property purchase.
- The bringing together of Habitat + Immobilier aims to offer a complete reading of the residential ecosystem, from renovation through to financing and purchase.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2026 edition offered conferences and practical workshops, including a conference organised by **UNIS** (Union des syndicats de l''immobilier) on the Friday at 3 pm on property, financing and renewable energy. The detailed programme for the 2027 edition will be published as the trade show approaches.

### Activities

2026 activities: **La Maison Confo** (an apartment fitted out by Conforama), the **chambre des erreurs** (an educational space), a plant market, a children''s area run at the weekend, as well as demonstrations and workshops.

### Community and networks

The Immobilier strand is organised in partnership with the magazine **Le 42 Immo**, a local property media outlet in the Loire.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc Expo de Saint-Étienne](/lieux/parc-expo-saint-etienne).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours (2026 edition):** Friday 10 am-9 pm (late-night opening), Saturday 10 am-7 pm, Sunday 10 am-6 pm. 2027 hours to be confirmed on the official website.
- **Entry:** free with prior online registration.
- **Exhibition venue:** Hall A of the Parc Expo.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- Applications to take part are made via the trade show''s official website ([salonhabitatdesign-saintetienne.com](https://www.salonhabitatdesign-saintetienne.com)) or the GL Events exhibitor area ([exposant.gl-events.com](https://exposant.gl-events.com)).
- Priority target: craftspeople, distributors and home and property professionals from the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region.

### For the visitor

- Free prior registration at [salonhabitatdesign-saintetienne.com](https://www.salonhabitatdesign-saintetienne.com).
- Allow half a day to a full day to cover both worlds, home and property, brought together in a single hall.
- The Friday late-night opening makes it easier to visit at the end of the day.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The Parc Expo de Saint-Étienne, managed by Saint-Étienne Évènements, is certified to **ISO 14001** (environmental management system). The site highlights three areas: energy management, waste reduction and recovery, and short supply chains for catering. Concrete measures cited: water-saving devices and presence detectors in communal areas, low-energy lighting, centralised climate management, LCD/LED screens to reduce paper, water fountains to replace plastic bottles, and selective sorting points distributed throughout the circulation areas.

No ISO 20121 certification specific to the event is mentioned to date. The detailed commitments relate to the host venue, not to a CSR approach specific to the trade show published separately.

## How the trade show has evolved

The 2026 edition, presented as the fourth edition, brought together the Salon de l''Habitat and the Salon de l''Immobilier in a single hall for the first time, linking home, renovation, financing and property into a coherent journey. This merger took the event to more than 130 exhibitors, including more than 50 property professionals. The next edition is announced for 12 to 14 March 2027 at the Parc Expo de Saint-Étienne. Detailed attendance figures are not published to date.', seo_title_en='Salon Habitat & Design Saint-Étienne 2027: dates, exhibitors, info', seo_description_en='Salon Habitat & Design in Saint-Étienne 2027: from 12 to 14 March at the Parc Expo. Over 130 exhibitors covering home, renovation, decoration and property. Free entry.' WHERE slug='salon-habitat-design-saint-etienne';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Open-field trade show for forage crops and grassland. Equipment demonstrations, harvesting techniques and grassland management.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The Salon de l''Herbe et des Fourrages is an open-field trade show dedicated to livestock farming and forage crops: "from the seed to its value in the ration". Equipment demonstrations in real-world conditions, a forage showcase and technical advice.
- An itinerant trade show that alternates each year between three major livestock-farming regions: the Centre at Villefranche-d''Allier (03), the East at Poussay (88) and the West at Nouvoitou (35).
- Next edition: **26 and 27 May 2027 at Nouvoitou (35)**, in the West.
- Most recent edition held: 20 and 21 May 2026 at Poussay (88), with 26,457 trade visitors and 171 exhibiting brands (official post-show report, press area salonherbe.com).
- Organiser: **Profield Events Group** (Torcy, 71).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers and distributors of haymaking, harvesting and grassland-working equipment, forage seed companies, service firms in animal nutrition and feed, and grassland and forage management consultants. The visitor base is professional: cattle, sheep and goat farmers, technicians, advisers and agricultural contractors.

The trade show is built around dynamic open-field demonstrations: more than 30 hectares of exhibition and equipment demonstrations, complemented by a forage showcase of more than 2 hectares presenting over 600 micro-plots of grasses, legumes, mixtures, mixed cereals, maize, beet and forage sorghum in real-world conditions.

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [salonherbe.com](https://www.salonherbe.com/). The 2026 edition brought together 171 exhibiting brands.

## Activities & community

### Advice area and forage showcase

The trade show is organised around technical hubs: live equipment demonstrations (mowing, tedding, raking, baling, silage-making), a forage showcase of more than 2 hectares presenting grassland species and mixtures, and an advice area run by 50 independent experts on grassland management, harvesting and value in the ration.

The editorial positioning takes a strong topical angle: adapting forage systems to climate change and feed self-sufficiency for livestock farms.

## On site: what you need to know

The trade show takes place on an open-field site, which changes for each edition depending on the host region. For the 2027 edition, the meeting point is Nouvoitou (35), in the West.

The information below corresponds to the organisation observed at the 2026 edition in Poussay and is liable to change for 2027:

- **Opening hours:** 9 am to 6 pm on both days (Wednesday and Thursday).
- **Visitor badge:** chargeable. Reduced rate for online pre-registration (5 euros incl. VAT for the day, 7 euros incl. VAT for both days), higher on-site rate (10 euros for the day, 20 euros for both days). Free entry for visitors holding an invitation, foreign visitors holding a passport and children under 15.
- **Access and parking:** site accessible by car, two free visitor car parks set up near the entrances. Free car-sharing service offered by the organiser.
- **Accommodation:** booking platform via the partner Revolugo.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- Beforehand: make contact with Profield Events Group via the exhibitor area of the official website regarding positioning on the open-field site.
- Anticipate the logistics specific to the open field: outdoor set-up, live demonstrations, forage showcase plots.
- Check the livestock-farming region for the edition (West in 2027 at Nouvoitou) to calibrate your offer and sales pitch.

### For the visitor

- Pre-register your badge online to benefit from the reduced rate.
- Plan for clothing suited to an open-field site and outdoor demonstrations.
- Target the hubs to visit in advance: equipment demonstrations, forage showcase, advice area.

