### Trajectory analysis

A steady growth trajectory since 2023: from 25,000 participants to 37,180 in 2026 (around +6% vs 2025), with a stable base of around 700 exhibitors. The show successfully completed its 2019 rebranding (Paris Healthcare Week to SantExpo) by broadening its scope from hospital equipment alone to social care, digital health and environmental transformation. The 2027 edition, from 25 to 27 May at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, extends this momentum by drawing on FHF backing to mobilise the entire institutional healthcare ecosystem. The 2027 theme and target figures will be published as the show approaches.', seo_title_en='SantExpo 2027 - Healthcare and Social Care Trade Show | Paris Expo Porte de Versailles', seo_description_en='SantExpo 2027: the major professional gathering for healthcare and social care, 25-27 May 2027 at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. HopitalExpo, GerontHandicapExpo and HIT brought together. 37,180 participants in 2026, 696 exhibitors, 304 conferences.' WHERE slug='santexpo-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for agri-food equipment and processing in the Grand Est region. Suppliers to the regional food industry.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **SEPAG** (Salon des Équipements, Process et Prestataires Agro-Alimentaire) is one of the three strands of **RSD3**, the "3-in-1" industrial event that brings together the RIST (industrial subcontracting), the SEPAG (agri-food) and the Drôme Digital Days (digital).
- **Organiser: the CCI de la Drôme** (alongside the CCI de l''Ardèche), and not Comexposium: the trade show is run by the chambers of commerce under general commissioner Dominique Ribet.
- **Upcoming edition: 2028**, at the **[Palais des Expositions Jacques Chirac](/lieux/palais-expo-jacques-chirac-valence)** in Valence. The RSD3 is held **every two years** (even-numbered years), alternating with a trade show dedicated to services: the next edition follows on from the one held on 21 and 22 April 2026.
- **Scale (2024 edition, overall RSD3 scope): 200 exhibitors and around 3,330 trade visitors** (organiser figures, all trade shows combined). The SEPAG on its own gathered around sixty agri-food exhibitors.
- Editorial focus: a **regional Drôme-Ardèche / Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes** trade show geared towards equipment, processing, packaging, marking, hygiene and service providers to the food industry, with a B2B matchmaking platform.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The SEPAG brings together suppliers and service providers to the agri-food industry, across six families set out by the organiser: Equipment and Processing, Packaging and Conditioning, Environment, Marking and Coding, Safety and Hygiene, and Services. The event is positioned on a strong territorial anchoring: at the 2026 edition, around 70% of exhibitors came from the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region.

The SEPAG does not exist in isolation: it takes place under the RSD3 banner, alongside the RIST (industrial subcontracting, services and supplies) and the Drôme Digital Days (digital solutions). An agri-food visitor therefore has access, on the same site, to a broader offer that also covers subcontracting and industrial digital.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of exhibitors can be consulted on the [official RSD3 website](https://www.rsd3.fr). Agoris does not reproduce brand names that have not been confirmed by the organiser for the upcoming edition.

### Quality of the visitor base

The published visitor figures relate to the RSD3 as a whole, and not to the SEPAG alone. For the 2024 edition, the organiser reported around 3,330 trade visitors, with a markedly decision-making audience: in the region of 28% company directors and 25% senior managers, with the remainder drawn from technical purchasing, production, manufacturing and R&D. These data are provided by the organiser and are not based on a public OJS audit.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The conference programme is shared at RSD3 level and accessible to SEPAG visitors. At the 2026 edition, it covered in particular: electronic invoicing (legal obligations from 1 September 2026), AI in industrial processes, generative AI in SMEs, IoT and real-time supervision, cybersecurity of industrial systems (Cyber OT, NIS2), augmented industry (Orange Business), energy efficiency and motor optimisation, solar production and consumption, water management, prospects for the nuclear sector (Orano, EDF, the EPR2 project), commercial strategy and prospecting, and even "Leading without burning out". The detail is published on the [official website](https://www.rsd3.fr/conferences).

### Awards and prizes

No official award or trophy is publicly documented for the SEPAG. This section will be completed if the organiser announces any.

### Community and networks

The RSD3 runs its communities under the "RSD3: Rist.Sepag.Ddd" identity (LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram). A B2B matchmaking platform is open to visitors so they can arrange business meetings in advance.

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the listing for the [Palais des Expositions Jacques Chirac](/lieux/palais-expo-jacques-chirac-valence) in Valence.

Specific to the trade show: the SEPAG runs over two days, a format adopted in 2026 to better fit companies'' needs (previously over a single day). Entry is free and reserved for professionals. The SEPAG shares the RSD3 hall with the RIST and the Drôme Digital Days: a single badge gives access to all three trade shows, to the meetings platform and to the lounge, business and catering areas.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="No exhibitor price list for the SEPAG/RSD3 is published online: the ranges below are indicative for a regional B2B trade show over two days and should be confirmed with the CCI de la Drôme." rows={[{ "poste": "Bare floor space (regional stand, ~9 to 18 m²)", "low": "€1,500", "high": "€4,500" }, { "poste": "Fit-out / equipped stand", "low": "€1,000", "high": "€4,000" }, { "poste": "Registration fees, utilities, insurance", "low": "€300", "high": "€1,200" }, { "poste": "Logistics, transport, staff, accommodation", "low": "€1,500", "high": "€5,000" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (regional stand, 2 days)", "low": "~€4,500", "high": "~€15,000" }]} footer="Indicative sector rates, not provided by the organiser. Request the exhibitor pack from the CCI de la Drôme for a firm quote." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- **6 to 4 months before**: make contact with the CCI de la Drôme, choose the relevant trade show (SEPAG agri-food) and book floor space.
- **3 months before**: finalise the stand, qualify regional targets, activate your profile on the B2B matchmaking platform.
- **1 month before**: arrange business meetings in advance, prepare equipment/process demonstrations, transport and installation logistics.
- **On site**: capture the decision-making audience (directors and company heads) and make the most of the cross-cutting RSD3 conferences.

### For the decision-making visitor

The SEPAG is a short, dense format: two days, an offer concentrated on suppliers to the food industry, with the bonus of access to the subcontracting (RIST) and digital (Drôme Digital Days) strands. Prepare a shortlist of needs (equipment, packaging, marking, hygiene, services), book your meetings via the platform and target the useful conferences (energy efficiency, industrial AI, electronic invoicing). The regional anchoring makes it an efficient gateway to service providers across Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The RSD3 does not publish a dedicated Commitments page and the trade show is not ISO 20121 certified. The verifiable CSR approach lies on the organiser''s side: the CCI de la Drôme co-organises [Dynamic R](https://www.drome.cci.fr/actualite/dynamic-r-2025-185-decideurs-et-salaries-inspires-et-5-laureats-recompenses-pour-leur), an annual corporate social responsibility event bringing together decision-makers and employees from the Drôme-Ardèche area (4th edition November 2025: 185 participants, CSR trophies awarded to 5 local companies). The CCI Drôme also supports companies in their environmental transition through a scheme co-funded with ADEME (energy audit, support with no upfront costs) and runs a Drôme Ecobiz community dedicated to QSE-CSR clubs. These initiatives concern potential exhibiting companies from the area, not the internal running of the trade show. At programme level, the RSD3 2026 conferences address transition themes (energy efficiency, solar production, smart water management) but these are conference topics, not commitments of the event itself.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors (RSD3)" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors (RSD3)" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2028 (upcoming)", "dates": "April 2028 (to be confirmed)", "lieu": "Palais des Expositions Jacques Chirac, Valence", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "2026", "dates": "21-22 April 2026", "lieu": "Palais des Expositions Jacques Chirac, Valence", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "2024", "dates": "2024 (exact dates not published)", "lieu": "Palais des Expositions Jacques Chirac, Valence", "visiteurs": "~3,330", "exposants": "200" }]} sources="Organiser data (CCI Drôme / RSD3). 2024 figures = overall RSD3 scope (RIST + SEPAG + Drôme Digital Days), not specific to the SEPAG. The SEPAG had around sixty exhibitors of its own." />

### Trajectory analysis

The SEPAG has made a structural shift: integrated into the RSD3, it abandoned its status as a standalone annual trade show to adopt a **biennial** rhythm (even-numbered years), alternating with a trade show dedicated to services. This "3-in-1" grouping pools visitors, conferences and the B2B platform, which boosts reported attendance but dilutes the legibility of the agri-food''s own figures: the 200 exhibitors and ~3,330 visitors reported cover all three trade shows, with the SEPAG accounting for around sixty stands. The move to two days in 2026 confirms a step up in quality, in service of an assumed positioning as the Drôme-Ardèche regional gathering for suppliers to the food industry.', seo_title_en='SEPAG 2028 Valence: dates, exhibitors, RSD3 | Agoris', seo_description_en='SEPAG 2028, the trade show for agri-food equipment and processing within the RSD3 (Palais des Expositions Jacques Chirac, Valence). Biennial, organised by the CCI Drôme-Ardèche. Dates, exhibitors, programme.' WHERE slug='sepag';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show of services, equipment, process and maintenance for industry. Centre-Ouest regional edition covering the Pays de la Loire and Brittany.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **SEPEM Industries Centre-Ouest** is the industrial gathering of the Grand Ouest (Pays de la Loire, Brittany). A generalist trade show of services, equipment, process and maintenance for the factory, organised by **GL Events Exhibitions Industrie**.
- Next edition: 10th edition, from 12 to 14 October 2027 at the [Parc des Expositions d''Angers](/lieux/parc-expo-angers), in Saint-Sylvain-d''Anjou.
- A biennial trade show (odd years): the 2025 edition (9th) was held from 7 to 9 October.
- 2025 review: around 450 exhibitors announced, of which at least 30% came from the Pays de la Loire (official source), and 43% first-time participants announced. The 2023 edition welcomed 5,370 visitors.
- Free entry with prior registration for professional visitors.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Equipment manufacturers and suppliers to industry across the entire production chain: production, maintenance, safety, environment, subcontracting. SEPEM is a proximity trade show whose catchment area corresponds to less than 2 h 30 of driving: at least 30% of the exhibitors at the 2025 edition came from the Pays de la Loire (according to the official site; the regional press mentions up to half).

The attendee base is strictly professional and technical: directors, production and maintenance managers, buyers, new works, design offices, R&D, instrumentation.

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official site: [angers.sepem-industries.com](https://angers.sepem-industries.com/). The 2027 edition is announced at around 450 exhibitors.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

A series of free conferences and round tables accompanies the trade show, covering the major industrial challenges of the moment: maintenance 4.0, artificial intelligence, decarbonisation, energy and digital transition, reshoring, cybersecurity, employment and training. Detailed programme published in the run-up to the show on angers.sepem-industries.com.

### Awards and accolades

The **Trophées SEPEM Angers** reward exhibiting companies in three categories: **Sustainable Innovation Award**, **Digital Transformation Award** and **Social and Societal Engagement Award**. 2025 winners: Bodet Time (Sustainable Innovation), Fuzzy Logic Robotics (Digital Transformation) and Alliance Caoutchouc (Social and Societal Engagement). Categories and winners for 2027 to be confirmed in the run-up to the show.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc des Expositions d''Angers](/lieux/parc-expo-angers). The site is located on Route de Paris, in Saint-Sylvain-d''Anjou: 35 min by train from Nantes, less than 1 h 30 from Paris-Montparnasse, at the crossroads of the A11, A85 and A87 motorways.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Tuesday and Wednesday 9 am-6 pm, Thursday 9 am-5 pm.
- **Visitor badge:** free entry with prior online registration, reserved for professionals.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: get in touch with GL Events Exhibitions Industrie (contact.sepem@gl-events.com), book a stand.
- 9 months out: apply for the Trophées SEPEM Angers (Sustainable Innovation, Digital Transformation, Social and Societal Engagement).
- 6 months out: prepare demonstrations and product launches, sales brief on the regional target.
- 6 weeks out: confirm meetings with the production and maintenance managers of the local industrial fabric.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free pre-registration online at angers.sepem-industries.com.
- Plan for a half-day to a full day depending on the scope (production, maintenance, safety, subcontracting).
- Target the conferences and workshops in advance: programme published several weeks before the show.

## CSR policy & initiatives

SEPEM Angers highlights the "innovative and responsible" approaches of industrial companies through its **Sustainable Innovation Award** and its **Social and Societal Engagement Award**, which recognise the reduction of environmental impact, well-being at work, inclusion, training and territorial impact. No CSR commitments page specific to the organisation of the event is published to date (source: angers.sepem-industries.com).

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "2027 (10th, upcoming)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "~450 announced" },
  { "edition": "2025 (9th)", "visiteurs": "~5,500 expected", "exposants": "~450 announced" },
  { "edition": "2023", "visiteurs": "5,370", "exposants": "n/a" }
 ]}
 sources="angers.sepem-industries.com, lejournaldesentreprises.com, robot-magazine.fr"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

SEPEM Centre-Ouest has, in just a few editions, established itself as the reference industrial gathering of the Grand Ouest. The 2023 edition brought together 5,370 visitors, and the 2025 edition (9th) confirmed the momentum with around 450 exhibitors announced and a high turnover rate (43% first-time participants announced). A proximity trade show by design, it draws on a strong regional anchoring. The 10th edition, from 12 to 14 October 2027, extends this positioning around the rising themes of industry: maintenance 4.0, artificial intelligence and decarbonisation. SEPEM Angers is part of the national network of SEPEM regional trade shows operated by GL Events ([SEPEM Toulouse](/salons/sepem-toulouse), [SEPEM Grenoble](/salons/sepem-grenoble), [SEPEM Colmar](/salons/sepem-colmar), [SEPEM Douai](/salons/sepem-douai)).', seo_title_en='SEPEM Industries Centre-Ouest 2027 Angers: dates, exhibitors, info', seo_description_en='SEPEM Industries Centre-Ouest 2027 in Angers from 12 to 14 October: trade show of services, equipment, process and maintenance for industry in the Grand Ouest. Exhibitors, conferences, Trophées SEPEM and practical info.' WHERE slug='sepem-angers';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for services, equipment, processes and maintenance for industry. Regional Eastern edition covering the Grand Est region (Alsace).', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **SEPEM Industries Est** is the regional Eastern edition of the SEPEM Industries network of trade shows, dedicated to services, equipment, processes and maintenance for production sites. It covers the Grand Est region (Alsace) and is held at the [Parc Expo Colmar](/lieux/parc-expo-colmar).
- Next edition: from Tuesday 21 to Thursday 23 September 2027 in Colmar.
- Operator: **GL events Exhibitions Industrie**, which runs the entire SEPEM Industries network.
- A proximity trade show: each city in the network returns every three years. In Colmar, the previous edition took place in June 2024 and brought together nearly 473 announced exhibitors (source: lejournaldesentreprises.com).
- A demonstration-focused format: more than one hundred machines in operation were presented at the 2024 edition (source: lejournaldesentreprises.com).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Industrial subcontractors and suppliers, manufacturers and distributors of production equipment, assembly, lifting, conveying, robotics and cobotics, measurement and control, cutting, machining, maintenance, industrial safety and on-site environmental solutions. The trade show is aimed at companies that equip or operate the factories of the Grand Est region.

The SEPEM Industries network adapts this positioning to each regional industrial area: alongside the Eastern edition in Colmar, there are [SEPEM Sud-Ouest in Toulouse](/salons/sepem-toulouse), [SEPEM Centre-Est in Grenoble](/salons/sepem-grenoble), [SEPEM Centre-Ouest in Angers](/salons/sepem-angers) and [SEPEM Nord in Douai](/salons/sepem-douai).

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors to come on the official website: [colmar.sepem-industries.com](https://colmar.sepem-industries.com/). The 2027 edition is announced with more than 450 exhibitors.

### Quality of attendance

- Strictly professional attendance, drawn from the industrial sites of the Grand Est region (production, maintenance, design offices, purchasing).
- Nearly half of the exhibitors at the 2024 edition were first-time participants (source: lejournaldesentreprises.com).
- Free entry for professional visitors with prior registration.

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The 2024 edition offered a cycle of technical conferences covering, in particular, maintenance, AI-assisted machine vision, decarbonisation, Industry 4.0 and the circular economy (source: lejournaldesentreprises.com). The programme for the 2027 edition is available on [colmar.sepem-industries.com](https://colmar.sepem-industries.com/).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Parc Expo Colmar](/lieux/parc-expo-colmar) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 21 September 9 am-6 pm, Wednesday 22 September 9 am-6 pm, Thursday 23 September 9 am-5 pm.
- **Visitor badge:** free with prior online registration, reserved for industry professionals.
- **Access:** Colmar Expo, avenue de la Foire aux Vins, 68000 Colmar; Basel-Mulhouse airport 62 km away, Strasbourg airport 66 km away.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months before: get in touch with the GL events Exhibitions Industrie team and choose positioning by sector (production, maintenance, environment, safety).
- 9 months before: book your stand and prepare machine demonstrations, a key feature of the trade show.
- 3 months before: prepare meetings with manufacturers from the Grand Est area, commercial briefing.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free pre-registration online with proof of industrial professional activity.
- Allow half a day to a full day depending on scope (equipment, maintenance, subcontracting).
- Target machine demonstrations and technical conferences in advance.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "2027 (upcoming)", "exposants": "450+ announced" },
  { "edition": "2024", "exposants": "~473 (announced)" }
 ]}
 sources="colmar.sepem-industries.com, lejournaldesentreprises.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

SEPEM Industries Est is part of a national network of proximity industrial trade shows operated by GL events Exhibitions Industrie: each regional area hosts its edition every three years, which makes Colmar the meeting point for the Grand Est region between two cycles. The 2024 edition confirmed the show''s positioning, centred on the demonstration of machines in operation and direct matchmaking between suppliers and production sites. The 2027 edition, from 21 to 23 September, continues this model with more than 450 announced exhibitors. Attendance figures and the final list of exhibitors will be published once the trade show has ended.', seo_title_en='SEPEM Industries Est 2027 Colmar: Grand Est industry show', seo_description_en='SEPEM Industries Est 2027 at Parc Expo Colmar from 21 to 23 September: equipment, processes and maintenance for Grand Est industry. Dates, exhibitors, access.' WHERE slug='sepem-colmar';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for industrial services, equipment, processes and maintenance. Regional Nord edition for the factories of the Hauts-de-France region.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- SEPEM Industries Nord is the biennial trade show for the Services, Equipment, Processes and Maintenance of industry in the Hauts-de-France region. It is held in Douai and organised by **GL events Exhibitions Industrie**.
- Next edition: 12th edition, from 25 to 27 January 2028 at Gayant Expo Douai.
- Latest reported edition (2026, 27-29 January): **12,306 participants**, **600 exhibitors** across nearly 10,000 sq m, with 80% stating they intend to return for the next edition (source: douai.sepem-industries.com).
- A proximity trade show: around 40% of exhibitors are companies from the Hauts-de-France region, reflecting a logic of short supply chains and industrial sovereignty.
- Classic SEPEM format: free entry, parking and catalogue, with a strictly professional visitor base.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Suppliers of services, equipment, processes and maintenance for industry: subcontracting, assembly, lifting and handling, robotics, measurement and control, machining and cutting, maintenance, safety, storage logistics. The trade show targets the factories and production sites of the Hauts-de-France region, an area with a high density of industry (automotive, rail, food processing, metallurgy, plastics processing).

Around 40% of exhibitors are regional companies, and 36% were new participants at the 2026 edition (source: pei-france.com, machine-outil.com).

### Notable exhibitors

The full list of exhibitors is available on the official website: [SEPEM Douai exhibitor list](https://douai.sepem-industries.com/content/liste-des-exposants).

### Quality of the visitor base

- 12,306 participants in 2026, for a strictly professional industrial visitor base (maintenance managers, design offices, production departments, purchasing, SMI directors).
- 52% purchasing decision-makers among visitors at the 2026 edition (source: douai.sepem-industries.com).
- 80% of visitors state they intend to return for the next edition (source: douai.sepem-industries.com).
- 110 innovations presented as previews at the 2026 edition (source: douai.sepem-industries.com).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2026 edition offered a series of conferences and round tables on the major challenges facing regional industry: reindustrialisation and industrial sovereignty, AI and Maintenance 4.0, cybersecurity, decarbonisation, and the appeal of industrial careers and recruitment. The 2025 edition had brought together 20 conferences and round tables led by around fifty experts (source: douai.sepem-industries.com). The 2028 programme will be published as the trade show approaches.

### Awards and prizes

The **Trophées SEPEM** reward the innovative and responsible initiatives of industrial companies. Three categories are open to participants: **Sustainable Innovation Award**, **Digital Transformation Award**, **Social and Societal Commitment Award**. The trade show''s home page also highlights **Les Fleurons de l''industrie**, a distinction dedicated to outstanding industrial companies. Categories and 2028 winners to be confirmed on the official website as the trade show approaches (source: douai.sepem-industries.com).

### Community and networks

The trade show includes an employment and careers area: at the 2025 edition, the job dating generated 70 interviews with 40% positive outcomes, and more than 300 secondary and high school students discovered industrial careers through immersive tours (source: douai.sepem-industries.com).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Gayant Expo Douai](/lieux/gayant-expo-douai) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 25 and Wednesday 26 January 2028 from 9 am to 6 pm, Thursday 27 January from 9 am to 5 pm.
- **Visitor badge:** free entry with online registration, reserved for industry professionals. Parking and catalogue are also free.
- **Access:** Gayant Expo is 30 minutes from Lille, 1 hour from Paris and 1 hour from Brussels by train, 20 minutes from Lille-Lesquin airport, and served by the A1, A2, A21, A23, A25 and A26 motorways.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published on the official website: participation requests are made via GL events Exhibitions Industrie. No figure is publicly available.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with GL events Exhibitions Industrie, book a stand (the trade show shows strong regional loyalty, so anticipate locations).
- 9 months out: apply for the Trophées SEPEM and the new products trail (showcasing the 110 preview innovations).
- 6 months out: prepare live machine demonstrations, brief the sales team with a focus on the Hauts-de-France industrial basin.
- 3 months out: register for the employment area / job dating if recruiting, prepare job descriptions.
- 6 weeks out: follow up with regional contacts, confirm appointments with maintenance and production managers.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free pre-registration online with proof of professional industrial activity.
- Allow half a day to a full day depending on scope (equipment, maintenance, subcontracting).
- Target conferences in advance: the programme is published a few weeks before the trade show.
- Take advantage of the free parking and catalogue, and of the proximity (a single day is enough for most regional visitors).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The SEPEM network, operated by GL events, places its trade shows within the group''s CSR approach, structured around 13 of the UN''s Sustainable Development Goals (source: gl-events.com/esg-rse). On the ground, the trade show showcases industrial companies'' responsible practices through the Trophées SEPEM (Sustainable Innovation Award, Digital Transformation Award, Social and Societal Commitment Award) and through themed trails (circular economy, decarbonisation) built into the conference programme (source: douai.sepem-industries.com).

No ISO 20121 certification specific to the Douai edition is mentioned to date on the official website.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "2028 (upcoming)", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" },
  { "edition": "2026", "visiteurs": "12,306", "exposants": "600" },
  { "edition": "2025", "visiteurs": "8,017", "exposants": "560" }
 ]}
