### Trajectory analysis

SEPEM Industries Nord has firmly established itself in Douai as the industrial gathering of the Hauts-de-France region. After a 10th edition in January 2025 (8,017 visitors, 560 exhibitors), the trade show was held exceptionally for two consecutive years in 2025 and 2026 before returning to its biennial rhythm. The 2026 edition marked a clear rise in attendance, to 12,306 participants for 600 exhibitors, driven by the themes of reindustrialisation, AI in maintenance and decarbonisation. The 12th edition, from 25 to 27 January 2028, will extend this positioning as a proximity trade show rooted in the regional industrial basin, with a high proportion of local exhibitors and a free format for professional visitors.', seo_title_en='SEPEM Industries Nord 2028 Douai: Hauts-de-France industrial trade show', seo_description_en='SEPEM Industries Nord 2028 at Gayant Expo Douai from 25 to 27 January: 600 exhibitors, services, equipment, processes and maintenance for Hauts-de-France industry.' WHERE slug='sepem-douai';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show of services, equipment, processes and maintenance for industry. South-East regional edition covering Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes and PACA.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- SEPEM Industries Sud-Est (formerly known as SEPEM Centre-Est, now referred to as SEPEM Grenoble on the official subdomain) is the Grenoble leg of the SEPEM circuit, the regional trade shows dedicated to **services, equipment, processes and maintenance** for industry. It is operated by **GL events Exhibitions Industrie**.
- Next edition: **5th edition, from 24 to 26 November 2026** at the **Alpexpo** exhibition centre in Grenoble.
- The trade show runs every two years in Grenoble: it is held in even years (2022, 2024, 2026).
- Figures announced for 2026: 430 exhibitors expected across 5,300 m², with at least 30% of the exhibitor offering coming from the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region.
- Review of the 4th edition (November 2024): more than 430 exhibitors, including over 40% regional players, plus 29 conferences and panel discussions (source: electroniques.biz).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Suppliers and equipment manufacturers for industry: assembly, lifting, conveying, robotics and cobotics, measurement and inspection, machining and cutting, maintenance, subcontracting, electronics, environment and safety. The SEPEM circuit is positioned around the regional short supply chain: at the Grenoble leg, at least 30% of the exhibitor offering comes from the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region. Attendance is strictly professional: industrial firms, maintenance and production departments, design offices, buyers and executives from the South-East area.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of exhibitors is on the official website: [grenoble.sepem-industries.com](https://grenoble.sepem-industries.com/partners). The trade show is organised by machine families (assembly, lifting, conveying, robots and cobots, measurement and inspection, cutting) rather than by brand villages.

### Quality of attendance

- A proximity trade show whose target is the regional industrial firm of the South-East (Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes and PACA)
- Around 4,700 visitors expected at the 2024 edition (source: presences-grenoble.fr)
- Free admission and catalogue for professional visitors

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The programme covers the operational challenges of industry. For 2026, three themes are highlighted: **Maintenance 4.0**, **artificial intelligence** and **decarbonisation**. The 4th edition (2024) featured 29 conferences and panel discussions (source: electroniques.biz). The detailed 2026 programme is published as the trade show approaches.

### Awards and recognition

The **Trophées SEPEM** reward the innovative and responsible initiatives of exhibitors. The 2026 categories and winners are to be confirmed as the trade show approaches.

### Community and networks

GL events Exhibitions Industrie drives a collective approach around the **Manifeste pour l''Industrie**, which promotes sustainable industry and the reindustrialisation of regions. SEPEM Industries brings together a circuit of regional trade shows in France, the other legs of which notably include [SEPEM Toulouse](/salons/sepem-toulouse), [SEPEM Colmar](/salons/sepem-colmar), [SEPEM Angers](/salons/sepem-angers) and [SEPEM Douai](/salons/sepem-douai).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Alpexpo exhibition centre in Grenoble](/lieux/alpexpo-grenoble).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 24 and Wednesday 25 November from 9 am to 6 pm, Thursday 26 November from 9 am to 5 pm.
- **Admission:** free for professionals, free catalogue, with prior online registration.
- **Access:** Alpexpo exhibition centre, avenue de l''Innsbruck, 38100 Grenoble. Served by buses 65, 67 and C3 (Alpexpo and Polesud Alpexpo stops), SNCF railway station 15 minutes away, direct access to the A48 and A41 motorways via the southern ring road. Free car park with 2,000 spaces.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with GL events Exhibitions Industrie, choose positioning by machine family.
- 9 months out: apply for the Trophées SEPEM.
- 6 months out: prepare the stand and product demonstrations, building on the trade show''s regional anchoring (at least 30% of exhibitors from Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes).
- 6 weeks out: confirm appointments with industrial firms from the South-East area, sales briefing.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free online pre-registration on the official website (named badge).
- One day is enough to cover the regional scope; target the conferences in advance (Maintenance 4.0, AI, decarbonisation).
- A proximity trade show: useful for sourcing regional suppliers and subcontractors through short supply chains.

## The trade show''s development

