### Trajectory analysis

The Grenoble leg of the SEPEM circuit has established itself as a regional year-end industrial event, on a biennial rhythm in even years. Expected attendance stood at around 4,700 visitors for the 2024 edition, with a base of roughly 430 to 450 exhibitors including a strong regional share (more than 40% in 2024). The 2026 edition, from 24 to 26 November at Alpexpo, retains this proximity trade show format, with 430 exhibitors announced across 5,300 m² and a conference programme centred on Maintenance 4.0, artificial intelligence and decarbonisation. The 2026 attendance figures will be published after the trade show.', seo_title_en='SEPEM Industries Sud-Est 2026: industrial trade show in Grenoble (Alpexpo)', seo_description_en='SEPEM Industries Sud-Est 2026: 5th edition from 24 to 26 November at Alpexpo Grenoble. 430 exhibitors announced, services, equipment, processes and maintenance for industry. Free admission.' WHERE slug='sepem-grenoble';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='A trade show for services, equipment, process and maintenance for industry. A regional format close to the factories.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **SEPEM Industries Sud-Ouest** is the Toulouse leg of the SEPEM network (Services, Équipements, Process Et Maintenance), a proximity trade show dedicated to solutions for industry: production, maintenance, subcontracting, automation, energy and logistics. Operator: **GL events Exhibitions Industrie**.
- Next edition: 22 to 24 September 2026 at the [MEETT de Toulouse](/lieux/meett-toulouse), in Aussonne.
- The SEPEM network has existed for more than 20 years and is rolled out across several French industrial regions. The Toulouse leg returns on a biennial basis: the previous edition took place in September 2024 at the same venue.
- A clearly stated regional positioning: at least 30% of the exhibitor offering comes from the South-West, as close as possible to the factories of the Toulouse region.
- New for 2026: a **Safety & Security Village** dedicated to industrial cybersecurity, data protection, site security, private 5G and risk management.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Equipment suppliers and machine manufacturers, automation and robotics integrators, maintenance service providers, subcontractors, suppliers of lifting, conveying, measurement and cutting solutions, energy and decarbonisation players, and publishers of digital solutions for the factory. The trade show targets a strictly professional audience: production and maintenance managers, design offices, industrial purchasing teams and technical departments.

The SEPEM format relies on live demonstrations and geographical proximity: it is aimed primarily at South-West industrial firms looking for concrete solutions without travelling to the major national trade shows.

### Notable exhibitors

Exhibitor list on the official website: [toulouse.sepem-industries.com](https://toulouse.sepem-industries.com/). The 2026 edition announces around 250 exhibitors, of which at least 30% come from the South-West. The trade show is set within a dense industrial region centred on aerospace and tech (Airbus, Thales, Safran and Continental are part of the regional ecosystem cited by the organiser) and on structured sectors across Occitanie.

### Quality of the audience

- A regional professional audience, recruited as close as possible to the production sites of the South-West.
- Free admission with registration, which favours an operational audience (technicians, site managers, maintenance teams).

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The 2026 edition structures its programme around the SEPEM network''s defining themes: Maintenance 4.0, artificial intelligence and decarbonisation. The trade show also offers dedicated spaces: **L''Atelier** (expert advice: recruitment, financing, energy transition, digitalisation, real estate) and **SEPEM Avenir**, a space for careers, training, employment and job dating designed to showcase careers in industry.

The **Safety & Security Village**, new for 2026, brings together the themes of industrial systems cybersecurity, data protection, site security and access management, private 5G and risk management.

### Community and networks

The SEPEM network positions itself around reshoring and short industrial supply chains, anchoring each edition in a regional area. It has held more than 50 editions since its creation and covers 8 industrial regions in France, including [Angers](/salons/sepem-angers), [Grenoble](/salons/sepem-grenoble), [Colmar](/salons/sepem-colmar) and [Douai](/salons/sepem-douai). For Toulouse, the anchoring draws on the aerospace, space and electronics sectors of the Occitanie region.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [MEETT de Toulouse](/lieux/meett-toulouse).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 22 and Wednesday 23 September 9 a.m.-6 p.m., Thursday 24 September 9 a.m.-5 p.m.
- **Visitor badge:** free admission and catalogue with prior online registration, reserved for professionals.
- **MEETT access:** tramway line T1, MEETT BEAUZELLE stop, bus line 30, MEETT stop, 7 minutes from Toulouse-Blagnac airport. 5,000 parking spaces on site.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: get in touch with GL events Exhibitions Industrie, choose your positioning (regional South-West offering or national).
- 6 months out: prepare live demonstrations, a key strength of the SEPEM format.
- 3 months out: possible inclusion in the Safety & Security Village or L''Atelier depending on positioning.
- 6 weeks out: arrange targeted meetings with industrial firms in the Toulouse region.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free pre-registration on the official website with proof of professional activity.
- One day is generally enough to cover the trade show, a human-scale regional format.
- Identify the themed spaces in advance: Safety & Security Village, L''Atelier, SEPEM Avenir.
- Make the most of the SEPEM Avenir space for recruitment and training matters.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
   { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition (Toulouse)" },
   { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
   { "edition": "2026 (upcoming)", "exposants": "~250 announced" },
   { "edition": "2024", "exposants": "n/a" }
 ]}
 sources="toulouse.sepem-industries.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

The Toulouse leg of SEPEM returns to the MEETT on a biennial basis (2024, then 2026). The trade show capitalises on a proximity positioning: at least 30% of the exhibitor offering comes from the South-West, serving a dense industrial region. The 2026 edition, from 22 to 24 September, adds a Safety & Security Village to the recurring spaces (L''Atelier, SEPEM Avenir) and confirms the network''s orientation towards Maintenance 4.0, industrial AI and decarbonisation. The 2026 exhibitor figure (around 250 announced) is a pre-show target.', seo_title_en='SEPEM Industries Sud-Ouest Toulouse 2026: dates, exhibitors, info', seo_description_en='SEPEM Sud-Ouest 2026 at the MEETT de Toulouse from 22 to 24 September: a proximity trade show for services, equipment, process and maintenance for industry. Free admission.' WHERE slug='sepem-toulouse';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for the hospitality and catering industry across the Grand Ouest. Equipment, products and services for the café, hotel and restaurant sector.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 22nd edition of Serbotel: **17 to 20 October 2027** (Sunday to Wednesday) at the Parc des Expositions de Nantes, a biennial trade show created in 1985 by Exponantes. Halls and floor plan not yet communicated at 18 months out.
- 2025 review: **31,000 visitors, 450+ exhibitors, 32,000 m² across 6 halls** over 4 days. The 22nd edition is targeting **35,000 visitors / 600 exhibitors** (2027 targets communicated by the organiser, to be confirmed after the official review).
- The leading regional trade show in the Grand Ouest dedicated to the café-hotel-restaurant sector: café-hotellerie-restauration, bakery-patisserie, food trades, butchery-charcuterie, snacking, professional kitchen equipment.
- **Nearly 20 contests and trophies** over 4 days in 2025, including the European Cup of Bakery, the Mondial du Pain, the World Oyster Shucking Championship and the Trophée Masse. Format embedded at the heart of the halls, dense visitor audience.
- **Structural change of operator on 1 January 2026**: Exponantes (Parc des Expositions, a subsidiary of CCI Nantes Saint-Nazaire) and the SPL Cité des Congrès de Nantes are brought together under a single operating company, in a mixed-economy model associating Nantes Métropole and the CCI (SPL or SEM legal form to be settled, source: Le Journal des Entreprises, infos-media-nantes.fr). Serbotel 2027 is the first edition operated by this new structure.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A multi-sector café-hotel-restaurant trade show, structured in 2025 around **7 sector universes** (source: serbotel.com):

- **Bakery, patisserie, chocolate-making, ice cream**: raw materials, oven equipment, ingredients, shop fit-out.
- **Food products, snacking, catering**: charcuterie, cheese, preserves, fresh produce, ready meals, food truck.
- **Kitchen equipment and café-hotel-restaurant material**: professional refrigeration, cooking, washing, kitchen furniture, utensils, food truck.
- **Drinks, bar, breweries**: cellars, wines, spirits, coffee, craft brewing, machines, distribution.
- **Institutional bodies and education**: apprentice training centres, chambers of trades, hospitality schools, professional organisations, specialist press.
- **Fit-out, furniture, decoration**: dining-room layout, terrace, signage, hospitality design.
- **Connected and high-tech solutions**: tills, payment, dining-room management, click & collect, trade software.

A strong presence of SMEs and mid-sized firms from the Grand Ouest (Pays de la Loire, Brittany, Normandy), regional agri-food businesses (dairies, canneries, independent breweries), national café-hotel-restaurant groups and national suppliers. International presence is more modest than at Equip''Hôtel Paris.

### Notable exhibitors

The 2025 exhibitor list is published on the [official Serbotel exhibitors page](https://www.serbotel.com/exposants/secteurs). The 2027 list will be published by the organiser when registrations open.

### Quality of the visitor base

- 31,000 trade visitors in 2025, coming mainly from the Grand Ouest but also from across France and a few neighbouring countries.
- Decision-maker profiles: artisan bakers, pastry chefs, chocolatiers, charcutiers, restaurateurs, café-bar managers, hotel establishment managers, café-hotel-restaurant wholesale purchasing officers, apprentice training centre and chamber-of-trades trainers, hospitality students.
- Trade show reserved for sector professionals (free badge on pre-registration).
- Strong regional concentration: Pays de la Loire (departments 44, 49, 53, 72, 85), Brittany (22, 29, 35, 56), Normandy (14, 50, 61), Vendée. A structuring geographical effect against Equip''Hôtel Paris.

## Activities and community

### Contests and competitions

Nearly 20 national and international contests organised over 4 days in 2025. Official labels verbatim (source: serbotel.com/concours/tous-les-concours-serbotel):

- **Coupe d''Europe de la Boulangerie Artisanale** (France, Spain and Italy on the 2025 podium).
- **Mondial du Pain**.
- **Championnat de France des Arts Gourmands**.
- **Trophée Mondial du Meilleur Plat Français**, 2025 winner: Dan Rodrigues (Brazil).
- **Trophée Passion International**.
- **Championnat du Monde des Écaillers & Concours du Meilleur Espoir Français**, 2025 winner: Benjamin Gilard.
- **Concours National du Meilleur Crêpier**, 2025 winner: Jean-Luc Rescamp.
- **Trophée Masse : la sélection du Grand Ouest**.
- **Challenge tes Sens**.
- **Trophée National de Restauration Collective Autogérée**.
- **Challenge des Jeunes Talents**.
- **Trophée du Partage**.
- **Les Concours Bouchers**.
- **Les Concours Charcutiers Traiteurs**.
- **Trophée National Traiteur Organisateur de Réceptions**.
- **Trophée Tables et Saveurs de Bretagne**.

The 2027 contests and their federation partners will be published by the organiser in the months preceding the edition.

### Conference and activity programme

Around fifty conferences and workshops in 2023 and 2025 on sector themes: employment, recruitment, training, succession, ecological transition. The **Restaurant des Chefs** (a culinary demonstration space embedded within the trade show) ran for 4 days. Bakery demo stages, technical workshops.

### Community and networks

A trade show anchored in the Grand Ouest''s regional café-hotel-restaurant ecosystem. Long-standing institutional partners: chambers of trades and crafts (CMA Pays de la Loire), CCI Nantes-Saint-Nazaire, trade federations (Confédération Nationale de la Boulangerie-Pâtisserie Française, Confédération Française de la Boucherie-Charcuterie-Traiteurs, UMIH, GHR), specialist press (Boulangerie Magazine, L''Hôtellerie Restauration, Néorestauration, Tendances Restauration, Snacking.fr, Tendance Hôtellerie).

### What''s new in 2027

The first edition operated by the **new single entity born of the merger** of the Cité des Congrès + Parc des Expositions de Nantes (effective 1 January 2026, mixed-economy model Nantes Métropole + CCI Nantes Saint-Nazaire, SPL or SEM legal form under arbitration, sources: Tendance Hôtellerie, Le Journal des Entreprises, infos-media-nantes.fr). The concrete consequence: a unified commercial point of contact, pooling of marketing tools between the Cité and the Parc Expo, possible joint activation of complementary congress rooms should conference capacity be needed. The new events hall **Le Laps** (2,500 seated places), delivered in the second half of 2026 at the Parc des Expositions, will be able to host the major plenaries and contest ceremonies.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc Expo Nantes Beaujoire](/lieux/parc-expo-nantes-beaujoire).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Halls**: not yet communicated for 2027. The 2025 edition occupied 32,000 m² across 6 halls of the Parc des Expositions.
- **Address**: Parc des Expositions de Nantes, route de Saint-Joseph de Porterie, 44300 Nantes.
- **2027 opening hours**: not yet published. 2025 edition reference: 9 a.m. - 6 p.m. on trade days, to be confirmed on the [Opening hours and services page](https://www.serbotel.com/infos-pratiques/horaires-et-services).
- **Visitor badge**: free on online trade pre-registration, on proof of café-hotel-restaurant activity.
- **Catering on site**: Restaurant des Chefs (demonstrations + catering), catering points in the halls, bars.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with the organiser, identify the sector universe (7 universes), request a stand quote.
- 9 months out: enter the federated contests (Coupe d''Europe de la Boulangerie, Trophée Masse, etc.; this goes through the partner trade federations, not directly through Serbotel).
- 6 months out: confirm location and stand brief, logistics for heavy equipment (cooking, professional refrigeration, food truck).
- 3 months out: team accreditations, Nantes accommodation (book early, October tourist peak in Pays de la Loire), commercial brief.
- 6 weeks out: activate partner networks (CMA, CCI, federations), Grand Ouest specialist press materials, prospect meeting schedule.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Trade pre-registration is mandatory for the free badge.
- Allow **1 to 2 days** to cover the 6 halls and attend at least one contest final.
- Flagship contests: check the timing of the finals (Coupe d''Europe de la Boulangerie, Mondial du Pain, Championnat du Monde des Écaillers), high attendance and high technical quality.
- A Sunday-to-Tuesday schedule is unusual on the café-hotel-restaurant calendar: make the most of the Sunday opening for artisan profiles who close on Mondays.

## Policy and CSR initiatives

The 2025 edition placed two structuring themes at the heart of its programme (source: Restauration21, Tendance Hôtellerie): **revaluing the trades** (succession, training, inclusion, mental health in the kitchen) and **ecological transformation** (carbon reduction, waste prevention, evolving production methods). Virginie Léger-Mathys, the trade show''s general commissioner, stated: "This 21st edition marks a turning point for Serbotel. We wanted a trade show in the image of the sector: passionate, creative and resolutely turned towards the future" (source: Restauration21, Tendance Hôtellerie, October 2025).

As of now, the trade show does not publish a dedicated ISO 20121 certification or a structured CSR page on serbotel.com. The CSR topic is carried through the programme (conferences, workshops) rather than through a certified events process, to be cross-checked with the new merged Cité+Parc Expo entity, which could formalise a consolidated CSR policy by 2027.

## How the trade show has evolved

