## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out (spring 2026): make contact with Comexposium, position your zone (animal, plant, regional gastronomy, world agriculture), choose your hall and floor space
- 9 months out (summer 2026): contractual commitment, validation of partner agreements for regions, trade bodies and breed associations
- 6 months out (September 2026): entries for the Concours Général Agricole (wines, dairy products, regional produce), animal competition registrations
- 4 months out (November 2026): validation of the scenography concept, stand-builder brief, logistics planning
- 2 months out (January 2027): team accreditations, accommodation, commercial brief, press kits, scheduling of sector meetings
- 3 weeks out (February 2027): delivery of materials, final team brief, activation of media campaigns and client invitations

### For the decision-making visitor

- Register as soon as the 2027 ticket office opens: Pro e-badge for priority entry and access to business events
- Favour Tuesday 2, Wednesday 3 or Thursday 4 March 2027 for structuring supplier meetings, avoid the public-saturated Saturdays and Sundays
- Plan your route by zone (animal, plant, regional gastronomy, world agriculture)
- For international delegations: head to Pavilion 7.1 world agriculture and to Serbia, the guest of honour
- Allow 2 full days to cover all the halls and attend several CGA competitions

