### Trajectory analysis

Le Bourget remains the oldest air show in the world and retains its status as the sector''s benchmark global gathering. The 2025 edition validates three structural indicators: **305,200 unique visitors** (+4.3% vs 2023), **141,000 unique professionals** of whom 38% were international, and **80 official delegations** representing 64 countries plus 5 international organisations. Its diplomatic and state dimension is unique in the French trade show market: no other gathering brings together so many heads of state, defence ministers and military chiefs of staff in a single week. The 2025 inauguration by Prime Minister François Bayrou continues this tradition. On the business side, commercial announcements running into tens of billions of dollars (Airbus dominant in 2025 with around 248 firm orders and 156 options, the standout Riyadh Air 25 A350-1000 at $9bn) confirm Le Bourget as a global signing venue, on a par with Farnborough in alternation. **The 2027 edition plays a role of symbolic consolidation**: the centenary of Lindbergh''s transatlantic crossing as the official narrative thread, and the carrying over of the 7 themes from 2025 (disruptive innovations, sustainable air mobility, defence, drones, space, AI and cybersecurity, quantum technologies) and of the Paris Air Lab for its 5th edition. On the industrial front, two trends intersect: the accelerated decarbonisation of air transport (SAF, hydrogen, hybrid-electric, structural lightweighting, AI in predictive maintenance) against the sector''s 2.5% of global human-made CO2 emissions, and the rebound in European defence budgets feeding military aeronautics (fighters, tactical drones such as the Aarok, missiles and the RAPIDFire ground-to-air defence system). Le Bourget 2027 will be the first global show to measure these two dynamics concretely over a full post-2025 cycle.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='siae-le-bourget';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='The world''s largest food innovation trade show. An essential gathering for the food industry, SIAL brings together the entire global food and beverage supply chain.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- SIAL Paris has run biennially in even-numbered years since 1964; exhibiting in 2026 means waiting until 2028 for the next Paris edition: skipping an edition means losing 2 years of visibility within the global food industry.
- 31st edition from 17 to 21 October 2026 at [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte), 5 days including the Saturday, a format unchanged across several editions.
- 7,500 exhibitors in 2024 from 127 countries, with nearly 285,000 trade visitors from 205 countries: SIAL is the world''s largest food innovation trade show, ahead of Anuga Cologne on the internationalisation criterion.
- Comexposium is the sole organiser (no structural co-organisation of the ANIA type), and the show is part of the SIAL Network (12 trade shows worldwide, 17,000+ combined exhibitors, 700,000+ professionals per year).
- The SIAL Innovation Awards celebrate their 30th anniversary in 2026; it is the most visible food innovation competition in the world, a powerful free visibility lever for the exhibitors who enter.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A general B2B food trade show covering 21 sectors: dairy products, meats, fruit & vegetables, beverages, fine groceries, frozen foods, seafood, ingredients & food preparations, organic, plant-based, halal, kosher, gluten-free, packaging, equipment. A strong presence of manufacturers, cooperatives, French and international SMEs and mid-caps, as well as official country pavilions (110 delegations in 2024).

### Notable exhibitors (2024)

Bonduelle, Danone, Lactalis, Savencia, Andros, LDC, Materne, Bel, Saint Hubert, Roquette, Tereos. On the international side: Mars, Nestlé, Unilever, Ferrero, Mondelez, Kerry Group, Olam. 7,500 exhibitors in total, the majority coming from abroad (127 countries represented).

### Retention rate

A biennial edition that has historically been highly loyalty-building: SIAL is the essential gathering for food procurement decision-makers, and few major players skip an edition. The steady arrival of new exhibitors (notably food-tech start-ups and DTC brands) renews around 25 to 30% of the exhibitor base at each edition.

### Visitor quality

Nearly 285,000 visitors in 2024 from 205 countries. The Top Buyers programme brought together 5,000 targeted international buyers with a declared €60 billion in purchasing power (€50 billion projected across the 8,000 Top Buyers targeted for 2026, Top Buyers scope only). 17 ministers and 50 ambassadors attended in 2024, alongside 110 official delegations. Dominant profile: large-retail procurement and sourcing, food service, importers, processing industries, specialist retail.

## Programme & community

### Conference programme

SIAL Talks: 5 days of conferences, workshops and themed round tables (consumption trends, the food transition, food-tech, the geopolitics of raw materials, retail, CSR). SIAL Summits: 3 premium tracks (paid, limited-audience formats), aimed at major-account decision-makers.

### Awards & accolades

The SIAL Innovation Awards, 30th edition in 2026, the most recognised global food innovation competition. 2024 winners:

- Gold: Préparations Galettes Végétales Sabarot (France)
- Silver: Super Greens moringa, Aryze (Mauritius)
- Bronze: Zero-Carb Sushi, KING Konjac (Finland)
- Own the Change CSR Award: Lupi Coffee

The winners receive a dedicated space at the show and extensive media coverage, a free lever for innovative SMEs and start-ups.

### Satellite events

SIAL Taste: a space for tasting and demonstrating product trends (not to be confused with former names such as Tastes & Trends). Official country pavilions. A food-tech start-up space. TV stages. Culinary stages with international chefs. Sector demonstrations (bakery, charcuterie, cheeses, wines).

### Community & networks

SIAL is part of the SIAL Network, the world''s leading network of B2B food trade shows: 12 shows (Paris, Shanghai, Guangzhou, Canada Montréal, Canada Toronto, India Mumbai launched in 2025, Interfood Jakarta, Malaysia, Djazagro Algiers, Gourmet Selection Paris, Cheese and Dairy Products Show). Network total: 17,000+ exhibitors, 700,000+ professionals per year. For exhibitors, the SIAL Network offers a coherent multi-market internationalisation pathway.

### What''s new in 2026

31st edition, 5-day format preserved, announced targets: around 295,000 professionals, 8,000 exhibitors, 280,000 m² (vs 270,000 m² in 2024). SIAL for Change is gaining a start-up strand: a new "SIAL For Change By The Foodies" category open to non-exhibiting start-ups, designed with the Hyssop agency. The SIAL Innovation Awards celebrate their 30th anniversary with a special anniversary staging.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Paris Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte), 8 halls in use, around 280,000 m² of exhibition space targeted
- **Transport access**: RER B, Parc des Expositions station, around 35 min from Châtelet. Roissy CDG 10 min away by shuttle. RER B traffic is very heavy at peak times, so allow 60 to 90 min of margin from central Paris at the start and end of the day
- **Parking**: Substantial on-site car parks, with predictable saturation on Tuesday and Wednesday (peak days). The daily rate is not negligible, so compare it with Roissy + shuttle
- **Accommodation**: Hotels in Roissy CDG, Aulnay-sous-Bois and Villepinte are fully booked 4 to 6 months before the show. The alternative of central Paris + RER B is more comfortable but more expensive. Book as soon as your attendance is confirmed
- **Opening hours & badges**: 10am to 7pm across all 5 days. Trade visitor rate: €90 on early-bird until 16 June 2026. Student/school rate €50, valid only on Monday 19 or Tuesday 20 October. Group offer from €80/person (organised groups). Free badges are available via exhibitor invitation codes
- **Services**: Multi-point catering in every hall (culinary stages, food courts, premium restaurants). Networking areas. A digital matchmaking service. The official SIAL app. A press area. Private meeting rooms available on reservation

## How much it costs to exhibit

