## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 18 months out (spring 2025): make contact with Comexposium; the strategic locations (hall entrances, corners, country pavilions) go very early at a biennial show
- 12 months out: confirm the stand concept, brief the contractor, enter the SIAL Innovation Awards (a demanding application, with closing dates several months before the show)
- 9 months out: commit to the Top Buyers programme if eligible (pre-qualified premium buyer targeting)
- 6 months out: finalise the stand plan, order construction, organise product logistics, complete health declarations if handling fresh produce or alcohol
- 3 months out: team accreditations, accommodation, sales briefing, quantified lead targets
- 6 weeks out: deliver materials, activate the SIAL app for matchmaking, schedule pre-arranged meetings

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Badge at €90 on early-bird until 16 June 2026, a significant saving versus the full rate
- The SIAL Talks programme is published in advance on sialparis.com, so identify the priority conferences
- Allow a minimum of 2 to 3 days: 8 halls and 7,500 exhibitors cannot be covered in 1 day
- Ask your usual suppliers for a free invitation code before paying for your badge
- The Top Buyers programme is reserved for pre-qualified major-account buyers (sourcing above an annual threshold), with applications via sialparis.com

## CSR commitment

SIAL Paris runs its CSR programme under the **SIAL for Change** banner. A CSR award was launched in 2024 with the Hyssop agency, and a new 2026 category, "SIAL For Change By The Foodies", is open to non-exhibiting start-ups to broaden access to CSR recognition. There is an operational partnership with the **French Red Cross**: 50 tonnes of products redistributed at the 2022 edition, with 200 volunteers mobilised during the show for collection and redistribution. 100% of the electricity used on site comes from renewable sources. Circular economy: 2,000 m² of stand materials reused from one edition to the next. SIAL communicates on a low-carbon event trajectory without having published a quantified 2030 or 2040 target to date.

## How the show has evolved

