### Trajectory analysis

SIAL Paris has been on a continuous growth trajectory since the post-Covid rebound of 2022. The 2024 edition, marking the 60th anniversary, set an all-time record with nearly 285,000 visitors from 205 countries, confirming its position as the world''s leading food innovation trade show, ahead of Anuga Cologne on the internationalisation criterion. The 2026 target (8,000 exhibitors, around 295,000 visitors, 280,000 m²) is consistent with this trajectory and remains achievable without a step change in format. The biennial even-year rhythm has been unchanged since the outset, and the 5-day format including the Saturday is confirmed. The structural challenge for Comexposium remains showcasing the Top Buyers programme and the SIAL Network as internationalisation accelerators for French exhibitors, in the face of competition from Anuga (biennial odd-year rhythm, complementary in the calendar).', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='sial-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for industry partners of the Grand Sud. Subcontracting, equipment, services and industrial supplies for the industrial sectors of Occitanie.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- SIANE is the trade show for industry partners of the Grand Sud: subcontracting, equipment, machine tools, industrial services and supplies, positioned as **the largest industrial gathering in the Grand Sud**.
- Next edition: **21st edition, from 13 to 15 October 2026** at the [MEETT in Toulouse](/lieux/meett-toulouse), free entry for professional visitors.
- Figures from the last edition with reported data (19th edition, October 2024): **over 14,000 visitors, 583 exhibitors and 484 buyers** (sources: usinenouvelle.com, laregion.fr).
- Organised by **Promo-Salons** (SARL Promo-Salons, Mondeville). The 20th edition took place in 2025.
- Signature features: demonstrations of machines and robots in operation, the **AI Village**, TV studios, a business convention and the **SIANE Trophies**.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Industrial subcontractors and equipment suppliers, spread across 13 official sectors: machining and mechanical engineering, sheet metalwork and boilermaking, cutting-stamping-spinning, thermal and surface treatments, foundry work, forging work, plastics processing, rubber, composites, ceramics and wood, tooling and mould manufacturing, special-purpose machines, special-capacity machinery, electrical engineering and electronics, industrial supplies and services (source: salonsiane.com/secteurs-dactivites). The trade show feeds the major sectors of the Grand Sud: aerospace and space, automotive, medical, electronics.

A strictly professional audience: principals, design offices, purchasing, production and maintenance managers. The last edition with reported figures counted 484 identified buyers (2024).

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is available on the official portal: [portail.salonsiane.com](https://portail.salonsiane.com/ListeDesExposants/indexPrevEdition.php). Winners of the 2025 SIANE Trophies notably included MITUTOYO, ZEISS, OCCISOLIS, ALTERNA ENERGIE, CICEM, SOTIMECO, MPRO, CLAUX & Fils and PredexIA (source: salonsiane.com/les-trophees-du-siane).

### Audience quality

- 14,000+ professional visitors and 484 buyers at the 2024 edition (sources: usinenouvelle.com, laregion.fr)
- An integrated business convention to structure meetings between principals and subcontractors
- A strong regional base in Occitanie, with the support of the Occitanie / Pyrénées-Méditerranée Region and the chambers of commerce of the Grand Sud

## Features & community

### Conference programme

The trade show runs a programme of conferences and TV studios on the major challenges facing industry: the industry of the future, digital transformation and artificial intelligence, energy efficiency and decarbonisation, employment and training, production competitiveness. The **AI Village** offers a demonstration space dedicated to artificial intelligence applied to industry. The detailed 2026 programme is to be published on salonsiane.com.

### Awards and accolades

The **SIANE Trophies** reward exhibitors in several categories: "Best stand", "Innovative solutions", "Energy efficiency / Decarbonisation", "Machine tools / Production", "Inter-company partnership / Co-contracting" and "Innovative company of Occitanie" (source: salonsiane.com/les-trophees-du-siane). The 2026 categories and winners are to be confirmed as the trade show approaches.

### Community and networks

The trade show draws on a broad network of institutional and professional partners across the Grand Sud: the Occitanie / Pyrénées-Méditerranée Region, Toulouse Métropole, CCI Toulouse Haute-Garonne and Aerospace Valley (sources: salonsiane.com/le-salon).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [MEETT in Toulouse](/lieux/meett-toulouse).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 13 October 9am-7pm, Wednesday 14 October 9am-midnight, Thursday 15 October 9am-5pm.
- **Visitor badge:** free entry for professionals, advance online registration recommended for faster access (named badge).
- **Address:** MEETT, avenue de la Concorde, 31840 Aussonne (Toulouse metropolitan area).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with the organisers, choose your positioning by sector (machining, sheet metalwork, treatments, special-purpose machines, services).
- 9 months out: apply for the SIANE Trophies (innovation, decarbonisation, best stand).
- 6 months out: prepare demonstrations of machines and robots in operation, a strong differentiating feature of the trade show.
- 3 months out: activate the business convention to lock in meetings with principals.
- 6 weeks out: sales briefing, targeting regional buyers across the Grand Sud.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free pre-registration on salonsiane.com for a named badge.
- Allow half a day to a full day depending on your scope (subcontracting, equipment, industrial AI).
- Identify the AI Village and the conferences on decarbonisation and the industry of the future in advance.
- Make the most of the business convention to plan supplier meetings.

## How the trade show has evolved

