UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **SILMO Paris**, the world fair for optics, eyewear and ophthalmic equipment, has been held every year in Paris since the 1960s.
- **Organiser: Comexposium** (a subsidiary of CCI Paris Île-de-France and Crédit Agricole Assurances).
- **2026 edition: from Friday 25 to Monday 28 September 2026**, at [Paris-Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte).
- **Audience (2025 figures):** 33,358 professionals, of whom 52% were international, up 6.5% year on year. More than 900 exhibiting companies representing around 1,500 brands, across 75,000 m².
- **Highlights:** the SILMO d''Or (the sector''s benchmark awards since 1994), the Optical Design Contest for young creators, and the SILMO Academy scientific congress.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

SILMO Paris brings together the upstream and downstream of the optics industry: frame manufacturers and brands, lens makers, contact lenses, workshop equipment and instruments, edging machines, low vision, sun protection, accessories and services for points of sale. On the visitor side: opticians, optometrists, ophthalmologists, distributors, buying groups, importers and retail buyers, with a strong international dimension.

### Notable exhibitors

More than 900 companies exhibited in 2025, representing around 1,500 brands. The official exhibitor list and the floor plan are published on the [SILMO Paris website](https://www.silmoparis.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

The 2025 figures report 33,358 professionals welcomed, of whom 52% were international and 48% French, an increase of 6.5% compared with the previous edition (source: Comexposium). The predominantly international visitor base positions SILMO as an export event for eyewear brands.

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The **SILMO Academy** forms the scientific strand of the trade show: a congress devoted to visual health, research and innovation, complemented by the **SILMO Talks** bringing together clinical experts and retail strategies. In 2025, a research grant of 10,000 euros was awarded in this context. The detailed programme for the upcoming edition is published online on the official website as the show approaches.

### Awards and accolades

- **SILMO d''Or**: awarded since 1994 (32nd edition in 2025), they reward excellence in creativity and innovation in the optics and eyewear world. The winged statuette is a mark of recognition displayed by the winners on their stands.
- **Optical Design Contest**: a competition open to design students, with a prize of 10,000 euros shared between the school and the winner (4th edition in 2025).
- **Prix de l''Entreprise Engagée**: an award recognising concrete CSR initiatives, in partnership with Hyssop.
- **International Optician of the Year Award**: presented in collaboration with the IOA (International Opticians Association).

### Community & networks

SILMO maintains an active professional community around news from the optics industry. The brand also runs international editions and events led by the organiser. Official announcements are relayed via the show''s press area and networks.

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking, transport (RER B, shuttles) and accommodation, see the venue page for [Paris-Nord Villepinte](/lieux/paris-nord-villepinte).

Specific to the trade show:

- **2026 dates:** from Friday 25 to Monday 28 September 2026, over 4 days.
- **Floor space:** around 75,000 m² of exhibition space.
- **Badge:** visitor registration and invitations are handled online on the official website; SILMO is a strictly trade-only show.
- The detailed floor plan (halls, international pavilions) is published on the website when registration opens.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="Indicative sector ranges: SILMO Paris does not publish a public price list. Request a tailored quote via the Exhibit page on the official website." rows={[{ "poste": "Bare space rental (per m²)", "low": "on quotation", "high": "on quotation" }, { "poste": "Fitted stand 12-18 m² (fit-out + furniture)", "low": "10,000 €", "high": "22,000 €" }, { "poste": "Premium stand 30-50 m² (bespoke design)", "low": "30,000 €", "high": "80,000 €" }, { "poste": "Logistics, transport, build-up/dismantling", "low": "3,000 €", "high": "12,000 €" }, { "poste": "Staff, accommodation, on-site communication", "low": "5,000 €", "high": "20,000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (small / large stand)", "low": "~20,000 €", "high": "~110,000 €" }]} footer="Indicative estimates, excluding official quotation. The actual budget depends on the floor space, the location (aisle, pavilion, international hall) and the level of fit-out." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- **9 to 12 months out:** book your space and choose your location (international pavilions and high-traffic areas go early).
- **6 months out:** brief your stand agency, apply for the SILMO d''Or and other awards, plan your international buyer prospecting.
- **3 months out:** logistics (transport of frames and samples, customs for international shipments), client invitations, pre-booked business meetings.
- **1 month out:** finalise the stand, brief the team, sales materials and export pricing.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Target priority pavilions and brands in advance via the online exhibitor list.
- Set up supplier meetings and negotiations before the show: 4 intense days across 75,000 m².
- Block out the relevant SILMO Academy / SILMO Talks sessions (visual health, retail, innovation).
- Plan your transport timing to Villepinte (RER B + shuttle) during peak hours.

## CSR policy & initiatives

SILMO Paris runs a dedicated CSR strand, built around a space and practical resources developed in partnership with Hyssop: thematic guides on sourcing, packaging and transport, and advice on reducing the industry''s footprint. The show also presents the **Prix de l''Entreprise Engagée**, recognising the concrete CSR initiatives of optics companies.

At the organiser level, Comexposium is certified Positive Company (2025), attesting to verified social, societal and environmental standards. The host venue, Paris-Nord Villepinte (Viparis), pursues a sustainable development approach structured around three pillars (environment, heritage, inclusion), detailed on its page.

## How the show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2026 (upcoming)", "dates": "25-28 Sept. 2026", "lieu": "Paris-Nord Villepinte", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "900+ (target)" }, { "edition": "2025", "dates": "Sept. 2025", "lieu": "Paris-Nord Villepinte", "visiteurs": "33,358", "exposants": "900+" }]} sources="2025 figures: Comexposium. 2026 dates: Comexposium communiqué following SILMO 2025." />

### Trajectory analysis

SILMO has established itself as one of the world''s leading optics and eyewear events, with a marked international footing: more than half of its visitors come from abroad. The 2025 edition returned to growth (+6.5% in attendance), confirming the show''s position as an export platform for frame and sunglasses brands.

Its recent trajectory combines an upscaling of content (the scientific SILMO Academy, SILMO Talks, the internationalisation of the congress) and the structuring of CSR across the industry. The 2026 edition continues this trend: September, Paris-Nord Villepinte, a 4-day format and an unchanged global positioning.', seo_title_en='SILMO Paris 2026: dates, exhibitors, SILMO d''Or | Agoris', seo_description_en='SILMO Paris 2026, the world fair for optics and eyewear, from 25 to 28 September 2026 at Paris-Nord Villepinte. 900+ exhibitors, 1,500 brands, 33,000+ trade visitors.' WHERE slug='silmo-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='24th edition of France''s annual commercial property gathering at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, following the structural relocation of 2025 from the Palais des Congrès Porte Maillot. 2025 results: 26,052 professionals, 470 exhibitors, 115 speaking slots.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **24th edition on 8, 9 and 10 December 2026** at **Paris Expo Porte de Versailles**, the second year at this new site following the structural relocation of 2025 from the Palais des Congrès Porte Maillot. SIMI is **the** annual gathering for French commercial property, organised by **Infopro Digital** since its creation in 2001 (24 years of operational continuity, same organiser).
- 2025 results: **26,052 professionals**, **470 exhibitors**, **115 speaking slots**. SIMI is not a volume trade show like the SMCL; it is an **ultra-qualified** trade fair targeting a narrow audience (property investment companies, developers, asset managers, advisers, large-account property departments, metropolitan authorities).
- 3 thematic pillars for 2026 announced by the organiser: **transforming the existing stock** (financing, decarbonising, reinventing uses), **producing value** (investing, operating, steering performance), **contributing to the economy** (property as strategic infrastructure). Clear reading: decarbonisation and the redevelopment of existing assets remain at the strategic core for 2026, in continuity with the 2025 Grands Prix.
- Operational management led by **Aminata Sy**, who succeeded Catherine Sachreiter. Editorial continuity confirmed: conferences co-organised with **the IEIF** (conference partner, not co-organiser of the trade show, a distinction that comes up regularly in the press).
- **Future City Lab** renewed for 2026 after its launch in 2025: a day dedicated to AI + territorial innovation **on Thursday 10 December 2026**, with an announced plenary, "Can AI be a lever for emerging from the crisis?". A clear signal of the place AI is taking in the commercial property value chain.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Listed and unlisted property investment companies, asset managers, fund management companies (real estate funds), developers, international commercial property advisers, banks and financiers, property departments of large user groups, metropolitan authorities and regions in a territorial marketing posture, technical service providers (property management, facility management, data, energy). SIMI covers the entire chain of office, logistics, business premises, investment hospitality and managed residential.

### Notable exhibitors

International advisers: **JLL, Cushman & Wakefield, Colliers, BNP Paribas Real Estate**. Property investment companies and asset managers: **Swiss Life Asset Managers France, Ardian** (Stéphanie Bensimon, Head of Real Estate at Ardian, chaired the jury of the 2025 Grands Prix SIMI). Developers and users: **Nexity, Engie, Stellantis**. Metropolitan authorities and regions present in 2025: **Aix-Marseille-Provence, Bourgogne-Franche-Comté, Centre-Val de Loire, Grand Reims**.

Full list of 2026 exhibitors: official directory on [salonsimi.com](https://www.salonsimi.com).

### Quality of the visitor base

26,052 professionals in 2025 over 3 days, representing a very high business density per m² of show floor. The majority of attendees are decision-makers: senior management, investment management, development management, asset management, and property departments on the user side. SIMI has historically operated as a **place of signature**: announcements of fundraising rounds, presentations of projects entering marketing, and investor / developer meetings.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**150+ conferences over 3 days** announced for 2026 (115 speaking slots in 2025, an expanded programme for the 24th edition). Conferences co-organised with **the IEIF** (Institut de l''Épargne Immobilière et Foncière) covering market analysis, property fund performance, and investment conditions. Formats: sector opening plenaries, thematic debates on the 3 pillars, technical workshops, and market study presentations.

### Awards & accolades

**Grands Prix SIMI**, jury chaired in 2025 by **Stéphanie Bensimon (Head of Real Estate, Ardian)**. 2025 winners:

- **Office building**: **Engie Harmony**, 94,811 m² on the former PSA site in La Garenne-Colombes. An emblematic operation converting a historic industrial site into a tertiary campus.
- **Business and industrial premises**: **ACTI-HALL Vaires-sur-Marne**, 26,252 m² on a redeveloped industrial brownfield.
- **Logistics and courier property**: the mixed-use **DAHER / SIMAERO Tremblay-en-France** building, 9,000 m², developer **Barjane**.
- **Jury''s favourite**: **Green Campus Poissy Stellantis**, 72,000 m², 8,200 employees, architect **Patriarche**.
- The **Housing and Accommodation Prize** and the **Patronage & Solidarity in the City Prize** round out the list of winners in additional categories.

Reading of the 2025 winners: 3 of the 4 main prizes reward **redevelopment of existing assets** (PSA, industrial brownfield, Stellantis site), which validates the 2026 editorial positioning ("transforming the existing stock" as the first pillar).

### Satellite events

**Future City Lab**: renewed for 2026 after a successful launch in 2025. A day dedicated to AI + territorial innovation on **Thursday 10 December 2026**. Flagship plenary announced: "Can AI be a lever for emerging from the crisis?". A format designed to bring local authorities, property operators and tech players into dialogue.

### Community & networks

Conference partnerships with **the IEIF**. Strong media coverage by the specialist press (Business Immo, Décideurs Magazine, Le Moniteur). Official SIMI app for exhibitor / visitor matchmaking.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Dates and opening hours:** Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9 and Thursday 10 December 2026. Detailed opening hours to be confirmed on salonsimi.com.
- **Venue:** Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, the second year at this site following the relocation of 2025. The press described the transition in terms of "clearer, smoother, more business" versus the historic Palais des Congrès Porte Maillot.
- **Visitor badge:** pre-registration required on salonsimi.com.
- **Services:** on-site catering, networking areas, investor VIP lounges, partner media TV studios.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor prices not published in open access: quotes on request from Infopro Digital. Premium positioning consistent with the target audience (international property investment companies, asset managers). For information, **2025 visitor prices** published as a guide (2026 edition to be confirmed on salonsimi.com):

- 3-day badge: €803 incl. VAT
- CLUB badge: €968 incl. VAT
- Innovation Day badge: €638 incl. VAT
- Wednesday day pass: €297 incl. VAT
- Thursday day pass: €352 incl. VAT
- Friday day pass: €253 incl. VAT

The 3-day badge at €803 incl. VAT is consistent with SIMI''s decision-maker positioning: the entry ticket naturally filters the visitor base towards business profiles with strong decision-making power.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact with Infopro Digital, choose your location (the good spots go quickly for the 2nd edition at Porte de Versailles).
- 6 months out: brief the stand builder, apply for the Grands Prix SIMI (timeline to be checked on salonsimi.com).
- 3 months out: stand plan validated, commercial brief focused on the 3 editorial pillars for 2026 (transforming the existing stock, producing value, contributing to the economy).
- 6 weeks out: team accreditations, accommodation (15th arrondissement area or partner hotels), appointment bookings via the official platform.
- 1 week out: final brief, investor application files ready, communication materials finalised.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Pre-registration on salonsimi.com.
- Identify in advance the IEIF conferences and the Future City Lab sessions on Thursday 10 December 2026 if AI is part of your business scope.
- Allow at least 2 days for a serious itinerary (1 day for visitors targeting 2-3 conferences and a limited number of exhibitor meetings).
- Request an invitation code directly from your usual suppliers or partners before paying for a full-price badge.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

Sustainable development policy led by Infopro Digital: limiting the carbon footprint of the trade show, **progressive LED lighting** on stands and activity zones, a waste-sorting policy. Beyond the operational side of the show, **decarbonisation** is positioned as the strategic editorial core for 2026: the first pillar ("transforming the existing stock: financing, decarbonising, reinventing uses") and the choice of 2025 Grands Prix winners that reward the redevelopment of existing assets versus new construction.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" },
 { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }
 ]}
 rows={[
 { "edition": "2025 (23rd)", "visiteurs": "26,052", "exposants": "470", "lieu": "Paris Expo Porte de Versailles (1st year)" },
 { "edition": "2024 and earlier", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a", "lieu": "Palais des Congrès Porte Maillot" }
 ]}
 sources="salonsimi.com, Infopro Digital, specialist press Business Immo"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

In 2026 SIMI is holding its **second edition at its new site**. The 2025 move from the Palais des Congrès Porte Maillot to Paris Expo Porte de Versailles was presented as structural by the organiser ("clearer, smoother, more business") and validated by the 2025 figures (26,052 professionals, 470 exhibitors, 115 speaking slots). 2026 will tell whether the "new site" effect holds in the second year, a key indicator for exhibitors hesitating to invest in a permanent location. On the editorial side, continuity is total: same organiser since 2001 (Infopro Digital), same conference partner (IEIF), same Grands Prix format, Future City Lab renewed. Operational management has changed (Aminata Sy succeeding Catherine Sachreiter) with no visible break in the 2026 positioning.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='simi';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='27th edition at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, a biennial trade show held to complement Sirha Lyon. 2026 results (formerly Europain): 35,500 visitors (+11%), 534 exhibitors, 15% international, across 3 pillars (bakery, patisserie, snacking) expanded to include the Coffee and Start-Up Hubs.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 27th edition of **Sirha Bake & Snack**: **16 to 19 January 2028** at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, a biennial trade show held in even years to complement Sirha Lyon (odd years).
- **Major rebranding in 2026**: the long-established Europain (created in the 1970s) officially becomes Sirha Bake & Snack. The europain.com site now redirects to sirha-bakeandsnack.com. The repositioning embraces the rise of snacking alongside bakery and patisserie.
- 2026 edition results (26th edition, 18-21 January 2026, Hall 1): **35,500 visitors (+11% vs Europain 2024)**, **534 exhibitors**, 15% international attendance (Belgian, Dutch, Italian, Spanish, American).
- 3 historic professional pillars (bakery, patisserie, snacking) reinforced in 2026 by a **new Coffee Hub** (an extension of the snacking scope) and a **Start-Up Hub**.
- Organiser: **GL Events and Ekip, now combined within a new company (2026 merger)**. Umbrella brand Sirha Food.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The offering is structured around the 3 historic pillars expanded in 2026. **Ingredients and yeasts**: Lesaffre, Puratos, Episens (Soufflet/InVivo group), Bleu-Blanc-Coeur. **Equipment and ovens**: Pavailler (deck ovens and rotary ovens), VMI (kneaders and mixers). **Snacking and take-away packaging**, **chocolate / patisserie / ice cream** (Valrhona leading), **training** (CFA, INBP, private schools). The 2026 Coffee Hub opened the trade show to roasters, machine manufacturers and players in the coffee shop economy.

### Notable exhibitors

Lesaffre provides strong long-standing support, notably through the **Bakery World Cup** (the SAF Lesaffre brand is the official partner). Confirmed presence in 2026 of Puratos, Valrhona, Episens, Pavailler, VMI, as well as a renewed Start-Up Hub that curates the sector''s young B2B ventures. Up-to-date exhibitor list on [sirha-bakeandsnack.com](https://www.sirha-bakeandsnack.com).

### Quality of attendance

- **35,500 professional visitors in 2026** (+11% vs Europain 2024), **15% international** and mostly European (Belgium, Netherlands, Italy, Spain) with a notable American contingent.
- Decision-maker profiles: independent bakers-patissiers, bakery and snacking chains, hospitality and catering F&B managers, industrial bakery retail buyers, trainers and schools, coffee shop concept creators.
- Free online pre-registration, paid badge on site (~€40 to €60 indicative).

## Activities and community

### Bakery World Cup

An iconic event of the trade show. **13th edition held on 20 and 21 January 2026** with the official support of SAF Lesaffre, organised by the Confédération Nationale de la Boulangerie-Pâtisserie Française. **2026 podium: South Korea gold medal, Taipei silver medal, France bronze medal.** Asia secures its 5th win in the last 6 editions, a strong signal of the sector''s professionalisation in the APAC region. The **Coupe de France des Écoles** takes place in parallel, training the next generation on the same technical stages.

### The three main stages

- **Bakery Stage**: demonstrations of bakery processes and methods (fermentation, breadmaking, deck vs rotary ovens, sourdoughs).
- **Sweet Stage**: high-end patisserie workshops, conferences and round tables.
- **Snack Food Stage**: sweet and savoury fast food trends, on-the-go formats, food concepts.

Several cross-cutting hubs round out the line-up (Coffee Hub, Start-Up Hub, packaging and take-away areas).

### Competitions and awards

- **Sirha Bake & Snack Awards 2026**: innovation prizes awarded to exhibitors, the first edition under the new brand.
- **Pépites de la Boulangerie**: a competition spotlighting artisans.
- **Trophée International de la Pâtisserie Française**: a benchmark competition on the patisserie stage.

### Conferences

A programme structured around **Snacking Trends 2026-2030**: plant-based transition, naturalness, responsible snacking, average ticket and margins, AI and bakery automation. The round tables bring in the sector''s economic players (12 million consumers/day, €15.1 billion ecosystem, average ticket €6.33 in 2025, i.e. +7%).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) page.

Specific to the trade show:

- **2028 dates**: Sunday 16 to Wednesday 19 January.
- **Opening hours** (2026 reference): 10am - 7pm on Sunday, Monday and Tuesday, 10am - 6pm on Wednesday (early close).
- **Visitor badge**: free online pre-registration on sirha-bakeandsnack.com, e-invitations distributed by exhibitors, direct registration also open. On-site rate ~€40 to €60 (indicative).
- **Cloakroom**: €2 per item.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published to date. Quote on request from the organiser (GL Events and Ekip combined, umbrella brand Sirha Food) via the exhibitor form on sirha-bakeandsnack.com. Several packages traditionally exist: bare stand (floor space rental only), fitted stand (carpet, partitions, lighting), turnkey packaged stand, and dedicated offers for young brands via the Start-Up Hub. Positioning by pillar (bakery, patisserie, snacking, coffee) influences the location zone and the rate per sqm. Figures not publicly available to date.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 18 months out: contact the organiser, choose a pillar (bakery, patisserie, snacking, coffee) and estimate floor space.
- 12 months out: apply for the **Sirha Bake & Snack Awards** (a lever for press visibility and a podium spot).
- 9 months out: finalise the stand according to the chosen package, brief the contractor, plan equipment logistics (ovens, kneaders, refrigerated display cabinets).
- 6 months out: prepare live demonstrations on the Bakery Stage, Sweet Stage or Snack Food Stage (well-attended technical stages).
- 3 months out: team accreditation, pre-scheduled visit plan, activation of international distributor networks (15% of attendance from outside France).

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free online pre-registration is mandatory to avoid on-site ticketing.
- Allow **at least 2 days** to cover Hall 1, the three main stages and the cross-cutting hubs.
- 20 and 21 January 2026 concentrated the Bakery World Cup: for the 2028 edition, aim for the finals days to capture the media coverage and the densest footfall.
- Coffee Hub: a high-potential novelty for coffee shop buyers, hospitality and premium fast food.

## Policy and CSR initiatives

The 2026 edition rolled out the **Sirha Collect** programme, a food-waste prevention scheme in partnership with specialist associations: repurposing of unsold goods on stands, circular economy applied to scenographies, end-to-end support for exhibitors on sustainability. The 2026-2030 conference programme explicitly includes plant-based transition, naturalness and responsible snacking as structural themes. No ISO 20121 certification specific to the trade show is mentioned to date.

## How the trade show has evolved

