### Trajectory analysis

Founded in **1983 as the Salon des Métiers de Bouche** (an initiative by Georges Delangle, MOF charcuterie, in partnership with the Lyon Chamber of Commerce and Industry and Paul Bocuse), the trade show became **Sirha in 1987** (Salon International de la Restauration, de l''Hôtellerie et de l''Alimentation). That same year, 1987, Paul Bocuse created the **Bocuse d''Or**, anchored in the show from the outset. Its biennial rhythm in odd-numbered years has structured the profession''s global calendar for several decades.

The 2025 edition marked a **+25% jump in attendance vs 2023** (257,363 visitors), consolidating its position as the global flagship. The Sirha Food umbrella-brand strategy (Europain, Marseille, Toulouse, Budapest, Istanbul, Geneva, Rio, Arabia) extends this momentum internationally, without displacing the centrality of Lyon. The 2027 trajectory builds on this foundation: the Bocuse d''Or final, the Pastry World Cup, the ICC, the Innovation Awards, an AI foodtech programme, and a CSR policy underpinned by Eurexpo Lyon''s ISO 20121 certification.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='sirha-lyon';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Sirha Méditerranée is the annual food service event for the Mediterranean basin, launched in 2026 in Marseille and operated by **Sirha Food**, a brand of the **GL Events** group that runs the Sirha ecosystem (Sirha Lyon, Sirha Bake & Snack).
- 2nd edition from 14 to 16 February 2027 at [Parc Chanot Marseille](/lieux/parc-chanot-marseille).
- Results of the 1st edition (15 to 17 March 2026): 14,000 professionals, of whom 45% were directors, chefs and decision-makers, more than 310 exhibitors and brands, and 1,300 chefs in attendance (sources: lechef.com, restauration21.fr).
- The trade show hosts two international competitions: the Europe selection for the **Bocuse d''Or** and the **Bouillabaisse World Championship**, whose first edition was held in 2026.
- **Sirha Collect** waste reduction programme: partnerships with charitable and community organisations made available to exhibitors to limit food waste and carbon footprint.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Producers and brands of food products, fine groceries, bakery and snacking, beverages, kitchen equipment, digital solutions for catering, and indoor-outdoor lifestyle. The trade show covers several food service sectors, from product to equipment. Strictly professional attendance: catering, hospitality, food trades and food distribution.

### Notable exhibitors

List of exhibitors on the official website: [sirha-mediterranee.com](https://www.sirha-mediterranee.com/fr/partners). The 1st edition brought together more than 310 exhibitors and brands (source: restauration21.fr).

### Quality of attendance

- 14,000 professionals at the 1st edition in 2026, of whom 45% were directors, chefs and decision-makers (sources: lechef.com, restauration21.fr)
- 1,300 chefs in attendance on site (source: restauration21.fr)
- Predominantly French attendance, open to international visitors with delegations from Italy, Sweden, Hungary and Norway (source: lechef.com)

## Events & community

### Conference programme

The **Food Forum** brings together experts and chefs around Mediterranean gastronomy trends: the 1st edition gathered around fifty speakers, among them the chefs Alexandre Mazzia, Gérald Passedat and Nadia Sammut (source: lechef.com).

### Competitions

The trade show hosts two international competitions: the Europe selection for the **Bocuse d''Or** (Bocuse d''Or Europe, won by Denmark at the 2026 edition) and the **Bouillabaisse World Championship**, whose first edition in 2026 was won by France (source: lechef.com).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Parc Chanot Marseille](/lieux/parc-chanot-marseille).

Specific to the trade show:

- Trade show reserved for professionals, access by personal badge (online registration).
- **Sirha Connect** app (iOS / Android) for networking, the programme and the exhibitor directory.

## CSR policy & initiatives

Sirha Méditerranée rolls out the **Sirha Collect** programme: a set of partnerships with charitable and community organisations, made available to exhibitors to fight food waste and reduce the trade show''s carbon footprint.

## How the trade show has evolved

