### Trajectory analysis

SITEVI remains one of the largest global gatherings for vine-and-wine, olive-growing and fruit-growing equipment, with attendance plateauing between 51,000 and 57,000 visitors since 2017. The 2025 edition marked a slight decline (-7% vs 2023) directly correlated with the **French wine-industry crisis** (vine-pulling, margin contraction, falling investment), while maintaining 1,000 exhibitors stable and 200 newcomers: a signal that the sector remains hungry for innovation despite the context.

The 2027 edition is doubly structuring. On the one hand, it is the **50th anniversary** of the trade show (created in 1977), with an expected symbolic mobilisation effect. On the other, it is the **first edition organised by AgriVitiEvents**, an SAS born on 14 April 2025 from a partnership between Axema (trade union of agricultural machinery manufacturers, 65%), Frédéric Bondoux (Profield Events Group, 17.5%) and Gaëtan Ménard (co-founder of EspritMeuble, 17.5%). Continuity of venue (Parc Expo Montpellier), name (SITEVI) and calendar (last week of November) is announced by Axema. To watch in 2026-2027: the commercial strategy, the possible repositioning around the agroecological transition, the CSR policy of the new structure and the published attendance target.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='sitevi-montpellier';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='42nd edition of the Salon International du Transport et de la Logistique at Paris Nord Villepinte Hall 7, alternating with Porte de Versailles in odd years. 2026 targets: 27,000+ professionals, 580+ exhibitors, 3,450+ business meetings, 80+ conferences.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **43rd edition of SITL** (Salon International du Transport et de la Logistique): from **23 to 25 March 2027** at **Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, Hall 1**. The trade show alternates between Paris Expo Porte de Versailles (odd years) and Paris Nord Villepinte (even years): the 2027 edition therefore returns to Porte de Versailles.
- Official 2027 targets communicated by the organiser: **27,000+ professionals**, **580+ exhibitors**, **3,450+ business meetings** via the MySITL platform, **80+ conferences**.
- 2026 edition (42nd, Paris Nord Villepinte, 31 March-2 April): stated targets of 27,000+ professionals and 580+ exhibitors. The post-show report had not been published as at the update date of this listing. For the record, the 2025 edition (41st, Porte de Versailles) gathered **26,750 attendees (+7% vs 2024)** and **542 exhibitors**.
- The trade show continues the "Métamorphose" undertaken since 2024 and presents itself as "a trade show in motion".
- Organiser: **RX France** (formerly Reed Exhibitions), a subsidiary of the RX group, which runs 350 events across 42 sectors and 25 countries.
- Dedicated matchmaking platform **MySITL** and a structuring CSR programme with the **Green Days** and the RX Responsible Trade Show charter.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

SITL brings together **10 sectors** of the transport and supply chain ecosystem:

- Transport and logistics services
- Intralogistics, automation and robotics
- Packaging, conditioning, pallets
- IoT technologies and information systems
- Alternative energies
- Logistics real estate
- Infrastructure
- Transport equipment
- Consulting, training, financing
- Cold Chain logistics

### Notable exhibitors

List of 2027 exhibitors on the official website: [sitl.eu](https://www.sitl.eu/). The trade show structures its offering around themed areas, including the **Métamorphose Center** (announced novelty, an innovation hub) and **Le Campus** (employment, training, recruitment).

### Quality of the visitor base

- Strictly professional visitor base: supply chain management, transport procurement, logistics operations, supply chain IT, logistics real estate, CSR and decarbonisation.
- As a benchmark, the 2025 edition gathered **26,750 attendees (+7% vs 2024)**, including a growing share of international visitors driven by the exhibitor ecosystem and the European programme.
- Figures communicated by the organiser; no public OJS certification as at this date.

## Activities & community

### SITL Innovation Awards

The SITL Innovation Awards reward concrete sector innovations every year (Operations, Intralogistics, Infrastructure, Services and HR Policy categories, plus special jury prizes). In 2025, 6 prizes were awarded from 72 applications (+33% applicants vs 2024), a volume rising continuously.

2025 winners for the record:

- **MSC France**: Infrastructure.
- **STILL**: HR.
- **Sealed Air**: Intralogistics.
- **Nomadia**: Operations.
- **Digital Logistic Services**: Services.
- **Dexory**: Special jury prize, Intralogistics category.

The 2027 list of winners and the application terms are published progressively on [sitl.eu](https://www.sitl.eu/).

### Conferences and keynotes

The 2027 programme is announced at **80+ conferences** over 3 days. Structuring themes from recent editions: decarbonisation, fleet electrification, artificial intelligence applied to the supply chain, warehouse automation, geopolitical resilience of supply chains, last mile, logistics real estate. The detailed programme is published progressively on [sitl.eu](https://www.sitl.eu/).

### MySITL matchmaking platform

Pre-show and on-site networking tool: agenda qualification, targeted exhibitor recommendations, advance appointment booking. Target of **3,450+ business meetings** in 2027.

### Community and institutions

Strong presence of professional transport and logistics organisations: Union TLF, AUTF, France Logistique, France Supply Chain, Aslog, sector federations for intralogistics and packaging. Specialist press desks set up at the trade show.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Hall location:** Hall 1, Paris Expo Porte de Versailles.
- **Dates:** Tuesday 23, Wednesday 24 and Thursday 25 March 2027.
- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 9am-8pm, Wednesday 9am-7pm, Thursday 9am-5pm.
- **Visitor badge:** professional pre-registration on [sitl.eu](https://www.sitl.eu/). 2027 price to be confirmed when ticketing opens (2026 price: €100 excl. VAT online, €200 excl. VAT on site).
- **Access:** metro lines 12 and 8 (Porte de Versailles station), trams T2 and T3a (Porte de Versailles stop).

## How much it costs to exhibit

**For visitors**, the 2027 price has not yet been published as at the update date of this listing. As a guide, the 2026 edition charged €100 excl. VAT online versus €200 excl. VAT on site. Check [sitl.eu](https://www.sitl.eu/) when 2027 ticketing opens.

**For exhibitors**, detailed public prices are not communicated for 2027: stand space is set by quote depending on location, format (equipped, package, bare) and the themed area chosen. Sales contact via [sitl.eu](https://www.sitl.eu/) or directly through the RX France teams.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with RX France, sector positioning among the trade show''s 10 sectors and choice of area (including the Métamorphose Center and Campus).
- 9 months out: apply for the **SITL Innovation Awards** (early submission recommended, 72 applicants in 2025).
- 6 months out: finalise the stand, configure the exhibitor profile on MySITL, qualify appointment targets.
- 3 months out: activate pre-booking campaigns (the MySITL platform concentrates a growing share of the trade show''s business).
- 1 month out: brief the sales team, train on the badge-scanning tool, prepare press content.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Professional pre-registration on [sitl.eu](https://www.sitl.eu/) (2027 price to be confirmed when ticketing opens).
- Activate your **MySITL** profile in advance to generate an agenda of qualified appointments.
- Target the decarbonisation, supply chain AI and last-mile keynotes, traditionally scheduled in plenary at the start of the trade show.
- Plan 2 full days to cover the hall and the themed areas, or 1 day for a single-sector focus.
- Optimal access via metro line 12 or 8 and trams T2/T3a (Porte de Versailles station).

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The trade show rolls out a structured editorial CSR programme:

- **Green Days**: dedicated programming on the decarbonisation of transport and logistics (alternative energies, electrification, biofuels, hydrogen, intermodality, warehouse energy efficiency).
- **Responsible Trade Show charter** by RX France: the organiser''s commitments on the trade show''s energy efficiency, waste management, eco-design of stands and exhibitor awareness.
- "Soyez VOUS" diversity and inclusion commitment carried by RX at the event.

No public ISO 20121 certification mentioned to date at the level of the trade show itself.

## How the trade show has evolved

