### Trajectory analysis

In 2027 SIVAL passes the symbolic milestone of its 40th edition, on a long historical trajectory (created in 1987, biennial then annual). The rise from 1,250 visitors at the first edition to nearly 24,000 in 2026 reflects a consolidation of the "only French trade show for specialised plant production" model. The stability of the 700 exhibitors / 34,000 m² pairing between 2025 and 2026 (713 then 700) indicates that the room for growth now lies in the quality of the mix (deepening internationalisation: 14% foreign exhibitors, 20 new in 2026, top 5 the Netherlands, Italy, Belgium, Spain, Germany) rather than in raw volume. Variables to watch for the 40th edition: capacity to attract international participation beyond the 55 visitor nationalities of 2026, and the trajectory of entries to the SIVAL Innovation award following the peak of 67 entries in 2026.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='sival-angers';
UPDATE salons SET description_en=NULL, editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The smarter E Europe positions itself as "Europe''s Largest Alliance of Exhibitions for the Energy Industry": an umbrella platform bringing together four trade shows in Munich, Intersolar Europe (solar), ees Europe (storage), Power2Drive Europe (electric mobility) and EM-Power Europe (smart energy management).
- Organised by Solar Promotion GmbH, in co-organisation with FWTM (Freiburg Wirtschaft Touristik und Messe GmbH & Co. KG). Annual frequency, in June.
- Next edition: 23-25 June 2026 at [Messe München](/lieux/messe-munchen), Munich. The conferences take place on 22-23 June 2026 at the ICM München.
- Organiser''s 2025 review (latest edition): 2,737 exhibitors from 57 countries and around 107,000 trade visitors from 157 countries. Targets announced for 2026: more than 2,800 exhibitors and 100,000 visitors or more.
- The sector award "The smarter E AWARD" recognises innovation in energy and mobility, with a ceremony on 22 June 2026 at 5 p.m. at the ICM München, the eve of the opening.
- 2026 editorial theme: "The Energy Future is Renewable", an integrated energy-system reading combining photovoltaics, batteries, EV charging and grid management.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers and suppliers across the entire renewable energy value chain: photovoltaic modules and inverters, stationary and mobile storage systems, charging infrastructure for electric vehicles, energy management and integration solutions, and associated software and services. The scope covers the four trade shows that make up the alliance.

### Notable exhibitors

The official exhibitor list by edition can be consulted on the [exhibitor page of The smarter E Europe](https://www.thesmartere.de/exhibitorlist). Among the profiles represented at the most recent edition are the leading global players in solar and storage.

### Visitor quality

According to the organiser''s 2025 review, around 107,000 trade visitors from 157 countries attended the alliance, a sign of a highly internationalised visitor base. The conferences and side formats brought together more than 2,600 participants.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The specialist conferences take place ahead of and during the trade show, at the ICM München, on 22-23 June 2026 for the upcoming edition. They cover the core topics of the energy system: solar and storage markets, sector integration, electric mobility and grid management.

### Awards and prizes

The "The smarter E AWARD" recognises innovations in energy and mobility across five categories: Photovoltaics, Energy Storage, E-Mobility, Smart Integrated Energy and Outstanding Projects. The 2026 ceremony is scheduled for 22 June 2026 at 5 p.m. at the ICM München, the eve of the trade shows'' opening. Applications are open to exhibitors of the Intersolar, ees, Power2Drive and EM-Power events worldwide (2026 submission deadline: 20 March).

### Community and networks

The alliance brings together the communities of the four trade shows around a shared theme, the integrated and renewable energy system. The motto of the 2026 edition is "The Energy Future is Renewable".

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the venue page [Messe München](/lieux/messe-munchen).

Specific to the trade show: the 2026 edition runs from Tuesday 23 to Thursday 25 June 2026. The event occupies a large footprint of the grounds, halls A1 to A6, B0 to B6 and C1 to C6, as well as the outdoor area. Announced opening hours: Tuesday and Wednesday from 9.00 a.m. to 6.00 p.m., Thursday from 9.00 a.m. to 5.00 p.m. A single ticket gives access to all four trade shows of the alliance.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="No official price list is published in open access. The amounts below are indicative for an international trade show of this format, to be confirmed with the organiser." rows={[{ "poste": "Bare space rental (per m²)", "low": "sector indicative", "high": "sector indicative" }, { "poste": "Fitted stand (fit-out, furniture)", "low": "sector indicative", "high": "sector indicative" }, { "poste": "Technical services (electricity, utilities, cleaning)", "low": "sector indicative", "high": "sector indicative" }, { "poste": "Logistics, assembly, communication", "low": "sector indicative", "high": "sector indicative" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (indicative)", "low": "n/a", "high": "n/a" }]} footer="The actual budget depends on the targeted trade show within the alliance (Intersolar, ees, Power2Drive, EM-Power), the floor area and the level of fit-out. Request a quote from Solar Promotion GmbH." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: book your space, as demand is high (the 2025 edition had 90% of the halls booked seven months before opening).
- 3 months out: submit an application for "The smarter E AWARD" if relevant (deadline mid-March, set for 20 March for the 2026 edition).
- 1 month out: finalise your stand, logistics and client invitations.
- 1 day out: option to attend the awards ceremony on 22 June at 5 p.m. at the ICM München.

### For the decision-maker visitor

Target the four trade shows in advance according to your priorities (solar, storage, EV charging, energy management), with a single badge covering all of them. Plan the conference sessions on 22-23 June at the ICM and exhibitor meetings across the three days of the exhibition.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The smarter E Europe has a dedicated sustainability page built around three pillars: responsible visitor participation, exhibitor practices (stand construction, mobility, catering) and venue commitment. The organiser states: "Nachhaltigkeit ist für uns kein Ziel, sondern ein Weg" (sustainability is not a goal but a path).

The host venue Messe München runs a structured sustainability programme: 100% green electricity supply, one of the largest rooftop photovoltaic installations in Europe (since 1998, more than 1 MWp), geothermal heating for halls C5-C6, a Net Zero 2050 target for the entire group, signatory of the Net Zero Carbon Events (NZCE) initiative and member of fairpflichtet (since 2014). No ISO 20121 certification specific to the event was identified in open access at the time of writing.

## The trade show''s evolution

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "2026 (upcoming)", "dates": "23-25 June 2026", "lieu": "Messe München", "visiteurs": "100,000+ (target)", "exposants": "2,800+ (target)" }, { "edition": "2025", "dates": "7-9 May 2025", "lieu": "Messe München", "visiteurs": "~107,000", "exposants": "2,737" }]} sources="Organiser''s review The smarter E Europe 2025; 2026 targets announced by the organiser." />

### Trajectory analysis

The smarter E Europe has consolidated its status as the largest European platform in the energy sector by aggregating four specialist trade shows under a common banner. The 2025 edition brought together 2,737 exhibitors from 57 countries and around 107,000 visitors from 157 countries, a high level of internationalisation. The 2026 calendar marks a shift towards late June (23-25 June) after a 2025 edition held in early May, something to watch for the following cycles. The 2026 targets, above 2,800 exhibitors, reflect an expansion dynamic driven by the simultaneous growth of solar, storage and electromobility.', seo_title_en='The smarter E Europe 2026 Munich: dates, exhibitors, awards | Agoris', seo_description_en='The smarter E Europe 2026: 23-25 June at Messe München. Energy platform of 4 trade shows (Intersolar, ees, Power2Drive, EM-Power), 2,737 exhibitors and 107,000 visitors in 2025.' WHERE slug='smarter-e-europe-munich';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='32nd edition at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, Pavilion 7, co-located and concurrent with the AMF Mayors'' Congress. 2025 results: 65,672 visitors (+8.4%), 1,380 exhibitors, 448 speaking slots, 600 journalists, 45 official visits.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 32nd edition of the **Salon des Maires et des Collectivités Locales (SMCL)** from **24 to 26 November 2026**, Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **Pavilion 7**. Co-located and concurrent with the **Congrès des Maires de l''AMF** (Pavilion 4). Since 1996, the SMCL + Congress pairing has remained the only national gathering to bring together the entirety of France''s territorial public decision-makers over three days.
- 2025 results (31st edition, 18-20 November): **65,672 visitors (+8.4% vs 2024)**, **1,380 exhibitors**, **448 speaking slots**, **600 journalists**, **45 official visits**, **176 candidates** for the Prix Innovation Territoriale (source: salondesmaires.com).
- The 2026 edition takes place in a distinctive political context: the first trade show of the **2026-2032 municipal cycle** following the March 2026 municipal elections. Official slogan: **"L''audace est locale"**. The partial renewal of municipal teams creates a 12 to 24-month commercial window for suppliers to local authorities, with newly elected contacts to educate about the offering.
- 2025 trade show survey: **62% of local authorities have an investment project in 2026**. Stated priorities: environmental transition (39%), construction (37%), health and social cohesion (28%), an ageing population (26%). A useful budgetary framing for calibrating the sales pitch at the trade show.
- Organisation: **Infopro Digital** (owner of the Groupe Moniteur since January 2014 through the acquisition of the ISH holding company) in partnership with the **AMF** (Association des Maires de France et des présidents d''intercommunalité, founded in 1907). The SMCL celebrates its **30th anniversary** in 2026.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers, service providers and suppliers to local authorities across the full range of municipal and inter-municipal responsibilities. A mix of large groups (Veolia, Suez, Engie, EDF, Bouygues Énergies & Services, La Poste, Orange Business, Caisse des Dépôts) and SMEs specialising in public procurement. A structuring presence of technical consultancies, territorial advisory firms and publishers of sector software (GIS, financial management, civil registry, town planning).

### Notable exhibitors

The full list of exhibitors is on the official website: [salondesmaires.com](https://www.salondesmaires.com/liste-exposants/).

### Quality of the visitor base

An audience 100% oriented towards local authorities:

- Mayors, deputy mayors, municipal and community councillors
- DGS (Directors General of Services), DGST (Directors General of Technical Services)
- Public procurement directors, town hall secretaries, public buyers
- Institutional partners: prefectures, State agencies, territorial professional federations

The SMCL is one of the rare French B2B trade shows where the entire visitor base is made up of public decision-makers or their direct institutional partners.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**448 speaking slots** at the 2025 edition (source: salondesmaires.com). Structuring themes for 2026, aligned with the investment priorities declared by local authorities: environmental transition and ecological planning, construction and renovation, territorial health and social cohesion, adapting to an ageing population, local finances, rural areas, cybersecurity for local authorities.

### Prix Innovation Territoriale

**7 main categories** (2025 edition, retained for 2026):

1. Energy efficiency
2. Low-carbon mobility
3. Sustainable development
4. Trusted digital technology
5. Ecological planning
6. Social ties (solidarity, longevity, inclusion)
7. Safety, prevention and risk management

Additional categories: Local dynamism and attractiveness, Development / housing / urban renewal. **176 candidates** in 2025. A free visibility lever for innovative exhibitors, with an application file to be submitted several months in advance.

### What''s new in 2026

- **Les Labs**: spaces for debate and co-construction between elected officials, territorial staff and exhibitors.
- **Les Atmosphères**: thematic zones structured around major public priorities (ecological planning, mobility, social ties).
- **Arène de l''Innovation**: a central pitching and demonstration space (not to be confused with the former name "Audace" used by some press outlets).
- **"Vis ta ville"**: immersive spaces reproducing territorial facilities (school, cultural centre, station, connected town hall).
- **Salon Sports et Parasports** co-located: around 140 exhibitors, parasport challenge.
- **Salon Biodiversité et Génie Écologique** co-located, linked to the "ecological planning" priority.

### Community & networks

A long-standing partnership with the **AMF** (created in 1907, more than 36,000 member municipalities). A regular presence of the main associations of elected officials (France Urbaine, Intercommunalités de France, AMRF, ADF, Régions de France). Institutional coverage by the Ministry of the Interior. 600 accredited journalists in 2025, a signal of national and local press visibility.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Location:** Pavilion 7 for the SMCL, Pavilion 4 for the Congrès des Maires AMF. Allow time to move between the two pavilions for visitors combining both.
- **Dates and opening hours:** 24, 25 and 26 November 2026. Detailed opening hours on salondesmaires.com.
- **Visitor badge:** **free for elected officials and territorial staff** with pre-registration and supporting documents (official''s card, public-sector employer certificate). Accreditation is also available for institutional partners and the press.
- **Footfall:** an intense week at Porte de Versailles (the SMCL mobilises the whole of France''s territorial public decision-making). Book accommodation and transport 3 to 4 months in advance, especially the Tuesday-to-Wednesday night (the heart of the Congress).

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are **not published** by Infopro Digital: quotation on application. As the SMCL is a "public procurement" trade show targeting 100% public decision-makers, the rates per m² have historically ranked among the highest in the French B2B landscape. Request the quotation well in advance: strategic locations (pavilion entrances, near the Arène de l''Innovation and the Atmosphères) go quickly.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 to 12 months out: quotation request to Infopro Digital, application to the Prix Innovation Territoriale in one of the 7 categories.
- 6 months out: stand order with a contractor, specific "public procurement" sales brief (won-contract references, accreditations, qualifications).
- 3 months out: final stand plan, sales argument adapted to the 2026-2032 municipal cycle (the first post-election trade show, many new elected officials to educate).
- 6 weeks out: team accreditations, accommodation.
- 1 week out: final brief on the specifics of the elected-official visitor base (electoral cycles, public procurement code, local authorities'' budget calendar).

### For the elected official or DGS visitor

- Mandatory pre-registration with supporting documents (official''s card, public-sector employer certificate).
- Allow 2 days for a full tour (Pavilion 7 + Pavilion 4 + the co-located Sports / Biodiversity trade shows); 1 day is enough for a visit focused on 2 or 3 investment priorities.
- Identify priority conferences in advance from among the 400+ announced speaking slots and the Labs corresponding to the authority''s projects.
- Systematically combine the SMCL visit with attendance at the Congrès des Maires AMF (Pavilion 4): it''s the same week, the same venue, and the editorial / political complementarity is strong.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

CSR is intrinsic to the SMCL''s positioning: **ecological planning** is one of the 2026 "Atmosphères", and the **Salon Biodiversité et Génie Écologique** is co-located. The investment priorities declared by local authorities place environmental transition at the top (39%), which shapes both the trade show''s editorial line and the exhibitors'' offering. The Prix Innovation Territoriale dedicates three of its seven categories to environmental themes (energy efficiency, low-carbon mobility, ecological planning).

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
