### Trajectory analysis

The SMCL celebrates its **30th anniversary** in 2026 (created in 1996 by the AMF and the Groupe Moniteur, which became Infopro Digital in 2014). Visitor growth of +8.4% between 2024 and 2025, with a stable exhibitor base of around 1,380. The 2026 edition opens a new political cycle: it is the first SMCL after the March 2026 municipal elections, which mechanically produces a turnover of the elected-official visitor base and therefore a heightened commercial opportunity for suppliers to local authorities (new teams to equip, train and advise). Worth watching: the effect of the "L''audace est locale" slogan on the showcasing of territorial innovations, and the traction of the Labs / Atmosphères / Arène de l''Innovation trio for exhibitors operating in demonstration mode rather than classic stand mode.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='smcl';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='26th edition of France''s leading B2B trade show for snacking and quick-service catering, at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, Hall 7.2. 2026 results: 450 exhibitors, 16,000 visitors, 1,800 innovations across 3 zones (Snacking, Parizza+Gusto, Smart Lab) plus The Coffee Place.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- 26th edition of the **Snack Show** (formerly Sandwich & Snack Show, official rebrand confirmed on snackshow.com, with sandwichshows.com 301-redirecting): **1 and 2 April 2026** at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **Hall 7.2**.
- Final 2026 results: **450 exhibitors**, **16,000 trade visitors**, **1,800 innovations and new products** showcased (consolidated post-show figures vs pre-show announcements of 400 exhibitors and 14,500 visitors).
- Organiser: **RX France** (RX group, formerly Reed Exhibitions). Not Comexposium, unlike several neighbouring food-sector trade shows.
- The 2026 format is structured around **3 themed zones**: Snacking (its historic core), Parizza+Gusto (an integrated Italian zone, with more than 100 exhibitors for the first time, broadened to sweet products and beverages), and Smart Lab (tech innovation).
- New for 2026: **The Coffee Place**, a dedicated coffee area positioned as a growth driver for snacking.
- 2027 edition: 24 and 25 March 2027, relocating to **Hall 7.3** (change of hall).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The Snack Show is France''s leading B2B trade show for snacking and quick-service catering. In 2026, the hundred or so square metres of Hall 7.2 bring together around **450 exhibitors** spread across the three zones of the offering:

- **Snacking**: French and international manufacturers of sandwiches, wraps, burgers, bagels and sweet snacking, ready meals for eating in or taking away, industrial caterers and own-label brands (private label).
- **Parizza+Gusto**: equipment makers and suppliers for pizza and Italian snacking (pasta, charcuterie, sauces, cheeses, Italian ready meals, Italian sweet products, beverages). The first edition to exceed 100 exhibitors in this integrated zone.
- **Smart Lab**: developers of point-of-sale software, online ordering solutions, flow management, kitchen robotics, eco-responsible packaging, dark kitchens and new operational solutions.

Added to these are suppliers of heavy equipment (pizza ovens, burger griddles, professional coffee machines, fast-cooking equipment), ingredients (oils, cheeses, plant-based snacking) and beverages (soft drinks, beers, juices, waters). The new **The Coffee Place** area deepens the coffee offering: roasters, machines, accessories and barista training.

### Quality of the visitor base

The trade show is **strictly B2B**, with a mandatory professional badge and proof of activity required. The **16,000 trade visitors** in 2026 break down across:

- Snacking chains and brands, brand managers and network management
- Independent commercial catering (bakery-snacking, food trucks, hot-food outlets, kiosks)
- Contract catering (central purchasing, site managers)
- Caterers, B2B delivery operators, dark kitchens
- Purchasing and R&D teams of manufacturers and own-label brands
- Hospitality schools and training organisations
- Trade press and sector institutions

The profile is highly operational: operators looking for products ready to list, equipment to compare in live demos, and suppliers to source for the season.

## Activities and community

### The flagship competitions

The 2026 Snack Show confirmed its position as the **national stage for snacking champions**, with more than 9 competitions and award ceremonies across the 2 days.

- **Les Snacking d''Or**: awards for exhibitor products and innovations, judged by a panel of professionals. Trade-press visibility and a post-show listing lever.
- **French Pizza Championship**: 20th edition, 130 selected candidates, 2026 winner **Christopher Pacaud**. One of the most widely covered competitions in the sector.
- **French Burger Cup by Socopa**: 2026 theme "**Burger of the future**", winner **Kévin Buchaillot**. A competition that draws the community of independent and chain burger chefs.
- **French Barista Championship**: new for 2026, organised by the **SCA** (Specialty Coffee Association). The winner qualifies for the international competition held in Panama. A natural tie-in with The Coffee Place.

### The Coffee Place

New for 2026: a dedicated coffee area positioned as a **growth driver for snacking**. RX France''s rationale: the average ticket rises with coffee add-ons (hot, iced, signature), and the coffee sector wants a dedicated professional meeting point away from consumer trade shows. Demonstrations, tastings, masterclasses and a French Barista Championship corner.

### Live activities

The 2 days combine culinary demonstrations on open stages (pizza, burger, signature snacking), talks from chefs and chain operators, business workshops (profitability, operations, recruitment, energy) and panel discussions on sector issues. The format stays tight at 2 days, unlike longer hospitality trade shows: maximum density for a high-throughput operator audience.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) page.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Hall**: 7.2 for the 2026 edition (Hall 7.3 planned for 2027).
- **Duration**: 2 full days, from Wednesday 1 to Thursday 2 April 2026.
- **Visitor badge**: online pre-registration on snackshow.com with proof of professional status. Free pre-registration, with a **charge applying on site** without pre-registration. No public access.
- **Catering on site**: Hall 7.2 and the Porte de Versailles catering areas. Given the theme, expect plenty of tastings on the stands.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published to date by RX France. Quotes on request via the exhibitor form on snackshow.com. Several packages traditionally exist at RX France trade shows: floor space only, turnkey fitted stand, and packages dedicated to young brands. Placement in Parizza+Gusto, Smart Lab or The Coffee Place affects the per-square-metre rate and visibility.

Figure not publicly available to date.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 10 months out: make contact with RX France, choose a zone (Snacking, Parizza+Gusto, Smart Lab, The Coffee Place).
- 6 months out: enter the **Snacking d''Or** or the sector competitions according to product category. Calibrate the innovation submission (the 1,800 new products in 2026 form a strong benchmark).
- 3 months out: finalise the stand, brief the contractor, brief the sales team for the 2 intensive days.
- 6 weeks out: plan pre-scheduled meetings with targeted buyers, and trade-press materials (LSA, Néorestauration, Snacking, France Snacking).
- 2 weeks out: activate the network (clients, prescribers, press) and brief the team on the live demos.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Free pre-registration is mandatory on snackshow.com to avoid the on-site charge.
- Intensive 2-day format: plan for **at least 1 full day** to cover a broad target, ideally both days to combine product sourcing and competitions.
- Target the winners of the Snacking d''Or and the competitions (Pizza, Burger, Barista) to spot the references validated by the sector.
- The Coffee Place: a new must-visit for operators adding a coffee offering to their format.

## Policy and CSR initiatives

The 2026 edition was positioned by RX France around the theme "**innovating for more sustainable snacking**". The "Our commitments" page on snackshow.com sets out the organiser''s commitments. The trade show forms part of the RX group''s **Net Zero 2040** policy (group climate commitment), which covers the energy management of editions, the circularity of stands and the measurement of each edition''s footprint.

On the content side, the sustainability angle runs through the competitions (the "Burger of the future" 2026 theme of the French Burger Cup, the eco-responsible focus of the Smart Lab and the Snacking d''Or) and the activities. No specific ISO 20121 certification is mentioned to date for the trade show.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
 { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
 { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" },
 { "key": "pavillon", "label": "Hall" },
