### Trajectory analysis

In 2026 the trade show carried out a **strong rebrand**: dropping "Sandwich & Snack Show" in favour of "Snack Show", with the domain switching from sandwichshows.com to snackshow.com (301 redirect). The strategic reading is crystal clear: snacking is no longer just about the sandwich, and the operator audience now spans pizza, burger, industrial catering, dark kitchens and coffee. The 2026 edition confirmed this elasticity with **450 exhibitors** (vs around 400 announced pre-show) and **16,000 trade visitors** (vs around 14,500 announced), a result above the public targets.

Three structural signals to note. First signal: **Parizza+Gusto exceeds 100 exhibitors** for the first time in the integrated Italian zone, and broadens to sweet products and beverages: RX France is bringing in-house a category that was once standalone. Second signal: **The Coffee Place** establishes coffee as a driver of growth in the average snacking ticket (6.33 euros in 2025, +7% vs 2024 according to sector data). Third signal: the **French Barista Championship by SCA** connects the trade show to the speciality coffee community and provides an entry point for suppliers previously absent. The change of hall for 2027 (moving from 7.2 to 7.3) suggests a logistical scale-up, with no break in format.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='snack-show';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for photovoltaic and thermal solar energy. Panels, inverters, storage, monitoring and installation solutions.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Renewable energy trade show: "Exhibition for the renewable energy sector in the Netherlands" (official baseline). The event has broadened its scope from photovoltaics alone to the entire renewable energy sector, with four central themes: solar, smart storage, EV charging and renewable HVAC.
- Organiser: Sustainable Solutions (based in Heerhugowaard, NL). The brand has been rebranded from "Solar Solutions Amsterdam" to "Sustainable Solutions Amsterdam"; the name "Solar Solutions International" is still used for the series.
- Upcoming edition: 15th edition, on 16, 17 and 18 March 2027 at [Expo Greater Amsterdam](/lieux/expo-greater-amsterdam) (Vijfhuizen, Amsterdam region).
- 2026 audience (organiser figures, not OJS-audited): more than 13,300 visitors and over 275 exhibitors at the 14th edition (10-12 March 2026).
- Profile: installers, distributors, wholesalers, EPCs and engineering firms in PV, storage, inverters and smart energy systems, with the Dutch market as the priority.
- Highlights: Innovation Boulevard and its "Best Innovation Award", a programme of seminars and Practical Hubs.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile
The trade show brings together manufacturers, distributors, wholesalers, installers, EPC companies and technology suppliers active in photovoltaics, energy storage, inverters, mounting systems and energy management solutions. The organiser states that it specifically welcomes companies from China, Hong Kong, Taiwan and Turkey, with dedicated regional agents. The rebrand to "Sustainable Solutions" reflects a broadening beyond solar towards renewable heating and cooling.

### Notable exhibitors
The official exhibitor list is published on the [organiser''s website](https://en.sustainablesolutionsamsterdam.nl/). Agoris does not reproduce unconfirmed brand names on the exhibitor page for the edition concerned.

### Visitor quality
The audience is overwhelmingly professional: installers, distributors and end users in the Dutch renewable energy sector. The organiser reports more than 13,300 visitors at the 2026 edition, up on the previous year. These figures are reported by the organiser and are not subject to a public OJS audit.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme
The trade show offers more than 30 practical seminars structured around four pillars: solar, smart storage, EV charging and renewable HVAC. Practical Hubs focused on hands-on implementation round out the offering.

### Awards and recognition
Innovation Boulevard showcases products and services launched within the last twelve months, with the "Best Innovation Award" (official verbatim wording), presented by an independent professional jury.

### Community & networks
The event is part of a European network of events in the same series, held notably in Kortrijk, Düsseldorf, Leipzig and Vienna. A Digital Event Planner and the YDEM lead scanning/export tool support visitors and exhibitors.

## On site: what you need to know

For access, parking and accommodation, see the venue page [Expo Greater Amsterdam](/lieux/expo-greater-amsterdam) (Stelling 1, 2141 SB Vijfhuizen, Amsterdam region).

Specific to the trade show: 15th edition on 16, 17 and 18 March 2027. Registration and badges are managed online via the Digital Event Planner on the official website. On site, the YDEM lead scanning app lets exhibitors record and export visitor contacts and seminar data.

## How much it costs to exhibit

<BudgetTable warning="No public rate card is published on the official website. The amounts below are indicative sector figures (a mid-sized European B2B trade show) and must be confirmed with the organiser." rows={[{ "poste": "Space rental (bare stand, by surface area)", "low": "4,000 €", "high": "14,000 €" }, { "poste": "Fit-out and stand (furniture, structure)", "low": "5,000 €", "high": "20,000 €" }, { "poste": "Logistics, transport, utilities", "low": "2,000 €", "high": "6,000 €" }, { "poste": "Staff, travel, accommodation", "low": "3,000 €", "high": "10,000 €" }, { "poste": "Marketing, leads, giveaways", "low": "1,500 €", "high": "6,000 €" }]} totals={[{ "label": "ESTIMATED TOTAL (indicative)", "low": "~15,000 €", "high": "~55,000 €" }]} footer="Rates not disclosed by the organiser: contact the sales team via sanne@sustainablesolutions.eu for a quote." />

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor
- 6 months out: book the space and choose the location (close to Innovation Boulevard or the Practical Hubs depending on your objective), apply for the Best Innovation Award if your product was launched less than 12 months ago.
- 3 months out: finalise the stand, brief the sales teams, activate the Digital Event Planner.
- 1 month out: client invitation campaign, appointment booking, YDEM lead scanning setup.

### For the decision-making visitor
Register in advance via the official website, target the relevant seminars and Practical Hubs (smart storage, EV charging, renewable HVAC), and walk Innovation Boulevard to spot market innovations less than twelve months old.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

An important distinction: the trade show''s theme (renewable energy) does not in itself constitute an event CSR policy. On that front, organiser Sustainable Solutions publishes no page of environmental commitments specific to the trade show (waste management, mobility, the event''s carbon footprint, ISO 20121 certification): no CSR section is accessible on en.sustainablesolutionsamsterdam.nl (five-item menu, checked June 2026). The host venue, Expo Greater Amsterdam, on the other hand displays a documented approach: the site has held Green Key Gold certification since September 2024 (an international label for congress venues committed to sustainability), its 26,000 m² roof has been fully covered with solar panels since 2002 (100% green electricity, surplus redistributed to local residents), and the site achieves a 50% reduction in water consumption, Waste2Energy treatment of waste, catering that is 95% porcelain or biodegradable, and offers EV charging points powered by solar energy. These commitments are the venue''s, not those of the trade show''s organiser.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable columns={[{ "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" }, { "key": "dates", "label": "Dates" }, { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" }, { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" }, { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }]} rows={[{ "edition": "15th (upcoming)", "dates": "16-18 March 2027", "lieu": "Expo Greater Amsterdam, Vijfhuizen", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "n/a" }, { "edition": "14th", "dates": "10-12 March 2026", "lieu": "Expo Greater Amsterdam, Vijfhuizen", "visiteurs": "13,300+", "exposants": "275+" }]} sources="Organiser figures (Sustainable Solutions), not OJS-audited." />

### Trajectory analysis
The defining feature of the recent cycle is the rebranding of "Solar Solutions" to "Sustainable Solutions Amsterdam": the trade show is no longer limited to photovoltaics but positions itself as the showcase of the renewable energy sector in the Netherlands, with four structuring pillars (solar, storage, EV charging, renewable HVAC). The 14th edition (March 2026) exceeded 13,300 visitors, confirming the maturity of the Dutch solar market and the rise of storage. The 15th edition (March 2027) extends this anchoring at Expo Greater Amsterdam, with a stable March schedule and an upgrade in content (seminars, Practical Hubs, Innovation Boulevard).', seo_title_en='Solar Solutions 2027 Amsterdam: dates, exhibitors, info | Agoris', seo_description_en='Sustainable Solutions Amsterdam (formerly Solar Solutions), 15th edition on 16-18 March 2027 at Expo Greater Amsterdam (Vijfhuizen). Over 13,300 visitors, 275+ exhibitors in 2026.' WHERE slug='solar-solutions-international-amsterdam';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='17th edition of the only B2B trade show in France covering the entire geotechnical chain, drilling and special foundations, at Eurexpo Lyon Hall 7 over 2 days. Record 2025 edition: 4,630 attendees (+8%) and more than 230 exhibitors across 6,000 m² indoors and 1,500 m² outdoors.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Solscope is the only B2B trade show in France covering the entire geotechnical chain, drilling and special foundations: water drilling, geothermal energy, gas, petroleum exploration, special foundations, geotechnical engineering. Compact 2-day format at Eurexpo Lyon Hall 7.
- The 2025 edition (16th, 18-19 June 2025) brought together 4,630 attendees and more than 230 exhibitors, a +8% increase in visitors versus 2023 (source: organisers). Record edition across 6,000 m² indoors and 1,500 m² outdoors.
- Biennial trade show, odd-numbered years, founded in 1992. Next edition: the 17th, in June 2027 (exact dates not yet published).
- Co-organised by ATTITUDE Consultants and RPI (Dominique Rousseau) since 2005.
- Backed by the sector''s leading institutional partners: USG, CFMS, SOFFONS, CINOV, SYNTEC Ingénierie, CFGI, SFEG, UFCMF, AITF, CFMR.
- A strong distinctive feature: an outdoor area dedicated to machine demonstrations (drilling, drilling rigs, heavy equipment), highly appreciated by visitors.
- Visitors: free for sector professionals, registration required.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Drillers, geotechnical and special-foundation companies, manufacturers and distributors of drilling equipment, suppliers of testing equipment, data-acquisition specialists, engineering consultancies, IT solution vendors for the sector. The trade show covers the entire chain: from the field driller to the geotechnical engineering consultancy, taking in machine manufacturers, laboratories and software vendors.

### Notable exhibitors

2025 edition (selection): Socomafor, Atlas Copco, CAJ Travaux Spéciaux, Geosec, complemented by suppliers of laboratory and in-situ testing equipment. Full list of exhibitors on the official website: [solscope.fr](https://www.solscope.fr).

### Quality of the visitor base

- 4,630 attendees in 2025, +8% versus 2023 (source: organisers)
- More than 230 exhibitors in 2025
- Target audience: drilling and special-works companies, geotechnical engineers, engineering consultancies, geologists, hydrogeologists, engineers, research and universities

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2025 edition was built around the theme "Geosciences: changes to factor in climate change". The programme combines three formats:

- A two-day scientific symposium, run in partnership with the sector''s learned societies and professional associations.
- Technical workshops and themed round tables.
- Machine demonstrations in the outdoor area (drilling, drilling rigs, special-works equipment), a format that has become the trade show''s signature.

### Awards & accolades

The Exhibitors'' Forum held its 6th edition in 2025, with around fifteen exhibitors selected to present their innovations in a pitch format before the community. This format showcases the latest products and services in the sector.

### Community & networks

Solscope is backed by the sector''s leading institutional partners: USG (Union Syndicale Géotechnique), CFMS (Comité Français de Mécanique des Sols et de Géotechnique), SOFFONS (Syndicat des Entrepreneurs de Fondations Spéciales), CINOV, SYNTEC Ingénierie, CFGI (Comité Français de Géologie de l''Ingénieur), SFEG (Société Française d''Études Géotechniques), UFCMF, AITF (Association des Ingénieurs Territoriaux de France) and CFMR (Comité Français de Mécanique des Roches). These partnerships establish the trade show as the unmissable gathering for the French sector.

Partner magazine: **Solscope Mag''**, the reference publication for the drilling and geotechnical sector, distributed to around 10,000 readers per issue and soon entering its tenth year.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Eurexpo Lyon](/lieux/eurexpo-lyon) venue page. The trade show takes place in Hall 7, complemented by an outdoor area dedicated to machine demonstrations.

Specific to this trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** free for sector professionals, subject to prior registration. Access is reserved for players in the geotechnical, drilling and foundations sector.
- **Opening hours:** 8.30am-6pm on both days.
- **Visitor parking:** chargeable at the exhibition centre.
- **Outdoor machine demonstration area:** open access within the exhibitor perimeter; bring safety footwear to approach the drilling equipment on demonstration.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published: quotes available on request from co-organisers ATTITUDE Consultants and RPI via the official website. As Solscope is a specialised two-day trade show in a compact format, with a dedicated outdoor area for demonstrations, budgets vary according to indoor space (a stand in Hall 7) and outdoor space (machine demonstration). Contact is made directly with the organisers.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: initial contact with ATTITUDE Consultants or RPI, choice between an indoor stand in Hall 7 and the outdoor demonstration area.
- 6 months out: booking space, application to the Exhibitors'' Forum to showcase an innovation.
- 3 months out: stand layout, machine logistics if running an outdoor demonstration, team accreditations.
- 6 weeks out: delivery of materials, commercial briefing on the sector.
- 1 week out: set-up, final team briefing.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Free professional badge, subject to prior registration.
- Compact 2-day format: allow at least one full day to cover Hall 7 plus the outdoor demonstration area.
- Identify in advance the scientific symposium sessions and machine demonstration slots that match your priorities (water drilling, geothermal energy, special foundations, geotechnical engineering).
- The Exhibitors'' Forum is a good entry point for scanning the sector''s latest products in a short format.

## ESG policy & initiatives

The 2025 edition, under the theme "Geosciences: changes to factor in climate change", placed the sector''s adaptation to climate challenges at the heart of the programme: geothermal energy, water-resource management, contaminated soils, foundations adapted to new risks. The geotechnical and drilling sector is structurally at the core of the energy transition (deep and surface geothermal energy) and the environmental transition (water, soil and natural-risk management), which naturally feeds into the trade show''s editorial content.

## How the trade show has evolved

