### Trajectory analysis

Solscope confirmed its trajectory of controlled growth in 2025: 4,630 attendees, +8% versus 2023, more than 230 exhibitors, across 6,000 m² indoors and 1,500 m² outdoors. A record edition for a biennial trade show founded in 1992, which has established itself as the only French B2B gathering covering the entire geotechnical chain, drilling and special foundations. The stable co-leadership of ATTITUDE Consultants / RPI since 2005, the anchoring at Eurexpo Lyon Hall 7 and the signature "machine demonstrations in the outdoor area" are the constants of the format. The next edition, the 17th, will take place in June 2027 at Eurexpo Lyon Hall 7 (exact dates to be confirmed by the organisers).', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='solscope';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='31st edition at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, Pavilion 4, across 4 areas (Consulting & Management, HRIS, Social protection, Training) and a multi-show format (5 co-located events). 2025 results: 9,140 visitors (+15%), around 250 exhibitors, 90+ conferences and workshops.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key facts

- 31st edition of Solutions RH: **8 and 9 April 2026** (Wednesday and Thursday) at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), **Pavilion 4**.
- Opening hours: Wednesday 9:00 to 18:30, Thursday 9:00 to 18:00. **Free admission with a B2B professional badge**, prior online registration required.
- A long-standing show in the French HR sector, created in the late 1990s, organised by **Infopromotions**, an independent French organiser for over 40 years (head office: 14 rue des Volontaires, 75015 Paris).
- 2025 results: **9,140 visitors (+15% vs 2024)**, **around 250 exhibitors**, **90+ conferences and workshops**. 2026 target: around 10,000 professionals.
- Multi-show format: 5 co-located events over 2 days, a shared visitor badge, economies of scale for HR, IS, training and internal communications decision-makers.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Solutions RH structures its offering around **4 areas** that cover the entire value chain of the HR function:

- **Consulting & Management**: HR consulting firms, change management, transformation support, coaching, organisational audit.
- **HRIS**: HRIS software vendors, core HR platforms, payroll management, time and absence management, talent management, digital recruitment.
- **Social protection & benefits**: health insurers, provident schemes, pensions, employee savings plans, luncheon vouchers, employee benefits, operational QVCT.
- **Training**: training organisations, LMS platforms, learning content, immersive training, certification.

The show addresses every type of company, with a balanced mix: **30% micro-businesses and SMEs** (fewer than 50 employees) and **21% large accounts** (more than 1,000 employees), the remainder being mid-cap and intermediate organisations.

### Visitor mix

The breakdown by function reflects the multi-show positioning:

- **58%** HR, Training and Internal Communications, the historic core target.
- **14%** IT, in keeping with the HRIS and Digital Workplace dimension.
- **11%** Finance, on payroll, social protection and benefits trade-offs.
- The remainder: general management, procurement, employment law.

### Visitor quality

Identified decision-maker profiles: company directors, HR directors and HR managers, Training managers, IS managers, Talent Acquisition managers, Internal Communications managers, Payroll managers. Mandatory online pre-registration with proof of professional status, a single badge valid across the 5 co-located shows.

## Activities and community

### The 5 co-located shows

A defining feature of Solutions RH: **5 events** take place simultaneously in the same Pavilion 4, with a single badge for the visitor.

1. **Solutions RH**: the historic heart of the line-up, consulting, HRIS, social protection, training.
2. **Innovative Learning**: formerly eLearning Expo, renamed to embrace all learning methods (digital learning, in-person, immersive, AFEST). Hosts the **Trophées du Digital Learning**.
3. **Digital Workplace**: intranets, collaborative tools, internal communications platforms, digital employee experience.
4. **Documation & iExpo**: information management, EDM, dematerialisation, document governance.
5. **Forum Cybersécurité, Cloud, IA**: a cross-cutting technical foundation, in keeping with the IT share of the visitor base.

This pooling creates a critical-mass effect: 10,000 professionals expected in 2026 over 2 days, whereas a standalone HR show would cap out at around 5,000 to 6,000 visitors.

### 2026 themes

The 2025 editorial themes are carried over and deepened for 2026:

- **AI applied to HR**: AI recruitment, CV scoring, conversational HR agents, attrition prediction, automation of administrative processes.
- **QVCT** (quality of working life and working conditions): the successor to QVT, an editorial thread that shapes several workshops and round tables.
- **Immersive training**: VR, AR, serious games, virtual classrooms, AFEST.
- **Prevention of visible and invisible disabilities**: disability policy, accessibility, awareness-raising, OETH.
- **Inclusion and collective well-being**: diversity, equity, workplace climate, prevention of psychosocial risks.

### Trophées du Digital Learning

The flagship competition of **Innovative Learning**, presented during the show on 9 April 2026. **More than 120 entries** were submitted for the 2025 edition, a sign of a trophy native to the ecosystem and recognised by the training sector. Categories open to vendors, training organisations, client companies and digital learning production agencies.

### Trophées de l''Engagement RH

A parallel distinction, 4th edition in 2026, run by a partner external to the show. Free entries until **17 April 2026**, jury deliberation on **6 May 2026**. Not to be confused with the Trophées du Digital Learning, which remain the native activity of the Innovative Learning ecosystem.

### Conference programme

**More than 90 conferences and workshops** over 2 days in 2025, with an equivalent volume planned for 2026. Mixed formats: plenary conferences, hands-on workshops, exhibitor demonstrations, company case studies. Fully free access with the show badge.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the show:

- **Pavilion**: 4, entirely dedicated to the 5 co-located shows.
- **Opening hours**: Wednesday 8 April 9:00 to 18:30, Thursday 9 April 9:00 to 18:00.
- **Visitor badge**: free with online pre-registration, B2B professional proof required. A single badge gives access to the 5 shows.
- **Official website**: solutions-ressources-humaines.fr. The .com domain redirects with a 301 to the .fr.
- **Catering**: see the Paris Expo Porte de Versailles listing.

## How much it costs to exhibit

