## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 18 months out (spring 2026): make contact with Comexposium and the FFC, positioning (manufacturer, equipment supplier, bodybuilder, energy provider, services), choice of hall (opening of Hall 4 +8,000 sqm in 2027), surface area negotiation.
- 12 months out (November 2026): commitment and signature, award entries (International Truck Innovation Award, Sustainable Truck of the Year), pre-booking of exhibitor badges (quota 1 / 3 sqm).
- 9 months out (February 2027): validation of the scenographic concept, briefing of the agency and stand builder, planning of vehicle demonstrators and transport logistics.
- 6 months out (May 2027): final plans, stand build order, haulier accreditations and HGV transport logistics, planning of world premieres and French premieres.
- 3 months out (August 2027): team accreditations, accommodation in the Eurexpo / Saint-Priest area or Lyon city centre, sales briefing, B2B meeting planning, international press kits.
- 6 weeks out (October 2027): delivery of materials, final team briefing, activation of media campaigns and invitations to fleet and local authority clients.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Register as soon as professional ticketing opens (spring 2027): **free visitor badge with pre-registration** on the official site.
- Favour Tuesday 16 or Wednesday 17 November for manufacturer meetings and the **ITOY gala evening** (International Truck of the Year presented on the Wednesday evening).
- Prepare your meetings via the Comexposium matchmaking tools and the exhibitor directories.
- For international delegations: get in touch with the interpreting services and the dedicated areas (25% foreign visitors in 2025, 100 countries represented).
- Allow 2 full days to cover the 108,000 sqm and the 30+ HGV/LCV manufacturers exhibiting in their own right.

## The trade show''s evolution

