### Trajectory analysis

Over some thirty years, the Sommet de l''Elevage has grown from a local agricultural show-and-sale event (8,000 visitors, 100 exhibitors in 1992) into the **leading European trade fair for animal production**, crossing a symbolic milestone in 2023 (115,000 visitors, 1,681 exhibitors) and setting a new exhibitor record in 2025 (1,770 from 34 countries). The move to the Grande Halle d''Auvergne in 2004 marked its shift to industrial scale. The succession of health shocks (BTV in 2024, LSD in 2025) demonstrated the resilience of the exhibitor model but also the fragility of farmer footfall when cattle shows are absent. The "guest country" strategy has clearly broadened beyond Europe since 2023: Georgia (2023), Kazakhstan (2024), Morocco (2025, the first African country). This opening up is part of French export-oriented livestock diplomacy. Variables to watch for 2026: the effective lifting of LSD health restrictions allowing cattle to return, the official announcement of the 2026 guest country, and the trade fair''s ability to win back the 115,000-120,000 visitor mark if cattle shows are reinstated.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='sommet-elevage-clermont';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='International livestock production trade show. The meeting point for animal husbandry professionals: cattle, pigs, poultry, goats.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key points

- **40th edition** of SPACE (Salon International des Productions Animales) on **15, 16 and 17 September 2026** at the [Parc Expo Rennes](/lieux/parc-expo-rennes), Bruz (35), across 11 sector-specific halls and 16 hectares of outdoor space.
- Official site: [space.fr](https://www.space.fr). Organiser: **GIE SPACE** (50% Rennes parc expo, 40% Chambre régionale d''agriculture de Bretagne, 10% FRSEA de Bretagne, source: Réussir). **Annual** frequency.
- Chairman of the GIE since June 2025: **Didier Lucas**, succeeding Marcel Denieul (source: Réussir).
- 2025 edition results: **102,528 visitors**, including **14,011 international visitors from 125 countries** (+11%), **1,230 exhibitors** from 40 countries, of whom 30% were international and 25% were new entrants. Record-breaking attendance on the Wednesday with 45,781 visitors.
- SPACE is the first French agricultural trade show to have calculated its carbon footprint: 52% of waste recycled, 100% French-sourced catering, 10,000 people transported by free shuttles in 2025.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A world-leading trade show for every livestock sector: dairy and beef cattle, pigs, poultry, sheep, goats, rabbits, horses, aquaculture. The offering covers genetics, animal nutrition and feed, livestock buildings, animal health, milking equipment, agricultural machinery, energy, effluent treatment and organic farming. Exhibitor profile is predominantly industrial (equipment manufacturers, seed companies, animal health firms, cooperative groups) with a strong international component (30% of exhibitors in 2025, compared with 34 countries in 2024 and 40 countries in 2025).

### Notable exhibitors

Official 2026 list at [space.fr/exhibitors](https://www.space.fr/en/exhibitors-list/67e11c942ee253be5ef22c49). 1,230 exhibitors in 2025, including 301 new entrants (25%).

### Quality of the visitor base

102,528 visitors in 2025, including **14,011 international visitors (+11%) from 125 countries** (an all-time record for the number of nationalities). Decision-maker visitor base: livestock farmers, cooperative and trading company directors, vets, technicians and advisers, large-retail and agri-industry buyers, foreign delegations (Top Buyers programme: around 30 international buyers from 13 countries in 2025).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**L''Espace pour Demain** is the trade show''s conference hub, featuring in 2025: 3 round tables and 18 expert workshops. The 2025 main theme was **"Agricultural Intelligence"** (AI applied to livestock farming). Recurring topics: food sovereignty, carbon footprint, adapting to climate change, the energy transition. **Forum Jeunes** (4th edition in 2025, new format), **Tech''Agri Challenge** (3rd edition, 7 student solutions in 2025), the first **AGREEN DEFI AI hackathon** launched in 2025. The 2026 programme is to be announced on the website.

### Awards & accolades

**Innov''Space** is the trade show''s official innovation label, created in 1995 (30th anniversary in 2025). Candidate products, equipment and services are assessed against two criteria: degree of interest for the farmer or end user, and degree of novelty compared with the existing offering. Official two-tier classification: **"1 star" or "2 stars"** for the winners, and **"3 stars"** for the jury''s special mention.

2025 honours roll: **43 winners**, including **7 "2 star" mentions** and **2 "3 star" mentions**. An all-time record for machinery, with 11 award-winning innovations in this sector. Over 30 years, Innov''Space has recognised 1,437 winners from nearly 3,500 entries submitted.

### Satellite events

**Aquaculture**: 120 dedicated stands in 2025, a sector in structural growth at SPACE. **Animal presentations and genetic competitions**: 750 animals exhibited in hall 1, with cattle, sheep, goat and horse competitions. **Job dating sessions** (80+ positions on offer in 2025). **International area** dedicated to foreign delegations and the Top Buyers programme.

### Community & networks

A structurally Breton and Greater West visitor base within the national target, but an openly global positioning via the international programme (125 nationalities in 2025, partnership with WTC Rennes Bretagne).

Partner specialist press: Réussir, La France Agricole, Web-agri, Paysan Breton, Filières Avicoles, PLM Magazine.

### What''s new in 2026

40th anniversary edition. Details of the 2026 programme had not yet been published at the time of writing. Internal social tensions within the GIE were reported by the press in 2025-2026 (cf. Réussir, *"Is there a risk that SPACE may not take place in 2026?"*), worth monitoring but with no cancellation confirmed to date.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Parc Expo Rennes](/lieux/parc-expo-rennes), 2 La Haie Gautrais, 35170 Bruz. Historical aliases: "Rennes Aéroport", "Parc des Expositions Rennes Aéroport". 11 covered sector-specific halls + 16 hectares of outdoor space used by SPACE.
- **Access by train + shuttle**: TGV to Rennes station (Paris-Rennes 1h25), then a **free SPACE shuttle** from the station. Three other free shuttles: Rennes city centre, Rennes airport, Saint-Malo. Shuttle information desk at Gate C, 8am-7.30pm during the 3 days.
- **Access by car**: 20 min from Rennes city centre, 3h from Paris (360 km by motorway), 1h from Nantes, Saint-Malo, Saint-Brieuc or Vannes. **Free visitor car parks** (A, B, C, E, K, M). Official SPACE car-sharing platform.
- **Opening hours**: 9am to 7pm on all three days.
- **Visitor pricing**: €20 for a day ticket, €33 for the 3-day pass. **Free for under-16s and international visitors** (source: official site).
- **Services**: cash machine on site, multiple catering options (central restaurants + food trucks along the outdoor aisles, 75% regional produce, 100% French), bicycle parking at Gate C.

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Parc Expo Rennes](/lieux/parc-expo-rennes) listing.

## Planning your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: make contact with SPACE organisation, apply for a stand location, choose a sector-specific hall (cattle, pigs, poultry, aquaculture, machinery, nutrition, etc.).
- 9 months out: submit an Innov''Space entry if launching an eligible product / service (1 star, 2 stars, or 3-star special mention).
- 6 months out: stand brief, application to the international programme (Top Buyers, delegations) if targeting export.
- 3 months out: team accreditations, accommodation in Rennes / Bruz (Brittany in September = high hotel pressure across the three nights of the trade show).
- 6 weeks out: scheduling of B2B meetings, sales brief and demos.

### For the decision-maker visitor

- 1-day pass €20 or 3-day pass €33. International visitors = free (international programme).
- Wednesday = peak day (45,781 visitors in 2025); favour Tuesday or Thursday for quieter meetings.
- Plan ahead: sector-specific halls by sector (dairy cattle, pigs, poultry, aquaculture, machinery, etc.), Espace pour Demain for the conferences, hall 1 for the animal presentations and competitions (750 animals).
- The free shuttle from Rennes TGV station = a fast option from Paris (door-to-door 2h30).
- Book accommodation at least 3 months in advance; Rennes and Bruz fill up across the three nights of the trade show.

## CSR policy & initiatives

SPACE positions itself as the **first French agricultural trade show to have calculated its carbon footprint** (source: "SPACE commits" page). A formalised carbon strategy makes it possible to identify the highest-emitting areas in organising the event and to guide reduction and offsetting actions.

Operational commitments in 2025:
- **Waste**: 52% of collected waste is recycled, 16 sorting points, 760 kg of biowaste recovered through methanisation with GRDF.
- **Catering**: 75% of restaurants serve regional produce, 100% French sourcing.
- **Plastics**: reusable cups at all catering points since 2019.
- **Mobility**: 10,000 people transported by the free shuttles in 2025, the SPACE car-sharing platform since 2023, bicycle parking at Gate C.

All of this is formalised in the **Charter of commitment** published on space.fr.

## How the trade show has evolved

