### Trajectory analysis

Created in 2012 and operated by RX France, Supply Chain Event has established itself as the annual Paris gathering for the digital supply chain. The trade show has broadened its scope from software alone to five areas covering information systems, control, transport, automation and consulting. In 2026, for its 14th edition, it leaves its autumn slot to settle in early December, on 1 and 2 December, in Hall 1 of Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. The figures communicated (more than 130 exhibitors, more than 40 conferences, more than 1,000 business meetings) are pre-show targets: no audited OJS figures have been published to date.', seo_title_en='Supply Chain Event 2026: dates, exhibitors, info | Agoris', seo_description_en='Supply Chain Event 2026, on 1 and 2 December at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. The digital supply chain trade show by RX France: exhibitors, conferences, awards and CSR.' WHERE slug='supply-chain-event-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for organic farming and alternative techniques. Open-field demonstrations and organic innovations.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Tech&Bio is the leading international trade show dedicated to organic farming and alternative techniques. It brings together organic and conventional farmers around the latest innovations, with demonstrations in real-world conditions across 18 hectares of crops.
- Organised by the **Chambre d''agriculture de la Drôme**, together with **Chambres d''agriculture France**, on the site of the **Lycée agricole du Valentin** in Bourg-lès-Valence.
- Held every two years (odd years). The 10th edition took place on 24 and 25 September 2025. The next edition is announced for **September 2027**, which will mark the trade show''s 20th anniversary.
- Results of the 10th edition (2025): nearly **21,000 professional visitors**, **more than 320 exhibitors**, 500 experts, 18 international delegations and more than 60 partners.
- The 2025 edition was marked by the launch of the **Les Éclaireurs - Prix de l''innovation bio et durable** competition.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers of agricultural equipment and machinery, suppliers of inputs and biocontrol solutions, seed producers and nursery growers, advisory bodies and technical institutes, cooperatives, chambers of agriculture, operators in the organic sector and stakeholders in agroecology. The visitor base is 100% professional: organic and conventional farmers, technicians, advisers and students from agricultural courses.

The distinctive feature of the trade show is the significant proportion of conventional farmers who come to learn about alternative techniques, making it a place for transferring knowledge between the two models.

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is available on the official website: [tech-n-bio.com](https://tech-n-bio.com/). The 10th edition in 2025 brought together more than 320 exhibitors and 18 international delegations representing around ten countries.

### Visitor quality

- Nearly 21,000 visitors at the 2025 edition, announced as 100% professional
- Organic / conventional mix: the trade show has historically attracted a high proportion of conventional farmers looking for technical alternatives
- Presence of experts (around 500 advisers and technicians from the networks and chambers of agriculture) to support visitors at the stands and demonstrations

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The 2025 edition offered **70 conferences** and more than **120 open-field workshops and demonstrations**, across 18 hectares of crops grown organically. The central themes covered the resilience of farming systems, adaptation to climate change, water management, the reduction of inputs and machinery. The programme and theme of the 2027 edition will be published as the trade show approaches.

### Awards and prizes

The 2025 edition launched **Les Éclaireurs - Prix de l''innovation bio et durable**, recognising winners across four categories: technological innovation, agroecological innovation, social and solidarity-based innovation, and international innovation.

### Community and networks

The trade show draws on the network of the Chambres d''agriculture and mobilises numerous partners from the sector (more than 60 for the 2025 edition). A Job Dating area, run in partnership with Apecita and Crédit Mutuel, connects companies, cooperatives and job candidates throughout the trade show.

## On site: what you need to know

The trade show takes place on the site of the Lycée agricole du Valentin (EPLEFPA), avenue de Lyon, 26500 Bourg-lès-Valence (Drôme), with open-field demonstrations across 18 hectares.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Visitor badge:** online registration on the official website, reserved for professionals. Access arrangements for the 2027 edition will be published as the trade show approaches.
- **Format:** open-air trade show; bring clothing and footwear suitable for walking through the demonstration plots.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates are not published on the official website: the commercial offer (stands, partnership packages, sponsorship, naming) is available on request via the exhibitor area. Organiser contact: Chambre d''agriculture de la Drôme, 145 avenue Georges Brassens, 26500 Bourg-lès-Valence. Figures not publicly available.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months before: get in touch with the Chambre d''agriculture de la Drôme, choose your positioning (stand, open-field demonstration plot).
- 9 months before: book your location and, where applicable, the demonstration crops to be planted ahead of the trade show.
- 6 months before: prepare your demonstrations in real-world conditions, the highlight of the trade show.
- 3 months before: apply to Les Éclaireurs if a new edition of the competition is run again, brief the team.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Pre-register online at tech-n-bio.com with proof of professional activity.
- Allow one to two days depending on your scope (conferences, workshops, open-field demonstrations).
- Identify in advance the conferences and demonstrations relevant to your farming system.
- Consider the Job Dating area for agricultural recruitment, open on both days.

## How the trade show has evolved

