### Trajectory analysis

Texworld was born in **1997 at the CNIT Paris-La Défense** with 37 exhibitors and 970 visitors, as an Asia-oriented textile sourcing event. Its acquisition by **Messe Frankfurt in December 2001** marked the industrial pivot: the German group integrated Texworld into its global portfolio of fashion and textile trade shows and gave it the international mobilisation capacity that structures today''s cluster. The move to the **Paris-Le Bourget Exhibition Centre in February 2007** offered the depth of halls needed to develop the cluster, then the renaming to **Texworld Paris in 2010** consolidated its Parisian identity. The **25th anniversary in 2023** marked the maturity of a trade show that had become biannual (February + September) and structured around three hubs co-located at the autumn edition. The February 2026 edition confirmed the post-Covid consolidation with 1,100+ exhibitors and 33 countries represented. The September 2026 edition capitalises on two levers. First, the Spring-Summer 2027 pre-collection calendar window, which justifies the presence of **Avantex** and the editorial weight of the **"Very Middle Ages"** trend book by Louis Gérin and Grégory Lamaud. Second, the **Texpertise Econogy** grid (Hub, Talks, Tour, Finder), which responds to the structural rise in CSR requirements among European principals, in a context of tightening regulation (CSRD, AGEC, digital product passport). The positioning remains consistent: a **Parisian sourcing platform for China, Turkey, India, South Korea and Taiwan origins**, extended by the South-East Asian, Maghreb and Bangladesh pavilions on the garment-making side.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='texworld-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Business convention for transport and logistics in the Mediterranean. A B2B meeting point between shippers and carriers.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Top Transport Europe** is the benchmark business convention for transport and logistics in France: a "one-to-one" format that schedules qualified meetings between decision-making shippers and service providers, organised by **Comexposium One to One**.
- Next Marseille edition: **34th edition, on 14 and 15 October 2026** at the [Palais du Pharo](/lieux/palais-du-pharo) in Marseille.
- Review of the 33rd edition (15-16 October 2025, Palais du Pharo): **3,735 business meetings** scheduled (around +10% according to voxlog.fr, +20% according to europe-camions.com), **170 exhibitors** and **345 shipper decision-makers** (source: europe-camions.com, post-show review December 2025).
- New for 2026: in addition to the annual Marseille meeting, Top Transport is launching an edition in the Grand Ouest region in **Saint-Malo on 10 and 11 June 2026** (Palais du Grand Large). The two dates are distinct: this listing covers the October Marseille edition.
- An unusual format: this is not a trade show with open stands but a platform of scheduled individual meetings, complemented by workshops, site visits and networking time.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Transport and logistics service providers on the supply side: road hauliers, freight forwarders and 3PL/4PL operators, TMS and supply chain solution publishers, players in decarbonised logistics and the energy transition of freight. On the demand side, decision-making shippers (transport, supply chain and logistics procurement departments) from major industrial and retail groups, bringing concrete projects.

### Notable exhibitors

Link to the official list of participants: [toptransporteurope.com](https://www.toptransporteurope.com/).

On the service provider side, recent editions have featured: DACHSER, FM Logistic, GEODIS, XPO Logistics, CEVA Logistics, Kuehne+Nagel, Jacky Perrenot, as well as technology solutions such as Shiptify, Transporeon and Upply.

On the shipper side, the 2025 edition brought together decision-makers from groups such as Ariane Group, Heineken, L''Oréal, Veolia, Decathlon, Saint-Gobain, Auchan, Carrefour, Groupe Bel, La Redoute, Lidl and Boiron (source: europe-camions.com, post-show review December 2025).

### Quality of attendees

- Strictly professional, pre-selected attendees: 345 shipper decision-makers bringing projects in 2025
- Meetings scheduled in advance in 25-minute slots, based on declared projects
- 3,735 business meetings generated in 2025 (source: voxlog.fr)

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

Beyond the one-to-one meetings, the 2025 edition offered around fifteen themed workshops on the energy transition and freight technologies, a "Fresque du Fret" decarbonisation awareness session, as well as two visits to operational sites (the Grans-Miramas multimodal terminal and the Marseille Fos port facilities). The 2026 programme will be published closer to the show (source: truckeditions.com).

### Community and networks

The 2025 edition hosted a hackathon organised with the AETL, mobilising around fifty students on transport and logistics innovations, with their work presented to a panel of professionals.

A TV studio named "Le Live!", produced by Néo 26, gave exhibitors and sector experts a live platform (source: truckeditions.com).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Palais du Pharo](/lieux/palais-du-pharo).

Specific to the show:

- **Opening hours:** Wednesday 14 October 2026 from 7:30 to 19:30, Thursday 15 October from 8:30 to 17:00 for the announced edition (to be confirmed on toptransporteurope.com).
- **Format:** participation by registration and prior profile validation; the meeting agenda is built in advance according to declared projects.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact with Comexposium One to One, choose the participation format and the number of meetings.
- 6 months out: qualify the target shippers and provide precise details of your offer to optimise meeting matching.
- 3 months out: prepare the 25-minute slots, prioritise high-potential projects.
- 6 weeks out: validate the scheduled meeting agenda, brief the sales team.

### For the shipper decision-maker

- Register and validate your profile on toptransporteurope.com, declaring your ongoing transport and logistics projects.
- Select the service providers to meet in advance via the matchmaking platform.
- Plan for a full day of scheduled meetings, complemented by workshops and site visits.
- Combine the one-to-one meetings with the value-added content (energy transition workshops, case studies).

## How the show has evolved

