### Trajectory analysis

Top Transport confirmed its "one-to-one" business convention model in 2025 with 3,735 scheduled meetings, on a base of 170 exhibitors and 345 shipper decision-makers (post-show review, source: europe-camions.com). The 34th edition, on 14 and 15 October 2026 at the [Palais du Pharo](/lieux/palais-du-pharo), continues this momentum. In 2026 the event takes a step in its geographic development: Comexposium One to One is opening an edition in the Grand Ouest region in Saint-Malo in June, complementing the long-standing Marseille meeting in October, with the aim of broadening the brand to new project owners. For transport and logistics exhibitors, it is the opportunity to meet decision-makers already qualified on concrete projects over two days, in a format that sets itself apart from conventional trade shows such as the [SITL](/salons/sitl) or [Intralogistics France](/salons/intralogistics-france).', seo_title_en='Top Transport Europe 2026 Marseille: transport and logistics convention', seo_description_en='Top Transport Europe 2026: 34th edition on 14 and 15 October at the Palais du Pharo in Marseille. A one-to-one business convention between shippers and transport and logistics service providers, organised by Comexposium One to One.' WHERE slug='top-transport-europe-marseille';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Contemporary and designer fashion trade show. Discover emerging brands and international designers.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Tranoï** is one of the leading dates for contemporary and designer fashion in Paris, dedicated to women''s ready-to-wear, accessories and lifestyle, with a strong selection of emerging and international brands. The trade show has been owned and operated by **GL Events** since 2020 (source: fashionnetwork.com).
- Two editions a year, aligned with Paris Fashion Week: a spring edition in March and an autumn edition in October. Next autumn edition: 1 to 4 October 2026 at the **Palais Brongniart**.
- March 2026 edition: 180 brands, nearly 45% of them new labels, organised into four curated segments (Italian Savoir-Faire, Designer Lab, Elevated Minimalism, Accessories & Lifestyle).
- October 2025 edition: more than 200 brands from around thirty countries.
- Recurring international programme **CANEX** (Creative Africa Nexus), led by Afreximbank, present for its eighth consecutive season in 2026.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Women''s ready-to-wear brands, emerging designers, accessories houses (bags, jewellery, eyewear) and lifestyle brands, with international labels making up the majority. Attendees are strictly professional: buyers from multi-brand boutiques, department stores, e-tailers and press agents, within the framework of Paris Fashion Week.

### Notable exhibitors

List of brands on the official website: [tranoi.com](https://www.tranoi.com/e/paris/content/page-exposant). The selection brings together brands from Europe, Asia and South America.

### Quality of attendees

- A B2B order-writing trade show, positioned as one of the observatories of emerging international fashion in Paris.
- October 2025 edition: more than 200 brands, illustrating the cosmopolitan dimension of the show.
- Aligned with the Paris Fashion Week calendar, which concentrates the presence of international buyers and press.

## Events & community

### Programme

The offering is structured into curated trails. For the March 2026 edition, the selection is split into four segments: **Italian Savoir-Faire**, **Designer Lab**, **Elevated Minimalism** and **Accessories & Lifestyle**.

The trade show hosts international programmes dedicated to emerging creativity, including **CANEX** (Creative Africa Nexus), led by Afreximbank, which showcases African and diaspora designers for its eighth consecutive season in 2026. The March 2026 edition also marked the arrival of the Hungarian scene through the Creative Hungary initiative (source: fashionunited.fr).

### Community and networks

Tranoï is part of the ecosystem of fashion trade shows tied to Paris Fashion Week, alongside [Première Vision Paris](/salons/premiere-vision-paris), [Texworld Paris](/salons/texworld-paris) and [Who''s Next Paris](/salons/whos-next-paris).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Palais Brongniart](/lieux/palais-brongniart) listing.

Specific to the trade show:

- **Opening hours:** visitor access from 10 a.m. to 7 p.m. (6 p.m. on the final day), exhibitor access from 9 a.m. to 7 p.m.
- **Set-up:** stand installation on 25 September 2026 from 3 p.m. to 8 p.m. for the October edition.
- **Badge:** professional accreditation via the official website and the GL Events exhibitor platform.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor rates not published. Applications to exhibit are made through the GL Events platform ([exposant.gl-events.com](https://exposant.gl-events.com/login/en?mire=358)). Figure not publicly available (sector benchmark: pricing per stand depending on segment and surface area).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact with GL Events and apply to the selection (Italian Savoir-Faire, Designer Lab, Elevated Minimalism or Accessories & Lifestyle trails).
- 6 months out: prepare the stand and merchandising, with the support of the included services (visual merchandiser assistance, storage, steamers, Wi-Fi).
- 3 months out: arrange buyer meetings and press activation within the framework of Paris Fashion Week.
- 6 weeks out: confirm priority meetings and commercial brief.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Prior professional accreditation on the official website.
- Allow one to two days depending on scope (ready-to-wear, accessories, lifestyle).
- Identify the segments and international programmes in advance (CANEX, guest scenes) to optimise sourcing.

## The trade show''s evolution

