### Trajectory analysis

Taken over by GL Events in 2020, Tranoï has consolidated its position as a benchmark trade show for emerging women''s fashion in Paris, with two annual editions aligned with Paris Fashion Week. The show relies on a curated selection (thematic segments) and on recurring international programmes such as CANEX, which anchor a cosmopolitan dimension: more than 200 brands in October 2025. In parallel, GL Events has shifted part of its offering towards a promotional format (Tranoï Showcase) from January 2025, refocusing the historic show on the women''s spring and autumn editions.', seo_title_en='Tranoï Paris 2026: fashion and designer trade show, dates and exhibitor info', seo_description_en='Tranoï 2026 at the Palais Brongniart: the Paris trade show for women''s fashion and emerging designers. Dates, brands, curated segments, CANEX programme and exhibitor access.' WHERE slug='tranofiliere-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='European mobility trade show. Public transport, rail, buses, urban mobility and collective transport solutions.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Salon Transports Publics / European Mobility Expo** is merging with the **Rencontres nationales du transport public (RNTP)** and becoming **Mobco** in 2026. The first edition under this name takes place from **9 to 11 June 2026 at the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), Hall 4** (source: mobco-expo.com/dates-lieu-et-acces).
- Mobco is organised by the **GIE Objectif Transport Public**, a body created by the **GART** (Groupement des autorités responsables de transport) and the **UTPF** (Union des Transports Publics et Ferroviaires).
- 2024 edition (in Strasbourg, under the name European Mobility Expo): around **11,000 participants** and **250 exhibitors** across nearly **20,000 m²** (source: gart.org, alenium.com).
- Expected for 2026: **more than 10,000** professional participants and **nearly 250 exhibitors**.
- Renewed format: a trade show and a congress brought together, one year in Paris, the following year in the regions.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Rolling stock manufacturers (buses, trams, rail), ticketing and operations and passenger information support systems (SAEIV), transport operators, mobility organising authorities, industrial players in the energy transition (electric, hydrogen, biofuels), mobility start-ups, developers and players in active travel modes (cycling, walking). A strictly professional visitor base: elected representatives and local authorities, decision-makers, operators, industrial players, entrepreneurs.

### Notable exhibitors

The list of 2026 exhibitors is on the official website: [mobco-expo.com/exposants-2026](https://mobco-expo.com/exposants-2026/). A dedicated start-up area brings together around fifteen young companies, and an active mobility area is run by the Réseau vélo et marche.

### Visitor quality

- A 100% professional visitor base: elected representatives and local authorities, decision-makers, operators, industrial players, entrepreneurs across the mobility sector.
- A strong presence of mobility organising authorities, members of the GART, and operators belonging to the UTPF.
- Congress and trade show brought together in a single venue, drawing public decision-makers and solution providers together.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

The GART and UTPF congress structures the programme around the sector''s major challenges: energy transition, military mobility, social inclusion and climate adaptation. The detailed programme and speakers are available at [mobco-expo.com/programme](https://mobco-expo.com/programme/). The trade show also offers technical visits and an innovation pitch area.

### Awards and accolades

The **Grands Prix Mobco** are presented on Tuesday 9 June 2026 at 12.00 on the Grande Scène of the Forum Mobco. They comprise:

- **Grand Prix Mobco Territoire Pionnier**: rewards an organising authority / operator pairing that has implemented an innovative or pioneering service in 2025.
- **Grand Prix Mobco Personnalité de l''année 2026**.
- **Grand Prix Mobco Innovations**, in four categories: "Energy transition", "Services for operators", "Services for travellers", "Developments and accessibility" (source: mobco-expo.com/grands-prix-mobco-2026).

The event also hosts the **Bus d''Or 2026** (source: mobco-expo.com/bus-dor-2026).

### Community and networks

Mobco draws on the two leading networks of French public mobility: the **GART**, an association of elected representatives representing the organising authorities, and the **UTPF**, the professional organisation of urban and rail transport companies. The active mobility area is run by the **Réseau vélo et marche**.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Hall:** Hall 4 (source: mobco-expo.com/dates-lieu-et-acces).
- **Opening hours:** Tuesday 9 and Wednesday 10 June from 9.00 to 18.30, Thursday 11 June from 9.00 to 17.00.
- **Visitor badge:** online registration via [mobco.badge.events](https://mobco.badge.events/FR/).

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: making contact with the organisation, choosing a positioning (standard stand or start-up area).
- 6 months out: preparing the stand plan and demonstrations, targeting the organising authorities and operators to meet.
- 4 months out: applying for the Grands Prix Mobco for eligible innovative solutions.
- 6 weeks out: confirming meetings with decision-makers, sales briefing on the congress themes (energy transition, opening to competition).

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Online pre-registration via the official badge platform.
- Identify the GART-UTPF congress conferences in advance according to your priorities (energy, inclusion, climate adaptation).
- Plan to visit the start-up area and the active mobility area to spot what is new.
- Attend the Grands Prix Mobco ceremony on Tuesday 9 June at 12.00 to identify pioneering territories and solutions.

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Édition" },
  { "key": "lieu", "label": "Lieu" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Participants", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exposants", "align": "right" }
