### Trajectory analysis

The trade show is the direct heir of the Salon Transports Publics, rebranded European Mobility Expo, which until then alternated between Paris and the regions (Strasbourg in 2024). In 2026, it merges with the Rencontres nationales du transport public (RNTP) to become Mobco, bringing together under a single banner the professional trade show and the sector''s historic congress. This consolidation positions Mobco as the benchmark gathering for sustainable mobility in France, championed by the two leading networks that are the GART and the UTPF. The format now alternates one year in Paris, the following year in the regions.', seo_title_en='Mobco 2026 (ex-European Mobility Expo): Paris mobility show', seo_description_en='Mobco 2026, born of the merger of European Mobility Expo and RNTP, from 9 to 11 June in Paris Porte de Versailles. Sustainable mobility trade show and congress: 10,000 participants, 250 exhibitors. Organised by the GIE Objectif Transport Public (GART, UTPF).' WHERE slug='transports-publics-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Annual congress of the Union Nationale des Économistes de la Construction. The meeting point for construction economics and project management professionals.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- The **Congrès UNTEC** is the annual national gathering of the **Union Nationale des Économistes de la Construction** (UNTEC), the representative trade body for the profession since 1972. The 2026 edition is the **54th congress** (53rd in 2025).
- Since 2025, the trade show element of the congress has been known as **Salon Actes** (standing for Aménagement Construction Territoires Economie Solutions), a format open to the entire construction, architecture and development sector. The Chartres edition is the **2nd edition** of Salon Actes.
- The next edition runs from 3 to 5 June 2026 at the [Parc des Expositions L''Iliade de Chartres](/lieux/parc-expo-iliade-chartres): general meeting and congress on 3 June, with the trade show open to all sector players on 4 and 5 June.
- Travelling format: the 1st edition of Salon Actes took place in Le Havre (Carré des Docks) in June 2025, with the 2nd edition in Chartres in 2026. The venue changes with each edition.
- Dominant theme of the 2026 edition: artificial intelligence and mastering it across the construction trades (source: batiactu.com).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers and material producers, vendors of trade software (construction economics, BIM, quantity surveying), engineering consultancies, and technical and constructive solutions across all trades. The visitor base brings together construction economists, project managers, clients, architects, engineering consultancies and sector businesses.

### Notable exhibitors

The exhibitor list is available on the official website: [actes-untec.com/exposants](https://www.actes-untec.com/exposants). Around a hundred exhibitors present their product and technical innovations. Among the exhibitors and partners of recent editions: Malerba, Tellier Brise-Soleil, IsoHemp, Construction21 (sources: malerba.fr, tellierbrisesoleil.com, isohemp.com, construction21.org).

### Quality of the visitor base

- A professional visitor base from the construction sector, strongly geared towards specification and project economics (construction economists, project managers, engineering consultancies).
- The 1st edition of Salon Actes in 2025 in Le Havre targeted more than 1,500 visitors (figure announced ahead of the event; no audited OJS report published to date).
- The congress also brings together UNTEC members for their annual general meeting.

## Activities and community

### Conference programme

The programme is built around the congress (general meeting and plenary sessions for UNTEC members) and Salon Actes, which is open to the whole sector. The 2026 edition placed artificial intelligence at the heart of the discussions (source: batiactu.com).

The show''s signature format: the **BATI.REX**, 15-minute expert talks held within the exhibition hall, organised around several themes: business management (administration, HR, entrepreneurship), feedback on landmark projects, and innovations in materials, techniques and processes. The 2026 edition added a strand of "feedback on life journeys".

### Awards and accolades

Salon Actes recognises both partner exhibitors and UNTEC members through trophy ceremonies (source: actes-untec.com, to be cross-checked via browser). Categories and winners are announced in the run-up to each edition.

### Community and networks

UNTEC is the representative trade body for construction economists and runs the congress through its Untec Services structure.

Salon Actes forms partnerships with sector media and networks, including Construction21 for the 2026 edition (source: construction21.org).

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for the [Parc des Expositions L''Iliade de Chartres](/lieux/parc-expo-iliade-chartres).

Specific to the trade show:

- **Access:** L''Iliade is reachable via the A11 from Paris (around 1 hr by car) and by train from Paris-Montparnasse (around 1 hr). Free parking on site (source: actes-untec.com/informations-pratiques).
- **Visitor badge:** prior online registration on the official website, reserved for sector professionals.
- **Travelling format:** the venue changes with each edition. Check the city and site of the upcoming edition on actes-untec.com before planning your visit.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact to book a stand via the official Salon Actes website.
- 6 months out: prepare the stand layout and product demonstrations.
- 3 months out: apply for the trophies and pitch a BATI.REX talk if relevant.
- 6 weeks out: schedule meetings with construction economists and specifiers.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Pre-register online on actes-untec.com with proof of professional activity.
- Identify the BATI.REX talks and project feedback sessions of interest in advance, according to your projects.
- Allow one to two days depending on scope (material innovations, trade software, specification).

## How the trade show has evolved

<HistoryTable
 columns={[
  { "key": "edition", "label": "Edition" },
  { "key": "lieu", "label": "Venue" },
  { "key": "visiteurs", "label": "Visitors", "align": "right" },
  { "key": "exposants", "label": "Exhibitors", "align": "right" }
 ]}
 rows={[
  { "edition": "2026 (54th congress, 2nd Salon Actes)", "lieu": "Chartres", "visiteurs": "n/a", "exposants": "~100" },
  { "edition": "2025 (53rd congress, 1st Salon Actes)", "lieu": "Le Havre", "visiteurs": "target: 1,500+", "exposants": "~100" }
 ]}
 sources="actes-untec.com, tellierbrisesoleil.com, batiactu.com"
/>

### Trajectory analysis

In 2025, UNTEC overhauled the trade show element of its national congress under a new brand, Salon Actes, opened up to the entire construction, architecture and development sector beyond members alone. The 1st edition in Le Havre brought together around a hundred exhibitors and targeted more than 1,500 visitors (a figure announced ahead of the event). The 2nd edition, in Chartres from 3 to 5 June 2026, confirms this travelling format and made artificial intelligence its common thread. Backed by a congress now in its 54th edition, Salon Actes builds on UNTEC''s historic roots in the construction economics profession while broadening out to project managers, engineering consultancies and manufacturers. The city and site of the following edition are announced at each congress.', seo_title_en='Congrès UNTEC 2026 Chartres: Salon Actes for construction economists', seo_description_en='The Congrès UNTEC and its Salon Actes 2026 bring the construction sector together from 3 to 5 June at the Parc Expo L''Iliade in Chartres: exhibitors, BATI.REX, programme. Practical info.' WHERE slug='untec-congres';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='World trade fair for equipment and services for vine, wine, fruit and vegetables. Innovations for the wine-growing and fruit-growing sectors.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Vinitech-Sifel 2026 holds its **25th edition** from **1 to 3 December 2026** at the [Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux](/lieux/parc-des-expositions-de-bordeaux). A scheduling shift compared with the initial organiser brief (24-26 November), confirmed by the official website.
- Organised by **Bordeaux Events And More (BEAM)**, the SAS that succeeded Congrès et Expositions de Bordeaux (CEB) in October 2022 and runs the Parc Expo plus 4 other Bordeaux event venues. No institutional co-organiser.
- A **biennial trade fair held in even years** since 1977, alternating with [SITEVI](/salons/sitevi-montpellier-2025) (Montpellier, odd years). It covers vine and wine, fruit growing, market gardening and olive growing.
- 2024 results: **37,000 entries** (vs a 45,000 target, -12% vs 2022), **750 exhibitors**, **80 countries** represented, **70+ conferences**. 2026 target: 40,000 professionals, 700 exhibitors, 70 countries, 50+ start-ups.
- **Innovation Awards** (Trophées de l''Innovation): 4 categories (Cultivation, Processing, Packaging, Marketing), 79 entries assessed in 2024, 20 medals (4 Gold, 5 Silver, 11 Bronze) plus 19 commendations. Gold Award winners 2024: INFACO (Cultivation), Naïo Technologies (Cultivation), Parsec Srl (Processing), Maubrac (Packaging).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

The leading international trade fair for equipment and expertise across the **wine-growing, fruit-growing and market-gardening** sectors. Five main segments: viticultural and winemaking equipment, processing equipment, packaging and logistics, services and consultancy, research and training. The target audience extends to agroecology, decarbonisation and the circular economy through the **Agroecological Transition Space**, supported by the DRAAF Nouvelle-Aquitaine and the Nouvelle-Aquitaine Regional Chamber of Agriculture.

### Notable exhibitors

Regular presence of the major viticultural equipment brands: INFACO (secateurs), Naïo Technologies (viticultural robotics), Pellenc, Bucher Vaslin, Della Toffola, Parsec Srl, Advanced Track & Trace, Wine & Tools. On the start-up side: 50+ young companies expected at the **International Start-Up Village**. The official up-to-date list is available on the [exhibitors page](https://www.vinitech-sifel.com/fr/exposants).

### Quality of attendees

A highly qualified profile: wine growers, fruit growers, market-gardening decision-makers, cooperatives, merchants, equipment manufacturers, technical institutes (IFV) and trade bodies. The leading international trio in 2024: Spain, Italy, Portugal. New delegations in 2024: Croatia, Georgia, Ukraine, Serbia, United Kingdom. Bernard Farges, chairman of the trade fair, positions Vinitech-Sifel as the sector''s forward-looking meeting point against a backdrop of industry turbulence (the wine-growing crisis, environmental transitions).

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

**70+ conferences, round tables and practical workshops** for the 2026 edition. Core themes: agroecology, export, new technologies, climate transition, processing and bottling, marketing. The programme is co-built with trade bodies, research institutes and the Nouvelle-Aquitaine Region. Wine & Spirit Profiling format for the analytical tasting of international wines and spirits.

### Prizes & awards

**Vinitech-Sifel Innovation Awards**: four official categories, verbatim: **Cultivation**, **Processing**, **Packaging**, **Marketing**. Three medal levels (Gold, Silver, Bronze) plus Commendations. Gold winners 2024: **INFACO** (F3020 Contactless secateurs with a contactless safety system, Cultivation category), **Naïo Technologies** (augmented autonomy mode for the Ted and Jo viticultural robots, Cultivation category), **Parsec Srl** (ADCML technology for the continuous analysis of malolactic fermentation, Processing category), **Maubrac** (Dispo bottle-positioning robot, Packaging category). 79 entries assessed in 2024, 39 awards in total: 4 Gold, 5 Silver, 11 Bronze, 19 commendations. Applications for 2026 are open via the [official website](https://www.vinitech-sifel.com/fr/programme/trophees-de-linnovation).

### Satellite events

**Vinitech Innovation Tours 2026**: turnkey export programmes to **Croatia** and **Argentina** (technical visits, B2B meetings, conferences, networking). **Sphère des Métiers**: a space dedicated to training and careers across the sectors. **Techno Show**: live equipment demonstrations. **Vinitech Games**: a playful trade fair activity format.

### Community & networks

International outreach via the **Promosalons** network across 7 countries (Bulgaria/Romania, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Portugal, Switzerland, Tunisia).

Long-standing specialist press: Vitisphere, Mon Viti, Réussir Vigne, La Vigne, Revue Française d''Œnologie, Réussir Fruits & Légumes, Agro Media. Official accounts @bordeauxvinitech (Instagram, LinkedIn).

### What''s new in 2026

25th anniversary edition. Strengthening of the **Agroecological Transition Space** (equipment, agroecology, processing, market distribution). Expansion of the marketing-support strand (a commitment following the 2024 review). Vinitech Innovation Tours extended (Croatia + Argentina, against a single destination per cycle previously).

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Parc des Expositions de Bordeaux](/lieux/parc-des-expositions-de-bordeaux), Bordeaux Lac district. 2024 trade fair area: **70,000 m²** of exhibition space.
- **Access**: Tram C, Parc des Expositions stop (about 20 min from the centre). By car: A630 ring road, exit 4 (Bordeaux Lac). Bordeaux-Mérignac Airport 15 km away. Bordeaux Saint-Jean station 6 km away (Paris-Bordeaux TGV 2h05).
- **Parking**: Parc Expo car parks P0 and P1 are accessible, paying. Heavy saturation over the 3 days, so favour tram C.
- **Accommodation**: Lac district (Parc hotels), city centre, or Bouliac/Mérignac. December is the low tourist season in Bordeaux, with reasonable availability outside any large simultaneous conventions.
- **Opening hours & badges**: Professional visitor registration on the official website, with a free badge until a deadline and paying thereafter. See the [Visit page](https://www.vinitech-sifel.com/fr/visiter).
- **Services**: On-site catering, press area, Wine & Spirit Profiling (tastings), Sphère des Métiers, Techno Show for field demonstrations.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: initial commercial contact with BEAM, choice of hall and stand size, application for the 2026 pre-publication exhibitor listing
- 9 months out: application for the **Innovation Awards** (4 categories: Cultivation, Processing, Packaging, Marketing). The awards timetable is published several months before opening
- 9 months out: International Start-Up Village option if eligible (young companies under 5 years old as a general rule)
- 6 months out: stand brief, sign-off on visuals, application for a Vinitech Innovation Tour if targeting Croatia/Argentina export
- 3 months out: team accreditations, accommodation (December = no major pressure, but book early to stay close to the venue), preparation of the press kit for Vitisphere/Mon Viti/Réussir
- 6 weeks out: invitation of qualified contacts via the official platform, scheduling of B2B meetings

### For the decision-making visitor

- Pre-register for a free badge before the deadline, paying thereafter (check the website)
- Select 2 to 3 priority focus areas (viticultural equipment, processing, packaging, agroecology): the trade fair is too broad to be covered in full in a single day
- Identify the 2024 Innovation Award winners in advance (results list online) to structure a technical itinerary
- Wine & Spirit Profiling: limited slots, book ahead
- Agroecology and export conferences: a detailed forward-looking programme is on the website, with high-density sessions

## ESG policy & initiatives

Vinitech-Sifel is produced by **Bordeaux Events And More (BEAM)**, operator of an exhibition centre located in a city of Bordeaux certified **ISO 20121** as an "innovative and responsible destination" and named European Capital of Smart Tourism in 2022. The ISO 20121 certification is held by the Bordeaux destination as a whole: to be cross-checked with BEAM on the exact scope applied to the trade fair (internal note).

The trade fair''s core ESG content runs through the **Agroecological Transition Space**, supported by the DRAAF Nouvelle-Aquitaine and the Nouvelle-Aquitaine Regional Chamber of Agriculture, in collaboration with trade bodies, research institutes and associations. This space promotes sustainable practices, decarbonisation and the circular economy for the vine-wine and fruit-vegetable sectors.

On the content side, the agroecology conferences and the Innovation Awards showcase impactful technologies (energy-efficient viticultural robotics, autonomous secateurs, low-carbon fermentation analysis, digital traceability).

## The trade fair''s evolution

