### Trajectory analysis

Vinitech-Sifel has been going through a downward cycle in visitor volumes for the past two editions (-7% in 2022, -12% in 2024 vs a 45,000 target), against a backdrop of a structural crisis in the French wine-growing sector (vine grubbing-up, falling consumption, export pressures). Organiser BEAM nonetheless claims an **improving quality of attendees**: decision-makers and prescribers geared towards investment in equipment, automation and the environmental transition. The 2026 edition plays the repositioning card: a 25th anniversary edition, an expanded agroecological space, strengthened marketing support (a defensive focus following the 2024 review), and doubled Vinitech Innovation Tours (Croatia + Argentina) to embed the export dimension at a time when French wine growers are seeking growth levers outside Europe. The alternation with [SITEVI Montpellier](/salons/sitevi-montpellier-2025) in odd years consolidates the French duopoly of technical vine-wine trade fairs.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='vinitech-sifel-bordeaux';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='10th edition of VivaTech at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, with +30% floor space and Germany as guest country of honour. 2025 review: 180,000 visitors, 14,000 startups, 3,600 investors, 171 nationalities represented.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- VivaTech 2026 celebrates its **10th edition** from 17 to 20 June at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, with **+30% floor space** (Hall 7 fully deployed across 3 levels, +20,000 sq m): the largest edition ever organised.
- **Germany as guest country of honour** (800 sq m stand, 200 startups, 14 Länder represented + 12 government entities) and **India as AI partner** following the global AI summit in Delhi in February 2026: a deliberate geopolitical tech positioning.
- The 2025 edition gathered 180,000 visitors (+9%), 14,000 startups and 3,600 investors. VivaTech has become the largest tech event in Europe and is closing in on the CES in Las Vegas in the B2B-startup segment.
- High 4-day B2B prices (Attendee 650 €, Startup 350 €, Investor 830 €) but **the investor ecosystem is highly concentrated here**: 640,000 B2B connections in 2025, Investors Office Hours new for 2026, Tech for Change Award.
- 2026 ownership: **Elvyr (Maurice Lévy) + LVMH/Les Echos**. Publicis Groupe sold its stake in August 2025 but remains a co-founder and historic partner. No financial fund-type investor on the holding company.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

A B2B tech trade show covering the full spectrum of innovation: generative AI, climate tech, mobility, health, retail tech, fintech, deep tech, quantum, robotics. 14,000 startups in 2025, targeting 15,000 in 2026. A massive presence of major groups (CAC 40, Fortune 500), corporate partners, international VC funds and country pavilions.

### Notable exhibitors

Major partners for 2026: BNP Paribas, Google, La Poste, LVMH, Orange. Long-standing presence of NVIDIA (Jensen Huang keynote, GTC Paris 2025), Mistral, Hugging Face, Meta, OpenAI, Anthropic, Alibaba, Canva, ElevenLabs, Alan. 50+ country pavilions in 2025, targeting 60+ in 2026 including new entrants Singapore, Oman and Zimbabwe.

### Retention rate

No public figure has been communicated, but the ecosystem effect is huge: the major founding partners (Publicis Groupe co-founder, LVMH, Orange, BNP Paribas, Google, La Poste) return every year since 2016. On the startup side, turnover is high (a "showcase" model of 1 to 3 years for most early-stage companies).

### Attendee quality

171 nationalities represented in 2025, making it the most international event in the French tech calendar. Decision-maker profile: startup CEOs/founders, corporate innovation leaders, VCs, business angels, family offices, tech journalists, government spearheads (12 German entities in 2026). Strong international press presence.

## Activities & community

### Conference programme

450+ speakers in 2025, 300+ product announcements. 2025 edition: Jensen Huang (NVIDIA, GTC Paris keynote), Arthur Mensch (Mistral), Emmanuel Macron, Joe Tsai (Alibaba), Yann LeCun (Meta), Sarah Friar (OpenAI), Mike Krieger (Anthropic), Thomas Wolf (Hugging Face), Cliff Obrecht (Canva), Alain Aspect (Nobel laureate). Speakers expected for 2026: Bernard Arnault (LVMH), Jean-Charles Samuelian (Alan), Mati Staniszewski (ElevenLabs), Yann LeCun.

### Awards & prizes

Global Awards Ceremony (the main ceremony). Next Startupper Challenge, 2025 winner Greeny Solutions. Tech for Change Award, 2025 winner Genesis. New for 2026: **Oscars de la tech**, an unprecedented awards format launched for the 10-year anniversary. Target: 1,500+ product demos at the show.

### Satellite events

New for the 10-year anniversary: **Takeover Champs-Élysées on 14 June 2026** (off-site, pre-opening weekend). Public festival on Saturday 20 June (ticket 20 €). Léon Marchand official ambassador for 2026. **Investors Office Hours**: a new format of structured meetings between startups and VCs. Impact Bridge powered by EDF: 1,500 sq m dedicated to sustainable innovation.

### Community & networks

Historic founding partners: Publicis Groupe (co-founder), Les Echos / Le Parisien (LVMH group). Network of country pavilions (60+ in 2026). Official B2B matchmaking platform: 640,000 connections generated in 2025. Target of 4,000+ structured business meetings in 2026. Official VivaTech app.

### New for 2026

10th anniversary edition. **+30% floor space** with the full deployment of Hall 7 at Porte de Versailles across 3 levels (+20,000 sq m). Germany as guest country of honour (800 sq m, the largest stand ever hosted, 200 startups). India as AI partner (following the global AI summit in Delhi in February 2026). New country pavilions: Singapore, Oman, Zimbabwe. Oscars de la tech. Takeover Champs-Élysées on 14 June. Investors Office Hours. Léon Marchand ambassador.

## On site: what you need to know

- **Venue**: [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), **Hall 7 across 3 levels** (2026 edition, +30% floor space vs 2025).
- **Transport access**: Metro L12 (Porte de Versailles, direct stop at Hall 7) or L8 (Balard). Trams T2 and T3a. In mid-June, tourist traffic in Paris is intense, so allow 30 to 45 minutes of leeway from the city centre.
- **Parking**: On-site and nearby car parks, heavily saturated over the 4 days. Favour public transport or private-hire vehicles.
- **Accommodation**: The 15th arrondissement (Convention, Vaugirard, Pasteur) as a priority. Book 4 to 6 months in advance, as mid-June concentrates several major Parisian events (Roland-Garros has just finished, summer festivals starting up).
- **Opening hours & badges**: Wed 17 to Fri 19 June: B2B days reserved for professionals. Sat 20 June: public festival, ticket at 20 €.
- **Services**: Multiple catering options on site in Hall 7. Networking areas and investor lounges. Investors Office Hours by appointment. TV sets, demo areas. Official VivaTech app for matchmaking.

## How much it costs to exhibit

