### Trajectory analysis

In 2025 Web Summit confirmed its status as Europe''s largest tech conference, with 71,386 attendees from 157 countries. The sold-out 2024 edition had drawn 71,528 attendees (the event''s record): the 2025 edition reflects remarkable stability at around 71,000 attendees. The standout development of 2025 was the strong growth in investor presence: 1,857 funds present, up 74% on 2024, against the gloomy trend in venture capital. The startup pool remains the core of the trade show, with 2,725 young companies exhibiting, of which 40% were founded by women. The 2026 edition, from 9 to 12 November in Lisbon, continues this momentum. The 2026 theme and target figures will be published as the event approaches.', seo_title_en='Web Summit 2026 Lisbon: dates, exhibitors, practical info', seo_description_en='Web Summit 2026 in Lisbon, 9 to 12 November: Europe''s largest tech conference. 71,386 attendees in 2025, 2,725 startups, 1,857 investors. Programme and info.' WHERE slug='web-summit-lisbonne';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Long-standing women''s ready-to-wear fashion trade show, founded in 1994 by WSN Développement, autumn 2026 edition at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles Hall 7. January 2026 cluster results: 1,760 exhibiting brands (1,200 Who''s Next), 38,000 unique visitors (+5% vs September 2025).', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- Autumn 2026 edition of Who''s Next: **5 to 7 September 2026** (Saturday to Monday) at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, **Hall 7**.
- Long-standing women''s ready-to-wear fashion trade show, founded in **1994** by WSN Développement. Core target: emerging and premium brands, multi-brand buyers, e-shops and department stores.
- Winter edition results, January 2026 (17-19 January, "Room 0126" scenography): **around 1,200 exhibiting brands** for Who''s Next alone, **1,760 brands** across the full cluster (Who''s Next, Bijorhca, Shoppe Object Paris, Salon International Lingerie, Interfilière Paris), **38,000 unique visitors** across the cluster, **+5%** versus September 2025.
- WSN''s longer-term target: **45,000 visitors** per edition across the cluster scope.
- Next winter edition announced: **17 to 19 January 2027** (Saturday to Monday), Paris Expo Porte de Versailles.

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Who''s Next organises its offering around two long-standing universes and category extensions:

- **Fresh** (created in 1996): young design, emerging women''s ready-to-wear brands, brands accessible in terms of wholesale pricing, high exhibitor turnover.
- **Fame** (created in 2002): premium women''s segment, established brands, a more structured positioning for middle-up buyers and high-end concept stores.
- **Accessories, lifestyle and beauty**: category extensions that round out the ready-to-wear offering, in line with the evolution of multi-brand assortments.

The January 2026 edition featured **30% new ready-to-wear brands**, confirming the offering''s renewal momentum, and saw five cluster trade shows deployed across Hall 7 (Who''s Next, Bijorhca, Salon International Lingerie, Interfilière Paris, Shoppe Object Paris), with the **first Paris edition of Shoppe Object** (the Paris iteration of the New York lifestyle and home show).

### Notable exhibitors

A mix of established international brands and young designers: **Leon & Harper**, **True Religion**, **Blundstone**, and a large **L''Artyrie** collective pavilion dedicated to emerging brands (collective stands of 4 to 30 m², a format designed for first-time show participation).

### Quality of the visitor base

- Independent French and European multi-brand buyers.
- Department store and specialist chain buyers.
- Ready-to-wear e-shops and B2B marketplaces.
- A growing number of international buyers, driven by the presence in Hall 7 of related trade shows (lingerie, jewellery, accessories, lifestyle).
- Fashion press, trend agencies, influencers.

Room 0126 cluster visitor pricing: **€55 incl. VAT in advance** online, **€70 incl. VAT on site**. The badge grants access to all cluster trade shows across the three days.

## Activities and community

### Conference and trends programme

A trends programme led by **Nelly Rodi** (fashion forecasting agency). Stage-based conference format, seasonal analyses, decoding of macro-trends and market focuses.

### Welcome Buyer Lounge

A space dedicated to international buyers: reception, concierge service, brand matchmaking, appointment booking, dedicated services. A lever for attracting and retaining overseas buyers, in line with the 45,000-visitor target across the full scope.

### Who''s Next Lab: AI applied to fashion

A programme dedicated to artificial intelligence applied to the fashion trades: assisted design tools, trend forecasting, supply chain optimisation, retail tech. A conference-plus-demonstration format, open to exhibitors and visitors alike.

### Ankorstore partnership

A structuring partnership since 2024 with **Ankorstore**, the European B2B marketplace. A digital extension of the trade show: exhibiting brands can activate their Ankorstore presence before, during and after the show, turning a physical encounter into a recurring commercial relationship on the platform.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles) listing.

Specific to the show:

- **Pavilion**: Hall 7, shared with the other trade shows in the Room 0126 cluster.
- **Dates**: Saturday 5 to Monday 7 September 2026.
- **Visitor badge**: €55 incl. VAT in advance, €70 incl. VAT on site, full cluster access.
- **Audience**: strictly trade, proof of business activity required at registration.
- **Weekend + Monday format**: a deliberate choice to include Saturday and Sunday to make access easier for independent multi-brand buyers.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Exhibitor pricing is not published by WSN Développement. Quotes on request from the sales team, with several packages available:

- **Individual stand** in the Fresh or Fame hub, with surface area of your choice.
- **L''Artyrie collective stand**: formats from 4 to 30 m², a solution suited to emerging brands at their first participation, with shared scenographic support.
- **Fame premium pack**: positioning and services dedicated to the premium segment.

The price per m² varies depending on the universe (Fresh vs Fame), placement and format (bare, equipped or packaged stand). The Ankorstore partnership can be built into the exhibitor pack.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 9 months out: make contact with WSN, choose a universe (Fresh or Fame), apply for the L''Artyrie collective stand for emerging brands.
- 6 months out: confirm the stand, brief the contractor, prepare the collection, activate Ankorstore if relevant.
- 3 months out: pre-show appointment programme, partner buyer invitations, press materials.
- 6 weeks out: finalise stand merchandising, brief the sales team, prepare for the Welcome Buyer Lounge if you have an international profile.
- 15 days out: activate social media, secure final appointments, handle stand delivery logistics.

### For the decision-making visitor

- Online pre-registration is strongly recommended (€55 incl. VAT vs €70 on site).
- The cluster badge grants access to the five trade shows in Hall 7: allow at least a full day to cover Who''s Next, plus half a day for the related shows depending on your business (lingerie, jewellery, lifestyle).
- Saturday: traditionally the busiest day on the independent buyer side.
- Identify Fresh (young design) and Fame (premium) brands in advance, depending on your retail positioning.

## CSR policy and initiatives

WSN Développement has structured its CSR commitment around the **Impact x Neonyt Paris** initiative, launched in partnership with **Messe Frankfurt** since September 2023. The initiative builds on and extends the **Impact** space created by Who''s Next in 2019, a pioneer in the sustainable fashion segment.

Eligibility criterion to be labelled Impact x Neonyt Paris: meeting **at least 75%** of the criteria of an eco-responsibility framework built with Messe Frankfurt (materials, traceability, production, social conditions, end of life).

Associated programming: **Smart Talks** in the Neonyt Knowledge Area, a short conference format focused on the concrete challenges of responsible fashion (recycled materials, supply chain, certifications, sustainable business models).

## How the show has evolved

