### Trajectory analysis

Wine Paris & Vinexpo Paris stems from the February 2020 merger of two historic trajectories: **Vinexpo**, created in 1981 in Bordeaux by the Bordeaux CCI (1st edition from 22 to 26 June 1981, 11,000 visitors and 500 exhibitors), and **Wine Paris**, launched in 2019 by Comexposium and itself the product of the merger of **Vinisud** (created in 1994) and **VinoVision** (2017). The alliance sealed in February 2020 led to the creation of **Vinexposium** on 14 September 2020, a joint venture between **Comexposium** and **Vinexpo Holding**. The first joint Wine Paris & Vinexpo Paris edition was held from 10 to 12 February 2020 at Paris Expo Porte de Versailles. In five editions, the trade fair has structurally changed scale: **52,622 visitors in 2025 (+28% vs 2023), 63,541 in 2026 (+20.75% international)** and **6,537 exhibitors** from 63 countries. The **overtaking of ProWein Düsseldorf**, achieved as early as 2025 (5,300 vs 4,200 exhibitors) and confirmed in 2026 (6,537 vs ~3,400), is shifting the European centre of gravity of the wine and spirits market towards Paris. The structuring into **3 worlds** (Wine Paris, Be Spirits, Be No) opens growth avenues beyond still wine, with a Be Spirits hub now at 370 exhibitors and 39 countries and a Be No world that is institutionalising the no/low segment. The **patronage of the President of the Republic** and CSR alignment via the **Net Zero Carbon Events Pledge** confirm an institutional positioning that reads clearly on an international stage.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='wine-paris';
UPDATE salons SET description_en='Trade show for workplace and office space design. Office furniture, acoustics, lighting and the design of professional spaces.', editorial_mdx_en='## Key takeaways

- **Workspace Expo becomes Workspace Paris**: the annual trade show for furniture, design and workplace fit-out now appears under this name, with the strapline "I LOVE MY WORKSPACE", and its official website has moved to [workspace-paris.com](https://www.workspace-paris.com/). Running since 2011, it is organised by **Weyou Group** (source: workspace-paris.com).
- 2027 edition: from Tuesday 16 to Thursday 18 March 2027 at [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles), Hall 1, with a late-night opening on the Wednesday until 9 pm.
- 2025 results: **20,910 professionals** (+2% vs 2024) and **305 exhibiting brands**, including 168 from abroad (sources: workspace-paris.com, Weyou Group 2025 results release).
- Launched for the 2026 edition, an international one-to-one business meetings programme invites major furniture distributors as well as architects and space planners from the leading European Design & Build agencies (Madrid, Barcelona, London, Amsterdam, Munich, Frankfurt, Düsseldorf) to 15-minute meetings with exhibitors, with travel and accommodation costs covered (source: Weyou Group release, April 2025).
- The 2026 edition (24 to 26 March) was co-located with SETA, the trade show for the working environment and procurement, also organised by Weyou Group (source: workplacemagazine.fr).

## Who exhibits

### Typical profile

Manufacturers and publishers of office furniture and seating, acoustic solutions (booths, mobile partitions, panels, suspended ceilings), lighting, floor and wall coverings, signage, audiovisual and videoconferencing solutions, greenery and landscaping, upcycled and reused furniture. More than half of the brands came from abroad in 2025 (168 out of 305), mostly from Europe.

### Notable exhibitors

The official exhibitor list is on the trade show''s website: [workspace-paris.com/exposants](https://www.workspace-paris.com/exposants). Among the brands listed for the 2026 edition were Bene, Dynamobel, Lyreco and 3DS Groupe.

### Quality of the visitor base

- More than 50% end users (decision-makers), 28% architects and project managers, 20% distributors in 2024
- 88% French visitors and 12% from abroad (49 nationalities) in 2025; 71% from the Île-de-France region and 29% from other regions
- Attendance by CAC 40 companies, major fit-out specialists, space planners and property firms (sources: Weyou Group 2024 and 2025 results releases)

## Programme & community

### Conference programme

The programme is built around keynotes and plenary conferences delivered by institutional partners, IDET & Workplace Magazine conferences, and workshops run by exhibitors (source: workspace-paris.com/programmes). In 2024, the 18 conferences and headline interviews played to a full house with more than 1,600 attendees (source: Weyou Group 2024 release).

In 2026, the "AUTREMENT" trends space, designed by architect Karl Petit, explored modular and adaptable spaces as an alternative to the traditional open-plan office (sources: workplacemagazine.fr, workinglife.fr).

### One-to-one business meetings

Launched for the 2026 edition, the business meetings programme draws on Weyou Group''s matchmaking platform: European Design & Build decision-makers with live projects are invited for two days of 15-minute face-to-face meetings with exhibitors (source: Weyou Group release, April 2025). The "Business meetings" page remains online on the 2027 edition''s website, with no 2027 schedule published to date.

## On site: what you need to know

Access, parking and accommodation: see the listing for [Paris Expo Porte de Versailles](/lieux/paris-expo-porte-de-versailles). The trade show occupies Hall 1.

Show-specific details:

- **2027 opening hours:** Tuesday 16 March 9 am-6 pm, Wednesday 17 March 9 am-9 pm (late-night opening), Thursday 18 March 9 am-5 pm.
- **Visitor badge:** free on request online, the trade show is reserved for professionals.
- **Press:** accreditation via the dedicated form on the official website.

## How much it costs to exhibit

Prices are not published on the official website. Four stand packages are offered: bare stand (floor marking), equipped stand (carpet, partitions, fascia, spotlights), packaged stand (full fit-out, a 3 kW electrical box and a furniture credit of €40 excl. VAT per sq m) and discovery package (boundary structure, basic furniture and reception desk).

Exhibitors can complement their presence with a 45-minute Expert Workshop: a 150-seat room equipped with audio/video, promotion across the official channels and a list of attendees supplied. Application to take part: contact@workspace-paris.com.

## Preparing your visit

### For the exhibitor

- 12 months out: book early. More than two thirds of the 2026 edition''s floor space was already booked eleven months before opening (source: Weyou Group release, April 2025).
- 6 months out: choose your stand package and apply for an Expert Workshop slot.
- 3 months out: keep an eye on the "Business meetings" page on the official website and sign up for the one-to-one programme as soon as the 2027 schedule opens.
- 1 month out: arrange your team''s presence for the Wednesday late-night opening (open until 9 pm).

### For the decision-maker visitor

- Request your free badge online at workspace-paris.com (proof of professional activity required).
- Check the "Business meetings" page in advance: the one-to-one programme connects decision-makers with pre-selected suppliers based on projects (2027 schedule not published to date).
- Note the plenary conferences on the programme: they were playing to a full house in 2024.
- The Wednesday late-night opening allows for an end-of-day visit.

## Policy & CSR initiatives

The organiser does not publish a dedicated CSR commitments page for the trade show to date.

Sustainability was nonetheless a stated focus of the 2026 edition: the "French Eco Waves" trail showcased made-in-France products, the reuse of materials and eco-construction, while the "Circular Pavilion" brought together 15 brands committed to reuse. Upcycled furniture is among the exhibition categories listed on the official exhibitor list (sources: ameublement.com, workinglife.fr, workspace-paris.com).

## How the trade show has evolved

