### Trajectory analysis

A trajectory accelerating sharply since 2023. The first edition in 2014 at Le Bourget laid the foundations of a French sector trade show (495 exhibitors, 7,200 visitors). The 2025 edition moved WNE into the category of the major global energy-sector gatherings, with 36,000 attendees and 25 national pavilions: a result of the civil nuclear relaunch in Europe (EU green taxonomy 2022, French EPR2 plan, European SMR programme), in the United States (Inflation Reduction Act, X-energy, Kairos Power and NuScale projects) and in Asia (programmes in India, China, Korea). The 2027 edition (7-9 December) will build on this momentum, with a clear positioning around the two themes "Nuclear Today and Tomorrow" and "Beyond Electricity". Of note: RX France (formerly Reed Expositions, rebranded in 2022) remains the operator, while GIFEN remains the institutional organiser that owns the event.', seo_title_en=NULL, seo_description_en=NULL WHERE slug='world-nuclear-exhibition';

COMMIT;